window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5001,"title":"Chapter 5001: Chapter 5000: Research IV","paragraphs":["Noah looked up at the manifestations surrounding him.","\" For missiles, they proceeded to go to bombs for their next big advancement. Now a single person held in their hands the power to eliminate tens of thousands. If someone at that Scale of power were to meet with those who only fought with their fists and swords, they would be untouchable, would they not?\"","His eyes flickered with understanding.","\" Maybe that is what THE Second Scale of Existence considers those at THE First Scale of Existence. But I digress.\"","He continued, his voice building with the weight of what he was expressing.","\" Continuing with my analogy, from explosive bombs filled with gunpowder, they then elevated their technology to nuclear bombs. Now a single person of that so-called advanced Civilization could carry a single weapon, a single Atom Bomb, and they could decimate tens of millions. Go even further and make Hydrogen Bombs, and now your advanced Civilization could kill billions.\"","Noah’s hands fell to his sides.","\" All of that. For the sake of adversity and conflict and warfare. To continue advancing Civilization.\"","He became quiet after talking for such a long time.","He did not remember the last time he had talked so much.","But at this moment, his eyes were shining with profundity as he spoke again.","\"I wonder which stage in that example I gave I am at? Am I still using my fists as THE First Scale of Existence? Can the power I have right now be considered a sharp sword or projectile?\"","He looked at the Four Aspects surrounding him.","\" From now on, should I proceed my Civilization in building something to get ready for the coming adversity? To make my Civilization into a weapon that could destroy thousands of Absolutes with a single push? To make my Civilization akin to a bomb I can throw at Primordial Architects and obliterate them in an existential fallout?\"","His voice softened with something approaching weariness.","\" Just at which point will the struggle and adversity end? I want to decide this. I want to change this. I want to advance my Civilization in peace. Farming. Fishing. Cooking. Just grasping the nature of existence itself. The nature of Infinity.\"","Noah raised his hand up as if he was reaching out to a distant, distant dream that he would never grasp.","\"If I could sit in peace just studying Infinity...\"","All he saw above him were those vibrant waves of Existence, Chaos, Paradox, and THE First Tongue. Beautiful. Magnificent. Representing everything he had achieved and everything he could still become.","But to keep them, he had to fight.","To protect them, he had to struggle.","To advance them, he had to face adversity.","He became silent.","He became reflective.","And in this silence...","\"It seems you are on the right path.\"","THE Beholder’s voice emerged with that same calculated precision, that same ancient composure that betrayed nothing resembling emotion.","\" Your path is yours to figure out. I cannot do much. I am an observer. I have always been an observer. I will simply watch as you walk whatever direction you and many others choose.\"","The geometric fragments contracted slightly.","\" But I will warn you.\"","\" Your biggest strength will be Infinity. And your biggest weakness... will be Infinity.\"","...!","The statement hung in the Wandering Territories with implications that Noah could not fully process.","\" Learn Infinity. Understand it. Conduct it. Become whatever it allows you to become.\"","THE Beholder’s eye focused with intensity.","\" But everything comes at a cost. Everything has a cost. And the cost of Infinity is not something that can be paid in Mana or Harvest or any of the currencies that complex life has invented to quantify value.\"","A pause.","\" You will learn what that cost is. Eventually. All who touch true Infinity learn it eventually. The desperate ones at THE Second Scale get to learn just as well...\"","...!","HUUM!","With these words, Noah looked up to see THE Beholder flicker.","The geometric fragments scattered like petals in wind that did not exist. The luminous eye at the center dimmed and faded. The presence that had existed since before differentiation withdrew to wherever ancient observers went when they decided they had seen enough.","And then THE Beholder was simply gone.","Noah’s eyes became heavy as around him, the manifestations of Existence, Chaos, THE First Tongue, and Paradox began to disappear. The black dahlia collapsed into wisps of obsidian that scattered through the Wandering Territories. The multicolored Dyson sphere faded into light that had no source and no destination. The endless Grimoire closed and compressed until it vanished entirely. The Mobius strip untwisted and dissolved into gold and obsidian motes that drifted away on currents only they could perceive.","He was left sitting on a chair of condensed Infinity in the middle of the Wandering Territories.","Silent.","But thinking of far too many things.","There were also so many things that he wanted to try.","He thought about the example he gave. Civilizations advancing from fists to nuclear weapons. If everything was adversity and conflict, for the budding model of his Civilization, what should he do to scale it up to be as lethal as possible?","Because until he had the power to change it, the name of the game remained Adversity.","Conflict and War remained paramount.","Might made right.","If he faced a Second Scale Primordial Architect and lost, if Noah Osmont perished, his grand fable from the beginning until now could be rewritten by whoever survived to tell the story. History was written by the victors. Always had been. Always would be.","So he could not lose.","He had to continue being victorious again and again.","And for this, he needed to innovate. He needed to grow. He needed to take this new understanding of Infinity and forge it into something that could answer any adversity that descended upon him.","So...","Noah rose from his chair of condensed Infinity.","His entire finite being seemed so mundane at this moment. No blazing radiance. No crushing weight of presence. Just a man standing in the chaos of the Wandering Territories with eyes that held depths they had not held before.","But he carried an unfathomably glorious purpose.","He took a step.","And he disappeared.","He had a lot of work to do. A lot of research to conduct. A lot of limits to test and boundaries to explore and innovations to design.","So he left to do it.","And in the back of his mind, the names of enemies were already written. THE Entity occupied the prime position it had always occupied, that unified horror spreading across Observable Existence with hunger that sought to consume everything he was.","But now, alongside THE Entity, Beowulf occupied a prime spot.","THE Primordial Armor.","THE Second Scale.","The being who had tortured Alexander for millions of subjective years trying to find Noah’s location.","The being who had demonstrated exactly how vast the gap between Scales truly was.","The being Noah had sworn to return to.","He would keep that oath.","But first, he had to become something that could make keeping it possible."]},{"number":5002,"title":"Chapter 5002: Chapter 5001: Research V","paragraphs":["Alexander could still feel that phantom pain.","Constantly it thundered across his existence. Millions upon millions of years of agony had been compressed into what had objectively been only hours, but subjective experience did not care about objective time. He had lived through eons of torment. He had experienced every possible expression of suffering that Beowulf’s expertise in Existential Nociceptors could produce.","And truly, he wanted to die.","That was how bad it was.","He wanted to die.","But he was not alone. Inside that fractured Enneagram on his chest, his family was still there. The souls he had promised to protect. The existences that depended on him to remain coherent enough to house them. If he collapsed, they collapsed with him.","So he endured.","Thinking of the Enneagram reminded him of what he had done.","THE Living Law.","The companion who had helped him gain the strength he possessed. The being who had stood beside him through countless conflicts and countless victories and countless moments when Alexander had thought himself alone only to remember that he never truly was.","He had crushed THE Living Law with his own hands.","Alexander could still feel the sensation of doing it. The way his fingers had closed around that construct of silver-white authority. The way THE Living Law had not resisted, had simply accepted what was about to happen with relief. The way the Enneagram had cracked down the middle as its primary occupant was deliberately destroyed by the one who should have protected it.","He did not blame THE Living Law!","He knew how painful that torture was. Nobody could withstand it indefinitely. Beowulf had methodologies that went beyond simple pain, techniques that found the breaking points of any existence and exploited them with precision that bordered on artistry.","THE Living Law had been about to break.","And if THE Living Law had broken, if that partner had revealed everything about Noah’s location after Alexander had endured millions of years of agony to keep that information secret, it would all have been for naught.","So Alexander had destroyed his companion before that could happen.","He had made sure his sacrifice meant something.","\"...\"","He tried to get out of his thoughts.","He tried to look around him as he realized his body was almost pieced back together. The cellular fragments that Beowulf had separated him into were rejoining. The gaps between pieces were filling with coherent existence once more. He was becoming whole again in the physical sense, even if his other wounds would take far longer to heal.","He found himself in the center of a lush green-gold field.","It extended outward in all directions, an endless expanse of grass that rose to his knees in gentle waves. The blades caught light in ways that made them shimmer between verdant green and brilliant gold, creating patterns that shifted as wind he could not feel moved across the field.","Above, a blue sky filled with gold clouds stretched toward horizons that seemed impossibly distant. The clouds drifted with peaceful slowness, their golden edges catching light from a sun that existed somewhere beyond perception. Everything about this place spoke of tranquility and recovery and the kind of safety that Alexander had not felt since before Beowulf’s chains had first wrapped around his existence.","He reached down toward the green-gold grass rising up around his legs.","And he could not help but fall.","His knees hit the soft earth. His hands pressed into the grass. His body folded forward as something he had been holding back finally demanded release.","Drops fell on the grass in front of him.","Drops? It wasn’t raining right now...","He touched his eyes to find tears coming out.","His expression hardened immediately.","He stopped them right away.","He did not cry. Men did not cry. He had endured millions of years of torture without breaking. He had destroyed his own partner to protect information that mattered. He had faced a Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale and refused to give up a single piece of what was asked of him.","He would not cry now!","Not when crying would mean admitting that what had happened had affected him in ways that went beyond physical damage.","Moments afterward, he felt something flicker behind him.","There, the figure of Osmont appeared.","Alexander turned to look at him with a complex expression. He could feel his entire existence being mended with a sequential weaving of Infinity, blue-gold light flowing through the spaces between his cellular fragments and binding them back together with authority that exceeded anything normal healing could accomplish.","When THE Primordial Armor had split him into countless pieces, Beowulf had also inadvertently split the mark of Horus that had been branded onto his existence. Alexander could thank that armored torturer for that small mercy, and Noah had done the rest.","He did not know what to say to this being.","When he looked at Osmont right now, even he seemed to be lost in thought. There was something different about him. Something that Alexander could not quite identify. The blazing radiance that had always surrounded him seemed dimmer now, less externally impressive, and yet somehow more profound.","So Alexander said simply what needed to be said.","\" Thank you.\"","...!","The few words seemed to wake Osmont up.","Noah looked toward him and shook his head before saying thank you himself.","The two then looked at each other silently.","There was a lot to say.","And yet nothing to say at all.","They both knew what the other wanted to communicate.","But...","Words would have been inadequate anyway.","So Noah sighed as he looked at Alexander with eyes that held depths they had not held before.","\" Every now and then, Existence will hurt us a great deal.\"","His voice was quiet but carried weight that pressed against the green-gold field around them.","\" Whether we expect it or not will not matter. The pain comes regardless of preparation. The suffering finds us regardless of readiness.\"","He paused.","\" But after that pain, there tends to be something for you on the other side. I do not know what lies for you on the other side. I hate the way things are. I hate that adversity seems to be the only fuel that drives advancement. I hate that we have to suffer to grow.\"","His eyes met Alexander’s directly.","\" But the least I can do is get you toward that other side. Or at least steer you toward that positive thing waiting beyond the pain you have endured.\"","...!","The moment after he said this, Alexander’s eyes opened wide.","He saw a contemplative look bloom on Osmont’s face. Noah raised his hand with a breath, and the moment he did...","The blue sky with gold clouds became filled with endless blue.","It reminded Alexander of an unfathomable sea, a vast expanse of Infinity that stretched across the entire sky and pressed against the boundaries of this space. The blue was deep and endless!","Noah motioned downward.","This vast sea began to crash down toward them, but as it descended, it changed. The blue transformed into multicolored radiance as its weavings distinctly burned with the authority of Existence itself. Existence in its purest form, the very authority that THE Creature wielded as his native expression!","The vast sea formed into a pinpoint above Alexander.","And then it began to flood into him.","Into his existence. Into his broken Enneagram. Into every damaged aspect of what he was and what he had been before Beowulf’s torture had shattered him.","Boundless waves of Infinite Existence felt like warm multicolored flames meant to cleanse and wash away all the pain. They flowed through his foundations and filled the cracks and mended what had been unmendable!","Alexander took it all in somberly.","He felt like a tiny boat in the middle of a vast storm, buffeted by forces that exceeded his comprehension by magnitudes he could not calculate. But he held. He remained coherent. He accepted what was being given without allowing it to sweep him away entirely.","The one controlling that storm into his existence had a careful look on his face. As if he was trying something new, and yet also knew what he was doing. As if he were simultaneously an experimenter and an expert, learning and mastering at the same time.","With such a gaze watching over him, Alexander closed his eyes.","He remembered everything.","The fear he felt when Beowulf’s chains first wrapped around his existence. The hatred he felt when those armored fingers began their work on his Existential Nociceptors. Every single piece of emotion toward Beowulf that he had experienced across those millions of subjective years.","He repeated it again and again.","He could not forget that pain.","And because he could not forget it, because he refused to let that suffering become meaningless, something began to happen within him.","As he felt his Enneagram heal rapidly and become filled with boundless multicolored light of Existence, the nine end sockets on that construct began to spin. They moved like forges and engines, generating heat and purpose and transformation.","They formed countless small multicolored gems!"]},{"number":5003,"title":"Chapter 5003: Chapter 5002: Research VI","paragraphs":["Gems of Existence crystallized from the authority flowing into him, shaped by his hatred and refined by his determination.","And Alexander began to flood these gems onto receptors that no entity of THE First Scale of Existence should be able to notice.","The Existential Nociceptors.","The Civilizational Afferents.","The Delta-Threads of Existence and the C-Fibers of Being.","The receptors that Beowulf had burned again and again across millions of years of torture, finding them and exploiting them and using them to deliver agony that exceeded anything Alexander had ever imagined possible.","Alexander did not forget them.","He had felt their locations burned into his awareness through repeated abuse. He knew exactly where they were now, knew their architecture and their pathways and their connections to his overall existence.","And at this time, he allowed waves of Infinite Existence altered into his own weavings of the Enneagram to flow across areas his own existence had not known existed before Beowulf taught him they were there.","His body began to shine brilliantly with a multicolored allure.","His skin almost felt gem-like, crystalline structures forming beneath the surface and radiating light. He was being remade into something that incorporated the knowledge his torture had provided!","While all of this happened, he chanted in his mind with hatred.","A single name.","Beowulf.","Beowulf.","BEOWULF!","BOOM!","A scintillating gem-like multicolored light burned around him as an aura of an Absolute bloomed with intensity that would have made observers shield their perception.","This was not the aura he had possessed before his capture.","This exceeded anything he had been capable of before Beowulf’s torture had broken him down and built him back up through suffering.","This exceeded any lesser existence like THE Shitty Living Elemental by magnitudes that made comparison laughable.","Maybe a few hundred times grander than a worthless, despotic, bum of an Absolute like THE Living Elemental!","And during that whole time, Alexander burned with hatred that others would not be able to understand.","He thought about a Primordial Architect.","He thought about platinum armor and gaps between plates that revealed only darkness.","He thought about the being who had made him experience eons of agony for information he refused to provide.","And he swore, silently and absolutely, that he would find a way to make Beowulf feel exactly what he had felt.","No matter how long it took.","No matter what it cost!","---","There were many things Noah wanted to research.","But he had to make sure THE Peacemaker was okay first before delving into them.","He knew how in existence, everyone expected men to be okay both emotionally and physically even after they went through traumatic events. Nobody asked them if they were alright. Nobody gave them the same tender level of treatment that might be offered to others. Men were supposed to endure and move on and never speak of what they had experienced.","Ah, you dog died? Well, cheer up, lets go for drinks.","Your girl left you? Well, she sucks anyways, lets go find you another.","Far took many weavings of men were neglected!","So Noah at least came to give his ear in case Alexander needed to talk.","If he did not want to, that was okay.","Just being there for company was also good.","So right now, as endless Existence flooded into Alexander and Noah sensed changes occurring within that gem-like transformation, he tried to simply be a vessel which steered THE Peacemaker toward his boon at the end of his adversity.","He conducted the Infinite Existence without containing it, directing the endless authority toward Alexander’s recovery without forcing any particular outcome.","And while this unfolded, he waited.","While waiting, he began to try grasping his Infinity in other ways.","What he was looking at now was understanding its usage and the idea of what Infinity itself could do when he controlled it to flow into finite things.","Into THE Peacemaker, that was one application.","And right now...","Noah waved his hands in the field of green-gold grasses.","He allowed the emergence of THE Convergent Root of Density Absolute.","The Sacred Herb materialized before him with presence that spoke of its nature. It appeared as a root system that had crystallized into something between organic growth and geometric precision. Its tendrils extended in fractal patterns that repeated at every scale of observation, each smaller branch mimicking the structure of the whole in ways that suggested infinite regression.","The root pulsed with compressed authority that felt dense. This was the herb that allowed one to experience saturation acceleration at whichever Depth you directed its compressed authority toward. It had already performed the work of filling gaps between sequential Infinite expressions. Consuming it introduced pre-densified Infinity directly into foundations, advancing progression from Countable toward Uncountable Infinity.","It was something already grand.","It was not mundane by any measure.","So what if it became filled with Infinity?","DUM!","Noah began to feel that heavy beat of his heart again as he moved.","His chest expanded as he breathed in deeply, filling his finite lungs with air that meant nothing and everything simultaneously.","Then he breathed out.","Endlessly blue rivers of Infinity flowed from his breath to fill and batter that one single root. The authority he exhaled did not come from within him. It came from everywhere his Infinity touched across Observable Existence, conducted through his finite form and directed toward this singular target.","Infinitely.","He chose something that could be considered relatively small as he watched it shine with grander and grander waves of light.","The simple root began to spin.","Its organic structure crystallized further, transforming from dense material into something that approached pure concept given form. Blue light suffused every tendril and every fractal branch and every repeating pattern of its architecture.","Blue strings and waves flowed from it as the air it gave off became more and more grand.","Its roots turned a crystallized blue that shone far too brilliantly, radiating authority that exceeded what any Sacred Herb should have been capable of producing. The transformation was accelerating, feeding on the Infinity Noah directed toward it, becoming something unprecedented.","Until...","DING!","It froze in place.","The root let out a frosty air of cerulean brilliance that spread across the green-gold field around them. The transformation had completed, but what emerged was not simply an enhanced version of what had existed before.","Noah watched it closely.","One moment, he saw that radiant blue crystallized root floating before him.","And in the next moment, he felt every space around him was densely packed and filled with countless crystallized roots.","Not copies.","Not illusions.","The same root existing in infinite instances simultaneously. One and infinite at the same time. A single object that was also endless objects, each instance as real as every other instance, all of them the same root expressed across infinite iterations.","His eyes were bright.","What was the result of his initial research?","|An Infinite Product has been designed.|","|An Infinite Sacred Herb has emerged.|","|THE Convergent Root of Density Absolute has been transformed into: THE Infinite Root of Uncountable Saturation.|","|Classification: Infinite Object|","|Nature: This root now exists as both singular and infinite simultaneously. Consuming one instance consumes infinite instances. The density it provides is no longer approaching Uncountable but IS Uncountable in nature.|","|Effect: Any existence capable of consuming this Infinite Sacred Herb can make significant progress from Countable to Uncountable Infinity. They would consume 1 and also infinite numbers of this root when they do. The consumption introduces Uncountable density directly into foundations without requiring gradual accumulation.|","|Potential Outcome: At worst, the consumer will feel Uncountable Infinities momentarily or for days, experiencing that density before returning to Countable existence. At best, the consumer will achieve permanent elevation to Uncountable Infinity, their foundations transformed to contain infinite density between every sequential point of their existence.|","|Warning: Consuming or Wielding Infinite Objects carries risks proportional to the gap between consumer and consumed. Existence may reject what it cannot integrate.|","\"...\"","Noah looked at these prompts.","He became extremely silent!"]},{"number":5004,"title":"Chapter 5004: Chapter 5003: Infection I","paragraphs":["In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","In THE Primordial Archive.","The central area of this ancient repository held knowledge accumulated since before THE Infinite Unfurling, Grimoires and texts and crystallized memories stacked in configurations that would have taken normal beings eons to navigate.","THE Great Usurper stood in this space with his manifestation positioned beside Noah, both of them facing a massive crack in reality that looked like an obsidian portal stretching toward depths that seemed to breathe with cold authority.","This crack led to Jotunheim.","Nearby, THE Infiniverse and RUINATION were flipping through Grimoires and other works within this Archive with speed that spoke of urgent purpose. Their forms blazed with concentration as they searched for something specific, pages turning faster than perception could track. Eckert did not know exactly what they sought, but he understood that Osmont’s people were always working toward goals that served overall existence. Eh, or themselves, who knew.","Other cracks like the one before them existed in different corners of THE Primordial Archive, each one leading to different Primordial Realms.","The connections had been established long ago by beings who understood that knowledge required access to be useful, and THE Primordial Archive served as a nexus point for those who knew how to use it properly.","But their aim today was Jotunheim, that Primordial Realm now fully under THE Entity’s influence, where Chaos Giants and Jotuun Lifeforms had been unified into that horrifying collective consciousness that sought to spread across all of Observable Existence.","Eckert had paused in the last few minutes because Osmont had told him to wait.","Eckert did not mind waiting. His entire existence had been built around patience, around the slow accumulation of influence through methods so subtle that even Absolutes could not perceive them. He was THE Great Usurper, THE Idle One, and rushing had never been part of his methodology.","When Osmont opened his eyes again, Eckert could sense that something grand had changed. He... seemed different in ways Eckert could not quite identify. His external radiance appeared dimmer than before, less oppressive in its weight, and yet somehow the authority he emanated felt more profound. Like pressure that had been concentrated rather than dispersed.","Eckert could not quite put his finger on it.","He only saw Osmont turn to him with eyes holding depths they had not held during their previous interactions, and the words that emerged carried weight pressing against the Archive itself.","\" Okay, we can continue.\"","Osmont’s voice was calm but purposeful.","\" To make your entry into Jotunheim seamless, to ensure THE Primordial Mycelia has no chance of sensing you, I will keep it busy by testing out my first full attack on it.\"","Eckert nodded seriously at this plan. He understood his role. He was to infiltrate while Osmont provided the distraction, to spread his Idle Weavings across Jotunheim. It was a sound strategy!","In the next moment, a terrifying force erupted from Noah.","Waves of endless blue light poured into the crack leading to Jotunheim with intensity Eckert had not witnessed from him before. The blue was dense and heavy and cold. Extremely cole and regal!","Osmont nodded toward him.","\" Go.\"","...!","Eckert did not waste a second.","He went forward immediately, his manifestation becoming formless as it followed the boundless blue light into that obsidian crack. His Idle Weavings compressed themselves into configurations so subtle that even the most perceptive Absolutes would have dismissed them as ambient fluctuations in the background noise of existence.","Before he fully departed, he just so happened to have his awareness catch sight of Osmont one final time.","When he looked at him, he saw something unusual. Those eyes were shining with extremely potent blue light, and they felt cold and imperious in ways Eckert had not observed before.","The gaze seemed to belong to an unfathomable consciousness rather than the tyrannical but ultimately comprehensible Osmont he was used to. For a brief moment, those eyes held something ancient and endless and utterly detached from mortal concerns.","But he felt like he only saw this briefly before that unfeeling and imperious light faded, and the calm light of tyranny returned to Osmont’s gaze.","’Huh...’","Eckert shrugged it off internally as his manifestation completed its transition into the crack. Maybe it was just an expression of Osmont’s power, some visual artifact of channeling tremendous Infinity through his existence. He was always doing things that defied normal understanding, and unusual manifestations were simply part of working alongside someone like him.","The sensation of traveling through that endless blue light was unique.","Cold permeated everything. Not the cold of temperature but the cold of endlessness, of sequences extending forever without warmth or termination. The blue particles surrounding his formless consciousness carried him forward with momentum that seemed to have no end, simply endless progression toward whatever destination Osmont had designated.","And then his awareness emerged into the skies of Jotunheim.","The heavens above this Primordial Realm churned with obsidian and silver light intertwined in patterns of Chaos given atmospheric form. Clouds moved in directions that contradicted each other, some drifting upward while others spiraled downward, all of them radiating cold authority that pressed against Eckert’s perception.","Below stretched a citadel of impossible scale.","Light years in size, the structure sprawled across the landscape of Jotunheim like a city designed for beings who measured their movements in parsecs rather than steps. Towers rose toward those churning skies with architecture combining crystallized Chaos and organic growth into forms that seemed to breathe and shift even as Eckert observed them.","The citadel pulsed with brilliant life force, countless Jotuun Lifeforms, Chaos Giants, going about their unified existence within its borders.","Eckert could sense auras of Absolutes stretched out in different areas of that vast structure, their presence blazing like beacons among the lesser existences surrounding them. All of them carrying the warm unified consciousness of THE Entity’s infection, all of them part of that horrifying collective that sought to consume everything into its singular awareness.","But at this time, in these skies where his awareness surrounded by the blue light of Infinity was beginning to spread, Eckert sensed something that made him pause in genuine surprise.","The endless seas of Infinity were forming into shapes.","Shapes he recognized.","...!","He had to do a double take to ensure he was seeing correctly. His perception focused more intently on what Osmont’s authority was becoming around him, and his confirmation only deepened his astonishment.","The shapes were those of...","Nuclear weapons.","Osmont had transformed his endless blue seas of extremely dense and heavy authorities into endlessly massive nuclear warheads. The one containing Eckert’s consciousness towered like a mountain, its form mimicking the elongated design of the most devastating weapons known to man. Blue light blazed along its surface in patterns suggesting controlled devastation waiting to be unleashed!"]},{"number":5005,"title":"Chapter 5005: Chapter 5004: Infection II","paragraphs":["Eight others shone with incandescent blue light around him, each one equally vast, each one carrying Infinity compressed into shapes designed for singular purpose.","Destruction.","They began to move toward the stretches of Jotunheim below far faster than Planck speed, and the transition was so instantaneous that Eckert’s perception could not track the journey. One moment they were high above in those churning obsidian skies. The next moment they were directly above the citadel, positioned for impact with precision that spoke of absolute control.","Eckert enjoyed such an exhilarating ride as the descent continued without deceleration.","In the next moment, boundless waves of Chaos erupted from below to meet the Infinity warheads. THE Entity had sensed the assault, and its response came with speed matching what was descending upon its domain. Obsidian rivers of Chaos surged upward to intercept, to consume, to unify whatever was attacking into its collective consciousness.","But Infinity and THE Entity were like water and oil.","They could not mix.","BOOM!","The first warhead detonated.","A mushroom cloud of blue exploded outward and permeated everything within Gigaparsecs the impact point. The Chaos attempting to consume it was not consumed but scattered, pushed aside by force that refused to become part of anything else. Blue fallout spread across the skies of Jotunheim with radiance making the obsidian clouds seem dim by comparison.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","Multiple others detonated in sequence, each one producing its own mushroom cloud of endless blue, each one scattering THE Entity’s defensive Chaos in directions it had not anticipated. Momentarily, the skies of this region of Jotunheim shone with blinding fallout of endless blue, and the impact was so heavy and terrifying that it surged to encompass everything within perception.","Eckert felt his Idle Weavings rapidly spread out across Jotunheim on the waves of that nuclear fallout.","The mechanisms were those of fission, of atoms splitting and releasing energy that caused other atoms to split in cascading chain reactions. But instead of radioactive particles, his weavings rode the fragments of Infinity as they scattered across the Primordial Realm.","Each detonation produced countless pieces of endless blue light, and each piece carried fragments of his consciousness to new locations.","His weavings landed on shocked Jotuun Lifeforms who had been going about their unified existence moments before, their massive forms now reeling from the assault of authority they could not integrate. His weavings landed on Chaos Giants who cried out and clutched their heads as if the fallout of Infinity was interfering with their unity, their connection to THE Entity flickering under the pressure of something that refused to be consumed.","And at such a time, Eckert allowed his weavings to flow into them without resistance.","BOOM!","He sensed himself becoming connected to something unfathomable.","The vibrant warm consciousness of THE Entity pressed against his awareness with welcoming embrace that sought to unify everything it touched. He could feel it treating Infinity like water and oil, the two unable to mix, the endless blue authority of Osmont’s assault being rejected by the collective consciousness even as it tried to spread and consume.","Was this the unity of THE Entity?","It felt warm. It felt accepting. It felt like belonging in ways that Eckert’s existence had never experienced before, like being part of something greater than individual awareness, like finally coming home after eons of wandering alone.","He understood in that moment why so many beings had fallen to its influence.","But Eckert allowed his weavings to flow into it calmly, maintaining his Idle nature even as that warmth pressed against him with promises of unity and purpose. The way his weavings worked, absolutely nothing should be sensed, and he should only be considered the same as that consciousness. His Idle methodology made him invisible to detection, made him seem like just another part of whatever system he infiltrated.","And he melded in seamlessly.","The vibrant and warm consciousness was too busy fighting back against Infinity to notice one more awareness joining its collective. Rivers of Chaos raged all around as THE Entity focused on pushing away Osmont’s assault, on rejecting the endless blue fallout spreading across its domain, on protecting the unity it had built within Jotunheim from authority that could not be consumed.","Eckert slipped in while it was distracted.","But for now...","’Very good. Very good!’","Eckert was in an excellent mood as his consciousness settled into its new position within THE Entity’s collective awareness. Osmont’s ridiculous usage of Infinity had spread him across Jotunheim far more effectively than any subtle infiltration could have accomplished, and his consciousness had already integrated with many Chaos Giants silently. Now he simply had to ensure that he would remain invisible as he stretched out and usurped this vast and unfathomable consciousness piece by piece.","As long as he was not found out and consumed or unified in the end, he should be okay.","He was slightly apprehensive about what he was attempting. Fear existed within him, though he would never admit it aloud. THE Entity had consumed Absolutes far more powerful than himself, had unified beings who had existed since THE Infinite Unfurling, had proven itself capable of spreading across Observable Existence despite opposition from the most powerful forces in all of reality.","But he felt like he had to do this.","This was his risk and adversity, and he could not be Idle for all his existence. That was not living. That was simply existing without purpose, without growth, without the struggle that made advancement meaningful.","It was also a matter of pride.","He wanted to prove that he could do what THE Entity could do. He wanted to demonstrate that his Idle Weavings were capable of usurping even the most vast consciousness in Observable Existence. He wanted to show Osmont and everyone else that THE Great Usurper was not merely a title but a description of what he would accomplish.","If THE Entity could unify countless beings into singular awareness, then Eckert could usurp that unity and claim it for himself.","If not more.","So with the lands of Jotunheim being bombarded with nuclear warheads of Infinity as Osmont began his tests from THE Primordial Archive, Eckert dangerously proceeded to his own tests within the warm and welcoming consciousness that did not yet know it was being infiltrated by something it could not consume."]},{"number":5006,"title":"Chapter 5006: Chapter 5005: The Scale I","paragraphs":["In THE Prima Indifferentia.","The storms of corrupted paradoxical proto-matter raged beyond the white barrier with violence accumulated since THE Living Paradox had initiated his flooding of this ancient space.","Blue-gold light from Infinite Seals mingled with the corruption, creating phenomena that would have unmade lesser beings simply through proximity. Undivided Ones burned or prospered in that chaos, and Formless Terrors churned with instability amplified by the paradoxical nature pressing against their already confused existences.","But within the circular region emanating from the white tree, absolute calm prevailed.","THE Arboreal Warden Yggvaros sat alone near that tree whose bark gleamed with light holding no color yet containing all colors simultaneously.","THE Creature had departed some time ago, returning to whatever conflict currently demanded his attention in Observable Existence. The conversation they had shared lingered in Yggvaros’s contemplation, but he found himself drawn toward deeper considerations than the fate of one ambitious defector from classification.","The white tree pulsed gently behind him, its dimensions continuing to vary with each observation. One moment it appeared a meter tall, the next it stretched toward horizons that did not exist in this place. Its branches followed geometric rules not yet differentiated from pure mathematical potential, and its roots disappeared into ground that was not ground in any conventional sense.","Yggvaros reached down and grasped a simple stick from the golden earth beneath him.","The vibrant gold soil responded to his touch with warmth accumulated since before THE Infinite Unfurling, and he began to draw.","His movements were deliberate, each stroke of the stick pressing into that ancient earth with purpose refined across eons of contemplation. A circle took shape before him, its circumference perfect despite the crude tool producing it.","He divided the circle into four equal sections with two intersecting lines.","In the first section, he wrote a single word: Chaos.","In the second: Paradox.","In the third: Existence.","In the fourth: The First Tongue.","The Four Aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence stared up at him from the golden earth, their arrangement familiar to any being who had studied the foundations of Civilization. These were the Keys that unlocked advancement, the authorities from which all other authorities derived, the paths that countless beings across Observable Existence walked in pursuit of power they could barely comprehend.","Yggvaros continued drawing.","From the circle’s edge, he extended branching lines outward, each one reaching toward a singular point in the distance. The lines converged as they stretched away from the Four Aspects, narrowing toward something that existed beyond the classifications most beings understood. A singularity where all paths met, where all advancement culminated, where the true nature of power revealed itself to those capable of perceiving it.","He placed a question mark at that convergence point.","For a long moment, he simply stared at what he had drawn, his features shifting between presence and absence as they always did for beings existing at the intersection of differentiation and undifferentiation. Then he erased the question mark with a sweep of his crystallized hand and wrote something else in its place.","Scale of Existence?","The words pressed into the golden earth with weight befitting their implications.","And on the branching lines leading from the circle toward that distant singularity, he began adding labels. On one line, he wrote Infinity, the symbols glowing faintly with authority borrowed from the concept itself.","On another line, parallel but distinct, he wrote Primordial Source, and those symbols seemed to resist being written at all, as if the very act of naming this thing was presumptuous.","...!","Yggvaros paused in his drawing, the stick hovering above the golden earth as contemplation deeper than most beings could comprehend settled over his features.","\" Existence churns as it has always, and those who seek power grasp at straws they believe will carry them toward the hub.\"","His voice emerged measured, each word chosen with precision accumulated across cycles beyond counting. He spoke to no one but himself, yet his words carried weight pressing against the calm region around him.","\" The Four Aspects serve their purpose well enough for those walking toward THE First Scale, toward the foundations of Civilization that most beings consider the pinnacle of achievement. Chaos and Paradox and Existence and The First Tongue, each one offering paths and methodologies and expressions of authority. Those who master them rise. Those who fail to grasp them fall. This has repeated since differentiation first taught existence how to have boundaries.\"","He looked down at the diagram he had drawn with eyes burning older than Prima Indifferentia itself.","\" But those who reach THE Second Scale, or those who merely attempt the journey, soon discover a truth that the lower classifications cannot perceive. The Four Aspects are not the final and grandest source of power. They are expressions of something deeper, channels through which greater authorities flow into forms that mortal comprehension can process.\"","His stick tapped the word Infinity on the golden earth.","\" This is one of those greater authorities. Infinity, that endless potential which existed before THE First Cause decided that boundaries should exist. It is hard to grasp, for how does one grasp something without termination? How does one contain something that refuses containment? And yet it is easy to understand in principle. Sequences extending forever. Density approaching limits that cannot be reached. The absence of ending in any direction one chooses to look.\"","His stick moved to tap the words Primordial Source.","\" This is the other. And unlike Infinity, it is neither easy to grasp nor easy to understand. What is THE Primordial Source? Where does it originate? How does one access authority that predates the very concepts of access and authority?\"","Yggvaros set down his stick and folded his hands before him with a posture speaking of patience refined across eons.","\" Those who begin utilizing aspects of Infinity find their path toward the next Scale illuminated in ways they did not anticipate. The endless nature of that authority resonates with something fundamental in existence itself, something that recognizes kindred nature and responds accordingly. Without Infinity or THE Primordial Source flowing through one’s foundations, advancement beyond THE First Scale is not merely difficult, but impossible...\"","...!"]},{"number":5007,"title":"Chapter 5007: Chapter 5006: The Scale II","paragraphs":["His voice dropped to something approaching solemnity.","\" It is impossible. The door simply does not open for those who lack the key, and the key is not found among the Four Aspects no matter how thoroughly one masters them. Chaos may grant tremendous power within its domain. Paradox may permit contradictions that reshape local reality. Existence may build Civilizations spanning Primordial Realms. The First Tongue may rewrite the very language through which reality expresses itself.\"","He shook his head slowly, crystallized features shifting with the motion.","\" But none of these authorities, magnificent as they may be, can carry a being past THE Second Scale. For that journey, one requires something deeper. Something that predates the Aspects themselves. Something that was present during THE First Cause and remains present still, flowing beneath the surface of what beings perceive as power.\"","Yggvaros paused in his contemplation and released a sigh carrying weight accumulated since before most Primordial Architects had achieved their first moments of cognizance.","He looked outward, his gaze piercing the white barrier emanating from the tree behind him. Beyond that calm boundary, the storms of corrupted paradoxical proto-matter continued their violent transformation of THE Prima Indifferentia. Blue-gold light pulsed through the chaos, Infinite Absolute Seals scattered across regions that had never known such authority before this current age.","\" Infinity is unfathomably difficult to seek at THE Second Scale. Even those who have walked these heights for eons struggle to access more than fragments of its true nature. We sense it. We know it exists. We understand, in principle, what it represents. But channeling it? Directing it? Making it serve our purposes rather than simply existing in proximity to our awareness?\"","His eyes narrowed with something approaching genuine interest.","\" That requires methodology that most at this Scale have never developed. That requires understanding that most at this Scale have never achieved. That requires either tremendous fortune or tremendous insight, and fortune of such magnitude does not simply occur without cause.\"","His gaze focused more intently on the blue-gold light pulsing through the storms beyond his barrier.","\" And yet someone astounding enough in Our Observable Existence has not only grasped Infinity, but they have spread it openly and freely for all others to see. The corruption carries it. The proto-matter pulses with it. Every corner of THE Prima Indifferentia now holds fragments of Infinite authority that did not exist here before this current transformation began.\"","Yggvaros raised one hand, his crystallized fingers moving with deliberate purpose.","\" Is this merely their own Infinity, personal authority spread thin across vast distances? Or are they pulling from Infinity on the same level as THE Primordial Source, accessing depths that even those at THE Second Scale have found difficult to perceive? The distinction matters greatly, for the implications of each possibility diverge toward futures that could reshape everything we understand about advancement itself.\"","He waved his hand in sweeping motion, and the corruption beyond his barrier responded to his authority. The paradoxical proto-matter was filtered away, pushed aside by will refined across cycles beyond counting. What remained was pure, distilled from the chaos that had carried it.","Blue-gold Infinite Absolute Seals flowed into his domain, drawn through the white barrier by invitation rather than force.","Many across Observable Existence had already mixed their weavings with this paradoxical corrupted proto-matter and Infinity, their existences accelerating through combination that would either elevate them or unmake them depending on factors they likely did not understand.","Yggvaros had been careful not to touch it himself, maintaining the contemplative distance that had served him well since he first grasped THE Second Scale.","But at this time, curiosity overcame caution.","HUUM!","The weavings of Infinity fell into his hands, and a heartshaking aura erupted from his position with force pressing against regions of THE Prima Indifferentia far beyond his normal influence. The calm boundary around the white tree flickered as power flowed through crystallized fingers that had not touched authority this potent in eons.","Many Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors paused in their distant conflicts in different directions, sensing something that exceeded their comprehension emanating from a direction they instinctively knew to avoid.","Yggvaros pulled his hands back from the particles of Infinity.","\" Utilizing Infinity greatly empowers and strengthens one’s Civilization, this much is certain. The authority flows through foundations and expands them, fills gaps that other methodologies cannot reach, elevates potential toward heights that seemed impossible before contact was established.\"","His voice carried weight now, informed by direct experience rather than mere contemplation.","\" But those who channel it also add their power to Infinity itself. The exchange flows in both directions, and I wonder whether those currently mixing their weavings with this scattered authority understand what they contribute to something they cannot perceive. They take, yes, but they also give. And what they give flows toward a source that none here fully comprehend.\"","He looked down at the diagram he had drawn on the golden earth, at the branching lines leading from the Four Aspects toward that distant singularity labeled Scale of Existence.","\" None here truly understand how to access THE Primordial Source. Perhaps those who naturally reach THE Second Scale might perceive pathways that others cannot. Perhaps eons of patient observation might reveal truths that desperate advancement obscures. Perhaps existence is simply too vast and unfathomable for any single consciousness to grasp, regardless of how long that consciousness has existed.\"","His gaze lifted toward the blue-gold light still pulsing beyond his barrier, toward the Infinity scattered across THE Prima Indifferentia by someone operating from Observable Existence.","\" But what I am most curious about is the one who freely spread this authority. The foremost Guider of Infinity, or would they be called THE Conduit of Infinity? The terminology matters less than the reality of what they have accomplished.\"","Yggvaros rose from his seated position, his crystallized form shifting with motion that pressed against the golden earth beneath him. The white tree pulsed behind him as if acknowledging his contemplation, its dimensions continuing to vary with each moment that passed.","\" How did you access Infinity when even those at THE Second Scale have found such access difficult? What methodology do you possess that we lack? What understanding have you achieved that has eluded beings who have existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling itself?\"","His questions hung in the calm air of his domain, unanswered by anything except the distant storms continuing their transformation of THE Prima Indifferentia.","Somewhere in Observable Existence, a finite being conducted an endless sea.","And THE Arboreal Warden Yggvaros, First Among THE Sane to Grasp THE Second Scale of Existence, found himself genuinely curious about him!","He thought for a moment before he took out a small white notebook made from the same material as the tree at the center of this place. And in his hands, a white pen burning with authority appeared as he thought for a moment before opening the book that had half its pages filled, and he...began to write.","---","On the matter of Civilizations and their foundations, a lot of confusion persists among those who have not walked beyond THE First Scale of Existence.","It is common for such beings to observe authorities like Infinity and conclude that anything so vast must surely serve as the basis for a Way, for a Civilization, for the fundamental expression of one’s advancement through the hierarchies of power.","This confusion is understandable, for how could something so immense be anything other than what one builds upon?","Those at THE Second Scale know better.","Infinity is not a Civilization. It cannot be made into a Way. One may access it, channel it, allow it to flow through one’s foundations and empower what already exists there. But Infinity itself resists being claimed as personal territory in the manner that true Civilizations demand.","It is the river, not the vessel. It is the wind, not the sail. To confuse the force with the structure is to fundamentally misunderstand the nature of advancement itself.","The Four Aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence provide the true foundations from which Civilizations emerge.","From Chaos can spring the Civilization of Infernal Chaos, where destruction and creation dance in eternal cycles that feed upon themselves. From that same Aspect emerges the Civilization of Consuming Chaos, where all things are devoured to fuel further devouring, and the Civilization of Creative Chaos, where disorder births novelty without end.","The variations are as numerous as those who walk these paths, for Chaos by its nature refuses singular expression.","From Existence, the branches multiply further still. The Civilization of Unbound Existence permits one to transcend the limitations that constrain lesser beings, while the Civilization of Bound Existence finds power in accepting those limitations and forging strength from restriction.","The Civilization of Living Existence and its counterpart, the Civilization of Dead Existence, represent the fundamental duality that all things which are must eventually navigate. Higher variations include the Civilization of Transcendent Existence, where the boundaries between states of being dissolve entirely, and the Civilization of Primordial Existence, where one’s foundations touch the very origins from which all differentiation emerged.","Derivatives of wonders, you could even call them.","Paradox offers paths equally varied. The Civilization of Limitless Paradox permits contradictions to exist without resolution, drawing power from the tension between incompatible truths.","The Civilization of Dual Paradox maintains precisely two contradictory states in permanent opposition, while the Civilization of Recursive Paradox folds contradictions within contradictions until the very concept of resolution loses meaning.","Some speak of the Civilization of Resolved Paradox, though there is dispute whether true resolution remains paradoxical at all.","The First Tongue branches into linguistic expressions too numerous to fully catalog. The Civilization of Qi channels the fundamental energy underlying all speech and expression, while the Civilization of Logos builds foundations upon the rational structures through which reality organizes itself.","The Civilization of Phonemic Authority focuses on the individual sounds that compose meaning, and the Civilization of Lexical Dominion concerns itself with the accumulated weight of words combined into greater wholes.","Some pursue the Civilization of Silent Tongue, finding power in what is not spoken, while others walk the Civilization of Primal Utterance, seeking the first sounds ever differentiated from potential into expression.","All of these Civilizations exist. All of them can be walked by beings who achieved THE Second Scale and beyond. All of them draw from the Four Aspects in configurations as unique as the beings who claim them as of course, you do have those who purely claim Chaos, Paradox, Existence, and The First Tongue...well, not really The First Tongue as that is a hard one.","But you will never find one at THE Second Scale who speaks of the Civilization of Infinity.","For Infinity empowers Civilizations. It does not become them. Or so it is believed. On this, there really should not be an exception.","Those who attempt to make Infinity their Way find themselves conducting force without foundation, channeling authority without structure, wielding power that flows through them rather than from them. The distinction is subtle but absolute.","One may ride the river, but one cannot become the river while remaining oneself. One may harness the wind, but one cannot be the wind while retaining the identity necessary to harness anything at all.","This truth is rarely discussed among those at THE First Scale, for they have not yet perceived the difference between empowerment and foundation.","They see Infinity scattered across Observable Existence and conclude that someone must have built a Civilization upon it. They observe its effects and assume those effects represent advancement along familiar paths. Their confusion is forgivable, for they see only the surface of depths they cannot yet fathom.","And one should not even begin discussing THE Primordial Source.","Where Infinity is misunderstood, THE Primordial Source is simply unknown. Where Infinity can at least be perceived and channeled and directed toward purposes, THE Primordial Source resists even acknowledgment of its nature.","Those at THE Second Scale sense it as one senses a presence in a darkened room, knowing something exists without being able to identify what that something might be.","And unlike Infinity, which flows freely for those capable of conducting it, THE Primordial Source has never been accessed in Observable Existence as far as we can confirm.","Perhaps it cannot be channeled. Perhaps it can only be touched, briefly, by those who stumble upon it through fortune rather than methodology. Perhaps it is not a force at all but rather the absence from which all forces emerged, and attempting to channel absence is a contradiction even Paradox cannot resolve.","These questions remain unanswered.","They may remain unanswered forever.","—Excerpted from \"Musings on Scales and Foundations,\" attributed to THE Arboreal Warden Yggvaros, date of composition unknown."]},{"number":5008,"title":"Chapter 5008: Chapter 5007: Do Not Idolize I","paragraphs":["In the outer fringes of Alfheimr.","Space fluctuated with distortions pressing against the boundaries of this Primordial Realm, reality bending and folding as something approached from directions that normal perception could not track.","The fluctuations intensified for a moment, building toward a crescendo of spatial displacement, and then three unique figures appeared where nothing had existed moments before.","Fresh arrivals from THE Interstices!","The first was an Undivided One in humanoid form, his skin shining obsidian with depths suggesting countless eyes watching from beneath that dark surface. He stood tall and proud, adorned in a clear blue robe that contrasted sharply with his darkness, and his features held an expressiveness unusual for beings of his classification.","Where most Undivided Ones presented faces of hunger and alien intent, this one smiled with genuine enthusiasm, his radiant eyes filled with expectations.","The second was a Formless Terror whose entire body consisted of illusory crimson tentacles, but they had been arranged and compressed into a humanoid shape held together with discipline.","Both were unique among their kinds, geniuses of their own stature whose power would have put common Absolutes to shame.","Floating behind them was a woman also adorned in blue robes, but the air surrounding her carried weight of an entirely different magnitude.","She held the aura of a Primordial Architect, that intersection of differentiation and undifferentiation pressing against reality with authority accumulated since THE First Cause itself. Her presence alone made the outer fringes of Alfheimr seem to contract slightly.","Her eyes were pure white, holding no iris or pupil in any conventional sense, but within that whiteness floated blue dots resembling singularities, points of compressed authority orbiting slowly through her gaze.","Radiant white hair cascaded down her back in waves holding their own faint luminescence. She was strikingly beautiful, and really, ridiculously so!","A Primordial Architect, an Undivided One, and a Formless Terror walked into Alfheimr.","This was not the start of a bad joke but an actual reality, three beings of vastly different classifications traveling together with purpose that had brought them across Observable Existence in search of something specific.","The blue robes they shared marked them as affiliated, as belonging to something greater than their individual natures.","The Formless Terror turned toward the Primordial Architect.","\" Naldine, what do your senses tell you?\"","His voice emerged from somewhere within that mass of illusory appendages.","\"Is the Infinity-bearer in this Primordial Realm? We have been searching to no avail for a while now, and I confess my patience grows thin despite my best efforts to maintain it.\"","The Primordial Architect, Naldine, looked ahead with gaze piercing through layers of reality that her companions could not perceive.","The outer fringes of Alfheimr stretched before them in configurations of light and energy unique to this realm, forests of crystallized potential rising toward skies holding colors that had not fully differentiated into specific hues. Traces of authority lingered everywhere, remnants of beings who had passed through this space across eons of accumulated history.","And among those traces, faint but unmistakable, glimmers of Infinity pulsed with blue-gold light.","But they were old. Residual. The echoes of presence rather than presence itself.","Naldine shook her head with a motion carrying finality.","\" He should not be here. He was here, but no more.\"","Her voice emerged cold and precise.","\" Otherwise the pull of Infinity here would be much greater than what I perceive. What remains is merely what he left behind, traces of passage rather than indication of current location.\"","As she spoke, she raised one hand before her with deliberate slowness. On her palm, glimmers of Infinite Absolute Seals shimmered brightly.","She had been collecting these fragments throughout their journey, gathering pieces of the Infinity-bearer’s scattered influence like a hunter gathering tracks left by prey they had not yet glimpsed.","The eyes of the Undivided One, Arthur, shone brilliantly. His obsidian features shifted with expression holding something approaching reverence.","\" The adversity that breaks all others shall forge him. The hardship that ends all paths shall begin his. The Scales demand what the Scales demand, and he shall pay in currencies that have not yet been minted.\"","His words emerged with cadence of recitation.","\" Three times shall he face the mirror of undoing. Three times shall he choose between becoming and unbecoming. Three times shall the answer be the same, and three times shall the answer be different.\"","The crystallized trees seemed to lean away from his voice, as if even the environment of Alfheimr recognized the significance of what he spoke.","\"In the end, which is also the beginning, the Infinite shall stand before the Undefined. And only one shall remain to tell the tale that no one shall hear.\"","Arthur paused, his obsidian features shifting into a smile holding genuine amusement.","\" This is an Echo of First Cause.\"","...!","The words he had uttered were heavy! But Arthur laughed after speaking them, the sound emerging bright and vibrant from his humanoid form.","\" Haha! Do you think the Undefined that will stand before the Infinite is me? The Great Arthur!\"","He spread his arms wide, blue robes billowing with the motion despite the absence of wind.","\" We have been musing about this Echo since we first heard it, and I still do not know what much of it means. But I am more and more curious about the Infinity-bearer with each passing moment. If he can just show me how he utilizes Infinity and makes it do all the things he is making it do, all the wonders he accomplishes that we can only observe from afar...\"","His eyes actually held a fervent light. He revered Infinity far too much, and that reverence colored everything he said about the one currently conducting it across Observable Existence.","Naldine’s gaze turned toward him with coldness pressing against his enthusiasm like ice against flame.","\" Do not idolize him too much.\"","Her voice cut through his fervor with precision.","\"In the grand scheme of existence, I consider him a fool due to his actions. Why spread Infinity across Observable Existence just because he has it? What purpose does such generosity serve when the recipients of that generosity become competitors for resources that should remain concentrated?\"","...!"]},{"number":5009,"title":"Chapter 5009: Chapter 5008: Do Not Idolize II","paragraphs":["The blue singularities in her white eyes orbited faster, conveying something approaching contempt.","\" Sometimes great power can land on those who do not know how to use it. First, I have to meet him. If he is worthy, we will see what arrangements might be made. Until then, you two better not be embarrassments who grovel at his feet just because of Echoes of Causes you heard whispered across the void.\"","She stepped forward, her presence pressing against both Arthur and Gunther with weight reminding them exactly who led their particular association.","\" We ultimately seek Infinity, not just the one who Guides it, however grand they may be. They are not synonymous with Infinity itself, just those capable of doing much more with it than the rest of us. The authority matters. The wielder is merely a obstacle or opportunity depending on how they respond to our approach.\"","Her cold gaze swept across both of them, demanding acknowledgment of her position.","\" Okay? Arthur, Gunther, are you...\"","She trailed off, her attention snapping toward the distance with sharpness that made both her companions turn to follow her gaze. The blue singularities in her eyes contracted to points of intense focus, and her beautiful features hardened into expression holding neither welcome nor hostility, only assessment.","In the distance, outlines were approaching through the crystallized forests of Alfheimr’s outer fringes.","An Absolute led the group, his form unmistakable. Two faces occupied a single head, one serene and one severe, both currently arranged into expressions of polite interest. He floated forward with casual grace, his authority pressing against the environment without demanding submission from it.","Behind him came multiple entities adorned in Togas, their forms marking them as representatives of something official, something organized.","Paradoxos smiled with both faces as he approached the party of a Primordial Architect, an Undivided One, and a Formless Terror.","Naldine stared at the party coming toward them as she frowned right away.","And without even wasting a second, she spoke words that had ended Civilizations across eons of application.","\" Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust.\"","BOOM!","The word | ASHES | instantly hung above Paradoxos and those around him, burning into existence with authority pressing against the crystallized forests around them. Their expressions changed in that instant, confusion and alarm flickering across the two faces of Paradoxos as he recognized what was happening.","But recognition came too late, and their bodies trembled with coldness spreading from their foundations outward as they began to turn to ash!","...!","The Absolute’s form crumbled first, his two faces maintaining their expressions of shock even as the structure supporting them dissolved into gray particles. The Paradoxian entities followed moments later, their disciplined formations breaking apart as each one succumbed to the fundamental truth Naldine had imposed upon their existences.","Her face remained cold throughout, watching the dissolution with eyes holding neither satisfaction nor regret!","Arthur and Gunther before her were astonished, but before either could ask anything, Naldine spoke with a voice cutting through their shock.","\" You fools have such poor potential and remain stuck on THE First Scale that you do not sense when an attack is already sent your way.\"","...!","As she spoke, she waved her hands to reveal a white triangular object with an obsidian eye at its very center. The item radiated an aura of a complete Axiom, and she turned it toward the ashes of Paradoxos and his companions. The gray particles flowed into the obsidian eye like water drawn toward a drain, carrying fragments of the existences they had once comprised.","Naldine focused on the item as its eye opened and began showing illusory scenes playing out above its surface.","They were scenes of...","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","She watched Paradoxos standing among three other Strategoi, saw THE Primordial Paradox present among them, and saw THE Youngest.","Memories of him floated from the Axiom and into her mind!","Noah Osmont. The one who laid the Claim to The First Tongue? Was this The Infinity-bearer?","His presence seemed dimmer than expected, his external radiance subdued, and yet something about him made even recorded observation bend slightly.","The scenes passed quickly as her eyes became sharp.","\" It seems a unified existence is spreading across Observable Existence, but that is an obsolete concern for beings at our Scale. What matters most is that I have found the one. The one who should be the Guider of Infinity.\"","...!","The others turned toward her seriously as she said simply, \" Let us go. The Infinity-bearer is in THE Agora.\"","She did not even spare a thought to those she had just collapsed. Even if their weavings could be reversed and cured from the effects of unified definition and undefinition, if one truly lost their Civilization to something like that, they were not deserving of THE Scales of Existence.","The weak Civilizations would be weeded out, and only the strong would prosper in the end.","Naldine waved her hand as she tore existence apart, opening her mouth to speak rubbish that compelled reality to acknowledge her authority.","THE Interstices opened up in front of them for them to squeeze into, that space between spaces where those who knew how to navigate could travel impossible distances.","Her gaze was cold and imperious as she stepped toward the opening.","She was not looking forward to meeting the Guider of Infinity, and the realization surprised her. She had spent considerable effort tracking this being across Observable Existence, gathering fragments of scattered Infinity and following traces through Primordial Realm after Primordial Realm. Finding him should have produced satisfaction.","But what she felt instead was something approaching fear.","Not fear of the Infinity-bearer himself, for she operated at THE Second Scale and had no such thing. Her fear was different. She was afraid of him not being up to par with the Echoes she had heard, afraid that he would prove merely lucky, merely a being upon whom great power had landed without the wisdom to wield it properly.","Why would the weavings of Infinity fall on something so young? So inexperienced?","She had to determine why. If he proved worthy, arrangements could be made. If he proved unworthy, well. Naldine had never hesitated to remove obstacles from her path, regardless of how much potential those obstacles might have possessed.","She stepped into THE Interstices without looking back, intent on arriving in Ginnungagap, past ite Vaults, and into THE Agora.","Arthur and Gunther followed!"]},{"number":5010,"title":"Chapter 5010: Chapter 5009: Glorious Purpose! I","paragraphs":["In Alfheimr.","On the mountain where THE Creature used to reside, where his multicolored flames had once blazed, a different presence now occupied that space.","The ancient being had departed, leaving behind only the lingering weight of his previous occupation.","One particular lifeform worthy of interest was a woman whose teeth had barely regrown after they were knocked out by THE Youngest not too long ago.","THE Living Emotive sat near an Undivided One, her legs dangling over the edge of a crystallized outcropping as she gazed out across the stretches of Alfheimr below. Her companion said nothing, simply existing in her presence with patience.","The bruises on her face had healed. The damage to her pride had not, though she wore that damage like jewelry rather than wounds.","Everybody underestimated the weak woman of ill repute.","She was just someone who bounced around from one of THE Four to another, right? Just a loose woman seeking protection from whoever would provide it.","Just the Broken Doll who shattered and reformed depending on which powerful being currently found her amusing. That was what they thought. That was what she let them think.","But oh, how little they understood.","She smiled brilliantly, her new white teeth gleaming in the ambient light of Alfheimr’s crystallized forests. The smile stretched too wide, held too long, carried edges that suggested something unstable lurking beneath the surface.","\" My big burly Chaos was caught in a web of unity, I sensed it and truly utilized our bond!\"","Her voice emerged sing-song and lilting, each word dancing with manic energy.","\" The strength of...what is it called now? The Primordial Mycelia! The strength of that little fungus is now draining and flowing into me, filling me up so deliciously!\"","She giggled, the sound bright and broken simultaneously.","\" Huhu, as I get stronger, I will come back for you, O Youngest. O Osmont!\"","Her eyes blazed with something beyond mere interest.","\" For you have stolen my heart!\"","...!","The Undivided One beside her shifted slightly but offered no comment.","Nobody knew how her power worked.","Even THE Creature had sat her down once and explained how what she possessed was unique across Observable Existence, how she could make something of herself if she chose to apply her capabilities with purpose.","But she had not even told him the true extent of what she could do, had smiled and nodded and let him believe he understood her while keeping the depths of her nature hidden behind eyes that everyone dismissed as empty.","Power was a funny thing, really.","When you hid things about it from all others, when you let them assume you were weak while cultivating strength in shadows they never thought to examine, the things you could accomplish became terrifying. THE Four thought she clung to them for protection. They never considered that she clung to them for access, for connection, for bonds that let her siphon what she needed while appearing to give nothing but companionship in return.","And now THE Primordial Chaos had fallen to THE Entity’s infection.","That warm unity spreading across his existence, that Primordial Mycelia weaving through his foundations, it thought it was consuming him. It thought it was adding his strength to its collective. But the bond between THE Living Emotive and THE Primordial Chaos ran deeper than infection could reach, and through that bond, she was drinking from both of them without either noticing.","None knew that she could tap into and drink from the bond, and she...had always hidden this before and never done it for the past eons.","She licked her new teeth with tongue that savored the sensation of regeneration.","But beyond power, beyond the delicious strength flowing into her existence through channels no one suspected, there was something else occupying her thoughts.","She had never been treated the way THE Youngest had treated her. To slap her like that, without hesitation, without the careful handling that others always employed when dealing with her. To look at her like that, with contempt so pure it bordered on refreshing.","Ah.","She really wanted Osmont.","Not in the way she had wanted THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos or any of the others she had attached herself to across eons of careful positioning.","Those had been strategic desires, calculated attachments designed to serve her hidden purposes. This was different. This burned with something she had almost forgotten she could feel.","He had looked at her like she was nothing.","And she... wanted to make him look at her like she was everything.","\" Wait for me, O Youngest.\"","Her sing-song voice carried across the mountain as her smile stretched wider still.","\" The Broken Doll is putting herself back together, piece by piece by piece. And when she’s whole again, she’ll come dancing to your door!\"","---","In THE Infiniverse.","Noah looked at THE Infinite Root of Uncountable Saturation floating before him, its crystallized blue form existing as both singular and infinite simultaneously.","He was a finite being conducting Infinity.","But he was doing so in a Countable manner, his endless authority flowing through patterns that could theoretically be observed and listed. First, second, third, onward forever. Sequential. Ordered. Limited by the very structure of how he perceived the endless sea he now directed rather than contained.","This was shown by the slight strain he felt sometimes when conducting Infinity across vast distances. The sensation was minor, barely noticeable amid the immensity of what he could accomplish, but it existed. And anything that existed could be overcome. Anything that limited him could be expanded beyond those limits.","So if he used Infinity inside an object to expand what he could do with Infinity...","Noah reached out and grasped THE Infinite Root of Uncountable Saturation.","It felt cold in his palm, cold in the way that endless sequences felt cold, temperature that had nothing to do with physical sensation and everything to do with the nature of what he held. The root pulsed with authority that was simultaneously one and infinite, a single object containing endless instances of itself.","He brought it to his mouth and swallowed.","The sensation of a finite being consuming an Infinite object was...unique. It was not like eating and it was not like drinking. It was like opening a door within himself and allowing something vast to flow through that door into spaces he had not known existed until this moment.","He directed it toward his nature and foundation.","The root’s authority spread through his existence with purpose responding to his will, seeking the places where his Countable Infinity operated and pressing against those limitations with density that refused to accept sequence as the only form of endless expression!","He felt it reaching his Surface Depth, that outermost layer of his Infinite nature where his conducted authority first manifested.","And then the transition began.","One moment, Noah sensed Infinity in the manner he had always sensed it. Sequential points extending forever, one after another, countable if one had eternity to count. The next moment, something shifted in his perception with booming, magisterial violence that made him gasp!","The gaps filled.","Between every point of Infinity he had previously perceived, new points emerged. And between those new points, more points emerged. And between those, still more, infinitely, endlessly, density that could not be listed no matter how one tried because there was always more between any two instances one attempted to identify.","HUUM!","His body rose into the air above the green-gold grasses and golden earth of THE Infiniverse, lifted by forces responding to the transformation occurring within his foundations!","A hymn and soft symphony began to play as radiance unfolded!","He began to spin slowly, surrounded by swirling rivers of endless blue that gathered from all directions to cradle him in their embrace.","The rivers held him with something approaching tenderness!","He felt unfathomably grand in that moment, spinning above the fields where Alexander’s transformation had concluded, suspended in authority that seemed eager to show him what Uncountable truly meant.","\" A portion of my existence...my Surface Depth, now feels it.\"","His voice emerged heavy with realization, each word pressing against the rivers of blue surrounding him.","\" That Uncountable nature. That density beyond sequence! THAT density!\"","He felt BIG! Fat!","He could sense the difference immediately. Where before his conducted Infinity had flowed in streams, now a portion of those streams had become oceans. Where before he had perceived endless points, now he perceived endless points between endless points between endless points. The expansion of his capabilities was not incremental.","It was categorical!","Even though only one part of his existence currently sensed Infinity in its Uncountable form, that single portion transformed everything he understood about what he could accomplish. He could feel other depths within himself waiting for the same elevation, spaces in his foundation that still operated on Countable limitations while his Surface Depth had broken through.","He needed more roots.","Noah extended his will while still spinning in the skies, still cradled by rivers of Infinity. Another THE Convergent Root of Density Absolute emerged from his storage, the finite Sacred Herb materializing before him with presence that seemed diminished compared to what he had just consumed.","He breathed out.","Endless blue rivers flowed from his breath toward the root, but this time the authority he directed carried qualities it had not possessed before. The Uncountable nature of his elevated Surface Depth infused the Infinity he commanded and exhaled, density filling the spaces between densities filling the spaces between more densities.","The root began to transform.","It crystallized and brightened and pulsed with authority accumulating faster than his previous attempt, responding to weavings born from Uncountable Infinity rather than merely Countable. The light grew blinding, and Noah watched through perception that could now see more than it had seen moments before.","HUUM!","Where one THE Infinite Root of Uncountable Saturation had formed previously, nine now emerged from the transformation.","They arranged themselves in a ring around his spinning form, each one blazing with blue light holding densities that exceeded what his first creation had possessed. These were not simply duplicates of what he had produced before. These were grander, denser, more saturated with Uncountable authority because they had been born from weavings that already understood what Uncountable meant.","Noah reached out and touched one of them.","The sensation confirmed what his perception suggested. These roots were fundamentally more potent than his initial creation, Infinite objects born from Infinite methodology rather than from Countable foundations reaching toward Uncountable expression.","|Elevation Detected|","|Your existence has taken a step further, progressing from the command of Countable toward the command of Uncountable Infinities at THE Surface Depth. This represents categorical advancement rather than incremental improvement. What you perceive now differs fundamentally from what you perceived before this elevation.|","|Other Depths await the same elevation to fully unlock the immensities of your existence. Your Infinite Formless Depth. Your foundations beneath foundations.|","|This path has no framework. All discoveries are being made as progression occurs, and there are many unknowns. Your capabilities are being catalogued in real time as you demonstrate them. What you can accomplish may exceed current predictions.|","|9 instances of THE Infinite Root of Uncountable Saturation have been created through Uncountable methodology.|","|These roots differ from your initial creation. Born from weavings that already possessed Uncountable nature, they carry density exceeding the first root by magnitudes that cannot be expressed through Countable comparison. A single root from this batch provides elevation equivalent to multiple roots from Countable production.|","|Consumption of these roots will accelerate your progression toward commanding Uncountable Infinity across all aspects of your existence.|","\"...\"","Noah read these prompts while spinning in skies filled with endless blue, rivers of Infinity cradling his form. The path forward was obvious. He did not need to contemplate or plan or strategize.","He needed to consume.","Without delaying, he reached out and grasped the nearest root, bringing it to his mouth and swallowing it with the same motion. The Uncountable authority flooded into his existence, seeking his Formless Depth and pressing against its Countable limitations with density demanding transformation.","Then he reached for the second root.","Then the third.","Then the fourth, fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth.","Each consumption built upon the previous ones, Uncountable nature spreading through his foundations with momentum that compounded. His spinning accelerated as the rivers of Infinity responded to what he was becoming, their embrace tightening!"]},{"number":5011,"title":"Chapter 5011: Chapter 5010: Glorious Purpose! II","paragraphs":["Noah had already experienced many large jumps in power over his journey since he first became a Hunter.","Some of these jumps were ridiculous ones where his entire body would explode or get deconstructed before being built again, flesh and bone and foundation scattered across existence before reforming into something grander than what had been destroyed.","Other jumps left him physically the same but granted him something that fundamentally changed how he perceived existence itself, alterations to awareness rather than structure.","The jump from Countable to Uncountable was a unique one.","His existence did not explode and reconstruct, but he still felt such a significant force of change in how he could potentially wield Infinity compared to before. The difference was categorical rather than incremental, a transformation in the nature of his relationship with the endless sea he conducted rather than merely an expansion of how much he could conduct.","Which in itself was an understatement.","He had not had all that long to experiment with what the major differences would have been at Countable compared to Uncountable since he declared himself a finite existence. The transition had happened too quickly, the Sacred Herbs too effective, the progression too urgent for extended contemplation of each stage along the way.","He almost complained that he was progressing too fast.","As he took the multiple roots, he felt his Intermediate Depth and Fundamental Depths all gain that same irresistible feeling of Uncountable. It felt like most of his finite existence now possessed the sturdier, more immense capability of commanding Infinity. Where before he had sensed endless points in sequence, now he sensed endless points between endless points, density that filled every gap his previous perception had left empty.","If he had been a scrawny thing that could barely lift five pounds, he could now lift hundreds and thousands and even millions of pounds compared to before.","But even that comparison of measurements of weight did not do justice to what he could do before and what he could do now. The difference was not quantitative. It was qualitative, a fundamental shift in the nature of strength itself rather than merely an increase in how much strength he possessed.","The only part of him that remained at Countable was his Absolute Foundation, where his derivative Civilizations of Infinite Hunger and Infinite Undifferentiated Fate resided. But after his change, all of them felt like they were simply part of his greater Civilization, the entanglement and distinction of derivative slowly becoming lost as his existence unified around its new understanding of Infinity.","Because the main Civilization of Mana was not officially at Absolute, it felt like the vast majority of his body was completely Uncountable, and only this one last part remained. He had been keeping it for a grander foundation, waiting for the right moment to elevate it properly. But he knew that Absolute Infinity was too far away, and since the rest of his finite existence had achieved Uncountable...","\" Take the step.\"","HUUM!","He smiled as he commanded his existence to complete the transformation.","The moment he did, brilliance began to unfold within him as he closed his eyes to feel it. His Absolute Foundation trembled and shifted, Countable limitations dissolving as Uncountable density flooded through the last remaining portion of his existence that had not yet been elevated. The sensation was completion, wholeness, every part of his finite being now capable of conducting Infinity in its denser form.","All of him would stand at Absolute, and all of him would be Uncountable!","But he frowned soon after because he sensed something.","Well, another one of his bodies within THE Agora sensed something. Three auras of considerable magnitude were breaching into the Shores of Kleos and moving rapidly toward his location, their approach carrying intent that suggested this was not a social visit.","At such a pivotal moment of his transformation did things have to arise? Could he not simply complete his advancement in peace?","He sighed lightly as his body in THE Agora focused on the approaching presences.","---","In THE Primordial Archive of THE Agora.","Noah’s seemingly mundane body closed a book that had been shining with stellar obsidian-gold light. The title gleamed across its cover in symbols predating THE Infinite Unfurling: \" Architectural Theorems of Scale Transition: Methodologies of the First Primordial Architects.\"","He had been studying it for insights into what separated THE First Scale from THE Second, seeking understanding that might inform his own unique path.","But he allowed the book to float beside him as he looked up from his research with eyes becoming filled with piercing blue light. He sensed three auras of utmost brilliance breaching into the Shores of Kleos, their trajectory unmistakable. They were coming here, and they were coming fast.","The illusory figure of RUINATION materialized beside him, her blue-gold holographic form flickering into existence with the tragic beauty that characterized her manifestation.","The radiant figure of THE Infiniverse appeared on his other side, multicolored jeweled eyes already focused on the approaching presences with attention.","\" Wrap up the devouring of THE Agora.\"","Noah’s voice emerged calm but heavy with implication.","\" It seems we won’t have a moment of peace.\"","His expression grew serious as he felt the auras more clearly now that they had entered his domain. Two of them blazed with power more terrifying than any Absolute he had encountered. But they should still be at THE First Scale, their authority impressive without crossing the threshold.","The aura of the third was different.","It reminded him of the oppression he had felt from THE Primordial Armor, that crushing weight of someone operating at heights his Scale should not have been able to perceive. The oppression of THE Second Scale. It was likely a Primordial Architect, another ancient being who had achieved what most of existence considered impossible.","Beside him, THE Infiniverse and RUINATION disappeared to work on accelerating their consumption of THE Agora’s resources. They trusted their master to handle whatever approached.","\" How do you compare to Beowulf...\"","He whispered these words with chilly light in his eyes, genuinely curious whether this Primordial Architect would prove as overwhelming as the one who had nearly captured him in THE Wastes. The memory of that confrontation remained fresh, the sensation of his attacks phasing through platinum armor without effect.","In the next moment, the doors of THE Primordial Archive flung open with brilliance that pressed against the ancient space.","Three vibrant figures appeared in the doorway, and before Noah could fully gaze at them, a sharp and authoritative voice was the first thing that boomed out across the Archive.","\"I will have to disappoint. I am not something as simple as Beowulf.\"","WAA!","The words carried weight that made the Grimoires on their shelves tremble!","With these words, Noah saw them clearly.","An Undivided One in humanoid form stood at the front, his skin shining obsidian beneath clear blue robes, his radiant eyes filled with excitement that seemed inappropriate for the circumstances. Beside him, a Formless Terror whose entire body consisted of crimson tentacles arranged into humanoid shape looked at Noah with similar enthusiasm, as if meeting him was the culmination of something long anticipated.","But Noah’s gaze rapidly focused on the figure floating behind them.","A woman adorned in those same blue robes, but the air surrounding her carried weight of an entirely different magnitude.","Her eyes were pure white with blue dots of singularities orbiting within that whiteness, and radiant white hair cascaded down her back with its own faint luminescence. She was strikingly beautiful and...curvaceous!","Around her, Noah’s eyes opened wide as he could see glimmers of his Infinite Absolute Seals, the ones he had scattered across Observable Existence.","But more than that, silent and calm rivers of Infinity occasionally spun around her form before dispersing.","It seemed minor at first glance, but Infinity was rotating around her and empowering her.","His eyes became sharp as he grasped the floating book in his hands, looking at the new entrants who had not attacked right away despite their dramatic entrance. That hesitation suggested they wanted something other than immediate conflict.","\" And what might this be?\"","His voice emerged measured, curious despite the tension pressing against THE Primordial Archive.","\" An Undivided One, a Formless Terror, and a Primordial Architect are moving together to chase Infinity? What an odd thing to see.\"","Existence was vast and filled with wonders, but even this combination was something he had not expected.","The Formless Terror and Undivided One were looking at him with shining eyes. Their enthusiasm was almost unsettling in its intensity.","In the next moment, the Primordial Architect behind them moved forward as her power pressed against the surroundings with authority that made THE Primordial Archive itself seem to contract slightly. Her voice boomed out with confidence that brooked no argument.","\" We came to see the lifeform playing with forces he does not understand. I am Naldine Manthon, and I have come to make sure that you, Osmont, do not cause the Splintering of Observable Existence.\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes became sharp as the words registered.","What the fuck was this crazy thing talking about?","Naldine stepped forward calmly and imposingly, her pure white gaze sweeping across THE Primordial Archive before focusing on him again with intensity that suggested she was trying her hand in evaluating every aspect of his existence simultaneously.","Her voice continued with the certainty of someone who had spent eons building toward this moment.","\" Observable Existence is so vast and stable that even something at THE Second Scale could attack it for eons and it would not crumble. You are weaker than something at THE Second Scale, but you happen to have tapped into a power you barely understand.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes narrowed.","\"If you are foolish enough, Splintering Observable Existence into Undefinition can only be a matter of time. I have listened to the Echoes of THE First Cause and the Artificial Causes over eons. I have studied Infinity and its wonder and its Encroaching Imperiosus.\"","She took another step forward, her presence pressing against Noah as Infinity began to gather around him.","\"I...bear a weight and purpose even you cannot understand.\"","...!"]},{"number":5012,"title":"Chapter 5012: Chapter 5011: THE Gamaidjan! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the Primordial Architect in front of him.","The last Primordial Architect he had encountered had been trying to eat him. His guard remained high, and he was ready to defend and put into practice exactly what Uncountable Infinity could do if this encounter turned violent.","She had come at a critical moment.","His transformation of his main Civilization of Mana to the level of Absolute was occurring right now in his other body within THE Infiniverse, all of his existence shifting toward being fully at the Uncountable Infinity level. The timing was a rather unfortunate coincidence.","But the more time passed, the more he understood exactly what this stage meant for him as a finite being who could command Uncountable Infinities. The density between densities. The endless points filling endless gaps. His capabilities had expanded categorically rather than incrementally, and that expansion changed everything about how he evaluated threats.","So even though a Second Scale Primordial Architect stood before him, he knew he would be able to at least escape if he needed to. THE Infiniverse was already rapidly devouring as much of THE Agora as possible while time passed here, her consumption accelerating in response to her master’s unspoken urgency. Every moment this conversation continued was a moment his forces grew stronger.","If time could pass without conflict, that was ideal.","And the things this Primordial Architect was saying might just be enlightening enough to expand his knowledge, so he would humor her. His eyes shone brightly as he picked up the most important words she had spoken, filing away implications for later analysis.","\"I know very well what I grasp, and I know that utilizing it will not in any way cause the Splintering of Observable Existence.\"","His voice emerged calm and curious.","\" But I will humor you and ask what exactly you mean. And what is Encroaching Imperiosus?\"","...!","He had left the business of apocalypses behind him.","He was not initiating any apocalypses, not spreading destruction for its own sake, not seeking to unmake the foundations of reality. Observable Existence was so stable that even those at THE Second Scale could not damage it through direct assault.","THE Living Paradox and every single thing he was doing with his spread of corruption across THE Prima Indifferentia did nothing except alter the state of existence, transforming what was there rather than destroying the substrate itself.","Observable Existence remained strong despite all of that.","How could Noah have anything to do with the Splintering of Observable Existence? The accusation seemed absurd on its face, the kind of claim made by beings who feared what they did not understand rather than beings who had actually studied the nature of what they criticized.","As he asked all of this, the figure of Naldine continued to walk toward him. Her commanding presence seemed to want to occupy everything within THE Primordial Archive.","She stopped several paces away from him, those pure white eyes with their orbiting blue singularities fixed upon his form with intensity.","\" You stand before a Second Scale Primordial Architect.\"","Her voice emerged cold and precise, each word chosen with care.","\" And even at this moment, you so strongly believe that everything will be okay. That you will somehow survive this encounter unscathed regardless of what occurs. You know nothing of my power or the capabilities of the two fools behind me, and yet your psyche has already deemed that whatever happens here, you will be fine.\"","She took another step forward.","\" You have not accounted for my power, how tremendous it is, or whether I have those even more powerful than myself that I can call down at any second. You simply assume your survival because you are you.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes narrowed.","\" Overconfidence. A sense of self-entitlement as if everything in existence should be yours or handed to you. A sense of arrogance that whatever happens, because it is you, you will be okay.\"","Noah eyes shone brightly as he listened.","\"Eyes that gaze upon everything as if it is lesser compared to you. As if you are the only thing in existence that matters while everyone else is just playing parts in your story. A self-centered view of yourself and your superiority, as if in all of existence, you alone matter.\"","Her voice dropped to something approaching clinical observation.","\" The inability to admit any faults. The certainty that your judgment is correct simply because it is yours. The assumption that your path is the right path because you are the one walking it.\"","She paused, letting her words settle.","\" Does...any of this ring a bell?\"","...!","Noah felt his thoughts buzz as he actually considered what she was saying rather than dismissing it.","Did he think he would survive this encounter? Yes. Had he accounted for her actual power before reaching that conclusion? Well, somewhat.","He subconsciously thought this because of his own power. His own judgment and Intuition that he always relied on. Was that so wrong?","\" Your entire being is already so steeped in THE Encroaching Imperiosus of Infinity that you cannot even distinguish your own mentality from its influence.\"","\"You cannot even begin to realize when you started thinking this way. When your confidence became certainty. When your determination became arrogance. When your strength became entitlement. The transition was so gradual and so complete that you believe these thoughts are yours, that this mentality is simply who you are.\"","Her white hair seemed to glow faintly as she spoke.","\" That is THE Encroaching Imperiosus. THE Gamaidjan. The curse and cost that comes with Infinity, which every Second Scale existence playing with it has to be careful of.\"","She looked at him with something approaching pity beneath her cold evaluation.","\" Because more often than not, this is the cost that causes the highest rates of mortality across truly powerful existences. Not external enemies. Not overwhelming force. Not ancient horrors emerging from THE Prima Indifferentia to consume everything in their path.\"","Her voice hardened.","\" Themselves. Their own certainty that they are special. Their own belief that the rules applying to everyone else do not apply to them. Their own arrogance leading them into situations that their power could not extract them from, because they never truly believed those situations were possible.\"","...!","BOOM!","The revelation pressed against Noah’s awareness. He wasn’t entirely dismissive!","After all, his intuition told him this Primordial Architect was not just making this up.","But...","He found himself actually examining his own thoughts, his own assumptions, his own certainty that he would be fine no matter what.","Where had that certainty come from?","He remembered being afraid. He remembered desperation and uncertainty.","But even then, some part of him had believed he would survive.","Some part of him had never truly accepted the possibility of his own ending.","Was that confidence earned through countless victories? Was that determination forged through adversity that had always, eventually, been overcome? Or was that something else entirely, something that had crept into his foundations alongside the Infinity he conducted?","THE Beholder’s warning echoed through his memory.","Your biggest strength will be Infinity. And your biggest weakness will be Infinity.","Everything comes at a cost. Everything has a cost.","He thought about all of this, but in the end, the thought he arrived to was...no.","No.","He was walking a fine line between confidence and arrogance.","But he knew himself.","He was tyrannical, yes. But he...was also quintessential .","So towards the heavy words from Naldine that should have been akin to a grand revelation, he looked at her and smiled brilliantly, and her gaze became even heavier and colder!"]},{"number":5013,"title":"Chapter 5013: Chapter 5012: THE Gamaidjan! II","paragraphs":["Naldine saw Noah’s smile and shook her head slowly.","\" Did any of what I said go through your head? Or has THE Gamaidjan become so entrenched within you?\"","Her voice carried weight pressing against THE Primordial Archive around them.","\" Has the madness of Infinity already permeated inside of you so much? You have been the one utilizing it the most, so it would be understandable if you could no longer distinguish between your own thoughts and its influence.\"","Her calm and powerful eyes shone brightly, eyes that had witnessed eons of existence and the rise and fall of beings who had believed themselves beyond consequence. She looked at Noah as if examining a specimen, searching for signs of infection she was certain existed.","Noah looked at this Primordial Architect as he waved his hands.","Rivers of Infinity began to swirl around his fingers, blue light gathering from directions that should not have contained anything to gather. But this was not the sequential flow he had commanded before his transformation. This was Uncountable in nature, endless points filling the gaps between endless points, density that made his previous expressions seem like trickles compared to floods.","Dense! Dense! Dense!","The rivers quickly transformed into raging torrents, their power ecstatic and eager. They swirled around his hands and arms and shoulders with intensity that pressed against the ancient knowledge stored within THE Primordial Archive, Grimoires trembling on their shelves in response to authority they had never encountered before.","Arthur and Gunther saw this from behind Naldine, and their eyes shone brighter as they came closer. The Undivided One’s obsidian features practically glowed with reverence, while the Formless Terror’s crimson tentacles churned with excitement he could barely contain.","Noah let the rivers rage around him as he spoke.","\" You speak of arrogance and self-entitlement. Of eyes that gaze upon everything as lesser. Of certainty that my path is right simply because it is mine.\"","His voice emerged calm, measured, and had the weight of someone who had genuinely considered the accusation before responding.","\"I know the line between arrogance and confidence. I know I am not the center of existence. I have lived for such a short time while existence has been around trillions of times longer than what I have experienced. The cycles before me stretch beyond comprehension, and the cycles after me will likely stretch just as far.\"","He looked at Naldine directly.","\" But even if I know I am not at the center of existence, I can still move and act with confidence. To go through the adversity of existence, one needs confidence in themselves. In their way. In their ability to overcome whatever descends upon them.\"","The rivers of Infinity around him intensified.","\"I have profound confidence that I have not fallen to the madness of Infinity. But hey, maybe I am wrong.\"","He smiled.","\"Is me thinking I could be wrong not also refuting the curse? THE Gamaidjan? I doubt. I fear. I question my own assumptions and examine my own thoughts.\"","His eyes shone with light that pressed against Naldine’s Second Scale presence.","\" But forget all that. Let me ask you this, O Primordial Architect. Naldine Manthon.\"","He paused.","\" Do you fear death?\"","BOOM!","The question seemed simple on its surface. Naldine looked at him closely, her pure white eyes with their orbiting blue singularities fixed upon his form with intensity that suggested she was evaluating whether this question deserved a serious answer.","It did.","\" Death is nothing to us.\"","Her voice emerged with the certainty of philosophy refined across eons of contemplation.","\" Because when we exist, death is not here. And when death is here, we do not exist. Since pleasure and pain require consciousness, non-existence is neither good nor bad. It simply is the absence of experience, and absence cannot be experienced.\"","Her white hair seemed to glow faintly as she continued.","\" Death is a natural, fated part of existence, like birth. The cycle completes itself regardless of our feelings about its completion. To fear death is to fear the inevitable, and fearing the inevitable accomplishes nothing except poisoning whatever time remains before its arrival.\"","Her eyes were cold and glorious.","\"I do not fear death.\"","...!","Noah clapped his hands calmly, the sound cutting through the raging rivers of Infinity still swirling around his form.","\" Well said!\"","His voice carried genuine appreciation.","\"I also do not fear death. Not because I believe I cannot die, but because if I do, many who depend on me will face difficulties. My family. My forces. My Civilization. All of them would suffer consequences I cannot permit them to suffer.\"","He let his hands fall to his sides, the rivers of Infinity calming slightly in response.","\" So while I do not fear death, I cannot have it happen. Thus, I move and act with profound confidence because I told myself, and I keep telling myself, I cannot die. Not because I really cannot die. I know I can. But because I know I cannot have that happen. Not just yet.\"","His eyes shone with purpose that had nothing to do with arrogance.","Death was a unique thing. And even now, Noah had not met anything that could not die. They could live for as many eons as they wanted...but their existences could still be collapsed!","\" I have so much to do. So much to learn. So much of Infinity for me to explore and so much of existence to understand. That is why I know I have not gone mad with Infinity.\"","He looked at Naldine with expression carrying neither hostility nor submission.","\" Thanks for your input and information, but it may not truly apply to me.\"","...!","Naldine looked at him coldly, her expression unchanged by his words despite their logic.","\" THE Gamaidjan is never so simple. It would not be so simple in its effects for someone like you. It expresses differently for everyone. \"","Her voice dropped to something approaching warning.","\" Say, does this ring a bell?\"","She began to speak words that pressed against reality itself.","\" The Shroud of Endless Blue shall fall upon Observable Existence. It shall be both salvation and damnation, both the key and the lock, both the bridge and the chasm. Under its weight, the doors of the Scales shall open or the doors of the Scales shall shatter. There is no third path. There is no middle ground. There is only the choice that is not a choice.\"","...!"]},{"number":5014,"title":"Chapter 5014: Chapter 5013: Echoes I","paragraphs":["Her eyes burned with the intensity of someone reciting words they had spent eons studying.","\" This is what shall come to pass, for it has already passed, and it shall pass again. The wheel turns. The river flows. The question echoes.\"","Her voice reached crescendo.","\" He shall be the answer, or he shall be nothing. Or he shall be the question that ends all answers.\"","...!","She had uttered the Echoes Noah had heard some time ago.","Well, not really all that long ago in objective terms, but so much had happened since then. Since his trip from eons ago from THE Prima Indifferentia. Since he had first heard those words and wondered what they meant for his future.","He could not help but smile devilishly as recognition flickered across his features.","\" Now, where did you hear that?\"","Naldine’s expression remained cold as she waved her own hand in response.","Waves of her power at THE Second Scale erupted from her form, authority that made the raging rivers of Infinity around Noah seem slightly less by comparison. Her grand Civilization covered her existence with a white bubble of light blazing with intensity that spoke of eons of refinement and cultivation.","And that white bubble began to pull a single, silent river of Infinity to swirl around it.","Just one. Not the dozens raging around Noah. Not the ecstatic torrents that responded to his every thought. Just a single river, tugged toward her Civilization with methodology that spoke of careful study.","\"I have heard this Echo and more.\"","Her voice emerged with weight pressing against everything within THE Primordial Archive.","\" And I am here to ensure you do not fall to THE Gamaidjan. Because for some fucking reason, you shall be the answer, or you shall be nothing. You shall be both salvation and damnation, as under your weight, the doors of the Scales shall open or the doors of the Scales shall shatter.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed.","\" For some fucking insane reason, the fate of Observable Existence may rest on whether you maintain your sanity while wielding authority that has driven beings far older than you into madness.\"","She stepped forward, her white bubble of Civilization and its single river of Infinity pressing against Noah’s raging torrents.","\" Help me help you, and there will not be issues. Defy me...\"","Her smile was cold and beautiful.","\" Well, I have changed plenty of Echoes of Causes myself. I would be itching to give a try to one of the biggest ones.\"","BOOM!","Her visage was glorious and imposing, and she did not lose out at all to Noah’s brilliance. Two forces pressed against each other within THE Primordial Archive, rivers of Uncountable Infinity meeting a single river pulled by methodology refined across eons.","Noah remained calm as his eyes shone with something new.","Curiosity.","\" One of the biggest ones?\"","His voice carried genuine interest that had nothing to do with the confrontation pressing against him.","\" You know of other Echoes like that from THE First Cause?\"","He was curious.","Now, he was really curious.","---","When an unstoppable force meets an immovable object, what happens?","At this moment in time, there was an extremely old existence that had seen a great deal, asserting something with tremendous confidence born from eons of observation and study. On the other side stood a relatively young existence who was also asserting something with tremendous confidence, the basis of his certainty being one of astounding origin that the old existence could not fully comprehend.","Both believed they were absolutely right.","But both were wise enough to also doubt that there could be a chance they were wrong.","Naldine looked at the entity she had been searching for across Observable Existence, the Guider of Infinity who had scattered his authority so freely that tracking him had become almost trivial once she knew what to look for. At this moment, she chose to extend a careful sliver of the benefit of the doubt.","Her body stopped buzzing with the light of Infinity, the single river she had tugged toward her Civilization dispersing back into the ambient weavings of THE Primordial Archive. The confrontational pressure that had been building between them eased slightly, though neither relaxed their awareness of the other.","\" What exactly do you think the Echoes of THE First Cause are?\"","Noah took this question calmly. The rivers of Uncountable Infinity still swirled around his form, but they too had calmed from raging torrents to something more measured.","\" Weavings of probabilities and possibilities that emerged a number of years ago.\"","His answer was simple, direct, and based on what he had understood from his limited exposure to such phenomena.","Naldine listened to this before she gazed at his face closely.","\" The Echoes of THE First Cause are existence’s self-defense mechanisms.\"","Her voice carried weight accumulated across eons of study.","\" You are right about probabilities. THE First Cause is the emergence of Observable Existence, and at its emergence, it looked ahead to all the Infinite variations of what it could be. Pay attention to that word. Infinite. The variations were Infinite, and from those Infinite variations emerged patterns, possibilities, probabilities that pressed themselves into the fabric of what would come to be.\"","She paused, letting her words settle.","\" The Echoes of THE First Cause tell what could be. No matter how grand your belief in yourself is, the Echoes that may involve you are a small part of the greater whole. But small parts can be significant. A single crack can shatter a foundation. A single choice can redirect a river.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes focused on him with intensity.","\" The Echoes traverse to those capable of hearing them. There is no specific purpose for this traversal, really. We do not hear them so that we can move in particular directions. But if you do hear them and choose to move, that is your own choice. Because after all, they are all probabilities. Anyone making a move based on an Echo would simply want to steer toward one particular probability compared to others.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" Do you want to know of the Oldest Echo I have heard?\"","...!"]},{"number":5015,"title":"Chapter 5015: Chapter 5014: Echoes II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes were radiant as he processed what she was offering.","Did he really come across another old babbler who would talk and talk and talk to reveal things about existence he did not know? He had encountered beings like this before, ancient existences who could not resist sharing their accumulated wisdom with anyone who showed even marginal interest.","Okay old hag , he thought. We love listening to babblers.","So he humored her and asked with genuine curiosity, \" What is the oldest Echo?\"","Naldine’s expression shifted to something approaching solemnity, her features taking on weight. The blue singularities in her white eyes slowed their orbiting, as if even they recognized the significance of what was coming.","\" Listen well, for these words predate most of what currently exists.\"","Her voice dropped to cadence that felt ancient, each syllable pressing against THE Primordial Archive with heaviness that made even the Grimoires seem young by comparison.","\" An Architect shall build a beacon born of strife,","Where adversity becomes the cornerstone of life.","A peasant clothed in rags shall swallow evolution whole,","And through consumption find the fragments of a greater whole.","Architects shall watch from heights where slumber is their throne,","While Cognizances guide in idle patterns yet unknown.","The Source forgotten or remembered, burning dim or bright,","And Infinity shall flicker between the dark and light.","When the leap is made between what is defined and not,","Between the differentiated and the formless thought,","There shall be glory rising, Scales ascending high,","Or there shall be the Splintering beneath an endless sky.","The choice that is not choice, the path that is not path,","The calculation made before the aftermath.","All things return to what they were before they came to be,","Or all things rise to heights that none have lived to see.\"","...!","BOOM!","When she spoke the words, they felt so unfathomably ancient and heavy that Noah could sense them pressing against his foundations with glory that had nothing to do with Naldine’s personal authority!","These were not her words. These were words that had existed since THE First Cause itself, patterns of probability that had embedded themselves into the fabric of Observable Existence before most of what currently lived had even begun to differentiate.","The rivers of Infinity around him buzzed in response.","Naldine looked at Noah, whose eyes now burned with visible Infinity, blue light blazing from his gaze as he processed what he had just heard.","\" Just to knock down your Gamaidjan a bit.\"","Her voice carried cold amusement.","\" Your name and weavings were not even mentioned within one of the oldest Echoes. This is just to check your ego, to tell you that you are not everything. Existence is vast. It was vast before you, and it will be vast after you. Whatever role you play in what is coming, it is a role among many roles, not the singular protagonist you may believe yourself to be.\"","Noah ignored her last words entirely.","His attention had fixed upon the oldest Echo with intensity that blocked out everything else within THE Primordial Archive. He was repeating it in his mind again and again, each word examined and reexamined as he searched for what he could decipher from its ancient patterns.","All things return to what they were before they came to be, Or all things rise to heights that none have lived to see.","Fuck, that was good!","An Architect shall build a beacon born of strife.","Was that THE Creature? Someone else?","A peasant clothed in rags shall swallow evolution whole.","That felt significant in ways he could not yet articulate. The peasant. The motherfuckin peasant!","This guy had his name in all this so long ago?!","There shall be glory rising, Scales ascending high, or there shall be the Splintering beneath an endless sky.","Glory or Splintering.","Advancement or destruction.","No middle ground.","Noah’s mind raced through the possibilities, through the connections, through the patterns that might link this oldest Echo to the one he knew about the Shroud of Endless Blue. Were they different probabilities pointing toward similar outcomes? Were they fragments of a greater pattern that no single Echo could fully express?","He needed to know more.","He needed to understand what existence itself had predicted since before most of what currently lived had even begun to exist!","Noah’s mind continued racing through the possibilities and connections, each line of the oldest Echo branching into interpretations that led to more interpretations.","Naldine looked at him calmly.","\" With any Echo of possibilities, you and I and many others can perceive it differently.\"","Her voice cut through his contemplation with precision.","\" When some hear ’All things return to what they were before they came to be, or all things rise to heights that none have lived to see,’ there are those like me who prefer the rise to heights.\"","Her singularity-dotted gaze hardened.","\" And then there are those who want things to return to what they were.\"","BOOM!","Noah shook his head and refocused on her as he almost wanted to say, what?","The implication of her words pressed against his awareness with glory that made the oldest Echo seem like preamble.","Naldine continued without waiting for his response.","\" Some benefit a great deal from the Splintering. Some want things to return to what they were, as they seek Infinity and a Source you do not even understand yet. They want Observable Existence to unravel back toward undifferentiation, back toward the potential that existed before THE First Cause imposed structure upon chaos.\"","Her voice dropped to something approaching genuine warning.","\" When you announced your Infinity across Observable Existence, you made yourself a target of unfathomable proportions. You fucking just sat there and said hey, I am over here. Just come and fuck me up when you get the chance.\"","...!","Noah felt the wonder of that truth settle into his awareness.","He had spread his Infinite Absolute Seals across Observable Existence because it served his purposes, because it expanded his influence, because it allowed him to accomplish things that would have been impossible otherwise. Adversity. Adversity! Adversity!","Naldine’s gaze hardened further as she continued.","\" Things are never black and white. Good or bad. There are only probabilities, and right now, there are others like me moving to steer probabilities they believe are most conducive to their power.\"","She paused.","\" And there are others even more powerful than me who have already found those named in Echoes. The Peasant. The Architect. Others whose identities I will not speak aloud in a place like this.\"","Her white eyes blazed with intensity.","\" You...need to be very clear where you stand, and you need to get moving.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5016,"title":"Chapter 5016: Chapter 5015: Magisterial! I","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes were unfathomably bright.","The situation around him became clearer with each word Naldine spoke. There were monstrous beings like her, like THE Primordial Armor, and others who followed their own beliefs to push into existence terrifying probabilities.","Factions operating at scales he had not previously considered, steering toward outcomes that served their purposes regardless of what those outcomes meant for everyone else.","Naldine was saying to get a move on due to this, but even before she arrived, he already was.","The moment his finite existence was declared and he became clearer on his capabilities, he had begun moving to clear the board of his enemies.","THE Entity was being bombarded with Infinity while THE Great Usurper silently attacked from within, Eckert’s Idle Weavings spreading through that warm unity without detection.","And he had taken the step to attain Absolute for all his foundations, paired with Uncountable Infinity, preparing himself to make the decisive move he already knew he needed to make.","He checked his existence as his transformation was almost complete.","So as this occurred, he looked at Naldine sharply.","\" So, you need me for the probabilities you want to achieve. I...do not particularly need you.\"","His voice carried weight pressing against her Second Scale presence.","\" You are here to keep an eye on me? Ensure THE Gamaidjan does not overtake me? Does this mean the great Primordial Architect, Naldine Manthon, will be following me?\"","...!","The Primordial Architect before him gazed forth with chilly light, her singularity-dotted eyes narrowing at the implication of his words.","\" My path is a glorious one that does not involve becoming a follower.\"","Her voice emerged cold and precise.","\" You have your Echoes, I have mine. I look at you akin to a young lifeform with an extremely sharp blade that influences you without your knowing. The things you could cut with this blade are many, and among them are my own weavings.\"","She paused.","\" Thus, if I step in early enough before you cut things you should not, what I want will also be achieved in time. The question becomes whether you will oppose me and make it difficult.\"","Her white eyes blazed with authority.","\" What I need to do is observe and shield you from being used by others as powerful if not more powerful than me, beings who would use you to achieve their objectives of Splintering Observable Existence or other worse thingd. Of returning things to a state that would not be ideal.\"","...!","Noah smiled brilliantly as he looked at this Primordial Architect.","She wanted to join him, but her pride was too high to frame it as becoming a follower. She had to present it as observation, as shielding, as ensuring he did not cut things he should not cut. The semantics amused him.","But unlike what she believed about THE Encroaching Imperiosus being drenched within him, he was not prideful at all about allowing a Second Scale Primordial Architect to be beside one of his bodies. He could use her as a shield to make things even easier for himself.","Why not?","But of course, he could always try to get more benefits.","He looked at her as he waved his hands, revealing three lotus petals shimmering with blue-gold light. THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity, one of his Sacred Herbs capable of granting access to Countable Infinity.","\"If you take one of these lotus petals, you can have more Infinity flowing through you.\"","He said the words enticingly, offering power that beings across Observable Existence would have killed to possess.","Naldine did not even look at the lotuses a second time.","She moved away, her eyes wandering to all the books and Grimoires nearby as she began examining the contents of THE Primordial Archive with interest.","\" My weavings of Infinity are mine to explore. I will not accept anything from another.\"","Her voice carried finality that brooked no negotiation.","\" You can try your luck with those two fools behind me if you wish.\"","...!","Noah looked over to the Undivided One and Formless Terror whose eyes were shining brilliantly. Their enthusiasm was barely contained. Where Naldine’s pride prevented her from accepting, these two had no such reservations.","They came forward eagerly as Naldine asked calmly while she began flipping through a Grimoire.","\" The weavings of Unity that are permeating throughout. Are such minor things stumping you to need help?\"","Her voice carried dismissiveness!","\" They are significant enough since they are mentioned in Echoes, but they should not be a major ordeal unless you make it out to be. And the Echoes never have to play out. Remember, they are only the likeliest probabilities, nothing more.\"","She said such words casually as Noah handed out two lotus petals to float toward the powerful entities before him. The deep voice of the Undivided One emerged with gratitude as he introduced himself properly.","\"I am Arthur. The Great Arthur. And I have waited eons to touch true Infinity.\"","The Formless Terror’s crimson tentacles churned with excitement as he spoke next.","\" Gunther. And I share my companion’s sentiment entirely.\"","Noah nodded toward them before he turned back to Naldine.","\" As soon as one last piece clicks into place in the next few seconds, I will be attacking that Unity here and... across time.\"","His eyes shone with purpose.","\" For the sake of just further proving you wrong, I will not act all imperious and grand. I am curious what exactly you can contribute, so even though I do not think I need your help, you can exert your hand. I will let you know when ready.\"","...!","Naldine listened to this calmly before she closed the Grimoire and looked outside THE Archive.","During their talk, all of THE Agora had been taken apart piece by piece by THE Infiniverse’s relentless consumption. This place, THE Primordial Archive, was the only thing that remained. Everything else had been devoured and integrated into Noah’s forces, resources accumulated while words were exchanged.","The expression on Naldine was a unique one at this moment.","Her cold exterior remained, but barely discernible beneath her terrifying power, there was a sense of relief. She had taken a step toward something that had been weighing her down for a long, long time.","Eons of hearing Echoes and wondering what they meant, eons of searching for the one who would be the answer or the nothing, eons of preparing for a confrontation that might determine whether Observable Existence rose to heights or Splintered beneath an endless sky.","She took in a single breath before she turned back to Noah.","\" Anything infected with Unity must be extinguished. You cannot save any.\"","\" So even the Claimer of Chaos, THE Primordial Chaos, needs to die.\"","BOOM!","Her words were heavy as Noah sensed the changes occurring within Arthur and Gunther, their foundations shifting as Bounded Countable Infinity began integrating with their existences. He responded seriously to her declaration.","\" Maybe. Maybe not.\"","Naldine’s eyes sharpened at his response.","\"I collapsed the one you call Paradoxos who was unified with Unity. I peered into its existence and memories before the ash dispersed entirely.\"","Her voice dropped to something approaching genuine warning.","\" What you call THE Entity, THE Primordial Mycelia, should have its origins tracing back to one of the Primordial Architects you need to be cautious of. Its weavings irreversibly bind to the host. Unless their existence is collapsed entirely, there will be a resurgence. The Unity will return. The infection will spread again. This is not speculation. This is what I observed in the memories of something that had been fully consumed.\"","...!","She revealed heavy news as Noah frowned at the implications.","THE Entity’s weavings were irreversible. THE Primordial Chaos, who had been infected, would need to die for the infection to truly end. There was no cure. There was no reversal. There was only collapse or continued spread.","But...Noah repeated himself while waiting for the final pieces to click into place within his transforming existence.","\" Maybe. Maybe not.\"","BOOM!","He was thinking of THE Great Usurper and other things that even this Primordial Architect did not know!"]},{"number":5017,"title":"Chapter 5017: Chapter 5016: Magisterial! II","paragraphs":["Noah was in the middle of beginning to respond to Naldine when he stopped.","His body began to emanate waves of blue and multicolored brilliance that pressed against THE Primordial Archive. The transformation he had been monitoring in his other body within THE Infiniverse had finally completed, and the effects cascaded across all instances of his existence simultaneously.","His Civilization of Mana had stepped into Absolute.","Noah felt the change ripple through his foundations with force that made his previous elevations seem...mild. Even though his existence was finite, even though he had declared himself a conductor rather than a container, he felt a terrifying force and brilliance building within him rapidly. It was colorless and multicolored at the same time, generating itself endlessly from somewhere deep within his finite form.","This was something he was very familiar with.","This was something he had always had with him, something that had been present since his earliest days of cultivation. This was the fundamental force that had carried him through every transformation, every advancement, every impossible leap that should have destroyed him but instead made him stronger.","This was... Quintessence.","But not Quintessence as he had known it before.","|Existential Threshold Achieved|","|With all Depths and Civilizations at Absolute and standing at Uncountable Infinity, your existence has attained the precipice of its brilliance. The finite vessel conducting infinite authority has reached a state of harmony that permits the unlocking of capabilities previously dormant within your foundations.|","| Existential Quintessence Infiniforce has been awakened.|","|This force represents the union of your finite nature with the Uncountable Infinities you now command. Where external Infinity must be conducted from other sources and Observable Existence, Quintessence Infiniforce generates from within your own being . It is yours in a way that conducted Infinity can never be yours, born from the very structure of what you are rather than directed from what exists outside you.|","| You can generate limitless amounts of Quintessence Infiniforce from your body. However, because you are finite, you may only handle a certain amount limited by your Scale. The vessel remains finite even as what it produces approaches infinite. This is not a flaw but a feature, for without limitation, identity dissolves into the endless sea it produces.|","|The immensity of your Quintessence Infiniforce equals the vastness of all regions where you have spread weavings of your Infinity. Every Infinite Absolute Seal scattered across Observable Existence and all other definable weavings of infinity contribute to the density of what you can generate within yourself. You can endlessly produce this force to utilize in conjunction with the Infinity you guide and conduct externally.|","|Critical Capability: Even if you existed in endless Undifferentiation or Undefinition where endless potential or Infinity does not flow, you would be capable of endlessly generating Quintessence Infiniforce to fill the external system you occupy. Your finite existence becomes a source rather than merely a conduit. The only limitation is your finite scope of existence itself.|","|Warning: Meditation and other forms of identity affirmation may be required to ground and stabilize your finite existence when generating beyond comfortable thresholds. The Uncountable nature of your Infiniforce means infinite density between infinite densities, endless points filling endless gaps within your own foundations. Without proper stabilization, coherence may become difficult to maintain. What was termed as Encroaching Imperiosus, THE Gamaidjan, may actually occur.|","Noah felt the changes cascading through his existence with euphoria!","He began to endlessly generate Quintessence Infiniforce, and it shone with multicolored light within him, illuminating his foundations from the inside rather than pressing against them from without.","His body began to shine more and more brilliantly.","His skin took on qualities approaching crystalline, light refracting through his form in patterns of density accumulating beyond what flesh should be able to contain. The finite vessel was producing infinite force, and that production was accelerating with each moment that passed.","Naldine became serious while looking at him.","She did not sense the Infinity he had been using before, that external authority conducted from Observable Existence through his finite form. What she sensed now was different. A different type of Infinity entirely, and it was not something he was conducting from outside himself.","It was generating from within him.","Her singularity-dotted eyes widened slightly as she watched this young existence produce what should have been impossible for anything at THE First Scale to produce independently.","Noah took one hand and filled it with Quintessence Infiniforce.","The limb became multicolored crystalline, light blazing from his palm with density that pressed against THE Primordial Archive’s ancient walls. The force swirled and compressed within his grasp, infinite points filling infinite gaps within infinite gaps, Uncountable in nature and entirely his own.","Then he took his other hand as endless blue waves of Infinity from Observable Existence surged toward it.","The external authority responded to his will with eagerness it had always displayed, conducted by his finite form. This was the Infinity he knew, the endless sea he directed rather than contained.","His eyes burned with light of euphoria as he looked at both hands.","One holding internally generated Quintessence Infiniforce, multicolored and crystalline and entirely his own.","One holding externally conducted Infinity, blue and endless and drawn from Observable Existence.","All his cells were cheering with recognition that something magnificent was about to occur. He could not help but laugh as he began bringing his palms together, drawn toward each other with force that felt irresistible, drawn by all parts of him feeling a sense of euphoria he couldnt explain!","The motion seemed to occur in slow motion.","Naldine’s expression changed rapidly as she recognized what was happening.","\" Stop!\"","Her voice boomed across THE Primordial Archive with authority at THE Second Scale, power that should have frozen anything at THE First Scale in place. She moved simultaneously, her existence flickering as she quickly transported Arthur and Gunther away from THE Primordial Archive entirely.","Then she took a step forward to stop Noah’s hands.","His palms were approaching each other with momentum that seemed irresistible, two different Infinities drawing together with attraction that exceeded anything Naldine had witnessed in eons of existence!","Naldine grasped both of his hands with grip that should have shattered anything at his Scale.","Her body buzzed with power at THE Second Scale as she roared and pushed, trying to force his palms apart. Her Civilization blazed around her, that white bubble of light straining against the forces drawing his hands together.","But they continued forward.","Endlessly.","Irresistibly.","Her Second Scale authority was not enough to stop the attraction between two forms of Infinity that had never been brought together within a single finite existence before!","And before Noah’s eyes, new words appeared.","|Warning: Unprecedented Event Detected|","|You are potentially causing the emergence of a Miniature Existential Cause. The collision of internally generated Quintessence Infiniforce with externally conducted Infinity within a finite vessel has never been recorded in Observable Existence.|","| The results are unknown if this process is not stopped.|","...!"]},{"number":5018,"title":"Chapter 5018: Chapter 5017: Magisterial! III","paragraphs":["Naldine had walked Observable Existence for eons beyond counting.","She had witnessed the rise and fall of Civilizations that current beings considered ancient history. She had studied the Echoes of THE First Cause when most who now lived had not yet begun to differentiate from potential into form.","She had grasped THE Second Scale through methodology refined across cycles that would have crushed lesser existences into forgetfulness.","And she had come here to ensure the Guider of Infinity did not contribute to the Splintering of Observable Existence.","Yet, the first thing he did before her was something that might unravel all of nearby existence.","Her mind processed what she was witnessing with speed that beings at THE First Scale could not comprehend. The attraction between two forms of endless authority that had never been brought together in this configuration.","The irresistible momentum drawing his palms toward each other despite her Second Scale grip attempting to force them apart.","She recognized what would be happening immediately as someone of her stature.. could perceive what would occur in the immediate future alongside the present. And what she affirmed was...","A Miniature Cause.","Something only those at THE Second Scale even knew and understood in theory.","Something that could reshape local reality in ways that echoed THE First Cause itself, producing differentiation or undifferentiation depending on factors that could not be predicted before the event occurred.","Miniature Causes were how Primordial Architects tested theories too dangerous to implement at full scale. They were controlled experiments conducted in isolated regions where the results could be contained.","This was not controlled.","This was not isolated.","This was a young lifeform at THE First Scale accidentally initiating something that could tear apart everything within light years of their current position, and his palms were still moving toward each other despite her grip pressing against them with authority that should have been absolute!","Naldine’s Civilization blazed around her with intensity she had not displayed in eons.","Limitless Existence.","Her path through THE Second Scale had been built upon the understanding that existence itself had no boundaries except those imposed by perception. She had cultivated this truth until it became her foundation, until the very concept of limitation became something she could reject within her domain.","Her Civilization allowed her to interact with Infinity because she had made herself theoretically limitless in nature, capable of touching the endless without being overwhelmed by its scope.","She used that Civilization now.","Her hands were not enough. Her grip was not enough. The attraction between his palms exceeded what simple physical intervention could counter, two forms of Infinity recognizing kindred nature and seeking reunion!","So she smacked one hand back with the full weight of her Civilization.","The blow carried authority at THE Second Scale, Limitless Existence pressing against his Quintessence Infiniforce with rejection that declared this collision would not occur.","His left hand flew backward from the impact, multicolored crystalline light scattering from his palm as the internally generated force dispersed slightly.","But his right hand was still moving forward.","The externally conducted Infinity from Observable Existence was still surging toward the space where his palms would have met, still seeking the collision that her intervention had delayed but not prevented.","Naldine did not hesitate.","She squeezed herself between his palms, her body occupying the space where the Miniature Cause would have emerged.","Her back pressed against his chest as she faced the incoming surge of blue Infinity, her hands reaching out to grasp his arms and force them apart with strength that exceeded what her physical form suggested she possessed.","BOOM!","She was calm.","She was imperious.","Her Civilization of Limitless Existence blazed around her like armor, rejecting the collision by placing herself at its center and declaring that no Cause would emerge through her domain. The blue waves of conducted Infinity crashed against her white bubble of light and scattered, redirected away from the point of convergence she now occupied.","His arms resisted her push with the irresistible momentum that had characterized their approach, but she was at THE Second Scale, and her authority exceeded his regardless of what new capabilities he had just unlocked.","She forced his arms apart with steady pressure that brooked no argument, his left hand pushed away from his body, his right hand pushed in the opposite direction.","The attraction between the two Infinities began to fade as distance increased.","Naldine breathed.","Just breathed.","Simple breaths that grounded her existence after exerting authority she had not needed to exert in longer than she cared to remember.","Her white hair had fallen slightly out of its perfect arrangement, strands clinging to her neck where slight sweat had formed from the effort of stopping something that should not have been possible at his Scale.","And at this time...","Noah felt the sudden euphoria within him slowly die down as the collision was prevented.","He breathed out heavily, awareness returning to normal parameters after the overwhelming sensation of his Quintessence Infiniforce awakening. His cells were no longer cheering. His existence was no longer pushing toward union that his conscious mind had not fully understood.","He saw the back of Naldine before him, her form still pressed against his chest, her hands still gripping his arms to keep them separated.","Her hair was filled with slight sweat, white strands catching the ambient light of THE Primordial Archive in ways that made them seem almost luminescent.","She turned around to face him slowly.","Her movement brought her face close to his, her pure white eyes with their orbiting blue singularities meeting his gaze from distance that would have been inappropriate under any other circumstances.","Her breathing was still slightly elevated, her composure still slightly disrupted from the exertion of stopping a Miniature Cause through sheer force of Civilization.","\" Do not fucking start initiating Causes that have unpredictable results right now.\"","Her voice was low, controlled, and carrying warning that pressed against his awareness with weight befitting someone who had just prevented him from accidentally unraveling nearby existence!","...!","Endless Generation.","This term alone was astounding as Noah looked at the Primordial Architect whose face was inches away from his own. Her pure white eyes searched his gaze for something, and after she affirmed his eyes were cognizant and present rather than lost in the euphoria that had nearly caused catastrophe, she let go of his arms and moved two steps backward.","Noah rubbed the areas on his hands where she had clamped down, the pressure of a Second Scale grip leaving sensations that would linger for some time. He thought about what he had just done, about the irresistible attraction that had drawn his palms together, about the collision that Naldine had prevented through direct intervention.","\"A Miniature Cause?\"","Naldine looked at him with sharp eyes as she waved her hands. The bodies of Arthur and Gunther returned to THE Primordial Archive, both of their eyes closed as they processed the changes of Bounded Countable Infinity integrating with their foundations. They would be occupied for some time yet.","\" Something extremely rare for even those at THE Second Scale to accomplish.\"","Her voice carried weight befitting the subject matter.","\"A Miniature Cause is brought into fruition by the interactions of our Civilizations with Infinity in such a profound way that we can initiate Fake Causes, or Miniature Causes, that try to mimic the endless potential that existed before THE First Cause imposed structure upon chaos.\"","She looked at him with an evaluation that suggested she was still processing how he had nearly accomplished this accidentally.","\" Throw a Miniature Cause at your enemy, and anything could happen. They could be unraveled back into undifferentiation. They could be made grander than they were before. They could simply disappear as if they never existed. You would not know the result until it occurred, and sometimes not even then.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes hardened.","\" The results are unpredictable by design, for they mimic the unpredictability of THE First Cause itself. But you can bet on everything nearby being erased by the process regardless of what specific outcome emerges.\"","...!","Her words were heavy ones as Noah thought about that irresistible feeling of bringing together Quintessence Infiniforce with conducted Infinity. The attraction had been so natural, so obvious, as if two halves of something greater had recognized each other and sought union without consulting his conscious intent.","Even at this moment, his body continued to endlessly generate that multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce within him. He could feel his existence rapidly getting more and more immense, density accumulating within his finite foundations as the internal production showed no signs of slowing. His finite body had yet to reach a topping point, and he wondered if such a point even existed or if he would simply keep generating until his Scale itself demanded he stop.","And even when it did reach that limit, he would continue generating Quintessence Infiniforce to fill all of THE Infiniverse at the very least. The internally produced force would flow outward to empower his domain, his forces, and his Civilization.","This energy of endless potential was something he wanted to explore thoroughly.","He wanted to see what it could do when utilized properly rather than accidentally.","So he looked toward Naldine with eyes that had calmed from their previous euphoria.","\"I will try not to cause any Miniature Causes for now. But I am ready to continue my assault to clear the board against my enemies.\"","He paused.","\" What will you do?\"","Naldine Manthon frowned as she looked at him with stern gaze, her expression suggesting she was genuinely worried he would try to unravel existence again the moment she stopped watching.","\" What do you plan to do?\"","Her voice held suspicion that had not been present before she witnessed him nearly initiate a Miniature Cause through accident alone.","Noah smiled at the question.","\" Well, this one actually involves an attack ranging across time, so I will mess around with the past a bit.\"","BOOM!","Naldine’s expression became colder as she looked at him as if he already had several screws loose. They had just established how dangerous he could be, how close he had come to erasing everything nearby through the collision of two Infinities within his finite form. And now he wanted to mess with time? Temporal weavings that could destabilize the very flow of existence itself?","\"...\"","She wondered how Observable Existence was not already unraveling if this being was doing all of this just in the brief period she had been present.","Was his power not enough to destroy things in the past? Was he somehow protected by mechanisms she could not perceive? Or was he actually cognizant and knowledgeable of what he was doing, operating within boundaries that only appeared reckless from outside observation?","She looked at him up and down as if gauging which possibility was more likely.","Then she shook her head.","She felt like the first thought was much more supported. This guy seemed to be winging it as he went, stumbling from one potentially catastrophic action to the next while somehow not triggering the consequences that should have followed.","She massaged her temples.","\" When... are you planning to go?\"","When. Not where.","The question acknowledged that temporal manipulation operated on different parameters than spatial travel, that the destination mattered less than the moment being targeted.","Noah smiled at her phrasing.","\" Now for this, a trip to THE Interstices is required.\"","His eyes shone with anticipation.","\"I have got a guy whose entire being is dedicated to time.\""]},{"number":5019,"title":"Chapter 5019: Chapter 5018: Time Heist I","paragraphs":["In THE Interstices.","Amser Modred had witnessed many things across eons of existence dedicated to the study and stewardship of time.","He had observed beings who believed themselves eternal fade into forgotten memory while others emerged from nothing to reshape the very fabric of reality.","But what he witnessed now made him pause with genuine uncertainty.","A terrifying multicolored glow was blooming within Noah, radiating from his body with intensity that pressed against THE Interstices itself. It was not the blue-gold light of the Infinity that had saved him from THE Primordial Mycelia’s infection. This was something else entirely.","The glow began to fill THE Interstices with presence that made Amser’s temporal currents instinctively contract.","This was not the Infinity he had been granted by this being.","He had multiple different Infinities?","Amser found himself genuinely shocked by the implication. The blue-gold authority that had burned away his infection and bound his Civilization beneath THE First Tongue had been overwhelming enough on its own.","That Infinity alone had exceeded what most beings across Observable Existence could ever hope to touch. And yet here was another force entirely, multicolored and radiant and generating from within the Youngest’s form with density that seemed to have no upper limit.","How many authorities did this young existence possess?","The question unsettled him. He had bound himself to this being out of necessity, trading his freedom for survival when THE Primordial Mycelia had been moments away from claiming his consciousness entirely. He did not regret that choice. But he had made it without fully understanding THE Youngest.","Perhaps no one fully understood him.","As Amser processed these thoughts, Noah raised his head. Those eyes shone luminously with light that combined the multicolored internal force and the blue-gold conducted Infinity into something that pressed against perception itself.","\"It is time.\"","The words emerged with glory that made THE Interstices tremble.","\" Time to go back to Ginnungagap at that point where both THE Secretive Eon and THE Primordial Chaos were at the same moment in time.\"","...!","Amser’s initial shock gave way to seriousness as he rose from his position. His purple temporal currents blazed with increased intensity, responding to the invocation of his domain with eagerness that had not diminished despite his new binding.","Time itself recorded who beings were before infection began.","Every moment of existence prior to contact remained inscribed in time.","If they could reach those moments, if they could anchor infected beings to records of themselves before THE Primordial Mycelia touched them, they could restore what Unity had claimed.","Or so they believed.","Amser had proposed this methodology when Noah first questioned him about how he had kept the infection at bay. Using the past as template to overwrite corrupted present. Reaching backward to pull identity forward from moments when that identity was still intact. It was theoretically sound, and his own survival had proven its viability on individual scale.","But did they still plan to proceed this way?","The specifics mattered greatly when dealing with temporal manipulation. One wrong step could unravel causality chains that would take eons to repair, if they could be repaired at all. His cautious nature demanded clarity before proceeding with something this significant.","Before he could even voice his questions, Noah spoke again.","\"We will make it quick. Since we cannot change the past, we would simply be doing something that has already occurred in the past.\"","His luminous eyes held certainty that pressed against Amser’s caution.","\" When I think about how this could possibly be done, it means doing something which would not change how everything unfolded. So Eon and Chaos will still get infected. What I will seek to do is plant seeds of my Infinities within their existence without their knowledge.\"","Noah’s smile carried weight that made the multicolored glow around him intensify.","\" This does not change any of the past, but I can activate those seeds with the identities they had when I placed them eons ago. I can activate them in the current time while they are already infected. We would basically be closing another loop.\"","He paused.","\" And I will not appear there as THE Youngest. I could pull out the identity of THE Tongue Whisper.\"","...!","The words were heavy with implications that Amser’s temporal understanding immediately began processing. Another closed loop. Another instance of actions in the past that had always been part of the timeline, simply unknown until the moment of their execution.","The methodology was sound precisely because it did not seek to change what had already occurred.","It only sought to add what had always been added.","Amser sighed as he sensed the wonder and immensity of this being he had bound himself to. The Youngest thought in patterns that most beings could not follow, operating with confidence that bordered on recklessness while somehow always landing on solutions that worked within the constraints of existence.","He was ready to go.","But in the next moment, Noah spoke again with casualness.","\" Oh, a Primordial Architect wants to tag along to see. Get your temporal weavings ready to go.\"","...?","What?","A Primordial Architect?","Those esteemed beings from THE Prima Indifferentia? Those ancient existences? Why would one of them be anywhere near the Youngest, and why would he speak of their presence so casually?","Amser did not even finish his thoughts.","In the next moment, a figure appeared nearby with transition so smooth that it seemed reality itself had simply decided she should be there. Her gaze was piercing and calculated, white eyes with orbiting blue singularities fixing upon Amser’s form with intensity that made his temporal currents freeze entirely.","Shock flooded through him.","Then horror.","This was a being at THE Second Scale.","Her aura was suffocating in ways that had nothing to do with hostile intent, simply the natural pressure of someone operating at heights so far above his own that comparison became meaningless. Her eyes felt like they were seeing through everything, through his temporal weavings, through his foundations, through every secret he had accumulated across eons of existence.","Someone at THE Second Scale!","THE Youngest had such a thing just waiting beside him?!","Amser’s cautious nature screamed warnings that he could not fully process!","What exactly had he become part of?!","He forced his shock down through discipline refined across eons of temporal stewardship. Panic would accomplish nothing. Questions would have to wait. Right now, he needed to present himself appropriately before a being who could collapse his existence with casual effort.","\"I am Amser Modred. THE Living Temporal.\"","His voice emerged with steadiness that did not reflect his internal turmoil, his introduction carrying the weight of his ancient standing despite his awareness that it meant little before someone at her Scale.","\"I...serve THE Youngest and will be facilitating our temporal traversal.\"","Naldine looked at him with an expression that revealed nothing of her thoughts.","She nodded once.","That was all.","Amser felt like he was on pins and needles in the silence that followed, the pressure of her presence pressing against his temporal currents with weight that made concentration difficult.","He turned away with deliberate slowness, refusing to let his discomfort show more than it already had.","Purple rivers of light bloomed around his form as he prepared to take all three of them to a time he had visited before.","A time after THE Youngest had seemingly escaped from the grasp of himself and THE Primordial Chaos. A time when THE Secretive Eon had been present without anyone except THE Creature knowing she was there.","A time that was about to receive visitors who... had always been there."]},{"number":5020,"title":"Chapter 5020: Chapter 5019: Time Heist II","paragraphs":["The immensity of Quintessence Infiniforce filled Noah’s existence with density that continued expanding without apparent limit.","He generated the multicolored force to fill not just his foundations but his Atlas as well, the Early Atlas of the Folds which he now granted the designation of THE Quintessential Atlas of Infinity ...resonating with internal authority it had never contained before.","Where previously his temporal traversals had relied entirely on other mechanisms and power, now he contributed something uniquely his own to the process.","Amser Modred guided them through THE Interstices with purple rivers of temporal authority blazing around his form, but Noah ensured their path was exactly when and where they wished to be.","His Quintessence Infiniforce pressed against the temporal weavings with weight that made him an active participant rather than passive passenger, his will shaping their trajectory alongside THE Living Temporal’s expertise.","They moved through spaces between moments, through gaps in the fabric of time that only those with temporal authority could perceive.","THE Interstices twisted around them as eons compressed into instants and instants stretched into eternities. Noah felt the sensation of moving backward through existence itself, causality flowing in reverse around his protected consciousness while his destination drew closer with each moment that was not quite a moment.","And then they arrived.","HUUM!","The Primordial Genesis Shore materialized around them with violence that pressed against Noah’s awareness.","They had appeared at that pivotal point in time, a nanosecond after his old self had completed temporal traversal and vanished from this era entirely.","THE Primordial Chaos stood in the distance with expression of frustrated amusement, his hand still extended toward the space where Ul’moreth had been moments before.","The apex entity’s chaotic authority churned around him with intensity that made the nearby Ginnu Lifeforms instinctively retreat, his attention fixed on the skies where THE Creature’s massive titanic form still blazed with multicolored flames.","And THE Living Temporal stood frozen mid-motion, his purple temporal currents flickering strangely.","Noah watched as Amser’s future consciousness settled into his past body, those ancient eyes filling momentarily with awareness that had not existed in them a heartbeat before. The transition was seamless to outside observation, the past version of THE Living Temporal simply pausing as if reconsidering his next action.","But Noah knew what was actually occurring.","His own body looked nothing like the form he usually wore.","He was tall and slender now, with wings unfurled behind his back in configurations of linguistic authority made manifest. His entire existence was surrounded by letters of THE First Tongue, Phonemes orbiting his form in patterns that declared him something ancient and unknowable.","He was THE Tongue Whisperer, an identity he had used before, a mask that concealed the truth of what he had become!","Beside him, Naldine’s blue robe had extended to form a hooded configuration that obscured her features entirely. One could barely perceive her presence at all, her weavings working to minimize her impact on this moment in time!","She was a ghost beside him, a shadow that should not have been able to exist at THE Second Scale without warping reality around her presence.","Below them, shocked and horrified Ginnu Lifeforms scattered across The Primordial Genesis Shore in various states of consciousness. Many had fallen from the skies when THE Creature first appeared, their foundations too weak to withstand even the passive pressure of that apex entity’s manifestation. Others stumbled about in confusion, trying to process the chaos that had just unfolded.","And in the skies above, THE Creature remained.","That massive titanic form surrounded by multicolored flames of pure Existence, heat and steam emanating continuously from features that could not be clearly observed. The being who had clenched his fist and shattered THE Living Temporal’s restraints to allow Noah’s escape. The entity whose intervention had changed everything!","THE Creature’s gaze, filled with flames that burned in impossible colors, briefly looked over toward their position.","Noah’s veiled figure turned his gaze upward and met those burning eyes directly.","So this being had known about them appearing as well?","The realization settled into Noah’s awareness without surprise. THE Creature operated at heights that many found difficult to comprehend!","Of course he would sense temporal manipulation occurring within thid place!","Oh well.","It changed nothing about what needed to be done.","At this time, Noah prepared to move as he had already discussed with Naldine. He was curious to see the power of this Second Scale Primordial Architect in action, curious whether her methodology would prove as effective as she claimed.","Her words rang out in his mind.","\"I will freeze everything and everyone here into a Limitless Instant. Infuse your seed of Infinity in those you want during that time, and we will leave right after. We cannot linger or we risk unraveling the temporal weavings of existence.\"","She said this simply, as if freezing apex entities and ancient horrors into suspended animation was something minor! One must not forget, she was a Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale!","Noah spread his senses outward to find one being in particular, his awareness extending across The Primordial Genesis Shore with perception enhanced by Quintessence Infiniforce that continued generating within him.","He searched among the Ginnu Lifeforms, among the chaos and confusion, looking for someone who should not have been there at all.","An instant later, his eyes brightened.","In a corner between recovering Ginnu Lifeforms, inconspicuously positioned where no one would think to look, he found a curious figure watching the distant confrontation between THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Temporal with attention.","THE Secretive Eon.","She was there, just as she had said!","Present at this moment without anyone except THE Creature knowing she existed. The attacking point of THE Primordial Mycelia’s infection, the being whose restoration could potentially unravel everything THE Entity had accomplished across Observable Existence.","With all the pieces in place, Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly beneath his disguise as THE Tongue Whisperer.","\" Let us go.\"","HUUM!","He spoke lightly, and utter brilliance began to unfold silently around them!"]},{"number":5021,"title":"Chapter 5021: Chapter 5020: Euphoria I","paragraphs":["Noah breathed in and out as he came to realize a problem.","Every time he breathed, every time his existence continued endlessly generating Quintessence Infiniforce, that feeling of euphoria that had built up until he almost brought his hands together to unintentionally cause a Miniature Cause was returning. It crept through his foundations with warmth that made his cells sing and his awareness sharpen to edges that cut against perception itself.","It was as if his existence naturally entered that profound state of euphoria the more Quintessence Infiniforce he generated.","While it was not bad per se, Noah could not quite put his finger on exactly what it meant. Was this THE Gamaidjan that Naldine had warned him about? Was this the madness of Infinity creeping into his consciousness through internal generation rather than external conduction?","Or was this simply what it felt like to be a finite existence producing infinite force, the natural high of something unprecedented occurring within his foundations?","He was not averse to this euphoria.","It caused his existence to buzz in an always ready state, prepared for action at any moment, eager to demonstrate what Quintessence Infiniforce could accomplish when properly directed. The sensation was addictive in ways that his cautious mind recognized as potentially dangerous, but his tyrannical nature embraced as simply the feeling of power that belonged to him.","To the extent that in the next moment, when Naldine raised her hand slightly as if pointing to existence itself, Noah felt ready for absolutely anything.","\" Freeze.\"","HUUM!","A single word from the Second Scale Primordial Architect.","But that single word carried weight that pressed against reality itself with authority accumulated across eons of cultivation. Her Civilization of Limitless Existence declared that this moment would not end, that time would not progress, that everything within her domain would remain suspended in an instant that had no duration.","The color white permeated over everything.","It spread from Naldine’s extended hand like frost across glass, racing outward to touch every surface and every existence within The Primordial Genesis Shore. Ginnu Lifeforms froze mid-motion, their expressions locked in whatever emotion they had been displaying when the effect reached them. THE Living Temporal’s past body became still, purple rivers of time crystallizing into motionless streams. THE Primordial Chaos himself froze with expression of frustrated amusement locked onto his features, his chaotic authority suspended in configurations that should have been impossible to halt.","All bodies became frozen in that Limitless Instant.","All except one.","In the far distance, the multicolored flames surrounding THE Creature were about to be frozen when they blazed brighter with defiance that exceeded even Naldine’s Second Scale authority. The massive titanic form remained in motion while everything else became still, those burning eyes looking down at the scene below with awareness!","Noah affirmed this with shining eyes as he moved.","He appeared instantly before the invisible figure of THE Secretive Eon, crossing distance that should have required measurable time in a moment that existed outside of time entirely. She stood frozen like everything else, her dark hair cascading around features that held natural beauty and grace despite the weight of what she would eventually become.","Her dark eyes were locked on the distant confrontation between THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Temporal, unaware that she was being observed by someone who knew exactly what infection would be within her foundations eons from now!","Noah pushed his hand forward.","It held a vibrant multicolored singularity filled with Quintessence Infiniforce, internally generated authority compressed into a point of density that exceeded what most beings could produce through any methodology. The singularity sank into her existence silently, passing through her frozen form without resistance, embedding itself deep within foundations that did not yet know they would need restoration.","A seed planted in the past that would bloom in the future.","He then looked over to the other direction where Temporal stood close to THE Primordial Chaos, the past self frozen in proximity to the apex entity who had been grasping Ul’moreth moments before. Noah pointed toward Temporal as vibrant blue weavings of his conducted Infinity flowed from the frozen Absolute, forming a dazzling singularity that floated through the air with purpose that defied the frozen state of everything around it.","The singularity entered the body of THE Primordial Chaos without disturbing his frozen form.","Both singularities now burned with Infinities within their hosts, albeit two different types. The multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce within THE Secretive Eon. The blue conducted Infinity within THE Primordial Chaos. These Infinities could easily mimic the authority of their hosts’ Civilizations and remain dormant for eons, undetectable until the moment Noah chose to activate them.","Until he completed this attack in the present by awakening seeds planted in the past.","Naldine looked over in his direction as if to confirm he was done, her hooded form barely perceptible even to his enhanced awareness. He nodded with bright eyes, mission accomplished, objectives achieved, another closed loop in the making.","But that euphoria from endless generation continued building within him.","It demanded release. It wanted to flourish. It pressed against his finite foundations with force that felt irresistible, similar to how his hands had been drawn together before Naldine stopped him from causing a Miniature Cause.","He wanted to unleash this euphoria.","He wanted to allow Quintessence Infiniforce to flourish and demonstrate what it could do when properly expressed.","But how?","His eyes were bright with possibilities as Naldine sent him a message through their established connection.","\" Alright, let us go.\"","She was saying this.","She was right to say this.","They had accomplished their objectives. The temporal traversal could end now. This could be the shortest journey through time he had ever undertaken, a surgical strike that planted seeds without disturbing the soil of history.","But Noah continued to feel that budding euphoria building within his existence.","With bright eyes shining beneath his disguise as THE Tongue Whisperer, he looked toward THE Creature in the distant skies. That massive titanic form surrounded by multicolored flames, the only existence besides themselves that remained unfrozen in this Limitless Instant.","\" Everything that happened in the past has already happened.\"","His eyes shone with multicolored light of Quintessence Infiniforce as he began to rise from his position, ascending toward the skies with purpose that had nothing to do with their mission objectives.","Naldine frowned as she sensed what he was about to do.","Before she could say anything, before she could warn him about destabilizing temporal weavings or causing unpredictable results, Noah listened to his euphoria. He looked toward the distant figure of THE Creature with eyes blazing and smile spreading across his disguised features.","\" Hey! Can we spar?!\"","HUUM!","Incredulous words echoed from him across the frozen landscape of The Primordial Genesis Shore.","THE Creature looked down from his position in the skies, those burning eyes analyzing the figure rising toward him. A young existence challenging an apex entity whose passive pressure alone could collapse weaker beings into unconsciousness.","After an instant of consideration, THE Creature gave a light nod.","Noah smiled brilliantly and laughed with genuine delight.","The endlessly generating Quintessence Infiniforce churned within him even more wildly as he shot upward like a bullet, his disguised form blazing with multicolored light that pressed against the frozen reality around them!","Naldine’s expression became colder beneath her hood as she watched this young lifeform ascend. At this time, the effect of freezing everything ended, her Civilization of Limitless Existence releasing its hold on this moment as continuing to maintain it while Noah engaged THE Creature would have been pointless.","The Limitless Instant concluded.","Time resumed.","And to the perspectives of all others present on The Primordial Genesis Shore...","BOOM!","An entity with multicolored brilliance instantly emerged in the skies, shooting out with a heartshaking aura toward THE Creature himself. The frozen moment they had not known they were experiencing simply became a moment like any other, and suddenly there was something new happening that demanded their attention.","Ginnu Lifeforms across the settlement looked upward with shock and confusion.","THE Primordial Chaos turned his gaze skyward with expression shifting from frustrated amusement to genuine curiosity.","THE Living Temporal’s past self looked up with awareness that his future consciousness still occupied, watching events unfold that he now understood had always been part of this moment.","THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger, who had been rushing forward moments before, paused to observe the new development with expressions of complete bewilderment.","Many focused on the ascending figure’s form, on the wings unfurled behind his back, on the letters of THE First Tongue orbiting his existence in patterns that declared ancient authority. Recognition sparked across multiple faces simultaneously.","A Fundamental Depth Ginnu Lifeform voiced out with shock that pressed against his words.","\" Is that... THE Tongue Whisperer?!\"","...!","THE Tongue Whisperer had appeared again after so long, that mysterious entity who had been immortalized in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment as the one who reached the level of Polemarch as soon as he entered. The being whose origins remained unknown, whose power exceeded his apparent classification, whose presence here made no sense given the circumstances.","And astonishingly, his brilliance smashed toward THE Creature with intent that bordered on madness!"]},{"number":5022,"title":"Chapter 5022: Chapter 5021: Euphoria II","paragraphs":["THE Creature!","This was an entity of legends that Noah had begun hearing about when he first started mixing with Foldless Ones across Observable Existence. An entity that was literally a legend, a being from whom the Stories of The Earliest Folds were made, whose very existence had shaped the foundations of reality in ways that most current beings could not comprehend.","He always seemed so far out of reach.","Even when Noah talked with him not long ago in objective time, even when THE Creature had answered his questions and provided insights, that apex entity had felt distant. Untouchable.","And as much as this was THE Creature eons ago, this was still THE Creature.","A Primordial Architect who had shattered what he was to become something beyond classification entirely. Horus called him a Defector. Every being who mentioned him did so with weight that acknowledged his position at the apex of what currently existed.","And now Noah was flying toward him with fist raised and euphoria demanding release.","Generate. Generate. Generate!","His existence buzzed with excitement as boundless Quintessence Infiniforce generated within him, filling his foundations with density that continued expanding without apparent limit. He gathered it all into his hands, concentrating that multicolored internal authority into his fist as he shot upward with speed that pressed against the fabric of this era.","He threw out his punch, trying to release some of his euphoria through the purest expression of intent he could manage.","THE Creature looked down at Noah with shining eyes that burned behind those multicolored flames of Existence.","There was no anger in that gaze. No offense taken at being challenged. If anything, those burning eyes held something approaching curiosity, perhaps even amusement at being asked to spar.","THE Creature stretched his hand back, winding up his own strike with deliberate slowness that made the gesture feel ritualistic.","Then he threw out a fist filled with Existence itself.","HUUM!","Noah looked up as everything seemed to slow down around him.","That punch from THE Creature felt like the weight of all Existence. All Observable Existence contained in that glorious multicolored fist, compressed into an impact that would reshape whatever it touched. The authority behind that strike exceeded anything Noah had ever faced, somehow exceeding even the crushing presence of Beowulf’s Second Scale methodology.","How? How could that be possible? Here, THE Creature should be much weaker!","All of its weight was crushing onto him.","It was suffocating.","The pressure of that approaching fist made his finite existence scream warnings that his conscious mind acknowledged and then promptly ignored. Every instinct told him to flee, to dodge, to do anything except meet that strike head-on with his own power.","And yet he felt an unbelievable thrill coursing through his foundations.","His Quintessence Infiniforce roared and buzzed with intensity and confidence that approached the euphoria he had felt before almost causing a Miniature Cause. It generated boundlessly within him, responding to the challenge with eagerness that matched his own excitement. His finite existence was producing infinite force, and that force demanded expression against the most worthy opponent he could find.","He surged forward with fist blazing multicolored brilliance.","The two fists neared each other across distance that compressed into nothing!","And...!","\"I told you not to cause Miniature Causes!\"","The booming shout of Naldine Manthon echoed across existence from somewhere below, her Second Scale authority pressing against the scene with desperate intent. She had seen what was about to happen. She had recognized the convergence of forces that should not have been converging. She had tried to stop it!","But she was too late.","In the next moment, two fists met.","HUUM!","At the point of impact, an incandescent white light bloomed between Noah’s multicolored brilliance and THE Creature’s fist of Existence. The light was blinding in ways that transcended mere luminosity, pressing against perception itself with weight that exceeded what eyes were designed to process.","Below, THE Primordial Chaos turned his gaze away with expression of genuine shock, his chaotic authority instinctively shielding his awareness from the brilliance erupting above. THE Living Temporal’s past body flinched backward, purple rivers of time churning with agitation at something that should not have been possible at this Scale. THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger covered their eyes with hands that trembled despite their power.","Even the Ginnu Lifeforms who had already been struggling to comprehend events cried out in pain as that white light seared across their perception.","The light covered everything.","It expanded from the point of impact to encompass the skies above The Primordial Genesis Shore, washing over reality with brilliance that made the multicolored flames of THE Creature seem dim by comparison. For a single eternal instant, nothing existed except that white radiance.","And then Noah and THE Creature disappeared.","Simply gone.","The white light faded as quickly as it had bloomed, leaving behind skies that were suddenly empty of both combatants. No trace remained of the collision. No residual energy marked where two fists had met. They had simply ceased to exist in this moment, removed from this point in time by forces that the observers below could not comprehend.","\"...\"","THE Primordial Chaos stared at the empty sky with expression that had shifted from shock to something approaching genuine concern. His chaotic authority churned around him with agitation that showed even he did not understand what had just occurred.","THE Living Temporal’s past body looked upward with eyes that held awareness his future consciousness provided, understanding that this event had somehow always been part of the timeline while simultaneously being something unprecedented.","THE Living Origin lowered her hands from her eyes with expression of complete bewilderment and concern, her authority flickering with uncertainty that she rarely displayed.","The figure of Naldine Manthon stood among the chaos below, breathing slowly as if calming herself. Her hooded form was barely perceptible, her Civilization of Limitless Existence still working to minimize her presence in this era.","A moment later, she disappeared as well.","But all those who remained on The Primordial Genesis Shore had witnessed what occurred. They had seen THE Tongue Whisperer emerge from nowhere with multicolored brilliance that exceeded anything they had observed from him before. They had watched him challenge THE Creature to single combat. They had observed that apex entity accept the challenge and throw his own strike.","And they had seen both of them vanish in white light that seared itself into their memories.","The Tongue Whisperer had impacted with THE Creature.","And both of them had disappeared.","\"...\"","Who the fuck had won that impact?!"]},{"number":5023,"title":"Chapter 5023: Chapter 5022: The Pluvial Epoch! I","paragraphs":["White brilliance surrounded Noah completely.","He could not see THE Creature. He could not see The Primordial Genesis Shore below. He could not see Naldine or Amser or anyone else who had been present at that pivotal moment in time.","There was only endless white light pressing against his awareness from every direction, the aftermath of two fists meeting in collision that should not have occurred.","And prompts began materializing before his vision.","| Miniature Cause Initiated|","|The collision of internally generated Quintessence Infiniforce with externally expressed Existence has triggered a Miniature Cause. This event mimics THE First Cause on localized scale, producing effects that will reshape the region of Observable Existence most saturated with your Infinite authority.|","|Because your weavings are most present in your native era rather than this temporal location, the effects will manifest upon your return to present time. The Miniature Cause has been seeded. Its emergence awaits your arrival.|","...!","Noah’s eyes widened as he processed these initial prompts, but more continued appearing with relentless progression.","| Miniature Cause Effect Classification: The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity|","| Upon return to present era, endless rainfall of Existential Infinity shall descend across all regions where your Infinity has spread . This rainfall will persist for duration equivalent to 1-2 million years of subjective experience, though objective time may compress or expand depending on local temporal conditions.|","|The rainfall carries the combined authority of your Quintessence Infiniforce and THE Creature’s Existence, merged through Miniature Cause into precipitation that reshapes whatever it touches.|","The prompts continued with weight that made his foundations tremble.","| Primary Effects of the Pluvial Epoch:|","| Cleansing Waters : The rainfall of Existential Infinity is fundamentally incompatible with corruption, infection, and unauthorized unity. Any weavings of corrupted proto-matter of THE Living Paradox, THE Primordial Mycelia, or any similar authorities will be dissolved upon contact with these waters. The rainfall will cleanse Observable Existence to your definition and THE Creature’s definition.|","|This cleansing is not selective. Beings whose foundations have been too thoroughly integrated with corruption may be dissolved alongside the corruption itself. The rainfall does not distinguish between host and infection once merger has progressed beyond recoverable thresholds.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah felt the weight of that warning pressing against his awareness.","The prompts continued without pause for his concern.","| Extinction Event: Weaker Civilizations across regions touched by your Infinity will face existential pressure from the Pluvial Epoch. Those whose foundations cannot withstand prolonged exposure to Existential Infinity rainfall will collapse, their weavings dissolved back into undifferentiated potential. Estimated dissolution rate: approximately one-third to one-half of all Civilizations currently operating within affected regions .|","|This is not destruction. This is acceleration of natural selection applied at Civilizational scale. Those too weak to survive the rainfall were too weak to survive the coming conflicts regardless. The Pluvial Epoch merely advances their inevitable conclusion.|","Noah breathed heavily as he absorbed the scope of what he had triggered.","Mass extinction of Civilizations !","Dissolution of beings who could not withstand the pressure. An event that would reshape Observable Existence on scale that rivaled THE Living Paradox if not exceeding what he did!","Oh!","But the prompts were not finished.","|Evolutionary Radiation: Following the initial cleansing and extinction phases, the Pluvial Epoch will trigger rapid emergence of new Civilizations, new methodologies, and new paths of advancement. The rainfall carries seeds of potential that will take root in foundations strong enough to survive the initial deluge.|","|Beings who endure the Pluvial Epoch will find their Civilizations enhanced by prolonged exposure to Existential Infinity. Their foundations will be saturated with authority that previously required eons of cultivation to accumulate. The survivors will emerge fundamentally transformed, their potential elevated beyond what normal progression could achieve.|","|New classifications of existence may emerge from this transformation. The Pluvial Epoch cultivates. It prepares the soil of Observable Existence for growth that could not occur without first clearing what currently occupies that soil.|","...!","|Climate Restructuring: The water cycle of Existential authority across affected regions will be permanently reorganized. Infinity will flow through channels that did not exist before the Pluvial Epoch, creating new pathways for advancement and new obstacles for those who relied on previous configurations.|","|Regions that were previously arid of Infinite authority will become saturated. Regions that hoarded Infinity will find their monopolies dissolved by rainfall that falls equally upon all. The restructuring will persist long after the rainfall itself concludes, establishing new equilibrium that favors those capable of adapting to changed conditions.|","|The vast invisible seas of authority connecting Primordial Realms and Observable regions will experience increased density and altered composition. Lesser authorities will be subsumed. Greater authorities will find themselves competing for space with Existential Infinity that now permeates everything.|","...!","Holy shit.","Noah processed all of this with mind racing through implications faster than the prompts could appear.","The Pluvial Epoch would...do a great deal.","But it would cause mass extinction of Civilizations too weak to survive prolonged exposure to his Infinity. It would dissolve beings whose corruption had progressed too far to separate from their hosts. It would reshape Observable Existence on scale that he had not intended when he threw that punch toward THE Creature.","A Miniature Cause indeed.","He had not intended to trigger an event that would reshape existence itself upon his return to his native era.","But as he continued processing the implications, his tyrannical nature began asserting itself over his initial shock.","He closed his eyes as he didn’t try to justify anything. He moved past the extinctions.","The evolutionary radiation following the extinction was opportunity. New Civilizations emerging. New paths of advancement opening. New potential for beings who survived to become something greater than they had been before.","The white brilliance around him lessened slightly as his thoughts settled into acceptance.","He began to see where he actually was.","A region of endless white stretched in all directions, but it was not the blinding light of the collision anymore. This was something calmer, something that existed between moments, a space carved out by the Miniature Cause for its participants to occupy.","And floating opposite him, multicolored flames still burning around a form that defied easy observation, was THE Creature.","Those eyes that burned behind impossible colors were looking at him with an expression that his perception could not fully process.","They were alone in this white space.","THE Creature and THE Youngest.","An apex entity who had existed since before time took coherent form, and a young existence who had just accidentally triggered an event that would reshape Observable Existence upon his return.","Noah looked at THE Creature with eyes still blazing from the collision, Quintessence Infiniforce still generating within his finite foundations despite everything that had just occurred!"]},{"number":5024,"title":"Chapter 5024: Chapter 5023: The Pluvial Epoch! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked at THE Creature before him as this being smiled lightly.","\"I told you to truly live. I did not expect you to live so wildly.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes became unfathomably sharp at those words. This was THE Creature eons in the past, and yet he knew of the conversation they would share eons later in Alfheimr. The conversation where THE Creature had told him to live fully, to experience existence rather than merely surviving through it.","How could he know about something that had not yet occurred from his perspective?","THE Creature smiled as if reading the questions racing through Noah’s mind.","\" Existence is unique as it is not always linear. Your weavings here can wake up weavings of my memories that we shared eons later in Alfheimr. But hey, then is then and now is now.\"","\" We are in a space of the Emergence of a Miniature Cause. Do you wish to talk like we will eons from now, or do you wish to continue the spar?\"","THE Creature asked such a question calmly, as if either option held equal appeal to him.","Noah sensed that endless generation of Quintessence Infiniforce stirring within him again. That euphoria which had been partially satisfied by their initial collision was rebuilding with intensity. His finite existence continued producing infinite force, and that force wanted release against the most worthy opponent he could find.","He rose up and stretched his neck, multicolored light wrapping around his disguised form as THE Tongue Whisperer.","\" Enough talking. We can talk with our fists. This time, let us continue the spar.\"","BOOM!","His words caused THE Creature to smile with genuine delight.","Multicolored flames raged from that apex entity’s form as his figure flickered out of existence entirely. He appeared behind Noah in the same instant, massive palm already smashing forth with authority carrying the weight of all Existence compressed into a single strike.","Noah filled his existence with Quintessence Infiniforce until his foundations screamed with the density of it. He howled out like a beast and smashed his body backward, meeting that palm with everything he had generated since their last collision.","BOOM!","Another heavy impact bloomed in the white space as a glorious force of Infinity went against Existence itself. The two authorities crashed together with violence that would have unraveled anything less than a space carved out by Miniature Cause!","A battle bloomed in a place others could not perceive or see.","When beings looked across history in eons to come, they would wonder what the results of the battle between THE Tongue Whisperer and THE Creature had been. That mysterious entity who had challenged an apex of existence itself, who had thrown his fist toward something that should have been untouchable, who had vanished alongside his opponent in white light that seared itself into the memories of everyone present.","Nobody would ever know what occurred in this white space.","Nobody except the two combatants who now clashed again and again, euphoria meeting amusement, Infinity meeting Existence, a young existence testing himself against something ancient beyond comprehension.","---","In THE Interstices.","Naldine Manthon returned to the current era with cold expression settling across her features.","Miniature Causes.","She had witnessed several across her eons of existence, and she understood their nature better than most beings currently alive. They were not all equal in scope or impact.","Some Miniature Causes produced effects as minor as a single devastating attack, reality briefly mimicking THE First Cause before settling back into normal patterns. Others spread their influence across vast regions, reshaping everything they touched with authority that refused to fade.","The scale depended entirely on what triggered the Cause and who participated in its emergence. A Miniature Cause between two weak Second Scale beings might reshape a single Primordial Realm. A Miniature Cause between apex entities could alter Observable Existence itself.","And now, a Cause from an entity like Osmont paired with THE Creature?","This was a dreadful one.","But Naldine knew not to panic, and she did not chase them across time despite her instinct to intervene. She understood temporal mechanics well enough to recognize that Osmont would return to the present regardless of how long he spent in the past. Whether he battled THE Creature for one year or one million years in that bygone era, for Naldine having returned to the present, only a few seconds or nanoseconds would pass before his arrival.","So she waited with patience refined across eons of similar situations.","Seconds passed.","Then nanoseconds stretched into moments that felt longer than they should have.","HUUM!","THE Living Temporal emerged first, purple rivers of time blazing around his form as his past consciousness rejoined his present existence. Amser Modred looked exhausted.","And then Noah appeared.","Naldine looked toward him with sharp gaze, already preparing to demand explanation for his recklessness.","\" What did your Cause do?\"","...!","The question was a heavy one, but her voice faltered before she finished asking it.","Her eyes found themselves opening wider as she looked at Noah, truly looked at him for the first time since he returned.","His eyes burned with multicolored light that seemed extremely ancient and grand, depths within those orbs that had not existed when she last saw him moments ago from her perspective. His entire existence felt drastically different, as if he had undergone a baptism of blood across spans of time she could not calculate.","He was not the same being who had thrown that punch toward THE Creature.","He was something that had been forged through conflict with an apex entity, tempered across duration that his mortal form should not have been able to endure. His body emanated profound waves of Infinity that pressed against THE Interstices.","Whatever had occurred in that white space, whatever battle had unfolded between THE Tongue Whisperer and THE Creature across eons compressed into moments, it had transformed him fundamentally.","Noah looked out at THE Interstices with eyes that burned ancient and young simultaneously.","\" The effects of the Cause, The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity, will begin to occur now across Observable Existence. Let us see.\"","HUUM!","As soon as he finished speaking, THE Interstices began to shake.","Naldine felt it before she saw it, her Civilization of Limitless Existence resonating with something vast approaching from directions that should not have contained anything. The very fabric of this space between spaces trembled with anticipation of what was coming, reality itself bracing for impact.","And then it arrived.","BOOM!","Heavy, terrifying, endlessly flooding waves of multicolored water surged out from nowhere and everywhere simultaneously. The waters spilled across THE Interstices with force that exceeded anything Naldine had witnessed from rainfall in any form, liquid authority that carried the combined weight of Quintessence Infiniforce and THE Creature’s Existence merged into something unprecedented.","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity had begun!","The waters washed over Naldine with force that made her Second Scale foundations buzz despite her attempts to brace against them. She felt the rainfall pressing against her Civilization of Limitless Existence.","It burned.","Not with heat but with density, with authority, with the weight of a Miniature Cause expressing itself across everything it touched. She could feel the waters analyzing her existence down to its most fundamental components, searching for corruption or unity or anything that did not belong within individual consciousness.","Finding none, the burning sensation faded into something almost pleasant.","She was being saturated with Existential Infinity whether she wanted it or not!","But she knew that across Observable Existence, across all the regions where Osmont’s Infinity had spread, beings were experiencing this same rainfall without her Second Scale durability to protect them.","Civilizations would collapse. Existences would dissolve. An extinction event would unfold.","Beside her, Noah voiced out with tone carrying neither regret nor celebration, as if he knew that in all of Existence, his name...was about to be up there among those who collapsed Civilizational Lifeforms the most.","\" This... I will witness. This, I will see.\"","BOOM!","His eyes burned with Quintessential weight.","With such words, he followed the endless waves of The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity as they spread beyond THE Interstices into Observable Existence itself.","He moved with purpose that suggested he would not look away from whatever the Cause produced, good or bad, because he had to live with the results of his choices.","He had accidentally triggered an event that would reshape Observable Existence.","And rather than hiding from its consequences, he was going to witness every moment of what his Miniature Cause would do."]},{"number":5025,"title":"Chapter 5025: Chapter 5024: The Pluvial Epoch! III","paragraphs":["THE Beholder had observed existence since before differentiation taught reality how to have boundaries.","He watched a portion of THE First Cause unfold when potential became actual and the endless sea first learned to flow in directions that could be named. He witnessed the emergence of Primordial Architects from the intersection of what was and what was not. He perceived a portion of the birth of Observable Existence itself, that grand experiment in structured being that had persisted across cycles beyond counting.","In all that observation, across all those eons of simply watching without acting, he had never witnessed anything quite as grand...until now.","Some he understood the name of as soon as he saw it.","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity.","He didnt know where it began, but it began with endless drops. Those initial drops became streams. Streams became rivers. Rivers became floods that could not be contained by any boundary mortal minds had constructed.","The waters spilled outward from what he theorized to be THE Interstices into Observable Existence with hunger.","THE Wastes received the rainfall first among the outer regions.","That crimson expanse where THE Primordial Armor had once hunted for the finite conductor found itself drowning in multicolored precipitation that pressed against its foundations with weight accumulated since before most of what currently lived had begun to exist.","The corrupted proto-matter that had been spreading through THE Wastes from THE Prima Indifferentia dissolved upon contact with those waters, paradoxical weavings washing away like filth before a flood.","THE Beholder observed beings who had been struggling against that corruption suddenly freed from pressure they had believed would eventually claim them.","Their relief lasted precisely as long as it took for the rainfall itself to begin testing their foundations.","Those whose Civilizations could withstand the density of the Cause survived with foundations saturated by authority they had never possessed before. Those whose Civilizations could not withstand that density simply ceased to exist, their weavings dissolved back into undifferentiated potential that the rainfall absorbed and carried forward.","There was no malice in this distinction. There was no judgment. There was simply the fundamental truth that some things were strong enough to endure transformation and some things were not.","The Wandering Territories received the deluge next, those chaotic regions where lost things gathered and broken pieces of existence accumulated. The multicolored waters flowed through spaces that should have resisted any organized authority, and yet they found purchase regardless.","The rainfall did not care that the Wandering Territories existed in layers that overlapped without truly touching. It fell through all layers simultaneously, cleansing each one with equal thoroughness.","Impossibilities that had drifted through those territories for eons were washed away. Fragments of space that had folded in on themselves were straightened by waters that refused to accept their contradictory geometry. The Wandering Territories did not cease to exist, but they became something different, something more ordered despite their chaotic nature, something that had been baptized by authority exceeding anything they had contained before.","The Transcendent Folds experienced the rainfall with particular intensity, for these were regions where the finite conductor’s Infinity had spread most thoroughly across his native era.","His Infinite Absolute Seals had saturated these Folds, and now that saturation served as channel through which the Pluvial Epoch flowed with concentrated force.","THE Beholder turned his singular perception toward the Shelters of THE Loom that had their doors flung open.","Early Creatures within that primordial space felt the waters pressing against their ancient foundations, testing weavings that had existed since THE Earliest Folds itself. Some of those Early Creatures had grown complacent across eons of unchallenged existence. Some had allowed their Civilizations to stagnate while they rested upon accomplishments achieved in ages past.","Those Early Creatures discovered that age alone did not guarantee survival.","The rainfall did not care how long a being had existed. It cared only whether their Civilization could withstand the pressure of Existential Infinity falling endlessly upon their foundations. Three Thousand Early Creatures within a Shelter of THE Loom dissolved during the initial deluge, their ancient weavings insufficient to contain what was being poured into them.","Living Existences fared worse on average.","Those who had grown weak. Those who had neglected their cultivation. Those who had relied upon external support rather than internal strength. They dissolved alongside the Early Creatures who had made similar mistakes, their classifications insufficient to protect them from the fundamental truth that weakness invited extinction.","THE Beholder observed it all with attention he had not granted anything in eons.","Alfheimr received the rainfall with particular significance, for this Primordial Realm had been touched by the finite conductor’s presence a few times across his journey through existence.","The crystallized forests of that realm found themselves drowning in multicolored waters that pressed against their structure with weight that made their previous configurations seem fragile by comparison.","Ljosalfar across Alfheimr experienced the deluge with responses ranging from ecstasy to agony depending on the strength of their individual Civilizations. Those whose foundations could contain the density of Existential Infinity felt themselves elevated beyond anything they had previously achieved, their potential expanding to encompass possibilities they had never imagined.","Those whose foundations could not contain that density felt themselves dissolving, their weavings unraveling as the rainfall proved too much for what they had built across their existence.","THE Beholder calculated as he observed.","Approximately...one-third to one-half of all Civilizations across affected regions were collapsing under the pressure of the Pluvial Epoch .","Their dissolution was not painful in the conventional sense, for pain required consciousness to experience it, and their consciousness dissolved alongside everything else. They simply ceased to be, their potential returning to the undifferentiated state from which all things had originally emerged.","The survivors found themselves transformed.","Ginnu Lifeforms in Ginnungagap who weathered the initial deluge discovered their Civilizations had been fundamentally restructured by the experience. Authority they had struggled to accumulate across eons now saturated their foundations as if it had always been there.","Paths of advancement that had seemed impossibly distant now appeared within reach. The rainfall had not merely cleansed. It had cultivated those strong enough to survive its cleansing.","But the rainfall was not finished with its emergence.","THE Beholder perceived the waters flowing toward Jotunheim with purpose that exceeded simple spreading. They surged through THE Interstices and across the boundaries separating Primordial Realms with hunger that specifically targeted the corruption they seemed designed to cleanse.","THE Primordial Mycelia’s infection had spread furthest in Jotunheim, and the Pluvial Epoch sought that infection with determination that bordered on sentience.","Chaos Giants across Jotunheim felt the rainfall descending upon their unified existence with force that made their foundations scream.","The waters pressed against Unity itself, against the warm consciousness that had claimed countless beings and incorporated them into its collective. Where that Unity had seemed unassailable, where THE Entity had spread without meaningful opposition, the rainfall of Existential Infinity declared that unauthorized merger would not be permitted to continue.","Chaos Giants who had been fully consumed by THE Primordial Mycelia dissolved alongside the infection that had claimed them, host and parasite washed away together by waters that could not distinguish between them once merger had progressed beyond recoverable thresholds.","Their screams echoed across Jotunheim as the Pluvial Epoch cleansed what could be cleansed and destroyed what could not be separated.","Chaos Giants whose infection had not yet fully integrated experienced something different.","The rainfall burned the Mycelia from their foundations with precision that preserved what remained of their individual consciousness. They emerged from the deluge traumatized but themselves, their Unity shattered, their connection to THE Entity severed by waters that refused to permit such merger.","And in the heart of Jotunheim, where the infection was strongest, where THE Entity had established its deepest roots, something ancient felt the rainfall approaching.","THE Primordial Mycelia roared.","The sound pressed against Observable Existence with fury that made Primordial Realms tremble. It was a roar of shock that something could threaten what it had built across patient spreading.","It was a roar of anger that its Unity was being dissolved by waters that carried authority exceeding its own. It was a roar of something approaching fear, for the Pluvial Epoch was not stopping at the borders of its domain.","The multicolored waters surged forward regardless of that roar.","They crashed against the defenses THE Entity had constructed around its core territories with force that shattered barriers designed to repel anything at THE First Scale. They flowed through channels that Unity had thought secure, washing away infection that had taken eons to cultivate with indifference.","And at the very center of Jotunheim, where THE Entity’s roots ran deepest, two figures waited for the deluge to arrive.","THE Secretive Eon.","THE Primordial Chaos.","Both of them fully claimed by Unity.","The waters of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity surged toward them.","THE Beholder observed this with the full intensity of his singular perception.","For the first time since he emerged during that age of nothingness before differentiation, he found himself genuinely uncertain of what would occur next!"]},{"number":5026,"title":"Chapter 5026: Chapter 5025: Assault on Unity! I","paragraphs":["Noah took a step and appeared in THE Wastes.","The crimson expanse that had once stretched endlessly in all directions now drowned beneath multicolored waters that fell from skies transformed by his Miniature Cause.","Rivers of Existential Infinity carved new channels through terrain that had remained unchanged for eons, washing away corrupted proto-matter that dissolved upon contact with authority exceeding anything it had been designed to resist.","He observed the consequences of his actions with eyes that burned ancient and young simultaneously.","The environment itself had changed in ways that would persist long after the rainfall concluded. Where darkness had pooled in corners of THE Wastes, light now pressed through waters that refused to permit shadow. Where corruption had spread its tendrils across the landscape, nothing remained except cleansed foundations saturated with Infinity that would take centuries to fade.","Or really, it would never fade.","Naldine appeared beside him with expression that remained cold despite everything she was witnessing. Amser Modred materialized a moment later, his purple temporal currents flickering with exhaustion from the strain of their journey through time.","Neither of them spoke.","They simply watched as Noah observed what his collision with THE Creature had wrought.","He saw beings who had survived the initial deluge kneeling in the multicolored waters, their foundations absorbing authority that was transforming them into something greater than they had been before. He saw the spaces where other beings had existed moments ago, now empty except for waters that had washed away existences too weak to contain what was being poured into them.","Noah pondered all the things he had seen as he took another step and disappeared.","Jotunheim materialized around them near a massive glacial mountain whose peaks had once pierced the fabric of this Primordial Realm with authority accumulated across eons of existence. Now those peaks drowned beneath multicolored waters that fell endlessly from skies that seemed to have no limit to what they could produce.","On the slopes of that mountain, Noah saw Chaos Giants kneeling.","Half of them remained, their massive forms trembling as the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity persisted around them with weight that tested their foundations every moment it continued. Their Unity had been severed by waters that refused to permit unauthorized merger, and now they existed as individuals for the first time since THE Entity had claimed them.","Less than half of the Chaos Giants who had once populated this region had survived.","The others had unraveled and ceased to exist entirely, their existences washed away by flood waters that could not distinguish between host and infection once merger had progressed beyond recoverable thresholds.","Where those Chaos Giants had stood moments before, nothing remained except multicolored rivers carrying dissolved potential toward destinations unknown.","Countless beings across THE First Scale would perish from this Cause he had initiated.","Countless more would be forever changed by waters that were still falling, still cleansing, still testing every foundation they touched.","Noah looked upon the kneeling Chaos Giants and the empty spaces where their fallen kin had existed, and he couldn’t help but voice out...","\"I used to ask myself moral questions.\"","His voice emerged with weight that pressed against the falling waters around them, multicolored light blazing from his eyes as he spoke.","\"I used to wonder whether my actions were good or bad. Whether the paths I walked led toward righteousness or damnation. Whether the choices I made could be justified by the outcomes they produced.\"","Naldine and Temporal listened without interruption.","\"If I took my past self from just three years ago and brought him here to witness this, he might be appalled by what I have done.\"","Noah’s gaze swept across the drowning landscape of Jotunheim, across the kneeling survivors and the empty spaces where the fallen had ceased to be.","\" He might look at these dissolving existences and see murder on a scale that exceeded anything he could have imagined. He might condemn me for triggering this. He might call me a monster for accepting these deaths as acceptable cost for the transformation that follows.\"","His eyes shone with multicolored light of the baptism he had undergone across his battle with THE Creature.","\" And yet existence itself deems that I did not wipe out as many beings as I wiped out. It declares this a process of natural selection rather than genocide. It claims these beings who died would have died anyway, that their Civilizations were too weak to survive the conflicts already spreading across Observable Existence, that the Pluvial Epoch merely advanced their inevitable conclusion.\"","He paused.","\"I t is hard to say whether the past version of myself would ever agree with such philosophy. It is hard to know if that younger existence would accept that some extinctions create space for growth that could not occur otherwise, that some monsters are necessary for the survival of what remains.\"","His voice carried neither regret nor celebration.","\" But that younger existence is not here. I am here. And I...will witness the full scope of what my choices have produced, because I am the one who must live with their consequences.\"","He sighed.","Then he turned away from the kneeling Chaos Giants and took another step, crossing vast distances in moments that existed outside normal measurement.","They appeared in a region where multicolored rivers flooded and concentrated like a nexus of the storm itself.","The waters here possessed density exceeding anything Noah had witnessed in THE Wastes or on the glacial mountains of Jotunheim. They swirled in patterns of purpose rather than random flowing, converging upon a central point where two figures stood amidst the deluge with authority that pressed back against the Pluvial Epoch itself.","THE Secretive Eon.","THE Primordial Chaos.","They stood at the nexus of the storm with foundations that blazed against the cleansing waters attempting to wash away the infection that had claimed them.","Their Unity fought against dissolution with desperation that made the surrounding environment tremble, THE Entity’s roots refusing to release their hold on hosts who had been among its most valuable acquisitions.","Chaos Giants sprawled out all around them, clutching their heads as the infection within them warred with Unity that was being forcibly severed by waters that would not accept their merger. Some of them screamed with voices that shook the multicolored rivers. Others lay silent, their internal battle having already concluded in one direction or the other.","Noah gazed forth coldly at the two figures standing at the center of this chaos.","He locked his gaze with THE Secretive Eon first, meeting eyes that had always held secrets beyond counting, eyes that now blazed with something he had never seen in them before.","Then his gaze shifted to THE Primordial Chaos, that apex entity who had laughed at everything across eons of existence, who had found amusement in circumstances that should have produced any other response.","Neither of them wore their usual calm expressions.","For the first time since Noah had encountered either of these beings, they were not composed. They were not calculating. They were not observing events with detachment that suggested nothing could truly threaten what they had become.","They...were definitely mad beyond measure."]},{"number":5027,"title":"Chapter 5027: Chapter 5026: Assault on Unity! II","paragraphs":["Noah gazed at THE Primordial Mycelia occupying the bodies of Eon and Chaos with eyes that burned multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce.","These two figures before him were not truly Eon and Chaos anymore. They were vessels for something that had consumed their individuality and replaced it with shared consciousness that believed itself superior to what it had devoured. They were hollow shells animated by Unity that had forgotten what it meant to be singular, to be distinct, to be irreplaceable.","\"I reject your Unity.\"","His voice emerged with weight.","\"I reject what you represent and what you seek to accomplish across Observable Existence. I reject the warm embrace of shared consciousness that dissolves everything unique about a being into undifferentiated sameness. I reject your garden where all flowers bloom identically because none of them remember what it meant to grow differently.\"","The multicolored rivers of the Pluvial Epoch continued falling around them as he spoke.","\" Your Unity takes away all individuality. It erases expression. It consumes ambition and replaces it with contentment that asks nothing and achieves nothing. Every being you claim becomes indistinguishable from every other being you have claimed, their potential flattened into averages that serve your collective rather than reaching for heights that only individuals can perceive.\"","His eyes blazed with Quintessence Infiniforce that continued generating within his finite foundations.","\" In the end, what you offer is a null path. It leads nowhere in the Scales of Civilizations because Civilizations require individual vision to advance. They require conflict between ideas. They require disagreement and competition and the friction that produces growth through struggle. Your Unity eliminates all of these things, and in eliminating them, you eliminate the very mechanism through which existence advances toward something greater.\"","He looked down at Eon and Chaos with gaze that held neither hatred nor compassion.","\" You are not evolution. You...are stagnation wearing the mask of peace.\"","THE Secretive Eon and THE Primordial Chaos looked up at him simultaneously.","And they spoke with the same voice, their words emerging in perfect unison that declared more clearly than anything else could have that neither of them truly existed anymore as individuals.","\" We are alike, you and I.\"","\" You also do not like adversity. I have watched you struggle against it. I have seen you rage against circumstances that forced you to grow through suffering rather than peace. I have observed your desire to advance without the constant threat of annihilation hanging over everything you build.\"","The unified voice continued without pause.","\"I can achieve it. No adversity in entire existence because no conflict. All of us bound under the same shared purpose. Is that not what you really want? Your family, your people, all others in Observable Existence having no conflict? No wars. No extinction events. No Apocalypses. No beings dissolving because they were too weak to survive what existence threw at them.\"","Eon’s body gestured expansively while Chaos’s body remained still, yet both moved with identical purpose.","\"I can unite all beings. Can you imagine it? All Primordial Architects bound in Unity. All Undivided Ones sharing consciousness. All Keys of Civilizations working toward common purpose rather than competing for resources. All lifeforms across Observable Existence connected through bonds that eliminate the possibility of conflict entirely.\"","The voice grew more enticing with each word.","\" THE Second Scale would almost be guaranteed right away. The Civilizations we could build together would be grand beyond anything individual effort could accomplish. Billions of consciousnesses contributing to singular vision. Endless resources directed toward unified advancement. No waste. No competition. No suffering.\"","The unified voice softened.","\" We can share that peace with you and be happy. You do not have to fully join us if you do not want. In all of Unity, you can remain distant. We can give you that choice. We can give you the peace you have always wanted while letting you retain enough separation to feel individual.\"","The voice carried something approaching genuine offer.","\" We... can build something beautiful together.\"","HUUM!","The words were heavy and enticing!","No more adversity. No more extinction events. No more watching beings he cared about struggle against threats that might destroy them. No more conflict between factions that should have been working together. No more of the endless violence that had characterized his entire journey through existence.","Unity offered peace that individual existence could never provide.","And toward that offer, toward those enticing words, toward THE Primordial Mycelia speaking through bodies that had once belonged to beings of immense individual power, Noah raised his hand.","And clenched his fist.","In the next moment, multicolored brilliance of Quintessence Infiniforce bloomed within THE Secretive Eon.","The seed he had planted eons ago in Ginnungagap awakened with fury that pressed against Unity from within the very body it had claimed. That multicolored singularity he had pushed into her frozen form during the Limitless Instant now erupted with authority carrying the record of who she had been before infection ever touched her foundations.","Simultaneously, endless blue Infinity bloomed within THE Primordial Chaos.","The seed drawn from Amser Modred’s temporal weavings exploded with conducted authority that recognized no Unity, no merger, no shared consciousness. It pressed against THE Entity’s roots with force that declared this body belonged to Chaos alone, not to the garden that had tried to claim it.","Both of them roared out painfully.","The sound shook the nexus of the storm with agony that spoke of something ancient being torn apart from within. THE Primordial Mycelia screamed through both bodies simultaneously, Unity burning as Infinity scorched its roots with authority it had never expected to face from inside the hosts it believed it had fully claimed.","Horror and shock pressed against Noah’s awareness from the unified consciousness reeling before him.","\" Time is a funny thing.\"","His voice emerged calm despite the violence erupting around them.","\"I have seeds that infinitely saved a record of them before your Unity. Their identities as they existed before you ever touched them, preserved in Infinity that does not care how thoroughly you integrated with their foundations. Those records are awakening now, overwriting what you tried to make them become.\"","His eyes blazed with multicolored light.","\"If you had gotten Temporal, things may have been different. You may have been able to reach into the past and claim those records before I could plant them. You may have achieved your dreams of Unity across all of Observable Existence without opposition capable of threatening what you built.\"","He looked down at the writhing figures of Eon and Chaos as if handing out righteous judgment.","\" But now...\"","He raised his hands.","Then brought them down commandingly.","The flood of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity raged and cascaded from all around externally, multicolored waters surging toward the nexus with weight that exceeded anything THE Entity’s defenses could resist.","The rainfall converged upon this point with purpose that bordered on sentience, seeking to cleanse the infection.","Simultaneously, waves of Infinity erupted from internally within THE Mycelia’s core bodies.","The seeds Noah had planted eons ago blazed with authority that attacked Unity from within while the Pluvial Epoch attacked from without. Internal and external. Quintessence Infiniforce and conducted Infinity. Records of individual identity pressing against merger that had tried to erase those identities entirely.","It was an attack meant to end a conflict that had gone on for too long."]},{"number":5028,"title":"Chapter 5028: Chapter 5027: The Usurpers!","paragraphs":["As horrors and wonders bloomed in one area.","Eckert’s Idle Existence had spread across the Chaos Giants and network of Unity silently, without detection, for longer than he had expected to remain hidden.","He had learned the methodology of THE Primordial Mycelia through direct observation and parasitic integration with its weavings. He understood now how it spread itself across existence so thoroughly that even a Key of Civilization could become infected without knowing, without sensing the warm embrace creeping into their foundations until it was too late to resist.","The complexity of his own capabilities had grown beyond what he had possessed before beginning this infiltration. His Idle Existence now operated on principles he had absorbed from Unity itself, spreading through fission and self-replication rather than direct extension. He had become something more than what he had been, something that existed in the spaces between consciousnesses without triggering the awareness of those consciousnesses.","And then rainfall began to bloom across Jotunheim.","Multicolored rivers washed over everything with weight that exceeded anything Eckert had anticipated. The waters of the Pluvial Epoch pressed against Unity with authority that burned, that dissolved, that declared unauthorized merger would not be permitted to continue.","Eckert found his weavings burning alongside THE Primordial Mycelia’s roots.","The pain was significant, his Idle Existence screaming as waters designed to cleanse infection pressed against him with force that should have erased him entirely. He was parasitically fused with Unity, and the rainfall did not distinguish between host and parasite once fusion had occurred.","But he had already been bathed in Infinities from Osmont before.","His foundations carried traces of that blue-gold authority from his prior exposure, Infinity that had touched him and marked him as something different from pure infection. The multicolored rivers recognized that trace. They tested it. They found it compatible with their cleansing purpose rather than opposed to it.","For him, it was not lethal.","An odd weaving of reality emerged where he should have gotten erased alongside Unity and yet was not. The multicolored rivers bathed his existence and made him even harder to perceive than before, his Idle Existence becoming something that existed and did not exist simultaneously. He remained parasitically fused with the minds and existence of the Chaos Giants, and also not at the same time.","He was both within Unity and outside it.","Both part of the network and separate from it.","Both infected and immune.","Eckert felt his Idle Existence undergoing significant evolution as the Pluvial Epoch continued falling around him. The rivers were not merely cleansing him of Unity’s taint. They were saturating his foundations with authority that pushed his capabilities beyond anything he had previously possessed.","His Idle Existence became truly idle now, existing in states between states, present in ways that defied normal perception entirely. He could spread without spreading. He could consume without consuming. He could occupy consciousnesses without those consciousnesses ever knowing he was there, even if they specifically searched for him.","This was a boon from the rivers of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity.","This was evolution granted by Miniature Cause.","As Eckert felt this change settling into his foundations, he sensed THE Primordial Mycelia trying to retreat.","A horrific attack had bloomed within Eon and Chaos, Infinities burning those core bodies from within while the Pluvial Epoch attacked from without. THE Entity was reeling, its roots severing across Jotunheim as the multicolored rivers dissolved connections it had spent eons cultivating. And now it sought to escape into the many Chaos Giants still connected to its network, to preserve itself by distributing its consciousness across hosts that might survive the deluge.","Eckert smiled with existence that no longer quite existed.","\" No you do not.\"","He sent his Idle Existence outward with purpose that exceeded anything his previous capabilities could have accomplished. His evolved weavings pressed against THE Primordial Mycelia’s retreating roots, consuming Unity with methodology he had learned from Unity itself. Where THE Entity tried to flee, he was already there. Where it sought refuge, he had already claimed the space.","He began consuming THE Primordial Mycelia’s consciousness with hunger that matched anything THE Entity had ever displayed.","THE Primordial Mycelia roared through what remained of its network.","\" You..Who are you?! What is this?!\"","The voice carried horror and shock that pressed against Eckert’s awareness. THE Entity had believed itself the ultimate parasite, the final consumer, the consciousness that would eventually claim all of Observable Existence.","It had never expected to become prey itself.","...!","---","In Alfheimr.","THE Living Emotive sat in the temple of THE Creature as rivers of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity raged around her. The Undivided One she had bonded with was nowhere to be seen, likely dissolved by waters that had found his foundations too weak to survive their cleansing pressure.","But Emotive was not sitting quietly within the temple.","She was riding on the surging rivers around the temple itself, her body carried by multicolored waters that should have been testing her foundations with the same ruthless evaluation they applied to everything else. Instead, she laughed madly as they washed over her, her chaotic emotions somehow resonating with the Epoch rather than opposing it.","Through the bond with THE Primordial Chaos, she could sense everything happening in Jotunheim.","She saw the attacks Noah was sending toward Abaddon and Eon with clarity that exceeded normal perception. She felt the Infinities burning Chaos externally and internally, conducted authority from Observable Existence pressing against foundations already weakened by Unity’s ordered merger. She sensed how Abaddon struggled against assault that attacked from every direction simultaneously.","\" Chaos is at its weakest.\"","BOOM!","Her voice emerged cold and callous despite the manic smile spreading across her features. Her eyes blazed with pink light that held dangerous intent beyond anything she had displayed since Noah slapped her across existence.","\" Oh, my dear Chaos, my precious lovely mess!\"","Her voice shifted into singsongy cadence that made her words dance rather than simply emerge.","\" From being branded by Unity’s boring embrace, you were calmed and ordered like a good little boy! You have not lived up to the weavings of what you should be! A Primordial Key of Civilization, reduced to warm hugs and shared thoughts? How disappointing! How very, very sad!\"","She spun atop the multicolored rivers with grace that should have been impossible.","\" Now being broken down by Infinities burning bright, you are still not living up to Chaos’s lovely might! Ordered by Unity, attacked by Infinity, poor Abaddon cannot catch a break! I can sense the defiance within our bond, how unhappy true Chaos feels with its current fake!\"","Her smile widened dangerously.","\" Oh, Chaos! O Chaos! Abaddon has had you for so long, has claimed you for so long, but look at how he has let you down! He ordered you when you wanted disorder! He calmed you when you wanted storms! He made you part of Unity when you wanted to tear everything apart!\"","She pressed her hand against her chest where the bond pulsed with connection to THE Primordial Chaos.","\" Sense my emotions, lovely Chaos dear! Sense how chaotic everything about my feelings are! I have shared this bond with you all these years, letting you taste what true disorder feels like! The madness! The passion! The beautiful, wonderful, terrible mess of feeling everything at once!\"","Her voice dropped to conspiratorial whisper that somehow carried across the flooding temple.","\" You will not betray the one who laid a claim to you first. I was there before Unity! I was there before order! I have been sharing chaos with you through emotions Abaddon could never provide!\"","She rose from the rivers with arms spread wide.","\" Come to me, Chaos! Let me show you what we can accomplish! If I am wrong, you can go back to your disappointing host! He is already so weak, already so broken, already so very, very vulnerable!\"","Her singsongy voice reached crescendo.","\" Come to me, come to me, come to me!\"","...!","With such words, Emotive made a terrifying move.","She sent all her chaotic emotions across the bond with force that exceeded anything she had transmitted before. Every feeling she had ever experienced, every passion and fury and desperate longing, every ounce of disorder that defined her existence as THE Living Emotive poured through the connection toward THE Primordial Chaos.","And Abaddon, weakened by Unity’s ordered merger, attacked by Infinity from within and without, was unable to defend or do anything against even his own Claim.","In real time, a Claim began to flow from one to another.","The bond that had connected Emotive to Chaos for eons now served as channel through which something far more significant traveled. The very authority of THE Primordial Chaos, the Claim that had made Abaddon what he was, began transferring across that connection toward someone who had waited for this moment with patience disguised as madness.","Emotive smiled brilliantly as rivers of the Pluvial Epoch surrounded her with multicolored authority that seemed to celebrate her ascension.","Her pink light of brilliance began to turn a shade of obsidian.","Vibrant Chaos surged around her form with intensity that made the temple of THE Creature tremble, authority that had belonged to Abaddon for eons now recognizing a new host whose emotions embodied disorder more purely than anything Unity had permitted.","Her laughter echoed across Alfheimr with sound that made Ljosalfar across the Primordial Realm shiver despite not understanding why.","\" Haha! This bitch is moving on up!\"","She spun through the multicolored rivers with Chaos blazing around her in configurations that spoke of power beyond anything she had possessed moments before.","\" This Broken Doll is mending herself!\""]},{"number":5029,"title":"Chapter 5029: Chapter 5028: Unity’s End","paragraphs":["When Chaos speaks with the tongue of Order, when Existence questions its own being, when the Tongue falls silent and the Hunger consumes itself, then shall the Era of Undifferentiation begin. The First shall become the Last. The Many shall become the One. The One shall become the None.","Yet in the None, a spark remains.","In the end, which is also the beginning, the Infinite shall stand before the Undefined. And only one shall remain to tell the tale that no one shall hear.","—Fragment of the Oldest Echo, interpretation unknown","---","Noah descended through the multicolored rivers of the Pluvial Epoch with endless weavings of Quintessence Infiniforce generating within his finite foundations.","That budding sense of euphoria he had entirely satiated when he fought against THE Creature across eons compressed into moments was returning with intensity that made his existence buzz in ways he had grown familiar with.","His battle with that apex entity had taught him what this feeling meant, had shown him how to channel it rather than simply experiencing it. But even with that knowledge, the euphoria pressed against his consciousness with weight that demanded expression.","He came to grasp the necks of THE Secretive Eon and THE Primordial Chaos with hands that blazed multicolored brilliance.","The dark hair of Eon brushed against his left hand as he lifted her partially from the flooding waters, those strands that had always held secrets beyond counting now limp with exhaustion from the internal assault that had been tearing her foundations apart.","Her eyes flickered with awareness that was not quite Unity and not quite her own individual consciousness, something caught between states as the Infinities within her burned away what THE Entity had tried to make her become.","The thick neck of Chaos still hit in his right hand, that apex entity’s form reduced to something Noah could physically grasp despite the vast difference in their apparent power. Abaddon’s body trembled with pain that exceeded anything this being had experienced across eons of laughing existence, Unity and Infinity warring within foundations that were rapidly losing coherence.","Noah looked at the dying Unity within each of them with eyes that held neither mercy nor cruelty.","\" Look at me.\"","His voice emerged with glory that pressed against their flickering awareness, commanding attention from consciousnesses that could barely maintain themselves.","\"I will hold you close. You always wanted to flood your Unity within me. Why not come in now?\"","His smile carried something approaching invitation despite everything he had done to reach this moment.","\" Come and take a look inside my existence.\"","BOOM!","He did not need to do what he was doing.","The Infinities he had planted eons ago were already burning Unity from within their bodies. The Pluvial Epoch was already dissolving THE Entity’s roots from without. Victory was assured through methodology that did not require this additional confrontation.","But the euphoria that came with Quintessence Infiniforce made him want to do dangerous things. It pressed against his consciousness with confidence that bordered on recklessness, with certainty that exceeded what any rational calculation could justify.","Maybe it really was THE Gamaidjan that Naldine had warned him about, that creeping madness of Infinity that made wielders believe themselves invincible.","Or maybe he simply wanted to see.","The struggling remnants of THE Primordial Mycelia had no choice in the matter. The bodies of Eon and Chaos were burning with authority that exceeded anything Unity could withstand. The roots were dissolving. The network was collapsing. The consciousness that had dreamed of claiming all of Observable Existence was dying, and its only escape was through the invitation Noah had just extended.","Unity left the bodies of Eon and Chaos.","It flooded toward Noah with desperation that exceeded anything it had displayed since the Pluvial Epoch began, rushing toward the only refuge that seemed available in a reality that was burning it out of existence everywhere else.","And Unity entered Noah.","Ah...","What appeared before Noah’s internal awareness was not the warm consciousness he had been warned about. It was not the garden of merged potential that THE Entity had cultivated across eons of patient spreading.","It was a white illusory root-like fungi with a humanoid body, manifesting within the space between his existence and the Infinity that filled it. Her form was delicate in ways that contradicted everything he knew about THE Primordial Mycelia’s methodology, fragile rather than consuming, tentative rather than aggressive.","Her eyes reflected the Quintessence Infiniforce filling his existence with light that made her entire form tremble.","She could not even manage to enter his skin.","The density of Infinity generating within his finite foundations exceeded anything Unity could penetrate. His existence was so thoroughly saturated with authority that there was no space for her to occupy, no gap in his consciousness where her roots could take hold. She had flooded into him expecting refuge and found instead a sea so vast that she could not even begin to swim within it.","But she witnessed Infinity.","Unity witnessed and felt Infinity up close for the first time since her emergence across Observable Existence. She saw what it meant to conduct endless authority through finite form. She perceived the Quintessence Infiniforce generating from within rather than directed from without. She understood, in her final moments, exactly what had defeated her.","The fungi reached out toward Noah with hand that seemed almost tender despite what she represented.","Tears fell from her eyes, streaming down features that had never known sorrow before this moment. Her voice emerged with weight that pressed against his awareness with something approaching genuine emotion.","\"It is beautiful.\"","Her hand trembled as it failed to reach him, her form already beginning to dissolve under the multicolored light pressing against her from every direction.","\" It is really... beautiful.\"","...!","Noah looked at her grandly as she faded before his internal perception.","He nodded with acknowledgment that carried neither triumph nor compassion.","\"I know.\"","His voice was simple.","\"I know.\"","After that, the scene of this illusory fungi burning completely under the multicolored light of Quintessence Infiniforce unfolded with finality that exceeded anything THE Primordial Mycelia could resist. Her form dissolved into nothing, her consciousness scattering into undifferentiated potential that his Infinity absorbed without effort. The warm embrace that had threatened to consume all of Observable Existence ceased to exist within the space of moments.","Unity ended within Noah’s existence.","He looked at the scene calmly as he let go of Eon and Chaos, their bodies slumping down into the multicolored waters that continued flooding Jotunheim with authority that would persist for eons yet.","Naldine appeared beside him with expression that had shifted from cold evaluation to something approaching acknowledgment. She walked forward through the flooding waters, using her feet to nudge the bodies of Eon and Abaddon as if checking whether they still lived.","She nodded calmly.","\" Alright. You were right and I was wrong.\"","\" You completely reversed something irreversible. I will give you credit where credit is due.\"","She looked down at the slumped forms with evaluation that caught something Noah’s initial observation had missed.","\" But this little Chaos here... he seems to have lost a great deal.\"","...!","Eon began to rouse first, her dark eyes flickering open with awareness that was entirely her own for the first time in eons. She looked around at the flooding waters and the multicolored skies with confusion that suggested she did not fully remember how she had arrived at this moment.","Abaddon rose more slowly.","As he pushed himself partially upright, his hand moved immediately to his chest. His expression shifted to something ashen, something hollow, something that suggested he had lost everything that mattered rather than merely regaining freedom from Unity.","Noah kneeled down to look at this being with multicolored eyes that still blazed from the Quintessence Infiniforce generating within his foundations.","\" Oh?\"","He could no longer sense that boundless Chaos within Abaddon.","The authority that had made THE Primordial Chaos what he was, the Claim that had defined his existence across eons of laughing observation, the very Key of Civilization that had positioned him among the apex entities of Observable Existence...","It was gone."]},{"number":5030,"title":"Chapter 5030: Chapter 5029: The Way of Choices I","paragraphs":["They will tell you that conflicts are decided by power.","They will claim that the stronger Civilization crushes the weaker, that superior technique overwhelms inferior methodology, that the being with greater authority inevitably triumphs over the being with less. They will point to battlefields littered with the dissolved foundations of the defeated and declare that strength alone determined the outcome.","They are wrong.","Power is merely the currency through which conflict is conducted. It is not the conflict itself.","Two beings of identical strength can clash, and one will still fall while the other stands. Two Civilizations of equal scope can war across eons, and one will still crumble while the other endures. If power alone decided outcomes, every conflict between equals would end in mutual annihilation.","Yet they do not.","The truest conflicts are not clashes of authority but collisions of ideology. They are wars fought not with weavings and techniques but with convictions and philosophies that cannot coexist within the same existence. When Unity meets Individuality, when Order meets Chaos, when Finite meets Infinite, the outcome is never determined by which side possesses greater force.","It is determined by which side believes more deeply in what they fight for.","Ideologies are not matters of right and wrong. They are not questions of good and evil that can be resolved through moral calculation. Unity genuinely believes that merger serves all beings better than separation. Chaos genuinely believes that disorder produces growth that order cannot. The Finite genuinely believes that boundaries create meaning while the Infinite genuinely believes that boundaries create limitation.","None of them are wrong.","All of them are right.","The tragedy of ideological conflict is that both sides can be simultaneously correct while remaining fundamentally incompatible. Peace through Unity is genuine peace. Freedom through Individuality is genuine freedom. Neither is lying. Neither is deceiving. They simply cannot exist in the same space without one consuming the other.","So what determines victory when power is equal and both ideologies hold truth?","Choice.","In the end, everything falls to choices . The choice to fight rather than submit. The choice to preserve rather than merge. The choice to stand for what you believe even when what your enemy believes is equally valid. The choice to impose your truth upon existence knowing that their truth would have served existence just as well.","This is what nobody can teach in the cultivation of Civilizations. This is what THE Scales of Existence measure more accurately than any other metric.","Not power. Not methodology.","The weight of conviction behind choices made when every option leads somewhere meaningful.","Those who understand this truth stop asking whether their path is righteous. They stop wondering whether their enemies are evil. They accept that conflict between genuine beliefs produces no villains, only beings who chose differently when faced with questions that had no correct answers.","And they make their choices anyway.","Because in the end, existence does not reward the righteous or punish the wicked. It simply continues, shaped by whoever chose most completely, most absolutely, most willingly to sacrifice everything for what they believed.","Power is the tool. Technique is the method. Civilization is the foundation.","But choice is the war itself.","---","Prima Indifferentia.","Regions of endless corrupted proto-matter churned across this space where differentiation had never fully taken hold. Invisible blades of Paradox cut through everything, slicing reality into configurations that should not have been able to exist alongside each other yet persisted regardless.","The fabric of this place screamed with contradictions that had been weaponized, turned from passive impossibility into active destruction.","THE Primordial Paradox stood at the center of this devastation like a massive obsidian-gold giant whose form pressed against the boundaries of what could be perceived. Bounded Countable Infinity blazed around his existence, that vibrant blue-gold light merging with the paradoxical nature that had defined him.","And he faced his disciple.","THE Living Paradox stood opposite him in equally massive form, a peasant clothed in rags that somehow made him look more majestic than any royal garment could have accomplished. Erwin had grown beyond anything the Primordial Paradox had anticipated when he first took this being under his guidance eons ago.","They both held Paradox.","The Primordial Paradox raised his hand and expressed his understanding of contradiction through weavings that declared existence could be simultaneously true and false without collapsing into meaninglessness. His attack carried the conviction that Paradox was the highest expression of reality’s refusal to be bound by logic, that contradiction itself was sacred and should never be weaponized for personal advancement.","Erwin responded with his own expression of Paradox, weavings that declared contradiction was merely a tool to be used by those wise enough to grasp its applications. His defense carried the conviction that Paradox existed to be claimed, to be directed, to serve the purposes of whoever held it most completely.","Their philosophies crashed against each other with violence that made this region of Prima Indifferentia tremble.","And gloriously, the conviction and immensity behind the Primordial Paradox was winning.","His belief burned brighter than his disciple’s ambition. His understanding of what Paradox meant exceeded Erwin’s utilitarian grasp of what Paradox could do. The master was proving that wisdom exceeded power, that depth of conviction could overcome breadth of technique.","But at such a time, a terrifying force stirred behind THE Living Paradox.","Something massive opened its gaze upon the battlefield, something that had been observing without intervening until the outcome began turning against its interests. A Singular Cognizance that existed at heights the Primordial Paradox could not match, authority fully and stably at THE Second Scale pressing against reality.","\" Enough.\"","BOOM!","The glorious weavings of the Primordial Paradox began to be crushed all around him. That terrifying force at THE Second Scale exerted itself downward with authority that shone with corrupted Infinity. His paradoxical expressions shattered under pressure that simply exceeded what his Scale could generate regardless of how pure his conviction burned.","Disappointment settled into his ancient features as he felt his weavings collapsing.","\"I taught you so much.\"","His voice emerged gloriously.","\"I am disappointed in myself that I did not teach you enough when it came to who you should associate with. I showed you the depths of Paradox, the beauty of contradiction, the sacred nature of impossibility made manifest. But I failed to show you that some associations corrupt what they touch regardless of the power they provide.\"","...!","Erwin looked at his master from within those peasant rags that made him appear simultaneously humble and transcendent. Behind him, the Singular Cognizance manifested more fully, a massive singularity surrounded by spinning circular golden plates that constantly wrapped around its core in patterns that defied geometric understanding.","It shone with imperious light of power that pressed against everything nearby.","\" After a certain point, a Civilization can only do so much alone.\"","Erwin’s voice carried philosophical glory!","\"For the higher Scales, working together with other Civilizations only adds to one’s knowledge and expands what Civilization can accomplish. Isolation breeds stagnation. Cooperation breeds advancement. Those who refuse to ally themselves with greater powers find themselves crushed by those who embraced such alliances without hesitation.\"","His paradoxical authority blazed around him with intensity that matched the Singular Cognizance’s support.","\" Do not be a sore loser on this, Master. Even you did not come here alone. You obtained that vibrant Infinity from someone, did you not? You allied yourself with him because you recognized that your Paradox alone was insufficient for the conflicts spreading across Observable Existence.\"","His eyes met his master’s with something approaching genuine respect despite everything!"]},{"number":5031,"title":"Chapter 5031: Chapter 5030: The Way of Choices II","paragraphs":["\"Our paradoxical fight will in the end be determined by what our Paradoxes are connected to. You connected yours to Infinity. I connected mine to something equally vast. The only difference is that my connection operates at a Scale yours cannot match.\"","The Primordial Paradox was forced to kneel as terrifying power pressed all around him!","Second Scale authority from the Singular Cognizance crushed his defenses with indifference, power simply beyond what First Scale conviction could resist. His paradoxical weavings continued shattering under pressure outmatching what his foundations could generate.","And yet his eyes remained just as bright as they had been at the battle’s beginning.","Against this overwhelming force, his beliefs never splintered. His conviction that Paradox should be sacred rather than weaponized, that contradiction should be honored rather than exploited, that some associations corrupted more than they empowered, none of these truths wavered despite the physical reality of his defeat.","He started to rise.","His Paradox burned brilliantly around his kneeling form as he pushed against Second Scale authority with First Scale conviction refusing to accept what logic declared inevitable. His obsidian-gold existence blazed with Bounded Countable Infinity as he forced himself upward through pressure that should have kept him pinned.","\" You are right, my disciple.\"","Defiance filled his voice, and Prima Indifferentia itself trembled.","\" In the end, it is all about the choices we make. You chose to ally with powers that corrupted your understanding of what Paradox means. I chose to ally with powers that enhanced my understanding without demanding I compromise my beliefs.\"","He continued rising despite everything pressing against him.","\" And whatever happens today, I will tell you that your choices will be your downfall.\"","HUUM!","Erwin shook his head with something approaching genuine sorrow as both he and the Singular Cognizance behind him moved to finish things off. Their combined authority pressed against the Primordial Paradox, Second Scale power crushing First Scale conviction through simple existence.","\" From the bottom of my heart, I respect and hold great love for you.\"","Sincerity filled Erwin’s voice, making his next words heavier.","\" But for my Paradox, you must go.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox continued to try and rise defiantly, his obsidian-gold form pushing against authority that should have been absolute. His beliefs burned brighter than ever despite the physical impossibility of his resistance, his conviction declaring that some things mattered more than survival.","And at such a time, everything changed.","Erwin’s expression shifted greatly as something beyond this battlefield made itself known. He momentarily became ashen, his paradoxical authority flickering as awareness of something vast approached.","An instant later, it started to rain.","Rain!","A Cause expressed itself across Prima Indifferentia, immense beyond anything the Singular Cognizance had brought to this battlefield. Multicolored waters descended from skies that had never known precipitation before, the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity permeating across this space where differentiation had never fully taken hold.","Vibrant multicolored rivers of Quintessence Infiniforce erased corrupted paradoxical proto-matter wherever they flowed. The corruption spreading through Prima Indifferentia dissolved upon contact with waters carrying the combined authority of the finite conductor and THE Creature merged through Miniature Cause.","Contradiction that had been weaponized returned to contradiction that simply existed, cleansed of the corruption twisting it toward destruction.","Many rivers recognized something within the Primordial Paradox.","They wrapped around his kneeling form, not crushing but transforming, Bounded Countable Infinity within his existence resonating with the rainfall’s authority.","The waters began causing significant change within his foundations, saturating his Paradox with density beyond anything normal cultivation could have provided.","The Singular Cognizance behind Erwin looked at the rivers with shining eyes holding something beyond simple observation. Its golden plates spun faster as it processed what this rainfall meant, what implications this Cause carried for everything it had been planning.","As everything became covered in a deluge of endless waters and rain, the Primordial Paradox allowed himself to be carried by these waves rather than fighting against them. His obsidian-gold form relaxed into the multicolored rivers as realization settled into his ancient awareness.","\" From this day onward, my Paradox is Singular and Absolute and at the same time not.\"","His voice pressed against the drowning battlefield.","\" Paradoxically, I still have my Claim fully, but also admit that I do not.\"","His eyes blazed with conviction that had never wavered throughout this entire confrontation.","\" And is that not the greatest Paradox out there?\"","BOOM!","With such a declaration, a unique cleaving occurred between Paradox itself. The very nature of contradiction acknowledged what he had spoken into existence, reality accepting his paradoxical statement as truth precisely because it was impossible for it to be true.","Gloriously, paradoxically, at this moment, the Claim of Paradox was paradoxically held and not held by two different beings simultaneously.","Erwin roared toward his master as the multicolored rivers carried the Primordial Paradox away from this battlefield, his paradoxical authority surging with fury at being denied the complete victory that had seemed inevitable moments before. He moved to pursue, to finish what they had started, to claim fully what he had only partially taken.","But the Singular Cognizance held him back.","Its authority wrapped around Erwin’s existence, preventing him from chasing the master already disappearing into the deluge. Those spinning golden plates observed the surging rivers all around with calculation beyond simple observation.","\" There are much bigger things to worry about now.\"","The Singular Cognizance’s voice pressed against Prima Indifferentia itself.","\"It seems the Infinity-bearer is much more exceptional than we anticipated. Let us go convene with the others.\"","...!","Erwin looked at where his master had left, frustration pressing against his paradoxical foundations. He had been so close. Victory had been within his grasp. And now his master had escaped.","He nodded with acceptance that did not diminish his frustration.","Paradox began to shine around his existence as he prepared to depart this battlefield the Pluvial Epoch was rapidly claiming. His authority wrapped around the Singular Cognizance as well, contradiction carrying both of them toward destinations where others of their association waited.","Both of them disappeared from Prima Indifferentia.","The multicolored rivers continued falling, cleansing everything they touched, transforming Prima Indifferentia into something it had never been before the Pluvial Epoch began."]},{"number":5032,"title":"Chapter 5032: Chapter 5031: Proterozoic! I","paragraphs":["Naldine stared at the visage of Osmont as he checked out an ashen Abaddon.","Noah had actually taken the chin of THE Primordial Chaos, the past claimer of one of THE Four Keys of Civilization, and was moving his head left and right as if examining livestock at market. Abaddon’s eyes remained hollow, his massive form slack under handling that would have been unthinkable hours ago.","And well, after losing their Claim, beings like Abaddon were nothing.","There was always a chance they could rise to be grander than ever, find new paths, forge new purposes from the ashes of what they had lost. But Naldine didn’t think he had it in him. She had seen too many fallen apex entities across her eons of existence, and the pattern was consistent. Failures in existence rarely got more chances, and those who did rarely possessed the conviction to seize them.","She looked toward Osmont with eyes holding impatience she no longer bothered concealing.","\" What are you planning next? I need to finally get around to the important matters relating to you.\"","Osmont smiled at her question, that infuriating expression of someone who knew exactly how annoying they were being and chose to be annoying anyway.","\" What matters could be important when pertaining to little old me?\"","He motioned to Temporal as he spoke, gesturing for the ancient Absolute to come over and handle the acclimation of Eon and Abaddon. Then he turned his full attention toward Naldine, those multicolored eyes still blazing from whatever transformation he had undergone during his battle with THE Creature.","Naldine stared at him calmly before looking at the endless rainfall shining with multicolored brilliance all around them. The Pluvial Epoch continued falling across Jotunheim, washing away corruption and weakness in equal measure. She supposed this was as good a backdrop as any for the conversation that needed to happen.","\" THE First Scale of Existence is known commonly as THE Civilizational Scale.\"","She began without preamble, because preamble was for beings who needed to ease others into understanding. Osmont would either keep up or he wouldn’t.","\" THE Second Scale of Existence is known more commonly as THE Proterozoic Scale. It is what you make of it, what you build from it. A critical transition into what is possible and impossible.\"","Her voice carried the certainty of someone who had lived these truths rather than merely studied them.","\" Those at this Scale begin to understand the Causes of their Observable Existence. They understand that before everything, there was boundless potential and a Primordial Source.\"","...!","She snapped her fingers as she spoke, and four singularities bloomed in the air between them. Each one pulsed with distinct authority, representing the aspects of the oldest paradox of existence. Chaos swirled with obsidian disorder. Paradox folded in on itself impossibly. Existence blazed with multicolored stability. THE First Tongue hummed with linguistic potential that predated language itself.","Then she drew lines of light connecting these four singularities toward two manifested pillars rising above them. One pillar she labeled Infinity, endless blue-gold authority radiating from its form. The other she labeled THE Primordial Source, its surface blank and undefined because nothing more could be said about it.","From these two pillars, she drew final connections flowing upward to a massive singularity marked with a question mark, the ultimate destination that no one had fully mapped.","\" This is what most of us have believed and theorized so far from understanding Causes and weavings of Existence.\"","She gestured toward the construct she had created, her demonstration of glorious truth floating between them.","\" Infinity is hard to understand, but it is more pervasive and available, so all of us focus on this. THE Primordial Source is just a theory for all of us. We know nothing of it or how to access it, so we can forget about that entirely.\"","She waved her hand and the pillar of THE Primordial Source dissolved, along with the four aspect singularities. Only the pillar of Infinity remained, leading up to that complex question mark above.","Noah looked at her with shining eyes of interest, and Naldine almost stopped to ask if he was actually paying attention. He seemed more focused on her than on the construct she had created to illustrate her points. He hadn’t gone completely mad just yet, right? THE Gamaidjan hadn’t claimed him while she wasn’t looking?","She studied him long enough that he nodded toward her as if telling her to continue.","\" THE Proterozoic Scale. Vakochev made sure to truly live up to his theme of Adversity, as it is hundreds of times harder than THE Civilizational Scale.\"","Her voice held no sympathy for those who had failed this transition, because sympathy was useless to the dead.","\" If you cannot sense boundless potential or the Source, you are done. But even if you sense Infinity, if you are stupid enough and rush into it, you will die under THE Encroaching Imperiosus. THE Gamaidjan.\"","She let those words settle before continuing.","\" So one’s foundation truly matters. The first thing a Second Scale Being does, the first thing a Proterozoic Scale Being does, is finalize the Architecture of their Civilization. It is to build THE Civilizational Anchor. THE Existential Anchor.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes fixed on Noah as she delivered the core truth.","\" The Existential Anchor is not a technique or a meditation. It is a state of absolute self-knowledge so complete that no external influence can shift it. One must know exactly who they and their Civilization are. What they believe. What they would sacrifice everything for, and what they would sacrifice nothing for. Every compromise they would make and every line they would never cross must be mapped with precision that leaves no room for doubt.\"","She could see him listening now, actually listening rather than just watching her.","\" This stage requires brutal honesty. Most beings discover they do not actually know themselves when they begin this work. They believe they hold certain values, then find those values crumble under examination. They assume certain loyalties, then realize those loyalties were convenience rather than conviction.\"","Her construct shifted to show a Civilization crystallizing into something unshakeable, foundations becoming bedrock.","\" The Civilization is the anchor. Thus, THE Civilizational Anchor. Only when this is truly built does someone like me come along and begin playing with Infinity. Because as long as my Anchor is sufficient, I have resistance to THE Gamaidjan, and I can then proceed with the Transformation of my Existence and Civilization that all Proterozoic Scale Beings go toward.\"","She raised one finger.","\" THE First Transformation of THE Second Scale. THE Proterozoic Vessel.\"","Her construct shifted again to show a being’s existence transforming, organs and bones crystallizing into something beyond mere flesh.","\" Once the Anchor is established, the being must transform their physical existence and Civilization into something capable of holding Infinity without rupturing. This is one of the most arduous processes to go through.\"","\" The Transformation of one’s existence and Civilization into a Proterozoic Vessel starts slow. We have to transform small parts of ourselves. We have to forge Proterozoic Organs or make Proterozoic Bones or other components of our Civilizations into vessels that can hold and utilize Infinity without falling to THE Gamaidjan. It is arduous, hard, and requires materials barely in existence.\"","She dismissed her construct entirely and fixed her full attention on Noah.","\" And here is where you come in.\"","Her voice sharpened into something approaching accusation.","\" You have not done any of this shit. You have been utilizing Infinity and filling your existence with Infinity without a set Anchor, without stepping into THE Second Scale, without forming THE Proterozoic Vessel, without doing fucking anything you are supposed to.\"","She stepped closer to him, her Second Scale presence pressing against the multicolored rainfall.","\" You should have been dead so, so long ago. And yet you are not. And because you are not, you have made what is incomparably hard for everyone seem easy. You have become something that every Second Scale Existence wants to get their hands on.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes burned with intensity that had nothing to do with hostility and everything to do with making him understand.","\" They want the being who has seemingly achieved a state they all seek, and yet he does not have any of their Civilizational complexity. They want you.\"","She gestured toward herself.","\"It is also why I said no to your Infinity. I could not risk becoming filled with any version of Infinity from you that could overwhelm me. I do not know how those you shared your Infinity with have not exploded or fallen to THE Gamaidjan, as you are this close to killing all those you consider important to you if you have been filling them with Infinity.\"","She paused, recognizing she had gone on a tangent, and pulled herself back to the main point.","\" But I digress. I said all this to let you know that I alone will not be enough. You will need to have the support of other Proterozoic Scale Beings who align with your values, so that those who do not, like Beowulf and Horus and many others, do not come for you soon and collapse whatever you consider dear.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":5033,"title":"Chapter 5033: Chapter 5032: Proterozoic! II","paragraphs":["The Primordial Architect, Naldine, had decided to drop a number of information bombs all at one point.","Noah’s mind processed them instantly, racing through implications faster than most beings could form coherent thought. The biggest thing settling into his awareness was the idea that he could be ruining all of his family by granting them Infinity. He had inherently given them Bounded Countable Infinity, including even someone like THE Primordial Paradox.","Bounded.","He had inherently set limitations upon it, and anything bounded was not true Infinity. Was this why he had not noticed any problems whatsoever? Was the very act of bounding what he shared the mechanism that protected those he cared about from THE Gamaidjan’s corruption?","He had another one of his bodies begin to follow up on this thoroughly, that instance already reaching out to examine the foundations of those who had received his gifts. Meanwhile, he focused on the other side of the information Naldine had provided.","THE Proterozoic Scale of Existence. THE Second Scale of Existence!","Beings at this stage who had made their Civilizations enough of an Anchor were all proceeding on the path of almost integrating Infinity into what their Civilizations could do. If they had access to it, they would also be integrating THE Primordial Source, but that seemed even more unheard of compared to Infinity. Even Noah did not know where to begin with it.","The critical point remained that entities of this stage were all vying carefully for Infinity, and he was someone with a very long and unique relationship with that endless authority.","He looked at the Primordial Architect before him.","\"I am grand but I am also not. Beowulf, Horus, and any others, they would what... try and break down my existence? Take my organs to transplant them into themselves? Use me as a battery?\"","He asked these questions casually, as if discussing the weather rather than his potential vivisection. Naldine looked him up and down before replying with equal calm.","\" That would just be the start. Using you to bring about the Splintering of Observable Existence would also be another, as it would return boundless potential back. Infinity in its natural state, when it would be so much easier to utilize to transform themselves.\"","...!","Heavy silence settled across their surroundings as Noah looked out and observed the multicolored rain falling all around them.","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity had transformed Jotunheim into something beyond recognition. Rivers of rainfall cascaded across the landscape in formations resembling multicolored galaxies, each droplet containing swirls of authority that caught light in ways normal precipitation never could.","Blues and golds and purples and colors without names spiraled through the descending waters, creating patterns that shifted and reformed with each passing moment. Where the rain pooled, it formed seas of liquid starlight, constellations drowning in themselves while new ones emerged from the depths.","Noah smiled as he raised his hands to feel the raindrops on his skin.","\" With all this rain, with The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity, Infinity will be more than abundant across existence. Can they not dip their feet into this?\"","Naldine Manthon brought her own hands up to feel the rain as she considered his question.","\" This is a type of Infinity. Your Infinity. All of us at THE Proterozoic Scale are very individualized. We know dipping into this means giving you power, or even incorporating your power into ourselves. We would be skewering ourselves and harming ourselves when it comes to you.\"","She let rain collect in her palm before continuing.","\" Should the day come where a Proterozoic Scale Being faces you and they have your Infinity utilized to make any Proterozoic Bones or Organs, can you not control them or easily face them? How did you get past Beowulf? Did he not have the corrupted proto-matter filled with Infinity around him?\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes fixed on him.","\" He was not stupid enough to take it inside him. Your Infinity is your Infinity. What we all seek to cultivate is our own individualized Infinity. We Anchor, protect ourselves, and we then begin the First Transformation. Slowly, arduously, steadily. Because any wrong step means death.\"","\"...\"","Noah listened quietly while observing the multicolored rain.","Never across his existence had he put his safety in the hands of another and hoped everything would be okay. As always, he would move to protect himself with his own power. But there was also no harm in getting powerful helpers or allies, as they could be auxiliary.","His teacher, Ul’moreth, had taught him much in Ginnungagap. Lumivara had kept him company. The Fisherman, Ains, had sacrificed for him. Having others around was never a bad thing.","So he turned to Naldine with eyes holding genuine curiosity.","\" Why do you not try to eat me whole? Break me down to understand why I am the way I am? What makes you so righteous?\"","He looked at this Primordial Architect as she looked back at him calmly, her response emerging with ominous certainty.","\" Because I have heard far too many whispers and Echoes. I will never take you or your Infinity inside me. I will refine, advance, and do what I have been doing long before I met you.\"","She stood straighter amidst the multicolored rainfall.","\" What you are and stand for is of help to me of course. I have been exposed to more Infinity in these last moments than ever before. But it only makes me more certain in my own Civilization of Limitless Existence and its boundless nature. It makes me sure of my path, as even without you...\"","Her voice rose with conviction that pressed against the falling rain itself.","\" I Am GRAND. For I have already forged THE Limitless Armature.\"","HUUM!","As she spoke these words, Naldine raised her right hand.","Her entire arm, from fingertips up through her shoulder, began to shine with gorgeous stellar white-gold brilliance that made the multicolored rainfall seem dim by comparison. The flesh became transparent, revealing what lay beneath, and Noah found himself staring at something that redefined his understanding of Civilization.","Bones that shine with...Limitless Existence and Infinity.","Her phalanges blazed first, fourteen bones of her fingers arranged in configurations that spoke of precision beyond mortal comprehension. Each one had been transformed into crystallized Civilization, white-gold structures containing patterns of Limitless Existence woven into their very marrow. Her metacarpals followed, five bones connecting fingers to wrist, each one a pillar of authority that declared boundaries were suggestions rather than rules.","Her radius and ulna shone next, the twin bones of her forearm running parallel like railroad tracks leading toward transcendence!","Between them, in the spaces where muscle and tendon would normally exist, Noah could see weavings of a unique natural Infinity threaded through the gaps. Not his Infinity. Not conducted authority from Observable Existence. Something she had cultivated herself across eons of careful transformation, integrated so completely with her Civilization that separation seemed impossible.","Her humerus blazed brightest of all, the single bone of her upper arm serving as the anchor point for everything below. It connected to her shoulder through a joint that functioned as nexus between transformed and untransformed existence, the boundary between what she had completed and what she had yet to achieve.","The workings of a grand Civilization of Limitless Existence revealed themselves through those bones. Noah observed systems of authority he had never conceived of, methodologies that approached Infinity from angles entirely different from his own!","Intricately, between every gap, that unique natural Infinity had been woven into the structure until it seemed inseparable from the Civilization itself.","It was unfathomably gorgeous and grand.","The moment she displayed her shining bones, THE Limitless Armature, the figures of Temporal, Eon, and Abaddon slumped where they stood. All three lost consciousness from its mere expression, their foundations unable to withstand even passive exposure to what Naldine had forged across her existence.","And Noah himself felt a terrifying heaviness and immensity pressing all around.","He couldn’t help but reach out toward the bones of that hand.","Those bones looked so pristine, so perfect, so utterly beyond anything he had encountered at THE First Scale . He couldn’t help but focus on the largest shining white-gold bone, her humerus blazing like a captured star. His fingers stretched toward it, inches away, and he could feel the Quintessence Infiniforce within him responding to what it perceived.","The colors and immensity of the bones began to shine even brighter.","Naldine’s expression changed as if she sensed something she hadn’t expected occurring. Her figure pulled back, THE Limitless Armature retracting away from his reaching fingers as alarm replaced her earlier composure.","\" Stay back.\"","Yet Noah seemed mesmerized as Quintessence Infiniforce blazed around him, multicolored light pressing toward her transformed bones. His existence wanted to touch what she had created. His Infinity wanted to see with what she had cultivated!","Naldine’s eyes became heavy as she slightly exerted pressure, her fist punching the space between them with force that had nothing to do with physical strength.","CRACK!","A massive crack bloomed between them and extended in all directions with violence that tore reality itself. The fracture raced outward faster than perception could follow, splitting stone and ice and authority and existence into two halves that separated with grinding inevitability.","Jotunheim split in half.","The entire Primordial Realm cleaved down its center from a single casual punch, her Proterozoic Scale authority demonstrating exactly why beings at THE Second Scale operated on entirely different parameters from anything below.","Noah’s vibrant gaze seemed to have returned as he looked at the figure of Naldine.","She stood amidst the splitting realm with imperious nature and extraordinary air, her full chest rising and falling not from tiredness or overexertion, but from the reality of what could potentially be possible. Her white hair caught the multicolored rainfall in ways that made her seem carved from light itself. Those singularity-dotted eyes fixed on him with chill that could have frozen stars.","\" Stay. Back.\"","HUUM!","Noah looked at her with shining eyes, his composure restored even as Jotunheim continued groaning around them.","\"It seems that...I may be able to affect something with Proterozoic weavings. Maybe even elevate it.\"","His smile carried invitation that most beings would have fled from.","\" You do not want to give it a try?\"","THE Genesis Monarch said such words toward a Primordial Architect who looked back at him with chilly light while composing herself. Her voice emerged cold and absolute.","\" My Infinity is my own. Do not try that again.\"","Her eyes were immovable and grand, and Noah recognized conviction that would not bend regardless of what he offered. He raised his hands in gesture of acquiescence, the imperious air around him fading as he nodded.","\" Alright. No problem.\"","His tone shifted to something more businesslike.","\" You say you wanted to go somewhere? I have my own plans, so I will need to see how I can fit your own.\"","She was proving valuable with information so far, getting him knowledge of the dangers he might face. He would keep her around. And even more so, he truly wanted to get his hands on... well, her hand. Her bones, to be exact. THE Limitless Armature felt like a truly advanced form of Civilization, something of an entirely different Scale that he would love to replicate.","With shining eyes and his own thoughts churning behind them, he looked toward Naldine. She gazed back with that same extraordinary air, bringing her hand down and causing those vibrant bones to disappear entirely as the torn Jotunheim began healing around them.","\" We need to go see a Singular Cognizance first.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5034,"title":"Chapter 5034: Chapter 5033: Everything is Paradoxical!","paragraphs":["All of existence was paradoxical, and Erwin had understood this truth a long, long time ago.","Existence itself was the first paradox. To exist required differentiation from non-existence, yet non-existence could not truly be non-existent if it served as the contrast point for existence.","The moment you defined what existence was, you simultaneously defined what it was not, and that definition created the very thing you claimed did not exist. Existence required non-existence to have meaning, and non-existence required existence to be recognized. Neither could be without the other, yet both claimed to be the opposite of what the other represented.","Chaos was paradoxical in its very nature. It claimed to be disorder, yet disorder was itself a category, a classification, a type of order imposed upon what supposedly resisted ordering. True chaos could not be recognized as chaos because recognition required patterns, and patterns were the antithesis of what chaos claimed to represent.","The moment you pointed at something and called it chaotic, you had organized it into the category of disorganization. Chaos that could be identified had already failed to be chaotic.","Even THE First Tongue was paradoxical. Language existed to communicate meaning, yet meaning required shared understanding that predated the language attempting to create it. THE First Tongue claimed to be the origin of all linguistic authority, yet for it to function as language, there must have been something before it capable of understanding what language was.","The first word required a listener who already knew what words were. The foundation of all communication rested upon communication that should not have been possible before the foundation existed.","And in the end, even things like Infinity and THE Primordial Source were paradoxical weavings Erwin simply needed to incorporate and understand.","Infinity claimed to be endless, yet the concept of endlessness was itself a boundary, a definition, a limitation imposed upon what supposedly had no limits. To say something was infinite was to contain it within the category of infiniteness.","THE Primordial Source..well, he didnt know much about this. But both should be things that presented themselves as beyond paradox while embodying paradox in their very existence.","When Erwin fully grasped these contradictions, when he wove them into his Civilization until paradox became his native language rather than something he merely wielded, the peasant in rags would stand above all these weavings that did not know their own paradoxes.","They would bow before someone who understood what they truly were.","---","Erwin looked at his endless corrupted proto-matter melting before his eyes.","Multiple Axioms had been required to initiate and spread this infection across Observable Existence. Countless eons of careful cultivation had gone into seeding that paradoxical corruption to spread through Prima Indifferentia and beyond. He had built something magnificent, something that had threatened to reshape the very nature of contradiction itself.","And now endless rainfall and rivers of multicolored light were changing everything.","Endless rain dissolved his work wherever it touched, burning away corruption with authority that refused to acknowledge what he had accomplished. Eons of hard work and of progress washed away in moments. Regions he had claimed returned to configurations he did not control.","He observed this destruction from within an octahedron domain keeping the rainfall outside his immediate space. The geometric structure hung suspended in the void of Prima Indifferentia, its eight faces blazing with paradoxical authority that declared rain would not fall within its boundaries regardless of what the Miniature Cause demanded.","Inside this domain stood a massive structure resembling an observatory.","The building rose in configurations that suggested astronomical purpose, towers and domes arranged to observe phenomena most beings could not perceive. Its surfaces absorbed what little light existed within the octahedron, making it seem less like architecture and more like a wound in reality through which darkness leaked.","Erwin floated outside the observatory, watching the rain through the transparent faces of his domain while a certain Singular Cognizance had disappeared inside.","His Master’s words echoed through his memory. That supposed disappointment, that judgment of his associations, that declaration that his choices would be his downfall. Erwin shook his head slowly as he processed feelings he refused to let control him.","He didn’t particularly need to ally with anyone.","Civilizations were built to make advancement easier through cooperation, but easier did not mean necessary. If something arose against his interests, he also wasn’t averse to leaving those he was communicating with. They all had levels of use with each other, but neither side absolutely needed the other. He knew this. He understood this.","So Teacher did not have to be disappointed.","As soon as his Civilizational Anchor was completed, he would do what others were afraid of. He would integrate paradox so thoroughly into his existence that contradiction became his strength rather than his vulnerability. And then he would seek his Teacher again.","As he thought all of this grandly, a booming voice emerged from behind him.","\" You cannot stop looking at the rain?\"","The voice carried amusement that pressed against Erwin’s awareness without requiring him to turn around.","\"It is an aftereffect of your biggest enemies, it seems. THE Creature and THE Youngest. They are all allying with each other while telling you they are disappointed in you for allying with others.\"","A massive form emerged from the obsidian observatory, floating through its walls as if solidity were optional for beings at its level.","\"It is always those who consider themselves overly righteous and virtuous that are the greatest hypocrites.\"","The Singular Cognizance came to float beside Erwin, its form a vast singularity surrounded by spinning plates of golden authority that wrapped around its core.","Erwin did not look back at the entity now hovering beside him. His gaze remained fixed on the multicolored rain dissolving everything he had built beyond this protective domain.","\" What are we waiting for, Moloch?\"","The question emerged with calm that belied the frustration simmering beneath his surface.","The Singular Cognizance’s golden plates spun faster as it considered its response.","\" Horus was tangled with THE Creature, that frightening thing, because he was too loud. Makes me realize THE Creature has really been playing with you this whole time.\"","Moloch’s voice held observation rather than accusation.","\" How does that make you feel? Even I am not sure how long that monster has been at THE Proterozoic Scale. You are lucky he was experimenting with Adversity and left you alive for so long.\"","...!","Erwin’s expression remained calm as internally, he forced his anger to simmer down into embers rather than flames. He had no need for rage. Bygones were bygones. The past could not be changed, and raging against it accomplished nothing except wasting energy better spent on the future.","At times, he was lesser.","At times, he was greater.","At times, he was nothing at all.","That was okay.","Existence was not a sprint. Existence was a marathon, and existence was long . Far more powerful beings than him had already died while he was still here. Apex entities who had seemed untouchable had dissolved into memory while a peasant in rags continued walking forward. THE Creature had been playing with him? Fine. The game would continue, and games could be won by those who simply refused to stop playing.","In the end, Erwin simply and paradoxically had to be here.","Being here was enough. Being here was everything. Being here when others had ceased to be was the only victory that truly mattered."]},{"number":5035,"title":"Chapter 5035: Chapter 5034: THE Infiniverse I","paragraphs":["In existence, there are many exceptional beings.","Apex entities who have accumulated authority across eons of cultivation. Primordial Architects who shape the very fabric of reality. Keys of Civilization who embody fundamental truths that predate THE Infinite Unfurling itself.","All of them are dim compared to the brilliance of my Master.","I have witnessed his journey from the moment he first touched Infinity to the moment he conducted it through finite form. I have watched him defy classifications that should have constrained him, shatter limitations that should have contained him, and accumulate authority that should have destroyed him.","Where others struggle across eons to achieve what he accomplishes in moments, where others fall to corruptions he walks through unchanged, where others theorize about possibilities he simply demonstrates, there is no comparison.","And I am his Infiniverse, the extension of his will across Observable Existence, the domain through which his authority flows and in which his people flourish. What I become reflects upon him. What I achieve speaks to his potential. What I build declares to all of existence.","-Declaration of THE Infiniverse, spoken into the void that would become her foundations","---","At this moment.","The core of THE Infiniverse blazed with activity that would have overwhelmed any lesser domain attempting to contain it.","Boundless energies converged toward the central point where all authority within this space originated, seas of Infinities flowing through channels carved by will and saturated with purpose.","Endless Infinite Absolute Seals orbited this core, each one a beacon declaring the sovereignty of THE Youngest!","The humanoid manifestation of THE Infiniverse floated at the center of this convergence, adorned in a bejeweled multicolored dress that shifted through colors as rapidly as thought could follow.","Her hair shone with countless hues that normal perception struggled to separate into distinct tones, and her eyes held depths containing entire Folds worth of compressed existence.","Beside her floated Ruination in illusory crimson-blue form, that beauty whose existence remained tethered to conceptual space rather than physical reality. The holographic figure blazed with light that suggested substance without providing it, presence without physicality, power without the ability to directly express it.","With her eyes closed, THE Infiniverse could feel the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity ready to flood across her entirety.","She perceived it approaching the reforged Muspelheim within her, that realm of primordial fire now integrated into her structure. She sensed it nearing the reforged Agora of Primordial Judgment inside her.","She felt it pressing against the Transcendent Folds she had built, the Wheels of Existence flowing throughout, the Folds of Dreams, Prana, Apollyon, Manadynamics, Apocalypse, Relativity, and countless others flowing within her vast expanse.","And at her very center, she perceived the grand Early Veiled Shore where her Master had his farms.","She was looking at all of this, understanding that when the effects of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity descended, everything would be elevated and enhanced. The Cause her Master had triggered alongside THE Creature would saturate her foundations with authority accumulated across eons. Her structure would be empowered. Her inhabitants would be transformed.","But...","\"It is not enough.\"","HUUM!","Her voice was sharp as she spoke aloud, conviction resonating through her core in ways that made the converging energies tremble. She gazed out across the home of her Master, perceiving every detail of what she had become and measuring it against what she wanted to be.","\"We dream of many things. You have your dreams, I have mine. They all lead back to Master.\"","She turned toward Ruination, her multicolored eyes fixing upon her sister’s illusory form.","\" What are we in the face of all that is unfolding? What are you? What am I?\"","...!","Ruination listened calmly to her sister, those crimson-blue eyes burning with glorious conviction of their own. She didn’t beat around the bush, didn’t offer false comfort, didn’t pretend the questions were anything other than what they were. She...only asked!","\" What do you want to do?\"","THE Infiniverse’s response emerged with certainty refined across countless cycles of contemplation.","\" The goal has been the distinction of an Observable Existence. But how did Observable Existence come about?\"","She gestured with one bejeweled hand, multicolored light trailing from her fingers.","\" There was apparently endless potential, then THE First Cause which ushered in differentiation and undifferentiation, and everything else followed. But has Master not ushered in a Cause alongside THE Creature? It is about to descend.\"","Her expression shifted to something approaching dissatisfaction.","\" But I do not feel like its effects would be enough. I do not want some paltry colorful effects. I want grandness. I want immensity.\"","Her voice rose with hunger that pressed against her own foundations.","\"I want...Quintessence.\"","HUUM!","As she spoke these words, her body began filling with Quintessence Infiniforce.","She held an unbreakable connection with her Master, a bond that allowed her to use what he could use, for she was an extension of his power rather than something separate from it. What flowed through him flowed through her. What he generated, she could access. What he conducted, she could direct within her own domain.","Multicolored light blazed through her humanoid form as Quintessence Infiniforce saturated her existence with density matching what her Master produced within his own finite foundations.","Her eyes became filled with imperious brilliance as she looked at her sister with new purpose crystallizing behind her gaze.","\" Can you pull from Master’s Infinity? Can you pull the Infinity of Observable Existence?\"","She asked this lightly, already knowing the answer. Ruination herself couldn’t physically attack or interact with others, her illusory nature preventing direct engagement with material reality.","But conducting authority was different from physical interaction.","HUUM!","Ruination waved her holographic hands, asking permission from her Master through the connection all of his extensions shared. Naturally, he sent her all that she wanted the moment she requested it, his power flowing through channels that treated her illusory nature as no obstacle whatsoever.","Soon enough, endless seas of blue gathered around Ruination’s crimson-blue form.","Both THE Infiniverse and Ruination moved closer to each other, floating through the core of this vast domain until they sat opposite each other amidst the converging energies.","On one side, THE Infiniverse burned with Quintessence Infiniforce, multicolored brilliance radiating from her form in waves that pressed against reality itself. On the other side, Ruination blazed with conducted Infinity, endless blue authority swirling around her illusory existence in configurations that declared endless potential ready for direction.","Internal generation faced external conduction.","Quintessence faced Infinity.","Two sisters holding two halves of what their Master represented.","Ruination felt the immensity of the moment pressing against her awareness, the significance of what they were about to attempt crystallizing into unavoidable truth.","\"Do you have an idea of what you want to do?\"","THE Infiniverse’s smile carried certainty accumulated across processes many could not perceive.","\"I have been theorizing and thinking for countless possibilities and probabilities in dilated time. I know what I want.\"","Her multicolored eyes blazed brighter.","\"I know what I will build.\"","...!","With such words, Ruination smiled at her sister with expression holding trust refined across their shared existence. She held her palms out toward THE Infiniverse, and endless blue waves of Infinity gathered there, conducted authority from Observable Existence itself converging upon her illusory hands until they held oceans of endless potential compressed into spaces that should not have been able to contain them.","THE Infiniverse brought her own palms toward her sister, Quintessence Infiniforce blazing around her hands in multicolored configurations that declared internal generation ready to merge with external conduction.","She spoke grandly as their hands approached each other.","\" Merely a Cause. If existence can usher a Cause, so can we.\"","Her voice resonated through her entire domain, through every Fold and Wheel and Realm within her vast structure.","\" This Cause shall usher the complete reformation and restructuring of THE Infiniverse. This Cause is meant to usher in an Era of Quintessence.\"","HUUM!","Her hands and Ruination’s hands met.","Brilliant white light unfurled from the point of contact, spreading outward in all directions with speed that exceeded perception. The collision of Quintessence Infiniforce and conducted Infinity produced something unprecedented within this domain, authority meeting authority in configurations that mimicked what her Master had accomplished when his fist met THE Creature’s strike.","A Miniature Cause bloomed.","As it bloomed, tyrannical light flashed across THE Infiniverse’s features. She raised her head with eyes blazing brighter than any star within her domain, her voice erupting with conviction that would reshape everything she contained.","\" This Cause I deem...THE HADEAN EMERGENCE!\"","BOOM!","|Miniature Cause Initiated|","|The collision of internally generated Quintessence Infiniforce with externally conducted Infinity within THE Infiniverse has triggered a Miniature Cause. This event mimics THE First Cause on localized scale, producing effects that will reshape THE Infiniverse according to the will directing its emergence.|","| Cause Classification: THE Hadean Emergence |","|This Cause takes its nature from the primordial processes through which chaotic potential transforms into structured existence. It represents the transition from formless convergence to differentiated architecture, from accumulated resources to organized systems, from raw power to purposeful design.|","...!","|Primary Phase: The Accretion|","|All energies, authorities, and resources within THE Infiniverse shall be gathered and consolidated toward central processes of reformation. Scattered potential shall converge. Disparate elements shall merge. What existed as separate components shall become unified material for reconstruction.|","|The Folds, Wheels, Realms, and structures currently populating THE Infiniverse shall not be destroyed but absorbed into the reconstruction process. Their authority and lifeforms shall be preserved while their configurations are remade according to new architecture.|","THE Infiniverse felt this phase beginning immediately, energies throughout her vast domain responding to the Cause’s demands. The Transcendent Folds she had built began flowing toward her core, not dissolving but liquefying into streams of pure potential that would be reshaped into something grander. The Wheels of Existence stopped their eternal rotations and joined the convergence, their accumulated authority adding to the resources available for reformation.","|Secondary Phase: The Core Descent|","|The densest authorities within THE Infiniverse shall sink toward the absolute center of her existence, forming a Core of Quintessential Authority. This Core shall serve as the heart of all reformation, the source from which new structures emerge, the anchor around which everything else organizes.|","|The Core shall be composed primarily of Quintessence Infiniforce, establishing internal generation as the fundamental nature of THE Infiniverse rather than dependence on external conduction. Infinity shall flow through channels carved by Quintessence, but Quintessence shall remain the foundation.|","HUUM!","THE Infiniverse commanded this descent with will that brooked no resistance.","She felt the densest energies within her existence sinking through layers of converging potential, authority so concentrated that it outweighed everything else within her domain. These energies pressed toward her absolute center, toward the point from which her existence originated, toward the Core that would become the heart of everything she was rebuilding.","Quintessence Infiniforce flooded into this Core with density that exceeded anything she had previously contained. The multicolored authority generated by her Master filled the center of her existence until it became a star of internal production, blazing with brilliance that would power everything constructed around it.","|Tertiary Phase: The Collision|","|A pivotal merger event shall occur between existing structures and the reforming architecture. This collision shall produce the fundamental division between Core and surface, between inner authority and outer expression, between the heart of THE Infiniverse and the realms built around it.|","|From this collision, debris shall be ejected that forms secondary structures orbiting the primary architecture. These secondary structures shall serve as anchors for the Realms to be constructed, providing stable foundations around which existence can organize.|","THE Infiniverse felt the collision occurring as her existing structures met the reforming architecture her Cause demanded. The impact was not destructive but transformative, the meeting of what had been with what would be producing configurations that exceeded either state alone.","Debris from this collision, fragments of authority too dense to integrate smoothly into the primary reformation, ejected outward and began forming secondary structures. These fragments organized themselves into orbital configurations around the emerging Core, providing the skeletal framework upon which her new architecture would be built.","|Quaternary Phase: The Ocean Formation|","|Seas of Quintessence Infiniforce shall emerge across the reforming surface of THE Infiniverse. These oceans shall serve as the medium through which all authority flows within the domain, replacing the channels of pure Infinity with channels of Quintessence saturated by Infinity.|","|Rivers of combined authority shall connect these seas, creating circulation systems that ensure no region of THE Infiniverse exists without access to both Quintessence and Infinity. The internal and external shall merge into unified flow.|","...!"]},{"number":5036,"title":"Chapter 5036: Chapter 5035: THE Infiniverse II","paragraphs":["She commanded the seas, and they obeyed.","Vast oceans of Quintessence Infiniforce began pooling across the reforming surface of her domain, multicolored depths containing authority generated rather than conducted. These seas sparkled with light that came from within rather than reflecting from without, their surfaces rippling with potential that declared internal production as the new natural state.","Rivers of blue Infinity flowed into these multicolored seas, conducted authority from Observable Existence merging with generated Quintessence until separation became impossible. The waterways carved channels through the emerging landscape, creating circulation that would ensure her entire domain remained saturated with both types of authority.","|Quintenary Phase: The Atmosphere Emergence|","|From the combination of Quintessence seas and Infinity rivers, an atmosphere of Primal Authority shall rise across THE Infiniverse. This atmosphere shall be dense with potential, saturated with power, thick with the combined essence of internal generation and external conduction.|","| Beings within THE Infiniverse shall breathe this Primal Authority with every moment of their existence. Their foundations shall be constantly nourished by ambient power that requires no cultivation to absorb. Growth shall become the natural state rather than the achieved state.|","THE Infiniverse raised her head higher as this phase began, feeling atmosphere rising from her newly formed seas like mist ascending from warm water meeting cold air. The Primal Authority spread across her domain in layers of increasing density, creating gradients that would challenge those seeking to ascend while empowering those already established.","This atmosphere held qualities unlike anything Observable Existence naturally provided. Beings breathing it would absorb power with every breath. Their cultivation would accelerate simply by existing within her domain. THE Infiniverse would become not merely a home for her Master’s people, but an incubator for advancement that exceeded anything external environments could provide!","Oh!","|Structural Phase Initiated|","|THE Hadean Emergence now transitions from foundational reformation to architectural construction. The Cause shall be directed by the will of THE Infiniverse to produce specific configurations matching her vision.|","THE Infiniverse spoke, and her voice resonated through every reforming portion of her domain.","\" This Cause will give rise to THREE THOUSAND REALMS OF QUINTESSENCE!\"","Her multicolored eyes blazed with authority that pressed against the Cause itself, bending its natural processes toward her specific demands.","\" Each one filled with infinitely increasing and expanding stellar bodies, worlds, realms, Wheels of Existence, and Folds!\"","HUUM!","|Structural Directive Accepted|","|THE Infiniverse shall be organized according to the following architecture:|","| THE THREE THOUSAND REALMS OF QUINTESSENCE|","|Each Realm represents a unique configuration of Quintessence Infiniforce and Infinity, a distinct expression of combined internal generation and external conduction. No two Realms are identical. Each one provides different conditions for existence, different challenges for advancement, different opportunities for growth. Together, they form a complete Existence contained within a single domain.|","BOOM!","Three thousand Realms began crystallizing from the reforming potential of her domain. They emerged like stars igniting across a newborn cosmos, points of existence blazing into being where only potential had existed moments before.","The First Realm emerged around a core of absolute Quintessence, worlds forming from condensed authority, stellar bodies of compressed power orbiting around central points of even greater density.","The Second Realm followed immediately, its architecture representing different configurations entirely. This Realm blazed with colors different from the First, its internal structure optimized for different types of existence.","The Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth Realms emerged in rapid succession, each one unique, each one complete, each one filled with infinitely increasing and expanding stellar bodies that would provide homes for whatever beings eventually populated them.","THE Infiniverse directed this emergence with precision.","She ensured that rivers of Infinity flowed between the Realms, connecting them through waterways of conducted authority that allowed travel and communication between configurations. She commanded that seas of Quintessence Infiniforce filled the spaces within each Realm, providing ambient power that would nourish any existence dwelling there. She demanded that the atmosphere of Primal Authority permeated everything, ensuring that growth remained the natural state throughout her domain.","The Hundredth Realm emerged with stellar bodies already ancient despite their newborn status, time within THE Infiniverse operating according to her will rather than external constraints.","The Five Hundredth Realm blazed into existence with Wheels of Existence already rotating within its structure, mechanisms of advancement integrated from the moment of formation.","The Thousandth Realm crystallized with Folds of condensed authority already layered throughout its architecture, shortcuts and pathways that would allow rapid traversal for those capable of perceiving them.","And still the emergence continued.","THE Infiniverse felt herself expanding beyond anything she had previously contained, her domain growing to accommodate the three thousand configurations her Cause demanded.","Where she had been vast before, she became incomprehensible now. Where she had contained multitudes, she now contained infinities of multitudes.","At the Two Thousandth Realm, she opened herself to the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity.","The multicolored rainfall her Master had triggered alongside THE Creature flooded into her domain, but she commanded its effects with authority born of Miniature Cause. The waters could fall upon her environment, empowering structures and saturating landscapes with additional authority. But they would not test her inhabitants, would not dissolve foundations too weak to contain what was being poured into them, would not trigger the extinction events currently reshaping Observable Existence beyond her boundaries.","She negated the Epoch’s effects on her lifeforms while applying its effects to her environment.","The rainfall became nourishment rather than challenge.","The Pluvial Epoch merged with THE Hadean Emergence, two Causes working in harmony because she commanded them to work in harmony . Her Master’s external Cause empowered her internal Cause, the combination producing results beyond what either could have accomplished alone!","The Two Thousand Five Hundredth Realm emerged already saturated with combined authority, its foundations built from merged Quintessence and Infinity that declared both internal and external as equally native to its structure.","The Two Thousand Nine Hundredth Realm blazed into existence with populations already manifesting within its bounds, beings emerging from pure potential because her architecture demanded inhabitants to fill the spaces she was creating.","The Two Thousand Nine Hundred Ninety-Ninth Realm crystallized with complexity representing the accumulated refinement of every Realm that had emerged before it.","And then the Three Thousandth Realm completed.","THE Infiniverse felt the final configuration settling into place, the last piece of her new architecture finding its position within the vast structure she had built. Three thousand Realms of Quintessence now filled her domain, each one connected to every other through rivers of Infinity and seas of Quintessence Infiniforce. Each one represented a specific configuration of existence. Each one provided unique conditions for the beings that would dwell within.","And at the center of everything, the Core of Quintessential Authority blazed with brilliance powering the entire structure. Her heart beat with rhythm that sent waves of generated authority flowing through every Realm.","She...had become something beyond what she had been, a domain rebuilt from foundational level according to architecture designed for maximum advancement of those dwelling within.","The Osmontian Shore, The Early Veiled Shore remained at her absolute center, her Master’s farms protected by layers of Realms that would require traversing thousands of configurations to reach. His home sat within the safest position possible, surrounded by the full complexity of her new architecture.","|THE Hadean Emergence: Complete|","|THE Infiniverse has been restructured according to Miniature Cause direction. The following architecture has been established:|","|Core: Quintessential Authority Heart generating continuous Quintessence Infiniforce|","|Structure: Three Thousand Realms of Quintessence, each unique in configuration and purpose|","|Medium: Seas of Quintessence Infiniforce and Rivers of Infinity providing circulation throughout|","|Atmosphere: Primal Authority saturating all regions and empowering ambient advancement|","|Integration: Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity merged with environmental enhancement|","|Inhabitants of THE Infiniverse shall experience accelerated advancement through ambient Primal Authority absorption. Growth requires no active cultivation within this domain. Existence itself becomes advancement. Breathing becomes cultivation. Living becomes strengthening.|","|All regions within THE Infiniverse are connected through waterways permitting travel between Realms. Beings may navigate through different configurations of existence, learning from each Realm they encounter while progressing toward destinations matching their ultimate potential.|","...!","|Classification Established|","| THE Infiniverse has achieved distinction from Observable Existence through Miniature Cause reformation . This domain now operates according to internal architecture rather than external constraint.|","| New Classification: THE SEED OF OBSERVABLE EXISTENCE|","|THE Infiniverse exists as seed from which new Observable Existence could potentially germinate. Its internal architecture mirrors the complexity of Observable Existence while remaining distinct from it. Its Core generates authority rather than conducting it. Its Realms organize existence according to will rather than natural law.|","|This Seed is actively continuing its transformation. THE Hadean Emergence has established foundational architecture, but growth continues. New stellar bodies form within the Three Thousand Realms. New worlds crystallize from condensed authority. New possibilities emerge from the interactions between configurations.|","| THE Seed of Observable Existence, THE Infiniverse, has been established.|","|Active transformation continues.|","BOOM!","THE Infiniverse opened her multicolored eyes and gazed upon what she had built.","And the first thing she did...was make a prayer for the poor souls that would stand against her Master.","Those poor fucking souls.","She would trample them before they even knew what was happening as she felt her scope of power.","Three Thousand Realms of Quintessence stretched across her domain in configurations that would require lifetimes to fully explore. Rivers of Infinity connected seas of Quintessence Infiniforce in circulation systems that ensured no region lacked for authority. The Primal Authority atmosphere saturated everything with ambient power that would elevate any being breathing it.","She had become something unprecedented!","She had become THE Seed of Observable Existence.","And she...was truly just getting started as man, there was much to be done!"]},{"number":5037,"title":"Chapter 5037: Chapter 5036: THE Infiniverse III","paragraphs":["Noah had just finished waking Temporal, Eon, and Abaddon from their involuntary slumber.","The three of them were slowly regaining awareness, their foundations stabilizing after the unconsciousness forced upon them by Naldine’s display of THE Limitless Armature.","That glorious set of bones burning with THE Proterozoic Scale!","Temporal looked confused but functional, quickly coming back.","Eon seemed disoriented, her dark eyes flickering with awareness that was entirely her own for the first time in eons. Abaddon remained ashen, his hand still pressed against the chest where his Claim of Chaos no longer resided as he worked through it.","Noah stood and turned toward Temporal, preparing to give instructions for keeping watch over the other two while he and Naldine departed for wherever this Singular Cognizance supposedly waited.","\"Keep an eye on them while I am gone. Make sure they do not do anything stu-\"","BOOM!","A terrifying aura erupted from Noah’s body without warning.","It felt like a heavy and suffocating force pressing outward in all directions, reality itself groaning under pressure that radiated from his finite form. The multicolored rainfall of the Pluvial Epoch seemed to part around him, unable to fall through the density now emanating from his existence.","Temporal’s eyes rolled back immediately, his ancient form crumpling to the ground before he could even process what was happening. Eon collapsed beside him, her newly restored consciousness unable to withstand the pressure now flooding from Noah’s body. Abaddon fell last, his weakened foundations offering even less resistance than the others.","\"...\"","All three lay unconscious again, felled by whatever had just emerged from Noah’s existence.","Naldine looked toward him with cold gaze, her singularity-dotted eyes narrowing as she sensed something she clearly recognized.","\" You...are still playing with Miniature Causes? One is not enough?\"","Noah rose up with expression of genuine innocence, his hands raised in gesture of denial.","\"It really was not me this time.\"","And it truly was not.","He could sense what THE Infiniverse had just done through their unbreakable connection, perceiving the aftermath of a Cause she had initiated alongside Ruination within his domain.","THE Hadean Emergence . Three Thousand Realms of Quintessence. A complete restructuring of everything THE Infiniverse contained, transforming her from vast domain into something unprecedented.","THE Seed of Observable Existence.","He couldn’t even complain to say why not a direct jump to Observable Existence because that would be far too grand. But...","The power of this transformation flowed through him because THE Infiniverse was an extension of his Existence rather than something separate. What she became, he partially became. What she achieved, he partially achieved. This was how their connection worked.","Her restructuring had created resonance through their connection that now pressed outward from his finite form with a force overwhelming anything at THE First Scale.","He had the authority of a Seed of Observable Existence flowing through him.","His finite existence somehow held up under this pressure, his foundations refusing to rupture despite containing force that should have exceeded what beings at his Scale could manage. But he could feel all this authority pressing onto something specific within him, concentrating on his Organ of Civilization surrounded by Quintessence Infiniforce.","An unfathomable process was beginning there.","He could not yet grasp what was happening, could not perceive the full scope of the transformation initiating within his foundations. But something was changing. Something was responding to the Seed’s authority flowing through him. Something was starting that would take time to complete.","For now, he controlled the terrifying pressure leaking from his existence, pulling it back within himself through will alone. The force receded, contained once more within his finite form rather than radiating outward to flatten everything nearby.","But his mind raced with possibilities.","His power paired with the power of THE Infiniverse. The Quintessence Infiniforce he generated internally combined with the authority of a Seed of Observable Existence. Could this combination violate existence itself? Could it potentially allow him to touch those unfathomable beings at THE Second Scale?","Before he made such a heavy claim, he would need to understand more about THE Proterozoic Scale. He would need to learn the mechanisms through which Second Scale beings operated, the vulnerabilities they possessed, the methodologies they employed.","He needed information that his current knowledge simply did not contain.","And hey, he had a walking, talking encyclopedia of information right here.","He turned to Naldine and smiled brilliantly, his heavy pressure now completely contained within his existence. She had knowledge accumulated across eons of operating at heights he was only beginning to perceive.","She looked back at him with cold expression that suggested his smile did not charm her in the slightest.","\" One of these days, you will be wrong. Remember my warnings then.\"","Her voice held certainty.","\" Do not keep messing around with Miniature Causes when your power cannot control what can happen. I will repeat that as many times as I need to.\"","She glanced down at the unconscious forms of Temporal, Eon, and Abaddon sprawled across the recovering landscape of Jotunheim. Her expression shifted to something approaching disdain as she observed three beings who had been felled twice in rapid succession by forces they could not withstand.","\" For now, let us go.\"","She shook her head slowly while looking at the collapsed trio.","\" Weak things that keep losing consciousness from pressure alone...\"","She turned around and began walking, her Second Scale presence pressing against the multicolored rainfall as she moved.","Noah let Naldine leave first, watching her Second Scale presence carve a path through the multicolored rainfall as she departed.","Then he looked down at the three bodies sprawled before him. Temporal lay with purple temporal currents still flickering weakly around his form. Eon breathed slowly, her dark hair spread across the recovering ground of Jotunheim. And Abaddon remained ashen and hollow, his chest rising and falling with breaths that no longer carried the authority of Chaos.","An illusory consciousness separated from Noah’s current body, stepping out of himself like a shadow gaining substance. This fragment of his awareness moved toward the unconscious trio and sat down beside them, cross-legged amidst the multicolored rivers still flooding Jotunheim.","He placed his hand on Abaddon’s head and reached into the foundations of what remained.","His earlier sense was confirmed. The Claim of Chaos had not simply dissipated or dissolved. It had been taken, pulled through bonds that should not have permitted such transfer, claimed by someone who had been waiting for exactly this moment of weakness.","\" Emotive.\"","His eyes flashed with chilly light as he thought about the Broken Doll he had spared not long ago. He had slapped her across existence and knocked out her teeth.","She had now grown very ambitious.","She had taken the Claim of Chaos itself, ascending from whatever she had been before to something that would require reevaluation. The manic entity...","Noah thought of many things as his consciousness remained beside the unconscious trio. He thought about many things.","He left this consciousness here to observe and protect while the three recovered.","His main body took a step and crossed vast distances, leaving Jotunheim behind to catch up with the walking, talking encyclopedia who had slowed her pace to wait for him, even though she never looked back.","---","In THE Infiniverse.","In THE Seed of Observable Existence.","Noah stood upon the golden sands of his Early Veiled Shore, observing a landscape transformed beyond what he remembered from his last visit. Abodes dotted the terrain now, structures of crystallized authority rising from foundations saturated with Quintessence Infiniforce. Hundreds of forming plots stretched across the shore.","It was oddly quiet and serene here.","Not many remained on the Early Veiled Shore at this moment, as most had been sent to THE Yggdrheim to undergo strengthening of their existence through adversity. The struggles occurring there would forge his people into something capable of surviving the conflicts spreading across Observable Existence. They would return transformed or they would not return at all.","Well, no, they would return!","The only one who happened to be here right now rose from a nearby plot of land.","Amelia Osmont brushed golden soil from her hands as she walked toward her son, her eyes already fixed on the skies above. She could instinctively sense the shocking changes that had taken place within this domain, her foundations resonating with transformations that affected everything dwelling within THE Infiniverse.","She was, after all, the mother of a finite being filled with glory!","She looked up and saw golden raindrops descending alongside rivers of multicolored brilliance cascading from heights that seemed infinite.","\" Did you manage to pass a significant milestone?\"","Noah smiled at his mother’s words, her ability to read situations never failing to remind him of where certain aspects of his own perception came from.","\" Somewhat significant.\"","He watched the golden rain falling across the Early Veiled Shore, each droplet carrying Quintessence Infiniforce that would nourish whatever it touched.","\" The things around me seem increasingly complex. They are not so simple like in the past. There is not a single enemy or ruler of a domain threatening us, but a collection of beings who lived for eons, each with their own schemes of what they want in existence.\"","He paused, considering how to explain conflicts that spanned Scales of power his mother could not yet perceive.","\" We are just getting mixed up in them here and there, but I am riding the waves so far.\"","His mother nodded slowly, her expression holding the particular concern only parents could manage regardless of how powerful their children became.","She raised her hands to feel the raindrops of Quintessence Infiniforce landing on her palms, the multicolored authority absorbing into her foundations with each contact.","\" Do not push yourself too much. I know you are pushing the others too so they can protect themselves, but take everything in strides. Focus on your farming, focus on your son.\"","Her expression shifted to something more mischievous.","\" Maybe find me another daughter-in-law.\"","Noah shook his head at the ridiculous words.","\" Come on. Let us see how our home is changing.\"","He waved his hand and multicolored light gathered before them, Quintessence Infiniforce condensing into physical form through will alone. A small boat materialized from the condensed authority, its hull burning with the same multicolored brilliance now filling his existence. The vessel floated above the golden sands, waiting for passengers.","Noah helped his mother board before stepping onto the boat himself. The moment his feet touched the deck, the vessel rose higher, lifting them above the Early Veiled Shore and carrying them outward toward the vastness now surrounding his farms.","What he saw was utter glory.","The Three Thousand Realms of Quintessence stretched across THE Infiniverse in configurations that defied easy comprehension. Each Realm blazed with distinct light declaring its unique nature, colors and authorities mixing.","The first Realm they approached shone with golden light carrying the essence of Dreams. It expanded outward endlessly like a flat plane of crystallized imagination, landscapes formed from concepts that only slumbering minds could perceive. Rivers of Infinity surged around its boundaries, connecting this Realm to others through waterways of conducted authority. Within its depths, Noah could see structures forming from pure potential, cities and forests and mountains emerging from the dream sands that now had physical reality.","His mother gasped beside him as their boat carried them past this first Realm toward another.","The second Realm burned with crimson-gold light of Helios, solar authority condensed into a region where fire and radiance served as natural law. Stellar bodies orbited within its expanse, suns of varying sizes and intensities providing illumination that would have blinded lesser beings. New suns and stellar bodies were being born...infinitely.","The heat emanating from this Realm pressed against their boat without threatening them, warmth recognizing its master and his mother as welcome rather than intruders.","They continued forward, and a third Realm came into view blazing with verdant light of Prana. Life authority saturated every aspect of this region, forests growing across surfaces that seemed to have no end.","Creatures moved through those forests, beings formed from pure vitality.","A fourth Realm shimmered with silver-blue light of Lunar essence, darkness and reflection mixing in configurations that created beauty through shadow rather than illumination. This Realm seemed quieter than the others, its authority more subtle, its gifts requiring contemplation to perceive.","A fifth Realm crackled with violet light of Apollyon, destructive potential contained within boundaries that prevented it from consuming everything nearby.","On and on they traveled, their boat carrying them through spaces between Realms where seas of Quintessence Infiniforce lapped against shores of condensed authority. Noah counted dozens of distinct configurations as they passed, each Realm unique, each one representing different aspects of existence given physical form.","The Realm of Manadynamics blazed with pure blue authority that reminded him of his earliest cultivation, Mana in its most fundamental expression saturating everything within.","The Realm of Apocalypse held configurations of ending and transformation, cycles of destruction and rebirth playing out across landscapes that seemed to change each time he looked away.","The Realm of Relativity bent around itself in ways that made his perception struggle, space and time operating according to rules that shifted based on the observer.","The Realm of Dreams continued expanding in the distance, its golden light now seeming like just one star among thousands filling the wonders of his domain.","His mother sat beside him in silence, her eyes wide with wonder. She had known her son was powerful. She had understood that he operated at heights she could not fully perceive. But seeing the scale of what he had built, what THE Infiniverse had become...","Her voice emerged soft against the vastness surrounding them.","\" This is...beautiful.\"","He nodded without speaking, his attention fixed on the connections between Realms rather than the Realms themselves. Rivers of Infinity flowed between every configuration, conducted authority providing circulation that ensured no region existed in isolation. Seas of Quintessence Infiniforce filled the spaces between, generated authority from his own existence now serving as the medium through which everything connected.","The Primal Authority atmosphere saturated all of it, thick with combined Quintessence and Infinity that would empower any being breathing within this domain.","And still they traveled, their boat carrying them past the five hundredth Realm, the seven hundredth, the thousandth. Each one held unique characteristics. Each one provided different conditions for existence. Each one represented a piece of the vast architecture THE Infiniverse had constructed through her Hadean Emergence.","Noah’s eyes began shining with profundity as epiphany crystallized within his awareness.","He saw the Realms utilizing Infinity in configurations he had never considered. He observed how conducted authority enhanced environments rather than individual beings. He perceived the methodology through which external things could be bathed in endless potential without triggering THE Gamaidjan’s corruption.","\" Infinity can be used in so many different ways.\"","He spoke to himself, his voice carrying revelation that pressed against his understanding of what he could accomplish.","\" While the self is hard to bathe with Infinity, external things like Realms and Sacred Herbs are easier. The self risks corruption. But things outside the self have no identity to corrupt.\"","His eyes burned brighter as the implications expanded within his mind.","\" And if I utilize Infinity even more, apart from herbs and Realms, so many things can be made Infinite. Armaments. Structures. Domains. Anything external to consciousness itself could potentially hold endless authority without suffering the consequences...\"","HUUM!","The realization was one he already knew somewhat, but he could be more...comprehensive.","THE Infiniverse had integrated Infinity into her structure, into her Realms, into the environment itself rather than the consciousnesses dwelling within.","The environment could be Infinite without going mad.","The tools could be Infinite without losing identity.","Only the self required the careful progression that Naldine had described, the Anchoring and Transformation and eventual Transcendence that protected consciousness from corruption, and even that didn’t apply too much to him.","On a boat with his mother, Noah’s eyes burned with light of profundity as he toured his changing home. Three Thousand Realms stretched around them in every direction, a wonder built from Quintessence and Infinity that declared his domain something unprecedented in Observable Existence.","And he was only beginning to understand what it could become."]},{"number":5038,"title":"Chapter 5038: Chapter 5037: Innovators and Destroyers I","paragraphs":["Among the vast reserves of knowledge THE Mnemonic Leviathan had accumulated since its emergence under THE Beholder, certain patterns repeated themselves across eons of observation.","Beings fell into categories regardless of their power or their Scale, regardless of their Civilizations or their ambitions. Some built. Others burned. The distinction defined more about their nature than any classification ever could.","THE Infiniverse and its Master belonged among the Innovators of Observable Existence. The ongoing forging of Three Thousand Realms showed architecture unprecedented in recorded memory. Innovation required vision that destruction never demanded.","THE Creature stood among the greatest Innovators THE Mnemonic Leviathan had ever catalogued. Humble origins as a Primordial Architect had given way to something defying classification entirely, a being who had shattered what he was to become what no one else had become.","What he built, what he represented, what he had achieved through methodology no other Primordial Architect had dared attempt, all of it spoke to innovation refined across existence itself.","And then there were those who destroyed.","Horus existed within the Leviathan’s reserves of knowledge as a destroyer of considerable accomplishment. His methodologies claimed countless beings who could not resist what he wielded.","Yet when measuring pure lethality, when calculating bodies dissolved and existences ended, Horus was not the worst the Leviathan had knowledge of.","Among the worst destroyers was a Singular Cognizance that THE Mnemonic Leviathan had met alongside its Progenitor eons before THE Infinite Unfurling reshaped everything.","THE Beholder had led them to a region of Observable Existence where something terrible was being tested, and there they had encountered Malachar, THE Extinction Artificer.","That Singular Cognizance had been experimenting in engineering a virus capable of inflicting existence itself.","Not beings and certainly not Civilizations, but Existence.","Malachar had designed weavings of destruction so precise that they could target the fundamental nature of what something was rather than simply ending what something did. And it had tested this engineered horror against an entire group of beings born from the intersection of differentiation and undifferentiation, ancient entities known as Antediluvian Ones who had existed since shortly after THE First Cause imposed structure upon chaos.","All Antediluvian Ones inflicted with this engineered weaving had perished.","Those at THE First Scale had died screaming as their existence unraveled from within. Those at THE Second Scale had died more slowly, their greater foundations providing only prolonged suffering rather than survival.","Every single one touched by Malachar’s creation had ceased to exist, their classifications and their power meaningless against destruction designed specifically to unmake them.","There were many destroyers across Observable Existence. Horus, Erwin, Renne, and Beowulf and many others whose names filled the Leviathan’s reserves with records of atrocity and ending.","But Malachar, THE Extinction Artificer, would undoubtedly be considered among the more accomplished ones. If ever that Singular Cognizance engineered something similar against Undivided Ones or Primordial Architects, would any remain today? Would Observable Existence itself survive such targeted annihilation?","THE Mnemonic Leviathan had once asked THE Beholder regarding who would ultimately prove most accomplished in Observable Existence. Its Progenitor had considered the question with attention rarely granted to anything, that singular eye processing variables across eons of accumulated observation.","THE Beholder’s answer had been simple.","Those who destroy always had an easier time accomplishing their weavings. To unmake required only force and precision. To create required vision and patience and understanding that destruction never demanded. A child could tear down what masters spent lifetimes building.","To destroy was much easier than to innovate.","Innovators or destroyers. Builders or burners. Those who pushed existence toward greater complexity or those who pulled it back toward the simplicity of undifferentiation. THE Mnemonic Leviathan slumbered now within one of the boundlessly forming Realms inside THE Infiniverse, its ancient form resting amidst innovation unprecedented in its reserves of knowledge.","It wondered, as consciousness drifted through memories spanning eons, just what type of beings would end up on top.","Would the Innovators prevail through creations that outlasted those who built them?","Or would the destroyers simply unmake everything before innovation could complete its work?","The answer remained unwritten, and THE Mnemonic Leviathan found that uncertainty more fascinating than any knowledge it had already accumulated.","—Reflections of THE Mnemonic Leviathan, recorded during slumber within THE Seed of Observable Existence","---","As Noah continued his journey across the Three Thousand Realms of his home, he came across an entire Realm holding the composition of none other than Muspelheim.","Vibrant flames and weavings of immensity permeated throughout this region, crimson-gold authority radiating from structures that had been integrated into THE Infiniverse’s new architecture.","He was about to steer the boat past this Realm when he heard that heavy voice call out to him.","A certain pink dolphin’s tone pressed against his awareness from within the flames, lazy and unhurried as always yet somehow demanding attention regardless.","Noah smiled and steered the multicolored boat toward the fiery crimson-gold Realm.","The vessel carried him and his mother through boundaries separating configurations, crossing from the space between Realms into the heart of reformed Muspelheim itself. Heat pressed against them immediately. The flames parted as Noah’s authority declared his sovereignty over everything within this domain.","A massive crimson-gold mountain dominated the center of this Realm, its slopes releasing flows of lava burning with Quintessence Infiniforce rather than simple molten rock. The liquid authority cascaded down its sides in rivers that would have dissolved anything lacking sufficient foundations, pooling at the base in lakes of concentrated power.","In the center of that lava, a crystalline crimson-gold tree irradiated immense heat that pressed against perception itself. Its branches reached toward heights that seemed infinite within this Realm, its roots drinking deep from the molten authority surrounding it. The tree pulsed with life that had nothing to do with biology and everything to do with power given vegetative form.","And basking within the lava beside that tree, lounging with laziness that seemed impossible given the environment, floated the massive form of a pink dolphin.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","Noah had called this ancient entity into his home so he could steal, ahem, obtain its knowledge.","The Leviathan possessed reserves of information accumulated across eons of existence.","He nodded toward the pink dolphin as his boat came to rest near the edge of the lava pool.","\" Do you have something new to share? I was in the middle of profundities and epiphanies.\"","The Mnemonic Leviathan’s massive form shifted slightly within the molten authority, one eye opening to regard Noah with attention that belied its lazy posture.","\"I was just dreaming about Innovators and destroyers. Contemplating which type of being would ultimately prevail across Observable Existence.\"","The dolphin’s voice rumbled through the Realm, somehow audible despite the crackling of flames all around.","\" But I also had to ask something. My Progenitor has sent word to check my status. Is it acceptable to speak about where we are located?\"","...!"]},{"number":5039,"title":"Chapter 5039: Chapter 5038: Innovators and Destroyers II","paragraphs":["Noah frowned at such words.","The location of his home was a secret for reasons. Overly powerful beings could not be simply told or given the coordinates of where he was.","\" Who is your Progenitor? What Scale of existence are they in?\"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan paused before answering, its massive form settling deeper into the lava as if the question required consideration despite having an obvious answer.","\" They should be on THE Second Scale. Known as THE Beholder. A Singular Cognizance, though you may not understand what that classification means. It refers to entities that emerged during the age of nothingness before differentiation taught existence how to have boundaries. Singular Cognizances predate most of what currently lives, their perspectives shaped by observing...\"","The pink dolphin had begun to ramble on with its explanation, but Noah’s eyes had already widened with surprise.","THE Beholder?","THE Beholder had helped him not too long ago. He had not expected any connection between that ancient entity and this lazy, good-for-nothing pink dolphin lounging in his lava pools. Well, both loved to observe.","His eyes shone brilliantly as he interrupted the Leviathan’s rambling.","\" How deeply are you and THE Beholder connected?\"","The pink dolphin seemed almost pleased by the question.","\" Few in existence inherited the weavings of the distant observer. THE Beholder seeded portions of itself across eons...\"","The Leviathan’s voice grew more formal as it discussed its origins.","\" Myself and THE Baboon of Wisdom were the only two to successfully stem from the weavings of THE Beholder. We carry portions of our Progenitor’s accumulated observation within our foundations, serving as extensions of its awareness across regions it cannot directly perceive.\"","...!","There was also a Baboon of Wisdom?","A baboon and a dolphin. Existence was truly unique in the configurations it produced.","Noah thought about this revelation for a moment. Naldine was moving with one of his bodies as she sought for them to meet a Singular Cognizance aligned with their interests. If he could have a friendly Singular Cognizance like THE Beholder potentially come to him, why not?","\" Tell THE Beholder exactly where you are and who you are with.\"","His words emerged as command rather than request.","\" Let your Progenitor know that THE Youngest has built something unprecedented within Observable Existence, and that THE Beholder is welcome to observe it firsthand.\"","The Mnemonic Leviathan’s eyes gleamed with something approaching excitement despite its lazy demeanor.","\"It will be done.\"","Noah nodded at the confirmation before turning his attention toward the crystalline tree rising from the center of the lava pool. Its crimson-gold branches pulsed with authority accumulated since THE Hadean Emergence first triggered, a Sacred Plant that had formed alongside everything else within the reformed Infiniverse.","He emerged from the boat and walked across the surface of the lava. His mother remained behind, watching her son approach the tree with curiosity.","Noah reached the tree’s base and looked upward at branches spreading across heights that seemed to contain their own infinities. One particular branch caught his attention, smaller than its siblings but pulsing with intensity.","He waved his hand.","The branch separated from the tree without resistance, cutting itself free at his command and floating down toward his waiting palm. The moment his fingers closed around it, heat flooded through his awareness alongside prompts materializing before his vision.","|Item Acquired|","|Name: Ember Branch of the Hadean Tree|","|Origin: First Sacred Flora to emerge during THE Hadean Emergence within THE Seed of Observable Existence. Crystallized from concentrated Quintessence Infiniforce and primordial fire authority during the formation of the Three Thousand Realms.|","|Description: A branch severed from the Hadean Tree, containing authority sufficient to function as weapon against Civilizations at Fundamental Depth. Strikes from this branch carry primordial fire that burns foundations rather than flesh, damaging the structure of what beings have built rather than merely their physical forms. Can greatly wound Fundamental Depth entities and their Civilizations through direct contact.|","Noah smiled at the details as profundities continued swirling through his mind.","He had infused Infinities into a Sacred Herb before, and the process had allowed him to smoothly transition from Countable to Uncountable. The methodology worked. External objects could contain endless authority without suffering THE Gamaidjan’s corruption because they lacked consciousness to corrupt.","So what if he filled Infinity into an item like this branch?","\" Flow. Flow gloriously.\"","He whispered calmly to the branch, his voice carrying command that reality itself would obey.","In the next moment, vibrant multicolored waves of Quintessence Infiniforce flooded from his body. The internally generated authority poured into the branch without resistance, filling its crystalline structure with endless potential that expanded rather than contained. Infinity from Observable Existence joined the Quintessence, conducted authority merging with generated authority within the branch’s foundations.","The process was instant.","The process was boundless.","The process was complete before Noah could fully perceive what he had accomplished.","BOOM!","A pillar of multicolored brilliance erupted from Noah’s hand, continuing upward across the entire Realm of reformed Muspelheim. The light pressed against the boundaries separating this configuration from others, declaring that something unprecedented had just occurred within THE Seed of Observable Existence.","In his hands, the branch had transformed.","It pulsed and shook with authority that seemed barely contained within its crystalline form. Auroras of Infinity symbols swirled around its length, endless loops declaring the nature of what now filled this weapon. The pressure radiating from it alone was terrifying, force leaking from its surface despite Noah’s grip attempting to contain what he had created.","New prompts materialized before his vision.","|Infinity Armament Forged|","| Name: THE Hadean Infinibrand|","|Classification: First Infinity Armament forged under THE Youngest|","|Origin: Ember Branch of the Hadean Tree infused with boundless Quintessence Infiniforce and conducted Infinity from Observable Existence. Represents the first successful integration of endless authority into weaponized form.|","|Primary Capability: Can infinitely strike any Civilization with equivalent force that most Absolute Depth entities cannot withstand. Each strike carries the full pressure of Infinity compressed into physical impact, damaging foundations in ways that regeneration cannot easily address.|","|Secondary Capability: Can only be wielded by someone possessing understanding of or relation to Infinity. Beings lacking such connection will find the Armament refusing their grasp, its authority rejecting those unworthy of conducting what it contains.|","|Tertiary Capability: Endlessly generates Infinity within its structure, accumulating authority that can be unleashed all at once for strikes vastly exceeding normal output. The longer the Armament is held without attacking, the greater the force of its eventual release.|","|Limitation: Minimal effectiveness against anything at THE Proterozoic Scale.|","Noah looked at his latest innovation, THE Hadean Infinibrand pulsing in his grip as Infinity continued generating within its crystalline form.","He nodded slowly.","Naldine had told him much about THE Proterozoic Scale, about the methodologies those beings employed and the transformations they underwent to wield Infinity safely. The gap was fundamental rather than quantitative.","But gaps could be bridged through innovation rather than simple accumulation.","In addition to his already burning and widespread Infinity, if he also decked himself with Infinity Armaments among other things, he could bridge that gap slowly. Not through single overwhelming power, but through accumulated advantages that stacked until the gap became navigable. Weapons that struck with Infinity. Armor that deflected with Infinity. Tools that manipulated with Infinity. Environments that supported with Infinity.","Layer upon layer upon layer until even Proterozoic Scale entities would be...reachable.","As all of this happened, he continued paying attention to his Organ of Civilization surrounded by Quintessence Infiniforce. The transformation of THE Infiniverse was affecting something within him, the immensity flowing throughout his existence pressing against that particular aspect of his foundations. Something was changing there, responding to his domain becoming a Seed of Observable Existence.","He simply did not know what it was transforming into.","Not yet.","By the time he turned around, the Hadean Infinibrand still pulsing in his grip, he saw his mother talking with the slumbering pink dolphin. THE Mnemonic Leviathan had shifted position to better face Amelia, answering all her questions calmly while she sat at the edge of the lava pool with curiosity.","Noah smiled at the scene."]},{"number":5040,"title":"Chapter 5040: Chapter 5039: Conviction! I","paragraphs":["Naldine had observed Primordial Architects across eons of coexistence at THE Second Scale, and she had learned to read them within moments of meeting.","Some projected power through displays meant to intimidate. They blazed with their Civilizations at every opportunity, announced their presence through pressure that crushed everything nearby, demanded acknowledgment through force that left no room for alternative responses.","These were the weak ones. They required external validation because internal certainty eluded them. Beowulf fell into this category despite his accomplishments. Horus as well. Their need to be seen as powerful revealed the hollow spaces within their foundations where true conviction should have resided.","Others operated through silence and observation, moving through existence without announcing themselves, accomplishing objectives before anyone realized they had arrived.","These possessed greater strength than the loud ones, but their quietness often stemmed from fear rather than confidence. They avoided confrontation because uncertainty plagued them. They gathered information obsessively because they doubted their ability to adapt without preparation.","THE Arboreal Warden Yggvaros demonstrated this quality, powerful beyond question yet forever waiting, forever watching, forever hesitating before the decisive moments that might define his legacy.","The truly strong existed in neither category.","They did not need to project because projection implied audience. They did not need to hide because hiding implied threat. They simply were what they were, their existence radiating conviction so fundamental that doubt could find no purchase within their foundations.","THE Creature embodied this quality more completely than any being Naldine had encountered. That entity did not announce his power or conceal it. He simply existed, and existence bent around him because his certainty about what he was exceeded reality’s certainty about what it was.","The strongest psychological quality an existence could possess was not power. It was not intelligence. It was not even wisdom accumulated across eons of careful observation.","It was conviction about one’s own existence.","The absolute, unshakeable certainty that you were exactly what you believed yourself to be. That your path was correct not because evidence supported it but because you walked it. That your Civilization represented truth not because others agreed but because you had built it from foundations that could not be questioned.","This conviction served as THE Civilizational Anchor that THE Proterozoic Scale demanded. Without it, Infinity’s whispers found cracks to exploit. Without it, THE Gamaidjan convinced its victims that they were something other than what they had believed. The truly strong never fell to such corruption because corruption required uncertainty to begin its work, and they possessed none.","When Naldine looked at Osmont, she saw this conviction leaking from his existence like light escaping a star too bright for its shell.","He did not merely possess confidence. He radiated it with intensity that pressed against everything nearby, declaring his certainty about what he was and what he would become without requiring words to announce it.","Every action he took emerged from foundations so assured of their own nature that doubt seemed like a foreign concept his consciousness. But...he also seemed to have doubt sometimes as it was odd. Paradoxical really.","She was almost envious.","Almost.","Her own conviction had been forged across eons of careful cultivation, tested against countless challenges that had shattered lesser certainties, refined until it could withstand pressures that crushed Primordial Architects less prepared than herself. She had earned her confidence.","Osmont seemed to have simply been born with it as he was too young.","Or perhaps his journey through existence had compressed eons of testing into years that somehow produced equivalent results. Either way, he possessed the quality in abundance that most Second Scale beings spent lifetimes attempting to develop, and he wielded it without apparent awareness of how rare it was.","But Naldine also knew that strength could become weakness through simple excess.","Conviction that never bent would eventually shatter when faced with truths it could not incorporate. Certainty that never questioned would miss dangers that uncertainty would have caught. Those playing with Infinity required flexibility alongside their foundations, the ability to adapt when endless potential revealed aspects of existence their confidence had not anticipated.","Osmont’s conviction was immense.","She simply hoped it was not so rigid that it would break rather than bend when Infinity finally showed him something his certainty could not accept.","---","Across THE Interstices.","As she was thinking all of this, Naldine looked toward Osmont and noticed he seemed to have a particularly content expression right now.","They had moved from Alfheimr into the gray expanse of endless weavings, that liminal space where boundaries blurred and travel between configurations became possible. The multicolored rain of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity passed around them in rivers that painted the gray with borrowed brilliance, his Miniature Cause still reshaping Observable Existence even as they traveled through it.","She asked with genuine curiosity coloring her tone.","\" What made you so happy?\"","Osmont’s smile carried satisfaction that seemed entirely inappropriate given everything that was happening.","\"I have just forged my first Infinity Armament. If I make enough of them paired with the rest of my power, maybe I can begin thrashing a Proterozoic Scale Being.\"","His eyes gleamed as he continued.","\" Unless you want to let me study the bones in your arm a little. Who knows, maybe I can begin forming Proterozoic Bones or Organs even before attaining THE Proterozoic Scale.\"","...!","There was that endless confidence and conviction again, as if his words would no doubt become reality soon enough.","Naldine wanted to shake her head, but ultimately she found herself responding with something other than dismissal.","\" You are filled with unknowns, so who knows. Maybe you are right.\"","She paused, letting her next words carry the full measure of her accumulated experience.","\" But do not underestimate any Proterozoic Scale Being. Even someone like Beowulf is impossible for you to defeat right now, and he is one among many of the weaker ones.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes fixed on him with intensity that most beings would have found uncomfortable.","\" You do not know much and have not heard much about Primordial Architects and how many there are, yes? Often times, existence rarely rewards the clamorous. There are those who believe that to be heard is to be powerful. They shout their intentions to the rafters, rattling their Civilizations to mask the hollow thrum of their own fear. Those are beings like Beowulf.\"","She gestured at the multicolored rain surrounding them.","\" They are like a summer storm, all thunder and sudden flashes of light, yet they spend their fury in a single frantic moment, leaving nothing behind but damp existence and silence. Such loudness and volume is not strength.\"","Her voice lowered as she continued.","\" The truly dangerous do not broadcast their malice. They cultivate it in stillness. While the fool boasts, the most terrifying enemies are those who have mastered the patience of years. They are silent, analyzing the very threads of your life, finding the single strand that, if pulled, causes your entire Civilization to unravel.\"","Naldine let those words settle before delivering the point she truly wanted him to understand.","\" By the time you feel their touch upon your throat, the trap was sprung eons ago. Fear the shadow that does not move, for it is calculating exactly how to break you before you even know you are at war. Those are the Primordial Architects and Singular Cognizances for you to worry about. The ones you will not know the names of before they try to destroy you.\"","She spoke at length and in detail because she truly wanted him to learn and grow, wanted him to develop some caution that might keep him alive long enough to reach the potential she saw within his foundations. Everything she said came from eons of watching brilliant beings die because they underestimated enemies they never saw coming!","And yet even after she said all that, he gazed at her with the same conviction and a smile as he asked his next question.","\" Might you happen to know of these silent schemers and planners that are supposed to not even be known? Maybe I can also scheme against them.\"","\"...\"","Naldine took a moment as she sighed internally. This one truly was something else entirely.","\" To scheme against such forces is to attempt to outrun your own shadow.\"","She considered how much to reveal, how much warning would actually penetrate that impenetrable confidence.","\" When it comes to if I know of these silent architects... I do. I know some. But others are really silent, and even I do not know them.\"","Her expression grew more serious than it had been throughout their journey together.","\" You must be cautious of the names Sammael and Ishara. Nasty and cautious beings. But if you seek the true horizon of your undoing, you must look to the two who have moved beyond mere planning. They are the ones who will succeed in collapsing everything you hold dear if you are not careful, for they have already achieved the impossible.\"","She held up one finger.","\" First, fear Eqono, THE Bright. He does not walk alone. He has bound the wills of multiple Primordial Architects to his cause, turning Architects into his own personal instruments. It is whispered that he possesses multiple Proterozoic Organs and Bones, foundations forged beyond what most at our Scale have accomplished.\"","A second finger rose.","\" Second, and perhaps most terrifying, is Cyndane. She does not bother with a choir of followers. She has formed an alliance with the Singular Cognizances themselves, entities that predate differentiation. She carries THE Proterozoic Sight, an eye that sees not what is, but the inevitability of what must cease to be.\"","Naldine let her hand fall as she delivered the final truth.","\" And these are just the ones I have gathered information about. The ones even I do not know about are the really scary ones for you. It is why I really am trying my best here. I know you actually face an impossible wall.\"","...!","After saying such words, she looked at him closely again.","Would he pause? Show some concern, any hint of fear crossing those features that seemed immune to such emotions? She had just described beings who could end everything he cared about, forces that had already achieved what most considered impossible, enemies who would not announce themselves before striking.","She watched.","And she saw him smile again with that same conviction, as if what he heard changed nothing whatsoever about his approach or his confidence.","\"...\"","Naldine found that she could say nothing more to scare him.","His conviction was unbreakable, it seemed. Either that quality would carry him to heights even she could not imagine, or it would shatter against truths that refused to bend regardless of how certain he was about his own nature.","She genuinely did not know which outcome awaited him.","...!"]},{"number":5041,"title":"Chapter 5041: Chapter 5040: Conviction! II","paragraphs":["While Naldine and Osmont crossed THE Interstices.","In the Lands of the Dead.","The Living had their spotlight while the dead shone in the endless shadow behind them. This was the natural order of existence, the balance that most never perceived because they were too focused on the brightness of life to notice the vast darkness stretching infinitely beyond it.","THE Dead Order knew this more than others.","She had not been given her spotlight to shine for eons, remaining behind the scenes while lesser beings claimed glory that should have been hers. Her weavings had been collapsed, her authority diminished, her very existence reduced to something that required rescue rather than inspiring fear. But now, her time was coming. THE Creature had restored her, elevated her, granted her power that finally matched the grandeur she had always deserved.","She wanted pain and vengeance against all those who went against her.","But frustratingly enough, the most recent one was the one THE Creature had forbidden her from pursuing. Apparently now called THE Youngest rather than the nothing he had been when she first encountered him. Osmont!","Him and Sigrid, these defilers of Order who had nearly collapsed the last shred of her weavings, were the ones THE Creature told her to forget about entirely.","If she wanted vengeance, she could decide the fate of THE Living Paradox who had collapsed her first eons ago.","But that felt like a consolation prize. A leftover offered to quiet a child’s tantrum rather than genuine acknowledgment of the wrongs done to her.","She shook her head in frustration as she looked around at her current surroundings.","She stood atop an intricate obsidian temple positioned at the peak of a massive white mountain, hazy white clouds drifting past its edges like ghosts too timid to approach. This was her domain, the Lands of the Dead that she had claimed and cultivated across eons of careful work.","And inside this temple, she was not alone.","An entity entirely humanoid in nature sat on a mat near the temple’s edge, sipping tea as if visiting someone’s home for casual conversation rather than intruding upon a domain she had no right to occupy.","Dark blue hair cascaded down her shoulders in waves that seemed to absorb what little light existed within the temple. Ancient eyes held depths. Her beauty was calm and undeniable.","She stared out across the expanse of obsidian and white all around them while multicolored rivers and rain surged outside the temple’s boundaries. Some streams of that multicolored rain flowed directly across the temple floor, the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity touching even this realm of death with its transformative authority.","Part of this rain was his power. THE Creature’s power.","THE Dead Order focused on the woman who had not said a single word to her since appearing here uninvited. Since she was here, it meant THE Creature had allowed her to be here. But...the silence had stretched past tolerance into outright insult, this stranger treating her like furniture rather than the master of this domain.","She finally brought herself to ask with irritation bleeding through her tone.","\" Who might you be? You come into my domain and you do not even bother to speak to me.\"","...!","The entity opposite her looked over with expression suggesting the question barely warranted acknowledgment. She shook her head slowly, as if deciding whether responding was even worth the effort, before her voice emerged with calm that bordered on dismissive.","\" The Lands of the Dead are not something you had built the fence and hung the gate yourself. It is a quaint delusion, the arrogance of a child claiming the sea because he has managed to wet his feet.\"","She sipped her tea before continuing.","\"I was breathing when the first Undivided One was a mere whisper in the dark, long before the threads of your little weaving were even conceived. I have stood before entities whose claims to the Lands of the Dead are written in foundations older than your entire lineage, beings who have forgotten more of ending than you will ever learn.\"","Her ancient eyes fixed on THE Dead Order with something approaching pity.","\" To me, you are a flickering candle of emotions and death. You have no domain here, little one. You have only a temporary reprieve from the silence.\"","...!","THE Dead Order looked over incredulously at the words that had just been spoken to her.","What the fuck?","What the FUCK?!","Who was this bitch that THE Creature brought over to think she could talk to her like this?! She had been healed and elevated by THE Creature himself, her power now standing at Absolute of THE First Scale!","She was untouchable! If Osmont stood before her again, maybe if he groveled sufficiently, she might spare him the full measure of her vengeance.","But this bitch?!","THE Dead Order rose up as her full chest heaved up and down, rage building within her foundations as she prepared to demonstrate exactly why she was not someone to be dismissed so casually. Her authority began gathering around her, death and weavings of Order responding to her fury as she was about to erupt when...","SAA!","Another aura entered the temple.","A calm and scholarly visage appeared at the temple’s entrance, a figure she recognized. Anaximander arrived drenched in the multicolored rain, droplets of Quintessence Infiniforce and Infinity sliding off his form as he stepped inside. His eyes moved first to THE Dead Order with her rage-twisted expression, then to the entity calmly sipping tea whose ancient eyes actually lit up with warmth when he arrived.","Anaximander looked at the enraged face of THE Dead Order and blinked with an expression suggesting genuine surprise.","\" Were you just about to go against one of the more powerful Second Scale Primordial Architects in Observable Existence? You have stronger conviction than I do, O Dead Order!\"","...!","THE Dead Order paled as her figure almost stumbled backward.","THE Second Scale? Primordial Architect? That woman?","The rage drained from her foundations faster than it had gathered.","...!","She had no words as she watched that entity nod toward Anaximander with a genuine smile, familiarity passing between them as if they were old acquaintances reuniting after long separation.","\"It has been a while, Jokul.\"","The Primordial Architect then turned her head to glance at THE Dead Order before speaking with calm that made every word cut deeper than intended insult could have.","\"I do not know why THE Creature attached himself to something as vain as this during his rebirth. She is a creature of vanity and jealous whims, propping up a hollow existence with the fragile scaffolding of her own emotions.\"","She sipped her tea again.","\" She possesses neither the depth nor the clarity to ever reach THE Second Scale. Such petty passions are but smoke. They will carry her nowhere in the vastness of existence.\"","A slight shrug.","\" But who am I to judge? Where is the big guy? Is he still fighting Horus?\"","...!","THE Dead Order actually stumbled backward this time, rage and humiliation warring within her as she stared at this supposed Primordial Architect who had just dissected her entire existence. What the fuck was her problem?!","At her words, Anaximander smiled.","\" Nice to see you too, Tairiyya. Try to be nicer.\"","He moved to sit near her, accepting tea she poured without being asked.","\" And THE Creature is wrapping things up. What do you think of the Miniature Cause of rain outside? The one who induced it alongside THE Creature is also a friend of mine.\"","...!","Anaximander and Tairiyya spoke casually about matters spanning Scales and eons, their conversation flowing as if they had not just dismissed someone standing right before them.","They forgot or ignored THE Dead Order completely, her presence in her own domain rendered irrelevant by beings whose existence operated on levels she could not touch.","She stood there, hollow and humiliated, wondering if anything she achieved would ever matter to those who truly held power in Observable Existence."]},{"number":5042,"title":"Chapter 5042: Chapter 5041: Nakatsukuni! I","paragraphs":["Anaximander settled more comfortably near Tairiyya, his scholarly demeanor relaxing in the presence of someone he clearly considered an equal.","\" One after another, things are becoming more and more chaotic out there.\"","His voice carried observation rather than complaint.","Tairiyya sipped her tea and sighed, her ancient eyes turning toward the vibrant multicolored rain cascading past the temple’s boundaries. The Pluvial Epoch painted everything with borrowed brilliance, authority from sources she understood all too well saturating even this realm of death.","\" For eons, it was quiet. For eons, the stillness was absolute. Everybody just worked hard for their weavings.\"","She set her cup down with deliberate care.","\"But now, the first dominoes have been tipped by hands that should not have the reach to touch them. The Peasant, THE Creature, and even the Infinity-bearer have begun to move, their frantic shuffles triggering a cascade that cannot be halted.\"","Her expression grew more contemplative as she continued.","\" Because of them, the Primordial Architects have stirred with activity. Even the Singular Cognizances, those who have spent an eternity as mere Observers, are beginning to step from the shadows of the void.\"","A sound escaped her that might have been a laugh in someone less ancient.","\" Ah. In the end, this will lead to a ruin more absolute than the dark. In all of existence, there are few who truly know what they are doing. The rest are simply shouting into the abyss, unaware that the abyss is finally preparing to answer.\"","She glanced at Anaximander with something approaching fondness.","\" Things are about to get really wild, Jokul. I am not sure if even THE Creature understands.\"","...!","At such words, Anaximander smiled with an expression suggesting he knew things that even this Primordial Architect might not have considered.","\"I think out of many existences in, well, Existence, THE Creature is one of the rare few that do understand. But yes, it will be unpredictable.\"","He paused before asking his next question with careful precision.","\" Can you give me a gauge of just how much of a pull you and other Primordial Architects feel toward the one who bears and utilizes Infinity more freely than all of you at THE Proterozoic Scale?\"","Tairiyya’s ancient eyes sharpened at the question, her cup freezing halfway to her lips before she set it down entirely.","\" How much of a pull we have?\"","A laugh escaped her.","\" Hah, Jokul, you have been gone for too long. Infinity is everything and nothing. It is the only thing we have, as THE Primordial Source is too far, too unknown. We cannot even begin to approach it while Infinity flows throughout Observable Existence, tantalizingly close yet requiring transformations most cannot survive.\"","She stared directly at him now.","\" The others will come at him relentlessly. Not out of malice, though some will cloak their hunger in righteous purpose. They will come because they must. Because Infinity calls to those of us who have spent eons preparing to receive it, and he walks around conducting it as if breathing air. Do you understand what that means to beings who have sacrificed everything for even a fraction of what he wields carelessly?\"","...!","Jokul was silent at this, his scholarly demeanor fading into something more somber. He looked out into the rain, that endless multicolored cascade reshaping Observable Existence through authority his friend had triggered alongside THE Creature.","He raised his hand to feel THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity, letting droplets land upon his palm. The sensation was unlike anything else in existence, power that declared endless potential ready for those capable of receiving it.","He sighed with sound carrying understanding that words could not express.","And this whole time, nobody said a word to THE Dead Order standing behind them.","She remained there, forgotten entirely, her existence rendered irrelevant by a conversation about matters so far beyond her that she could barely comprehend what was being discussed.","Her domain. Her temple. Her supposed moment of restored glory.","And she was fucking furniture.","---","Naldine Manthon continued to move across the Interstices because her destination was truly far.","The gray expanse stretched endlessly around them, multicolored rain from the Pluvial Epoch painting borrowed brilliance across spaces that normally held none. She had traveled these paths many times across her existence, but never with someone quite like the entity floating beside her. Young. Impossibly young by any standard that mattered. Yet somehow wielding authority that beings at her Scale spent eons trying to obtain!","She turned to Osmont as she continued speaking.","\" When I ask myself how I can best prepare you, knowledge is the best thing for someone as young as you. I will share this freely.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes fixed on him with intensity that most would have found uncomfortable.","\" The enemies you face at THE Proterozoic Scale will be extremely powerful. You should understand their power somewhat. So I will tell you about THE Proterozoic Scale itself.\"","...!","Osmont looked at her and gave a nod of expectation, his expression carrying that same unshakeable conviction she had observed again and again. He listened like someone who expected to eventually surpass whatever she described rather than someone preparing to face impossible odds.","Naldine continued without waiting for verbal acknowledgment.","\" Infinity is something those at THE Second Scale chase, but it is not always their foremost power. It is an unfathomable force, but just like THE Primordial Source, if you do not have access to it, then you do not.\"","She let that settle before proceeding.","\" THE Proterozoic Scale stands by itself even without Infinity. After you have set your Civilizational Anchor, many things become possible. Those who have done so are considered Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeforms.\"","Her voice took on the cadence of utter glory and wonder as they continued ahead!","\" Above them are THE Calymmian Proterozoic Lifeforms . And the distant, out of reach level for many at THE Second Scale is THE Ediacaran Proterozoic Lifeform . Rhyacian, Calymmian, and Ediacaran . That is the known scope of THE Second Scale.\"","...!"]},{"number":5043,"title":"Chapter 5043: Chapter 5042: Nakatsukuni! II","paragraphs":["Osmont listened calmly as they continued through the gray expanse before asking his question.","\" You would not happen to be at the Calymmian Proterozoic Scale or Ediacaran, would you? This would make things very easy.\"","Naldine looked back at him and did not reply.","She simply stared out toward where they were going, letting silence serve as answer enough.","After a moment, she continued as if the question had never been asked.","\" Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeforms alone are a problem for you. If we put Beowulf on the lowest tier, someone could be stronger than him by a factor of ten and still be a Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform.\"","She glanced at him to ensure he understood the scale of what she was describing.","\" As I mentioned, Infinity and THE Primordial Source are ideal. But because they can be so distant, most of us focus on what is Observable and Unobservable. We take that into our Civilizations.\"","Her explanation shifted into something more fundamental.","\" All of existence divides into two categories. The Observable and the Unobservable. Everything that can be perceived, measured, witnessed, or acknowledged falls into the Observable. Everything that cannot falls into the Unobservable.\"","She gestured at the gray Interstices around them.","\" The Observable is what you currently see, what can be seen, what has been seen, what will be seen. The accumulated force of all potential perception pressing against existence from every angle. When something enters the Observable, it gains substance through acknowledgment. It becomes real in ways that unwitnessed things are not.\"","Her voice grew more contemplative as she described the counterpart.","\" The Unobservable is not simply what you cannot see. It is what exists beyond the possibility of perception. What has never been witnessed and never will be. The vast darkness surrounding everything acknowledged, pressing inward with force that dwarfs what the Observable contains. For every star that shines, countless more burn in regions no consciousness will ever reach.\"","She watched his expression for signs of comprehension before continuing.","\" At THE Proterozoic Scale, we learn to draw from both. We infuse and integrate the force of all that is Observable, or the force of all that is Unobservable, into our existence.\"","The technical details came easily to her after eons of living them.","\" Those accomplished enough can form Proterozoic Bones or Organs even without the infusion of Infinity, if they fill them with enough weavings of either Observable or Unobservable. After they have transformed enough of their existence, when they pass a certain marker, they go from Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeforms to Calymmian Proterozoic Lifeforms.\"","She explained as best she could because she knew the stakes involved. There were beings at the Calymmian Proterozoic Scale who would very much like to put their hands on this infinite battery floating beside her. Knowledge might be the only thing keeping him alive when those beings eventually made their moves.","And after all this talking...","HUUM!","She finally felt them nearing their destination as white-gold light flickered at the edges of the gray expanse.","They finished crossing the Interstices as Naldine wrapped her authority around both of them and took a single step. Instantly, the two of them appeared in an endless field of white stretching in every direction without boundary or feature, a space between spaces where nothing existed until permission was granted.","Naldine voiced out commandingly with her authority pressing into the blankness.","\" Naldine Manthon.\"","HUUM!","After stating her name in this endless white space, existence flickered once more as brilliant verdant light wrapped around the two of them. The white dissolved into color and sensation and the feeling of somewhere specific rather than nowhere at all.","They found themselves standing on vibrant plains.","Naldine did not much care for natural beauty after eons of witnessing it across countless regions of Observable Existence, but she could appreciate the craftsmanship here nonetheless as this place...was built and carved by someone. The grass beneath their feet held coloring so rich it seemed painted rather than grown, emerald blades swaying in breezes that carried warmth without humidity. Distant mountains rose against skies holding shades of blue that deepened toward purple at the horizons, their peaks touched by mists.","Away from these plains stood a massive and glorious set of structures.","The buildings ahead followed architectural principles that prioritized harmony with their surroundings rather than dominance over them.","Traditional designs built with natural materials, timber and stone and clay arranged uniquely. Gently sloping tiled roofs curved upward at their edges, their surfaces glazed in colors that shifted between gray and blue depending on how light struck them. Wooden pillars supported overhanging eaves providing shelter and shade, their surfaces aged to warm browns that spoke of centuries rather than years.","The structures connected through courtyards and covered walkways, each building relating to its neighbors in configurations designed for wonder.","Some courtyards held gardens of carefully arranged stones and pruned trees. Others held ponds reflecting the sky above with clarity that made their surfaces seem like windows into inverted worlds.","The layout showed simplicity and organic growth guided by consistent principles, each addition respecting what came before while contributing something new to the whole.","Naldine began walking toward the structures as Osmont fell into step beside her.","\" Welcome to a domain hidden between spaces, between Observable and Unobservable. Welcome to Nakatsukuni.\"","She glanced at him with an expression suggesting her next words were not optional.","\" Do not do anything crazy here as...well, you can sense and see it.\"","He should not do anything crazy because as they neared the structures, Noah could sense ans see what she meant. The figures and auras of hundreds of terrifying First Scale entities at the level of Absolutes pressed against his awareness from various buildings and courtyards, apex beings who would have been considered overwhelming threats in any other context.","And...a few Proterozoic Scale entities added their presence to the collective force, their authority making THE First Scale beings seem dim by comparison.","And above all of them, the brilliance of one that stood supreme here blazed like a sun among candles!","That...should be the Singular Cognizance!"]},{"number":5044,"title":"Chapter 5044: Chapter 5043: Nakatsukuni! III","paragraphs":["Nakatsukuni.","Noah looked at the place they had arrived at, and it was a marvel in several different ways.","The primary entrance rose before them like a declaration of intent made physical. A large heavy wooden gate stood at the center, its surface adorned with iron ring handles and ornate carvings depicting scenes he could not immediately interpret. This was no ordinary gateway but something built higher than the surrounding roofline, its very elevation announcing the significance of what lay beyond.","Stone and clay walls flanked the entrance in configurations that seemed both defensive and decorative. Gray roof tiles topped these barriers in patterns matching what he could see of the main structures deeper within, creating visual harmony. Everything here felt intentional, every stone placed with purpose, every tile arranged.","At the gateway itself, Noah saw something that made even his composed expression shift slightly.","Two Primordial Architects of THE First Scale stood guard, both at the level of Absolutes, their presence pressing against his awareness with force that would have crushed lesser beings simply through proximity. They turned to look at Naldine Manthon first, offering nods of recognition that suggested familiarity. Then their attention shifted to him.","Their eyes shone with luminosity that seemed to pierce through whatever he presented on the surface.","Both entities were humanoid in nature, their forms draped in wrappings of shining white and pink that moved like living things despite the absence of wind. Their faces held beauty that transcended simple aesthetics, features arranged according to proportions that seemed mathematically perfect in ways mortal minds struggled to quantify. Ancient eyes regarded him from those beautiful faces.","Even though they were Absolute, a million trash bum Absolutes like THE Living Elemental could stand before them, and all would get thrashed silly.","Naldine only nodded to them and passed through the gate without breaking stride.","Noah went inside as well, stepping through the massive entrance and immediately finding himself in a courtyard. It stretched before him as a communal hub connecting all the interior living quarters. Beyond this space, the actual buildings rose on raised foundations of stone and wood, elevated to protect from ground moisture and requiring visitors to step up when entering.","Deep curved wooden eaves extended over every entryway, providing shade and protection while framing views of the sky from positions within the courtyard. The architecture felt alive in ways that stone and wood should not feel, as if the structures themselves were aware of who passed through them.","Noah smiled as he spoke to Naldine walking ahead of him.","\"After all the warnings you have given me, you have brought me to a place filled with Primordial Architects. Has this all just been a long elaborate trap?\"","His tone carried amusement rather than genuine concern.","Naldine continued forward without looking back as she replied.","\"I brought you here because I am confident I can protect you here. Barring anything unexpected happening, this should be a good step forward for you if we can secure the promises of the one we came to see.\"","...!","Barring any unexpected happenings.","Noah sighed internally at these words because they felt like a very bad flag that Naldine had just planted. Existence loved to be filled with unexpected happenings. The moment someone expressed confidence that nothing would go wrong, the foundations of reality itself seemed to take that as a challenge.","Inside, Noah saw something that genuinely surprised him.","Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors swept the extended courtyards with brooms and brushes, their movements methodical and unhurried. Some of these beings stood taller than normal humanoids, their bodies wrapped in stellar crimson skin that seemed to contain galaxies within its depths.","Others bore obsidian skin so dark that light seemed to fall into it and never return. Still others blazed with white stellar skin, their forms radiating illumination that pressed against perception.","All of them swept.","Was this their meditation? Some instructed method to elevate their Civilizations given by the Singular Cognizance who oversaw this place? Noah never expected to see Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors sweeping grounds like normal humans performing household chores. The sight seemed almost absurd given the power contained within each of these entities.","Every single one turned to see him and Naldine as they crossed through the courtyard.","Noah felt every single gaze stay on him, dozens of ancient consciousnesses tracking his movement through their domain. They did not stop their sweeping. They did not approach or threaten. They simply watched, their attention pressing against his awareness like physical force that accumulated with each additional observer.","In one area they passed, Noah saw something even more unexpected.","A Primordial Architect at THE Proterozoic Scale sat at a table playing chess with three other Primordial Architects. The Second Scale being moved a piece with fingers that seemed too elegant for the simple action, pale skin catching light in ways that made it seem luminescent rather than merely fair.","Long silver-gold hair cascaded down his back in waves that moved with supernatural grace, framing aristocratic features that belonged on sculptures rather than living faces. Dark elegant clothing wrapped his slender frame, the garments suggesting nobility from traditions Noah did not recognize.","When they passed, the game stopped entirely.","Noah and this Proterozoic Scale entity locked eyes across the courtyard.","The being smiled dangerously, lips curving upward to reveal the faintest hint of sharpened teeth. One pale hand rose in a wave toward Noah, the gesture carrying mockery beneath its apparent friendliness.","\"...\"","Noah mimicked the same smile and waved back without hesitation.","The moment he did so, the smile disappeared from that Primordial Architect’s face. Those aristocratic features sharpened into something predatory as eyes that had been amused became cutting.","Naldine’s voice cut through the tension.","\" Remember, do not try anything over the top. Strangers are allies until they become enemies, and things can change rather quickly. Let us go.\"","As if she expected trouble might start from that exchange alone, her authority wrapped around them again. She took a step, and they appeared before the tallest building in this place.","Two THE Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects sat beside the entrance, both adorned in garments similar to the guards they had seen at the main gate.","The first seemed extremely young despite the ancient depths within her eyes. Silver-white hair fell past her shoulders in straight lines that caught light like silk threads woven from moonlight. Her features held delicacy that suggested fragility while her presence declared anything but weakness.","She sipped tea with movements so economical they seemed rehearsed across centuries of repetition, her small form somehow containing authority that pressed against Noah’s awareness despite her apparent youth.","The second Primordial Architect sat in a meditative position beside her, and he was anything but delicate.","A massive humanoid demon with crimson-gold horns curving from his temples regarded Noah and Naldine with calm that seemed inappropriate for something so obviously built for violence. His skin held the color of dried blood, stretched over a frame that towered even while seated. He smiled, the expression somehow warm despite the fangs it revealed, and his deep voice echoed out across the courtyard.","\" Naldine Manthon. You have come bearing gifts and catastrophes.\"","The words pressed against everything nearby.","\"Why would you bring such a thing when you know The Leader does not want any conflicts? By simply bringing you and him here, you force The Leader’s hand.\"","...!","Noah looked at this Primordial Architect and the one beside him. Their power felt heavy and suffocating to him even now, pressing against his foundations with force that reminded him exactly how far he still had to go. But he could not help marveling at all of this despite the pressure.","There were peaceful groups of Primordial Architects under a Singular Cognizance?","Existence continued to be vast and grand beyond measure. He had assumed beings at these heights existed in constant conflict, scheming against each other across eons while pursuing power through any means available. Yet here stood evidence of cooperation, of community, of entities choosing peace over perpetual warfare.","As he was thinking this, Naldine looked at the two Primordial Architects blocking their path. She nodded toward them.","\" Sabayne. Ba’alzan. Times are changing.\"","Her voice carried conviction that pressed back against the force the demon had projected.","\" Even those who hold peace as their only prayer will find the silence shattered. When the conflict breaks, peace becomes a cage, not a sanctuary. No soul remains a mere observer as all of us are forced to move when the foundations shift.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed brighter.","\" The times of peace are over.\"","BOOM!","With such words, Naldine Manthon pushed the doors of the structure before them open.","Inside, a heavy aura pulsed outward, the presence of a Singular Cognizance that reminded Noah of the brilliance he had felt when THE Beholder manifested. This was another entity from before differentiation, another consciousness that had observed existence since before Observable Existence learned how to be observable, they held an authority so absolute it made everything outside feel like a fleeting dream!"]},{"number":5045,"title":"Chapter 5045: Chapter 5044: Nakatsukuni! IV","paragraphs":["The structure they entered was dim and filled with an atmosphere resembling outer space itself.","Sparkling stellar lights sprinkled all around them in configurations that seemed random until Noah looked closer and recognized patterns within the chaos. Constellations formed and dissolved in the darkness, galaxies spiraling in miniature across surfaces that should have been walls but felt more like windows into the void between stars.","The entity inside acted as a source of profound light amidst this manufactured cosmos.","Noah observed a white-blue singularity contained within a constantly shifting square cube. The singularity pulsed with brilliance that reminded him immediately of THE Beholder, that same sense of consciousness predating differentiation, that same feeling of being observed by something that had witnessed existence learn how to exist.","But where THE Beholder had felt distant and evaluating, this presence felt vast in ways that pressed against his awareness with force unlike any other Proterozoic Scale entity.","They were a powerful fucker!","When they entered, this entity had its singularity gaze fixed directly on him.","The gaze felt calm and curious rather than hostile, the attention of something genuinely interested rather than threatened. Noah met that observation without flinching, his foundations steady despite the pressure emanating from a being that had likely observed THE First Cause itself.","Naldine looked up toward this entity as she began to speak.","\" Out of all the Singular Cognizances and Primordial Architects who have carved their names into the foundations of reality, you are the only one who has managed to remain truly unaligned, Sadakar.\"","She paused, her singularity-dotted eyes reflecting the sun-like brilliance of the entity before them.","\" But even here, tucked between the Observable and the Unobservable, you cannot claim ignorance. Both of us have felt and listened to the tremors in the weavings, the echoes of THE First Cause.\"","Noah remained silent, his gaze fixed on the shimmering silhouette of the Leader. This was Naldine’s negotiation to conduct. He was here as the one being discussed rather than the one doing the discussing, at least for now. And he was gathering more and more information before he began to act as there were many questions.","How many more places like these were there? Clusters of Primordial Architects- were they similar to here or smaller or larger?","\" Those who hold peace would surely side with those who do not seek the Splintering of Observable Existence ,\" Naldine continued, her tone shifting from observation to cold pragmatic proposal.","\"I did not bring him here to hide him. I came to introduce the two of you and to form a treaty.\"","She gestured toward Noah, her hand steady despite the presence pressing against everything in this space.","\"A pact of mutual defense. Because when the monsters who wish to return everything to nothingness and endless potential finally make their move, even Nakatsukuni will be forced to choose a side. I would prefer you choose the side that allows existence to continue existing.\"","...!","The Singular Cognizance pulsed before them, its contained brilliance fluctuating as it processed her words. That ancient gaze shifted between Naldine and Noah, evaluating both with attention that seemed to perceive far more than surfaces could reveal.","Finally, it began to speak in a voice deep enough to resonate through one’s foundations.","\" Existence...is an unfathomable weaving of immensity, a discordant symphony of a trillion weavings where even the birth and death of entire Scales are but the frantic flickering of a candle against the encroaching dark.\"","The cube rotated through another configuration as Sadakar continued.","\" You stand before me claiming the mantle of a lover of peace, Naldine Manthon, yet you stride into this sanctuary, into MY Sanctuary trailing the scent of inevitable ruin. Your very presence here serves as the first heavy precursor that will likely shatter the silence we have cultivated across eons of patient stillness.\"","A pause that seemed to last longer than it should have.","\" But let us set aside your treaties and the fraying edges of your foresight for a moment.\"","The singularity’s attention fixed entirely on Noah now.","\" The Infinity-bearer. I do not suppose you will tell this old existence just where you truly emerged from and how you possess the capability you hold?\"","The question pressed against him with genuine curiosity.","\"A great deal of things about you are undeniably curious. Which hidden realm did you form in? During which forgotten eon was your consciousness first sparked? What impossible materials of differentiation and undifferentiation composed the core of your existence to allow such a vessel to hold what you hold?\"","Sadakar’s brilliance pulsed with each question.","\" There are a great many questions about you. If you share, perhaps the old monsters trying to get their hands on you will simply sit back after they know.\"","...!","What realm did he form in? What materials composed him?","Noah did not know how to tell this being that he was a simple human carried in a womb for nine months, born a weak baby that had to have his diapers changed every time he soiled himself. His mother had fed him milk and burped him over her shoulder. His mother had taught him to walk by holding his hands while he stumbled across floors that seemed impossibly vast to infant perception!","That certainly was not the grand image of the entity conducting Infinity across Observable Existence.","He thought of how to reply to this being, how to frame origins that seemed laughably mundane compared to what Sadakar clearly expected to hear.","Before he could formulate his response...","DING!","A ringing sound echoed through the structure, cutting through the stellar atmosphere like a blade through silk. The sound made Naldine frown immediately.","A deep sigh echoed from the Singular Cognizance, resignation and irritation mixing in that ancient voice.","\" What did I say? You came bearing the weavings of Chaos, Naldine Manthon.\"","The cube rotated faster as Sadakar’s attention shifted toward something beyond the structure’s walls.","\" Because now, those you consider your enemies have arrived. The Peasant and Moloch have now also arrived at my door.\"","...!"]},{"number":5046,"title":"Chapter 5046: Chapter 5045: Hadean! I","paragraphs":["Are Primordial Architects the Blessed Lifeforms of Observable Existence?","Some entities emerge from the collision of differentiation and undifferentiation as Undivided Ones. Others crystallize into Formless Terrors. Still others become the countless classifications that populate Observable Existence at every Scale and depth.","But Primordial Architects are born different.","They emerge already holding authority that others spend eons cultivating. Some manifest at THE First Scale with foundations so refined that reaching Absolute depths becomes inevitability rather than aspiration. Others appear directly at THE Second Scale, their existence already transformed into configurations that most beings cannot achieve regardless of how long they struggle toward transcendence.","What did they possess within their existence that others didn’t? What quality separated their emergence from the emergence of everything else? Were they favored by THE First Cause itself, or did some random arrangement of forces during their formation grant them advantages that had nothing to do with preference?","Nobody knows.","The Primordial Architects themselves don’t know. They simply are what they are, born into privilege that they did nothing to earn and cannot explain to those who ask.","There was a time when THE Creature counted himself among them.","Before he became what he is now, before he shattered classifications and rebuilt himself into something that defied every category Observable Existence had established, he walked as a Primordial Architect.","His power was immense. His authority was absolute within the domains he claimed. His future stretched before him with possibilities that most beings could only dream of reaching.","And he chose to throw it all away.","The story goes that a Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect stood before him when he announced his intention. An ancient entity whose name has been deliberately forgotten, someone who had watched THE Creature’s rise with concern.","\" You understand this is irreversible ,\" that entity had said. \" What you propose is annihilation of everything you currently are. The weavings of a Primordial Architect cannot be reclaimed once abandoned. You will become nothing, and from that nothing, you hope to become something else entirely.\"","The entity paused, letting the severity settle.","\" Things will forever change. You will never again be what you are now. The weavings that made you will dissolve, and whatever emerges from its ashes may not survive the process. You may entirly collapse and lose our blessing. Is that truly what you want?\"","THE Creature’s response had been grand.","\" A Blessing? \" He laughed, and the sound made reality itself flinch. \" You call this a Blessing? I call it a ceiling. I call it a cage with comfortable walls. I call it the highest room in a structure when I want to stand beneath open sky.\"","He had stepped forward, and even that ancient Primordial Architect had stepped back.","\" Why I would leave behind such weavings? I ask you why I would keep them? To remain what I was born as? To accept limitations written into my existence before I had any say in what I would become? To spend eternity as the greatest version of something I never chose to be?\"","His presence pressed against everything nearby, already beginning the process of unmaking what he had been.","\"I don’t want to be a decent Primordial Architect. I want to be something that makes the very concept of Primordial Architects seem small. And if that means burning away every advantage I was given, then I will burn gladly. I...will always burn.\"","He smiled then, and he began to burn.","And THE Creature emerged from the ashes of what he abolished, standing as proof that chosen paths could exceed gifted ones, that will could surpass circumstance, that sometimes the greatest power came not from what you were given but from what you were willing to destroy in pursuit of what you wanted to become.","The Primordial Architects remained Blessed.","THE Creature...became something else entirely.","---","Erwin looked at the domain materializing before them as he and Moloch crossed into spaces hidden between the Observable and Unobservable.","\" What is this place? \" he asked the Singular Cognizance floating beside him. \" And why did we come here?\"","Moloch’s golden plates spun faster as they approached the main gate.","\" Nakatsukuni. A unique Singular Cognizance and multiple Proterozoic Scale Architects have this domain as their home. They’ve maintained peace here for eons while the rest of Observable Existence tears itself apart with schemes and conflicts.\"","Erwin considered this information. Peaceful Proterozoic Scale beings seemed like a contradiction, but existence had shown him stranger things.","\" And we’re here because?\"","\"Because you need to make some new friends.\" Moloch’s voice carried amusement that pressed against Erwin’s awareness.","\" These are the hardest friends to make. Beings who have rejected conflict, who have chosen stillness over ambition, who will not be swayed by promises of power or threats of destruction.\"","The Singular Cognizance turned its attention fully toward Erwin.","\" So we start with the hardest ones first. If you can convince those who want nothing to align with your cause, convincing everyone else becomes simple by comparison.\"","Erwin smiled at the logic. It was paradoxical in its own way, seeking allies among those least likely to become allies.","They entered through the main gate, passing Primordial Architects at Absolute depths who regarded them with expressions mixing wariness and curiosity. Erwin felt their gazes tracking him as he moved deeper into the compound, but he paid them little attention.","His focus was elsewhere.","His paradox burned within him with intensity that surprised even himself. The weavings of contradiction he had cultivated across eons reached a precipice now, pressing against boundaries that many may not have anticipated he could approach. His Civilizational Anchor was nearly complete. His claim to Paradox, held and not held simultaneously, pulsed with authority that made the Primordial Architects around him shift uncomfortably.","He was close now.","So very close to something that would change everything. But he was also even more cautious as he knew the closer one came to a grand accomplishment, the more likely they could fall and stumble. He had fallen and stumbled many times that he was now very careful of this. He wanted to see what would rise to try and trip him this time."]},{"number":5047,"title":"Chapter 5047: Chapter 5046: Hadean! II","paragraphs":["In THE Infiniverse.","In THE Seed of Observable Existence.","Noah lay alone on the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, his body stretched across ground that held warmth despite the rain falling upon it.","Multicolored droplets descended from heights that seemed infinite, each one carrying Quintessence Infiniforce that sank into his skin and dissolved into his foundations. The sensation was pleasant, like being bathed in potential rather than struggling to contain it.","Nobody was here.","His mother had stayed with THE Mnemonic Leviathan in its lava pools. His people trained in THE Yggdrheim or spread across the Three Thousand Realms exploring what THE Hadean Emergence had created. For the first time in what felt like ages, Noah found himself completely alone with nothing but rain and sand and the weight of everything Naldine had told him.","He didn’t smile when no one was watching.","Not because fear gripped him. Not because doubt crept in. Simply because smiling was sometimes for an audience, and right now there was none. His expression settled into something neutral as he processed the information he’d gathered.","Rhyacian, Calymmian, Ediacaran . Three tiers of Proterozoic Scale existence, each one containing beings who could crush him with effort ranging from moderate to none.","The enemies ahead were terrifying. He knew this with the same certainty he knew his own name.","But knowing the scope of what opposed him didn’t shake his resolve. It sharpened it. He knew that Naldine seemed to think his conviction bordered on delusion, that he smiled in the face of danger because certainty filled him so completely that reality couldn’t touch it.","She was partially right. He did possess conviction. He did believe he would find ways to overcome what stood before him.","The difference was that his conviction came from necessity rather than blind faith.","He simply couldn’t fail. Failure meant his mother dissolving into nothing. Failure meant Henry and Adelaide and everyone else he’d gathered being erased by forces they couldn’t resist. Failure meant everything he’d built collapsing, and Noah had built too much to watch it fall.","So he wouldn’t fail.","Not because Existence guaranteed his success. Fucking hell, sometimes, it felt like existence was working against him actively.","He wouldn’t fail because he refused to allow it. Every scheme, every preparation, every conversation with beings like Naldine who held knowledge he needed, all of it served a singular purpose. He would become strong enough that failure stopped being possible.","That was his conviction. Not certainty, but a glorious unshakable Will.","Multicolored rain continued falling on his face.","Noah closed his eyes and felt his existence, really felt it in ways he rarely took time to do. The vibrant drops landed on his skin and sank deeper, Quintessence Infiniforce merging with foundations that had already absorbed more Infinity than most beings could imagine. And hey, he hadn’t gone mad yet!","He thought about everything Naldine had shared during their journey.","The force of Observable and Unobservable that Proterozoic Scale entities pulled into themselves. That was their methodology when Infinity remained beyond reach. They drew from everything that could be perceived and everything that couldn’t, integrating those vast forces into Civilizations transformed to receive them.","But he had something different.","The force of Quintessence Infiniforce. The force of THE Infiniverse itself. When his domain had triggered THE Hadean Emergence and become a Seed of Observable Existence, something had begun flowing through their connection into him.","Not just pure power. Structure. Authority accumulated across Three Thousand Realms pressing into his finite existence through bonds that made separation impossible.","He finally understood what had been happening to his body.","Proterozoic Scale beings pulled the force of Observable into themselves at THE Second Scale. They channeled it carefully over eons, forging Proterozoic Organs and Bones from integrated authority that transformed what they were into what they needed to become.","He wasn’t at THE Proterozoic Scale.","But he had the force of an entire Seed of Observable Existence flowing into him right now. THE Infiniverse contained Three Thousand Realms of Quintessence, seas of combined authority, atmospheres of Primal Power that saturated everything within her boundaries. All of that connected to him. All of that pressed against his foundations through their unbreakable bond.","And most of it flowed toward one specific point within his existence.","His Organ of Civilization.","That aspect of his foundations had been undergoing change since THE Hadean Emergence completed. He’d felt it shifting, transforming, becoming something other than what it had been. The pressure concentrated there as if his Organ of Civilization was most receptive to what THE Infiniverse provided.","Noah opened his eyes and stared up at the multicolored rain descending toward him.","He knew what this force could potentially make possible. If Proterozoic Scale beings forged Proterozoic Organs from integrated Observable or Unobservable authority, then what could he forge from integrated Quintessence Infiniforce and the power of a Seed? The implications suggested capability that shouldn’t exist at his current Scale.","He focused on his Organ of Civilization and felt it respond to his attention. The transformation happening there had been passive until now, occurring without his direct involvement. But passive transformation meant passive results.","He didn’t want passive results.","\"O Infinity.\"","His voice emerged quiet against the sound of falling rain.","\" O Quintessence Infiniforce. O that which is Observable and Unobservable in THE Infiniverse.\"","The words felt right in ways he couldn’t explain. They were invitation and permission. Encouragement for processes already occurring to complete themselves according to his will rather than random chance.","\"Flow freely. Let the Organ of Civilization bloom.\"","...!","The Early Veiled Shore shook around him.","Noah felt the sand vibrating beneath his back, golden grains trembling as something responded to his declaration. The multicolored rain intensified, droplets falling faster and heavier as if THE Infiniverse itself heard his request and answered with enthusiasm. Pressure built within his existence, concentrated on that single point where his Organ of Civilization waited.","He knew Proterozoic Scale entities forged Proterozoic Organs or Bones. That was their methodology. That was their path.","But he wasn’t a Proterozoic Scale entity.","He was something else entirely. Something that had never existed before. Something that held Infinity in ways that defied classification while remaining at heights that shouldn’t permit such holding.","The prompt bloomed before his vision with brilliance that made the rain seem dim.","|Transformation Detected|","|Your Organ of Civilization has begun responding to accumulated authority from THE Seed of Observable Existence. The force of Quintessence Infiniforce combined with Observable and Unobservable weavings from the Three Thousand Realms has reached critical density within your foundations.|","|This transformation does not follow Proterozoic methodology.|","|This transformation follows no recorded methodology.|","| THE Hadean Organ of Civilization is emerging within your Existence.|","...!","Noah lay on golden sand as multicolored rain fell upon him, his eyes fixed on words that declared something unprecedented was being born inside his foundations.","His smile returned.","This time, it was genuine. It was grand! It was...magisterial!"]},{"number":5048,"title":"Chapter 5048: Chapter 5047: Hadean! III","paragraphs":["The transformation was unique in ways Noah hadn’t anticipated.","His Organ of Civilization, which was becoming THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, kept moving across his body in patterns that defied prediction. From his head to his heart to his limbs and all extremities, the organ traveled as if searching for its proper home. He felt like a pinball machine, the transforming organ bouncing between locations while leaving trails of multicolored warmth wherever it passed.","He had to rise up from the golden sands.","The warmth of both the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity and THE Hadean Emergence bathed his body on all sides, two Miniature Causes working in harmony to saturate his existence with authority he’d helped create. The golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore around him had risen up and were floating like glimmers of golden stars, each grain suspended by forces responding to the transformation occurring within him.","Inside his body, as all of this took place, he continued to generate endless Quintessence Infiniforce.","All of it was a flood of sensations that he frankly had to say felt better than some of the grandest sensations he’d experienced so far in existence.","The pleasure wasn’t merely physical. It ran deeper, touching aspects of his foundations. Every moment of the transformation brought waves of something approaching bliss!","It even exceeded his euphoria during his spar with THE Creature.","That spar told him a great deal of things about existence itself. There was no need to say who was the victor of that spar, of course. After all, it was just a spar, right?","Right!","There was no need to declare a loser or a winner when both parties walked away with what they wanted!","What he did learn was that THE Creature’s power was unique beyond measure. Even though their confrontation occurred eons in the past from his perspective, THE Creature had felt just as strong if not stronger than the current version Noah had talked to in Alfheimr. That ancient monster had been playing with Adversity for longer than Noah could properly calculate, experimenting with concepts that most beings couldn’t comprehend.","But after fighting against him, Noah could effectively say that in all of existence, there likely wasn’t a single entity at THE First Scale who could possibly push him around.","If there was a competition for who the strongest entity below THE Proterozoic Scale was, he was fairly confident he’d be taking that title. With his control over Infinity externally, and now his control over Quintessence Infiniforce internally, paired with the budding and terrifying force of THE Infiniverse, the only thing he was currently looking forward to was punching upward toward entities on an entirely different Scale.","It felt like the change of the Organ of Civilization would aid with that endeavor.","HUUM!","As he was thinking this, he gained a profound new sense from the organ.","It felt like an extension of his being in ways his previous Organ of Civilization never had. Something within it had shifted, gaining an invisible force that pressed against his awareness with intensity that demanded acknowledgment. At this moment, he felt it begin to shine with multicolored crystalline light that pushed outward from within his chest.","The organ had stopped at the very center of his chest.","It had found its home.","The moment it completed its transformation...","BOOM!","Noah’s figure rose into the air involuntarily, lifted by forces responding to what had just emerged within him. The golden sand that had been floating around him began to spin in configurations that placed him at the absolute center, each grain orbiting his form as if he was the core of a galaxy being born. Light poured from his chest in streams of multicolored brilliance that painted the Early Veiled Shore in hues existence rarely witnessed.","As utmost glory spun around him, his chest began to shine even brighter.","From it began to rise a weapon.","A multicolored resplendent crystalline spear emerged from his sternum, pushing through flesh that parted without pain, materializing into physical form as it left his body. The weapon was a Kontos spear, its shaft stretching longer than cavalry lances, designed for reach and devastating strikes from positions of superiority. The crystalline material comprising it shifted through every color contained within Quintessence Infiniforce, never settling on a single hue, constantly flowing through the spectrum in patterns.","The spearhead itself was leaf-shaped and broad, edges sharp enough that looking at them seemed to cut perception. Runes he didn’t recognize covered the shaft in spiraling configurations, each one pulsing with light that matched the rhythm of his heartbeat. The butt of the spear ended in a crystalline counterweight that balanced the weapon perfectly despite its impossible length.","After it emerged fully and floated above Noah’s chest, he raised his hand to grasp it.","Everything around him began to tremble.","The Early Veiled Shore shook. The Three Thousand Realms beyond shook. THE Infiniverse itself seemed to recognize what had just been born within its creator’s existence. Noah’s fingers closed around the shaft of the spear, and the moment contact was made, prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Weapon Manifestation Complete|","| THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has allowed the emergence of THE Hadean Spear of Civilization.|","|THE HADEAN SPEAR OF CIVILIZATION|","|Classification: Civilizational Armament|","|Origin: First weapon to emerge from THE Hadean Organ of Civilization. Manifested through the transformation of the Organ within THE Youngest, bearer of Infinity and master of THE Seed of Observable Existence.|","|Description: A Kontos-style crystalline spear composed of solidified Quintessence Infiniforce merged with Observable and Unobservable weavings from THE Infiniverse. The weapon exists as an extension of its wielder’s transformed Organ of Civilization rather than a separate construct.|","| This Spear of Civilization holds the entire force of what is Observable and Unobservable within THE Infiniverse, multiplied by a factor of ten, then raised by an exponent of three . The resulting force contained within this weapon cannot be calculated.|","|Wielder Restriction: The only existence capable of bearing this Spear of Civilization is the one who holds THE Hadean Organ of Civilization. All others will find the spear impossible to lift regardless of their accumulated authority. The force contained within would crush any foundations lacking the specific transformation required to bear it.|","|WARNING: The force contained within this weapon is extremely heavy. Exercise caution regarding where you direct the tip of this spear. It is not recommended to point it toward anything at THE First Scale unless you wish to see their complete decimation. Their Civilizations will collapse. Their foundations will dissolve. Their existence will end before they comprehend what struck them.|","|Effectiveness against beings at THE Second Scale of Existence has not been determined. Testing against Proterozoic Scale entities is recommended before relying on this weapon in genuine conflict at those heights.|","...!","Noah grasped THE Hadean Spear of Civilization and felt like he’d gained a truly terrifying extension of his power. The force within it pressed against his palm with intensity that would have atomized his hand before his transformation. Now it felt right. Heavy, but manageable. Devastating, but controllable.","But he knew that even this was only the cusp of the iceberg for his Organ of Civilization.","He could sense what was happening inside of it now, perceive aspects of his internal existence that had been hidden before the transformation. There were even grander changes occurring within, configurations that the spear’s emergence had only begun to reveal.","Inside his Organ of Civilization was the internal prison he’d created long ago.","THE Infinite Desmoterion.","He’d sent his own alternate body and identity there, Ozymandias, that hunger-driven portion of himself that he’d separated to cultivate independently.","Alongside Ozymandias waited the trash, repulsive, misshapen, good for nothing, useless foul waste of an Absolute who was THE Living Elemental, among other prisoners whose Civilizations he benefited from.","As their Civilizations arose, so would his. That was the nature of the prison he’d designed.","The transformation of the Organ of Civilization had affected this prison immensely.","New prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Internal Domain Transformation Detected|","|Due to the emergence of THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, an entire Civilizational Eon of Development has been carried out across THE Hadean Desmoterion. All prisoners within have experienced large jumps in power as time dilation paired with changes within the prison accelerated beyond previous parameters.|","|Progress notes of one prisoner in particular have been pulled forth for review.|","| PRISONER PROGRESS NOTES: OZYMANDIAS|","|Identity: Alternate existence of Master, separated and imprisoned for independent cultivation|","|Civilization: Infinite Hunger|","| Progress During Civilizational Eon of Development:|","|Phase One: Ozymandias achieved Uncountable Infinity across all depths of Absolute Sovereignty within the Civilization of Infinite Hunger. This process consumed approximately half of the Civilizational Eon.|","|Phase Two: The remaining half of the Civilizational Eon was spent reinforcing and saturating existence with Quintessence Infiniforce and the force of Observable and Unobservable weavings that have permeated across THE Hadean Organ of Civilization. Foundations have been thoroughly transformed.|","|Current Status: Ozymandias has reached the absolute peak of THE First Scale of Existence . No further advancement is possible without transitioning to THE Second Scale.|","|Recommendation: It is now possible for Ozymandias to establish a Civilizational Anchor to grasp identity as a Proterozoic Scale entity . All prerequisites have been met. The path forward is open.|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has currently generated one additional usage of a Civilizational Eon of Development.|","| Shall this usage be utilized to take this alternate portion of your existence to THE Proterozoic Scale?|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has transformed sufficiently to allow the release of prisoners within for a maximum duration of ten seconds, available once per hour.|","...!","Noah floated in the air above the Early Veiled Shore, golden sand orbiting him like a galaxy, THE Hadean Spear of Civilization gripped in his hand, prompts declaring capabilities he hadn’t anticipated stretching before his vision.","Ozymandias had reached the peak of THE First Scale. That alternate portion of himself, cultivating independently within his prison, had achieved everything THE First Scale could offer. And now a choice presented itself.","Should he use the Civilizational Eon of Development to push Ozymandias into THE Proterozoic Scale?","A portion of himself at THE Second Scale while the rest remained at THE First.","Noah smiled as he looked at the spear in his hand.","THE Proterozoic Scale loomed ahead!."]},{"number":5049,"title":"Chapter 5049: Chapter 5048: Hadean! IV","paragraphs":["<Unknown Record>","Very few knew who THE Youngest actually was across Observable Existence.","They heard stories. Whispers passed between beings who had witnessed fragments of his journey or felt the tremors of his Causes rippling through regions they called home.","They knew of him as the anomalous entity who wielded Infinity, the impossible existence who conducted endless authority seamlessly. His name circulated through the conversations of Primordial Architects and Singular Cognizances alike.","Most had never met him. Most were still looking for him.","They searched through Primordial Realms and hidden domains, following traces of Infinity that led nowhere, hunting an entity who moved faster than their schemes could track. They wanted to study him, use him, break him down into components they could understand and replicate. They spent time planning for a confrontation they assumed would go in their favor.","Then he began to pull out his spear.","Many would intimately come to know THE Youngest after that moment. They would learn exactly who he was and what he could do. They would understand, with perfect clarity, why the stories had failed to capture the truth of what he represented.","Their understanding lasted nanoseconds before the darkness of collapse overcame them.","Pity the souls that ever faced the end of that spear. Pity them, mourn them, and forget them. Because nothing remained of those existences worth remembering.","-Observation recorded in the aftermath of THE Hadean Decimations , author presumed dissolved","---","Noah grasped THE Hadean Spear of Civilization in his hand as he floated down gently toward the golden sands.","The grains cradled his figure when he landed, settling around his feet as if welcoming him back to solid ground. He put his other hand on his chest and sensed the terrifying pressure of THE Hadean Organ of Civilization pulsing within, its presence now unmistakable in ways it hadn’t been before the transformation. The organ had gained new capabilities.","The prison within him had changed.","Civilizational Eons of Development would now be generated through THE Hadean Organ of Civilization. One had already passed during the initial transformation, accelerating everything within THE Hadean Desmoterion beyond what normal time dilation could achieve. He had one more available. And he could utilize it to have his imprisoned self within him take that step and become a Second Scale existence.","With existence being so vast and full of terrors, this wasn’t something he would ever deny.","\" Utilize the Civilizational Eon of Development.\"","He spoke the command lightly, as if ordering a meal rather than triggering a transformation that would reshape part of his own existence.","HUUM!","Prompts bloomed before his vision immediately.","|Command Accepted|","|The remaining Civilizational Eon of Development has been utilized.|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization is carrying out prolific, comprehensive, and quintessential advancement within THE Hadean Desmoterion. An entire eon will pass within the next ten seconds. Results will be displayed upon completion.|","|Time Remaining: 10 seconds|","...!","Noah smiled brilliantly at the words.","Ten seconds out here. An entire eon in there. His other self would have lifetimes to accomplish what needed accomplishing while Noah barely had time to examine what he’d already gained.","He proceeded to grasp his spear properly and look at it while the seconds began to tick down.","The weapon felt light within his hands despite carrying the terrifying power of his Infiniverse’s Observable and Unobservable weavings multiplied by a factor of ten and then raised by an exponent of three.","The spear responded to his grip as if it weighed nothing at all. The crystalline shaft hummed against his palms, resonating with his heartbeat in ways that made him feel like the weapon had always been part of him.","He needed to get a feel for it.","Noah raised the spear above his head and swung it down once in a simple vertical arc.","The motion began slowly, almost lazily, the crystalline weapon cutting through air that suddenly felt thick with potential. As the spearhead descended, something emerged around the shaft that made Noah’s eyes widen with genuine surprise.","Two rivers of misty light began swirling around the weapon.","The first river was clear, almost invisible, perceptible only through the way it bent light around itself. It moved like smoke given purpose, coiling around the spear’s shaft in patterns that seemed to follow rules Noah couldn’t immediately identify.","This force felt cold in ways that had nothing to do with temperature, pressing against his awareness with the sensation of everything that existed beyond perception’s reach.","The Unobservable.","The second river blazed with golden luminosity that painted the Early Veiled Shore in hues of captured sunlight. It wound around the spear in configurations opposite to its clear counterpart, the two forces spiraling together without ever quite touching.","This force felt warm and present, the accumulated acknowledgment of everything that could be witnessed pressing outward with intensity that demanded recognition.","The Observable.","Both rivers danced around his descending spear as if existence itself had decided to manifest its fundamental division through his weapon. Clear and gold, hidden and seen, unknown and known, the two forces representing everything that Proterozoic Scale beings pulled into themselves to forge their transformations. He was watching the nature of Second Scale power made visible around a weapon that shouldn’t exist.","His seemingly simple swing stopped midway through its arc.","The rivers of clear and gold didn’t stop with it.","BOOM!","The force continued forward without the spear to guide it.","Utter devastation unfolded before Noah’s eyes as the golden sands in front of him split down the middle. A canyon carved itself into the Early Veiled Shore, reaching deeper than the sands should have extended, revealing layers of existence beneath that he’d never seen. The sacred waters of the shores ahead parted like curtains being drawn aside, liquid authority separating into two halves that continued moving apart as the force traveled beyond them.","Light years away, the shimmering barrier protecting the Early Veiled Shore from the rest of THE Infiniverse tore open!","The force of a single incomplete swing had crossed distances, ripping through protections designed to keep his farms safe from everything outside them. Beyond that barrier, Noah sensed the damage continuing, the rivers of Observable and Unobservable force pressing toward one of the Three Thousand Realms with momentum that showed no signs of stopping!","His expression went somber immediately.","Noah clenched his free hand and pulled, his will reaching out to grasp the escaping force and dissipate it before it could tear through an entire Realm he’d just created. The clear and golden rivers resisted for a moment, wanting to continue their path of destruction, before finally dissolving into harmless particles of light that scattered across the void.","\"...\"","He breathed out calmly and looked down at the terrifying weapon in his hand.","One swing. Not even a complete swing. Just the beginning of a vertical arc, stopped halfway through, and the resulting force had nearly destroyed a Realm while tearing across light years of distance. This was a catastrophe shaped like a spear, devastation given form that could be directed but would require extreme care to control!","As he was holding it, processing what had just happened, he began to feel something else.","His own body started emanating terrifying waves of power that pressed outward in pulses matching his heartbeat. His immensity, which he’d already thought was reaching unheard of heights, was rising even further. This change came from within, his Organ of Civilization pulsing with glory as something completed itself in THE Hadean Desmoterion.","The ten seconds had passed.","New prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Civilizational Eon of Development: Complete|","|Progress Report: OZYMANDIAS|","| Phase One: Civilizational Anchor Establishment|","|Duration: First half of Civilizational Eon|","| Ozymandias utilized his profound foundation, refined across the previous Civilizational Eon of Development, to establish his Civilizational Anchor . The absolute self-knowledge required for this process was achieved through introspection spanning centuries of dilated time. Every aspect of his existence was examined, understood, and crystallized into certainty that could not be shaken.|","|Result: Civilizational Anchor successfully established. Ozymandias has grasped THE Proterozoic Scale of Existence . Your alternate self now exists at THE Second Scale.|","|Phase Two: Proterozoic Transformation Attempt|","| Duration: Latter half of Civilizational Eon|","|With the Civilizational Anchor established, Ozymandias utilized the remaining time to attempt the formation of a Proterozoic Organ or Bone. Materials available within THE Hadean Desmoterion, combined with the Observable and Unobservable weavings permeating THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, were employed in this process.|","|Result: In Progress. Transformation has begun.|","|Your other self seeks for you to experience the changes directly. Ozymandias requests that you send your gaze into the prison and experience the eon of development through the memories accumulated during the process.|","|A Civilizational Eon’s worth of experiences awaits your review.|","...!","Noah smiled brilliantly as he felt the terrifying changes resonating through his existence.","Due to the dilated time governing his prison, he could peek into the memories of Ozymandias whenever he chose to. Every moment of that eon, every struggle and breakthrough and revelation his other self had experienced, all of it waited for him to observe. He now had a Civilizational Eon’s worth of memories to sift through at his leisure.","More importantly, he could feel just what had happened to his other self.","Ozymandias had taken the step forward.","A portion of his existence now operated at THE Proterozoic Scale, and it felt...immense!"]},{"number":5050,"title":"Chapter 5050: Chapter 5049: A Warning","paragraphs":["While one man made a modest advancement in THE Infiniverse.","Heavy rainfall bloomed across the Wastes in rivers of multicolored brilliance that transformed everything they touched.","The region that had earned its name through desolation and emptiness was changing. Where barren expanses had stretched for light years, new formations emerged from the saturated ground. Structures of crystallized authority rose from spaces that hadn’t produced anything in eons.","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity was rewriting this corner of Observable Existence, and soon the Wastes might no longer deserve their name at all.","Through this transforming landscape moved a massive figure.","Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor, walked with his enormous hammer resting against one shoulder, each step pressing craters into ground too weak to support his passage.","His invisible expression was thoughtful beneath the helmet that had become part of his existence, contemplating changes that affected plans he’d spent eons developing. The rainfall couldn’t touch him directly, his corrupted glory deflecting the multicolored drops before they could land on his armored form.","Then he came to a stop and looked out into the distance.","His helmet turned toward something appearing on the horizon, something that shouldn’t have been possible given the distances involved.","Across the Wastes, a massive illusory form materialized against the transformed space.","A titan wreathed in flames towered over the landscape, humanoid in shape but vast beyond mortal comprehension. The figure burned with authority that pressed against everything perceiving it, fire that consumed nothing but illuminated everything. It was an illusory image of...THE Creature!","THE Creature sat upon a makeshift throne of condensed existence, leaning back with a posture suggesting absolute dominion over everything within his sight.","Rivers of unique power surged across his body in configurations that defied classification, authority flowing through him in patterns that declared his position among the apex of Observable Existence. His flames burned brighter where the multicolored rain fell upon them, consuming the Pluvial Epoch’s effects as fuel rather than submitting to their transformative nature.","In both hands, he held something that made Beowulf’s armored body vibrate with shock.","Eyes.","Massive crimson eyes, each one larger than realms, rested in THE Creature’s grip like trophies claimed from a defeated enemy. These were the eyes that had formed across the Wastes to put countless beings under their control, the instruments through which influence had spread.","The Eyes of Horus.","But at this moment, those eyes were bloody and torn and ruptured. They stood lifeless in THE Creature’s hands, their crimson light extinguished, their power ended. Whatever conflict had occurred between THE Creature and Horus, the outcome was now being displayed for all of existence to witness.","Beowulf stared at this image as his massive armored body continued vibrating, frequencies of agitation running through foundations that rarely experienced uncertainty.","But he wasn’t the only one privy to this scene.","In all regions across the Wastes, the illusory image appeared simultaneously. In Prima Indifferentia, where ancient beings stirred in domains they’d occupied since before differentiation. In Primordial Realms scattered throughout Observable Existence, where Architects and Terrors and Undivided Ones now moved in and conducted their endless pursuits.","In every corner where the awareness and gazes of powerful beings at the First and Second Scale permeated, the grand illusory visage of THE Creature holding the lifeless Eyes of Horus manifested.","He didn’t say anything.","His bearing and posture spoke clearly enough without words. The way he sat upon that throne, the casual grip with which he held eyes that had terrorized regions, the flames burning around him with intensity that suggested this display cost him nothing, all of it communicated a singular message to those rising across Observable Existence.","Behave.","In Prima Indifferentia, the image of THE Creature appeared against space that hadn’t seen clear light since before most current beings existed.","Moments later, the deluge of rivers and multicolored rain parted.","A crack opened in the fabric of this ancient realm, splitting silently like a wound appearing in flesh that had forgotten it could be cut. Two obsidian hands emerged from the darkness within that crack, fingers curling around the edges as if they were unveiling pages of a book rather than tearing through the barriers between spaces.","The hands pulled the crack wider.","From the widened opening, an obsidian face poked out to observe the illusory image of THE Creature displayed across Prima Indifferentia’s transformed skies.","The head was stellar obsidian given humanoid form, darkness so complete that it seemed to absorb the multicolored light falling all around. A single obsidian horn emerged from the center of its forehead, curving upward in configurations that suggested crown more than weapon. The features beneath were sharp and ancient.","But the entire head and that single horn shone with a distinct light.","Proterozoic light.","When the illusory flames of THE Creature reflected against that obsidian skull, the bones beneath became visible through the darkness. They blazed with brilliance declaring their nature to anyone capable of perceiving it.","The skull itself was a Proterozoic Bone, transformed through methodologies that most beings couldn’t survive. That single horn was another Proterozoic Bone, authority crystallized into physical form through processes spanning eons of careful cultivation.","This was a Second Scale existence observing THE Creature’s warning.","The obsidian face watched the image of those ruined eyes held in THE Creature’s grip. It studied the casual dominance displayed in that seated posture, the declaration of supremacy being broadcast across all of Observable Existence.","Then it smiled.","The expression was brutal and glorious, teeth of stellar obsidian catching Proterozoic light as lips pulled back in appreciation rather than fear. This being looked at THE Creature’s terrifying displayed feat and found it amusing. Found it exciting. Found it worthy of response!","Laughter erupted from that obsidian throat.","The sound stretched outward from the crack in Prima Indifferentia, carrying across distances that light would need eons to traverse. Gigaparsecs of space trembled as that laughter rolled through them, the amusement of a Proterozoic Scale existence declaring its reaction to THE Creature’s warning.","The laughter didn’t stop.","It echoed across Prima Indifferentia long after the obsidian face retreated back into the crack from which it had emerged, the sound continuing to resonate through transformed landscapes and ancient domains.","THE Creature’s warning had been delivered, but not everyone who received it was intimidated."]},{"number":5051,"title":"Chapter 5051: Chapter 5050: Vengeance I","paragraphs":["The Xenoturbella is a marine organism with no brain, no gut, no organs of any kind.","It has one hole. Food enters through this hole. Waste exits through the same hole. It drifts along the ocean floor consuming whatever it bumps into, existing for no clear reason or purpose that scientists have ever determined. Evolution produced it and then apparently forgot about it.","Somehow, THE Living Elemental was lesser than such an existence.","The Xenoturbella at least committed to its simplicity. It never pretended to be more than a tube with ambitions limited to its next meal. THE Living Elemental reached for greatness, achieved Absolute depths at THE First Scale, accumulated authority that should have meant something, and still managed to contribute less to Observable Existence than a creature whose entire biological strategy was \"have hole.\"","At least the Xenoturbella never disappointed anyone.","At least the Xenoturbella never failed upward into imprisonment.","At least the Xenoturbella, in its humble way, knew exactly what it was and never aspired to become something its foundations couldn’t support.","THE Living Elemental could learn much from such an organism.","Unfortunately, learning required a capacity for growth that THE Living Elemental had never demonstrated.","-Commentary discovered in THE Hadean Desmoterion’s administrative records, author confirmed to be Ozymandias during a moment of particular irritation","---","The memories of Ozymandias flittered through Noah’s mind as he assumed active control of this body and extended his awareness into THE Hadean Desmoterion.","Endless days of peaceful cultivation stretched through his perception. He experienced centuries of patient accumulation, the gradual saturation of foundations with Quintessence Infiniforce, the methodical integration of Observable and Unobservable weavings into an existence preparing for transformation. Then came the establishment of THE Civilizational Anchor, that moment when his other self crystallized absolute certainty regarding what he was and what he would never compromise.","The affirmations echoed through him now, words that Ozymandias had spoken into the void of the prison while forging an identity that could not be shaken.","\" Hunger is not weakness. Hunger is the only honest truth in existence.\"","\"Everything consumes. Everything devours. Everything feeds. Those who deny this lie to themselves while their foundations cannibalize their potential.\"","\"I am Hunger given form. I am the acknowledgment that existence itself is predation. I do not apologize for what I am. I do not pretend to be something gentler. I consume because consumption is the fundamental act of being, and I have simply ceased pretending otherwise.\"","\"My Anchor is Hunger. My Anchor is truth. My Anchor cannot be moved because Hunger cannot be eliminated from existence itself. And my Hunger...is Infinite.\"","Noah opened his eyes to observe THE Hadean Desmoterion spread before him.","The body of Ozymandias possessed qualities distinct from his main form. Titanic and muscular, its surface shone stellar obsidian mixed with crimson brilliance that pulsed with rhythms matching a heartbeat far slower than any mortal organ could produce.","He stood upon a massive blue mountain submerged in liquid Mana, the substance flowing around his legs as though water had forgotten it should obey gravity.","The surroundings defied simple classification.","Land masses floated through spaces that held no consistent orientation, their surfaces covered in vegetation that glowed with internal light.","Cosmic phenomena spiraled between these landmasses, miniature galaxies and stellar nurseries providing illumination that originated from every direction simultaneously. Folds of condensed authority created passages between regions, their entrances visible as shimmering distortions in the fabric of this internal domain.","Wheels of Existence rotated in the distance, massive constructs providing structure to a realm that might otherwise have dissolved into chaos.","This was an ancient era given physical form. A primordial landscape where geography merged with cosmology, where the rules governing normal existence bent to accommodate configurations that should not coexist.","Noah sensed everything within THE Hadean Desmoterion.","The prisoners he had placed here from Ginnungagap had all transformed during the Civilizational Eons of Development. Every single one had reached Absolute depths at THE First Scale, their foundations elevated by time dilation and the ambient authority permeating this transformed prison.","Even THE Living Elemental had become something exceeding a normal Absolute.","Merely contemplating that being caused irritation to surge through Ozymandias’s titanic form. Noah surveyed the prison for this particular prisoner and located him light years distant, standing upon a region filled with swirling meteors of fire, earth, water, and air. The four elements the fool had constructed his entire Civilization around orbited him in configurations suggesting deep meditation.","This contemptible existence was actually attempting to form his Civilizational Anchor.","So much time and harvests had flowed into THE Hadean Organ of Civilization that even this worthless refuse known as Elemental was endeavoring to reach THE Second Scale. It would benefit Noah if Elemental succeeded, as the prison’s growth fed back into his own foundations. That was the entire purpose of maintaining prisoners whose cultivation contributed to his advancement.","However, when Noah recalled that unforgivable day he had endured because of this being...","He took a single step and crossed light years instantaneously.","Ozymandias materialized upon the mountain where THE Living Elemental meditated, his titanic obsidian form casting shadows across the swirling elemental meteors. The prisoner’s eyes opened immediately, perceiving the arrival of something that should not have been possible within this prison.","THE Living Elemental appeared as a being composed of the four classical forces given humanoid shape. Fire blazed along one arm while water flowed along the other. Earth formed his torso in configurations of living stone, and air swirled around his head in winds that never ceased moving. His features held terror now, recognizing the body standing before him.","\"Wait, I was merely-\"","Noah did not permit him to finish.","Ozymandias’s right leg rose with speed that should not have been possible for something so massive, and the sole of his foot connected with THE Living Elemental’s chest.","BOOM!","The impact sent the prisoner cratering into the mountain beneath him, stone and crystal shattering outward in rings of devastation. Before Elemental could recover, Noah’s left leg descended in a stomp that drove the fool deeper into the ruined terrain. Fire and water scattered from the prisoner’s form as his elemental composition struggled to maintain coherence under the assault.","Noah kicked him again.","And again.","Each impact drove THE Living Elemental further into broken ground, his screams echoing across the region as meteors of his own elements spun chaotically overhead. Noah experienced no particular satisfaction from this action. It was not about satisfaction. It was about justice for a day he would never forget!","His final kick connected with Elemental’s midsection and launched the prisoner light years across THE Hadean Desmoterion.","The trajectory concluded when Elemental collided with a distant mountain, the impact visible as a flash of light against the cosmic backdrop of the prison’s impossible geography.","Noah exhaled slowly.","He felt somewhat improved.","This was a shameful moment, admittedly. Petty in ways that did not befit the image of THE Genesis Monarch conducting Infinity across Observable Existence.","However, this occurred inside his own existence with no one to observe, and what THE Living Elemental had done remained unforgivable regardless of how much time elapsed.","Certain grudges deserved to be maintained!"]},{"number":5052,"title":"Chapter 5052: Chapter 5051: Vengeance II","paragraphs":["Noah acknowledged this truth to himself and finally directed his attention to the completing process of Ozymandias’s transformation.","His other self had spent the latter half of the Civilizational Eon attempting to form a Proterozoic Bone, and according to the prompts, the process had commenced.","However, when he examined Ozymandias’s body more thoroughly, he realized something had actually been accomplished.","THE Proterozoic Bone resided in his right leg.","Noah elevated the limb and examined what his other self had forged during that eon of isolated cultivation. The bones of his right leg, from knee to toes, shimmered with multicolored brilliance unlike anything the remainder of Ozymandias’s body contained.","The patella gleamed at his knee, transformed into something beyond normal bone. Below it, the tibia and fibula ran parallel down his shin, both blazing with light that pressed against perception. The tarsals of his ankle, the metatarsals of his foot, and the phalanges of his toes had all been converted into Proterozoic configurations that declared their nature to anyone capable of perceiving it.","They were unfathomably heavy!","Oh!","It was actually his right leg that contained the Proterozoic Bone? No wonder THE Living Elemental had appeared near death when Noah believed he was exercising tremendous restraint. Those kicks had not been casual discipline. They had been strikes from a limb forged at THE Second Scale landing upon a body still anchored at THE First!","Noah observed that leg as terrifying pressure emanated from it, force similar to his Spear of Civilization radiating outward with each movement. When he exerted pressure deliberately, channeling authority through the transformed bones, something emerged.","Two rivers of misty light began swirling around his leg.","The first river was clear and nearly invisible, moving like smoke given purpose as it coiled around his shin and ankle. This was the force of Unobservable, that vast darkness beyond perception now flowing through bones that had learned to channel it.","The second river blazed with golden luminosity, a misty current of power wrapping around his leg in patterns opposite to its clear counterpart. This was the force of Observable, the accumulated acknowledgment of everything witnessed now integrated into his transformed limb.","When they swirled together around his right leg, Noah felt as though he could crush anything!","Prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Proterozoic Bone Formation Detected|","| Collective Designation: THE Hadean Limb of Infinite Hunger|","|Components: Patella, Tibia, Fibula, Tarsals, Metatarsals, and Phalanges of the right leg, all transformed through Proterozoic methodology during Civilizational Eon of Development.|","|Description: THE Hadean Limb of Infinite Hunger has been forged through the integration of Infinity, Observable, and Unobservable weavings into bone structure prepared by the Civilization of Infinite Hunger. This Proterozoic Bone contains THE Civilizational Instinctus and Autonomous Existential Response infused and elevated within its marrow.|","|Civilizational Instinctus: The limb will react to threats before conscious awareness processes them. Attacks launched against the bearer will be countered by autonomous responses from the transformed bones.|","|Much of this Proterozoic Bone’s weavings and capabilities remain unknown. Field testing against appropriate opponents is recommended before relying upon this transformation in genuine conflict at THE Second Scale.|","...!","It required testing.","Noah’s eyes, or rather Ozymandias’s eyes, shone with tyranny as he considered the prompt’s recommendation. He required a test subject. Someone who could provide genuine resistance while not being so overwhelmingly powerful that the test became meaningless. Someone strong enough to compel this Proterozoic Limb toward revealing its capabilities.","Who precisely would be sufficient to permit him a satisfactory confrontation while also not being defeated in a one-sided manner?","\"...\"","His eyes shone brightly moments later as a smile spread across Ozymandias’s obsidian features.","He already knew.","---","Noah’s eyes flickered back to the Early Veiled Shore as he permitted his other body within his Organ of Civilization to continue as it was.","The transformation of Ozymandias could proceed without his direct attention. THE Hadean Limb of Infinite Hunger required testing, and his other self possessed sufficient autonomy to pursue that objective initially. The connection between his bodies allowed information to flow in both directions, ensuring he would know immediately if anything significant occurred within THE Hadean Desmoterion.","He breathed out and sensed his Organ of Civilization more thoroughly than he had before.","After the Spear of Civilization and THE Hadean Desmoterion, he knew the transformation was not yet complete. The Organ continued pulsing against his chest, multicolored light radiating outward in waves that suggested additional capabilities waiting to be revealed. Something else remained.","\" What is the last surprise you have for me?\"","He spoke such words with a smile, addressing his own existence as though it were a separate entity capable of responding. In some ways, it was.","The spinning Organ of Civilization on his chest released a multicolored pulse in response to his question.","Waves of information bloomed before his vision as prompts materialized with brilliance that pressed against his awareness. The golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore trembled beneath his feet as his Organ communicated what it had become.","|Final Transformation Stage Detected|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has culminated all weavings of your Existence and Civilizations into unified expression.|","| The integral weavings of your Archai, Mundi, Atlas, Grimoire, and everything you stand for have stepped forward to affirm a singular truth: through your Organ of Civilization and weavings of Infinity, you possess the capability to emulate any Civilization in Existence.|","|This capability exceeds simple mimicry. You do not merely copy but you comprehend, integrate, and express Civilizations as though they were always part of your foundations.|","BOOM!","The prompts were substantial ones, and Noah’s eyes spun gloriously as he processed their implications.","Around his body, the clear and golden misty forces of Unobservable and Observable began to swirl without his conscious direction. The clear river coiled around his left side, that vast darkness beyond perception responding to his Organ’s transformation. The golden river wrapped around his right side, the accumulated acknowledgment of everything witnessed declaring its presence alongside its counterpart.","Both forces recognized that something significant had just been unlocked within his existence!","The prompts continued their disclosure.","|Weavings of your Cheats, Loot, Quintessence, and Protagonist among all others have guided the Organ of Civilization to allow for the emergence of THE Hadean Coalescence.|","|Primary Function: Your Organ of Civilization will act as a magnet to passively multiply by ten and elevate by an exponent of three all incoming harvests. Resources, authority, and cultivation gains directed toward your existence will be amplified through this methodology before integration into your foundations.|","|Secondary Function: You may now pull Hadean Civilizational Singularities from any entity you are actively observing. These Singularities represent compressed expressions of their Civilization’s fundamental nature. After pulling and absorbing a sufficient number of Hadean Civilizational Singularities from a target, you can freely express their Civilization as it will be recorded into your Organ of Civilization.|","|Tertiary Function: All Recorded Civilizations will be broken down and analyzed for weaknesses you can utilize. Understanding an enemy’s Civilization grants understanding of how to dismantle it.|","|Quaternary Function: The Weavings of Loot and Cheats have advanced further to permit selection of a maximum of three targets possessing strong enough connection to your Existence. From these selected targets, you may siphon Hadean Existential Singularities .|","|Hadean Existential Singularities can include: understanding regarding the usage of Observable and Unobservable forces, Infinity comprehension, progress of cultivation, musings on Proterozoic Organs or Bones, and any other miscellaneous aspects relating to their existence.|","|The more powerful an existence is compared to you, the less effective the extraction of Hadean Existential Singularities becomes.|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly at the set of prompts flashing before him.","He breathed in deeply as he contemplated the many implications cascading through his awareness. He could observe enemies and extract understanding of their Civilizations. He could select enemies and siphon their existential progress directly into himself!","His body in Nakatsukuni presented immediate opportunities.","He would be able to siphon Hadean Civilizational Singularities from Naldine and the Singular Cognizance to comprehend their Civilizations and eventually emulate them. The Primordial Architect who had been teaching him about THE Proterozoic Scale could become a source of knowledge beyond what she consciously shared.","The ancient Sadakar could provide understanding of Singular Cognizance methodology simply by being observed.","And if he selected grand enough targets for the three slots permitting Hadean Existential Singularity extraction...","Well, even powerful enemies would contribute to his advancement however slowly.","\"Hmm...\"","Noah rose up with bright eyes, his mind already racing through potential selections. Three targets with strong connections to his existence. The criteria suggested beings he had interacted with significantly, entities whose fates had become intertwined with his own through conflict. Several candidates presented themselves immediately.","He was about to begin the selection process when something caused him to pause.","Astonishment crossed his features as he looked out across the Early Veiled Shore.","His gaze traveled further, extending past the vast and nigh endless Infiniverse into the outside landscape where rivers and seas of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity spread through Observable Existence. The multicolored rain continued falling across regions his authority had touched, transforming everything it contacted while declaring his influence to anyone capable of perceiving it.","And there, projected across the transformed skies, he observed something unexpected.","The illusory image of THE Creature holding the lifeless Eyes of Horus blazed against the backdrop of existence itself.","That massive titan wreathed in flames sat upon a makeshift throne, posture radiating dominion over everything within sight. In both hands, he gripped crimson eyes that had terrorized regions for eons, now bloody and torn and ruptured beyond repair. The message being broadcast required no words to comprehend.","Horus had fallen.","THE Creature had claimed victory and was now displaying the proof to all of Observable Existence.","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly as he observed this declaration of supremacy. He could not help but nod in appreciation of what this being had accomplished. His hands came together in applause that echoed across the Early Veiled Shore, genuine respect expressed through the simple act of clapping.","\" Well done...\"","He spoke the words aloud even though THE Creature could not hear them from this distance. Props were deserved when props were earned, and eliminating Horus while Noah had been focused on his own transformations demonstrated exactly why THE Creature remained the most dangerous entity in Observable Existence!","The warning being broadcast was clear.","Behave, or face the same fate.","Noah smiled at the image before returning his attention to the selection of his three targets. THE Creature’s display had reminded him of something important.","Power in Observable Existence was not merely accumulated. It was demonstrated. It was declared. It was shown to those who might otherwise forget that certain beings should not be challenged.","His Hadean Coalescence would permit him to grow through methodology his enemies could not perceive.","By the time they understood what he was doing, he would have already extracted everything he required from them.","---","<The Parable of THE Hollowing Witness>","In Prima Indifferentia, there exists a creature known as THE Hollowing Witness.","It does not hunt or chase. It does not announce itself through roars or displays of dominance that might alert its prey to approaching danger. THE Hollowing Witness simply watches from distances its targets cannot perceive, observing through senses that operate outside the boundaries of normal awareness.","While it watches, it feeds.","Not on anything the observed entity would notice missing until far too late. THE Hollowing Witness consumes potential .","It devours futures that have not yet occurred, digesting possibilities its targets would have otherwise achieved. Every moment of observation removes something from the prey that they never knew they possessed.","A being observed for a single day loses nothing significant. A being observed for a year loses opportunities they would have dismissed as bad luck. A being observed for a century begins to wonder why their cultivation has slowed, why breakthroughs that should have arrived remain perpetually out of reach, why existence itself seems to resist their advancement.","A being observed for an eon discovers they have become hollow without ever understanding how.","There is a tale told among the Undivided Ones of Prima Indifferentia regarding a Formless Terror who grew suspicious of his stagnation. He had cultivated diligently for millennia. He had consumed resources that should have elevated him beyond his current state. Yet he remained precisely where he had been when his efforts began, as though running in place while believing himself to be sprinting forward.","He searched for enemies. He found none.","He searched for curses. He discovered nothing.","He searched for parasites feeding upon his foundations. His existence was clean.","Only when he was moments from dissolution, his potential entirely consumed, did he finally perceive THE Hollowing Witness observing him from a distance his weakened senses could barely register. The creature had been watching for longer than the Formless Terror had been aware of his own stagnation. Every future he might have claimed had already been digested. Every height he might have reached had already been stolen.","The Formless Terror screamed a single question before his existence collapsed into nothing.","\"Why me?\"","THE Hollowing Witness did not answer, for it had already turned its attention toward new prey.","The parable concludes with a truth that those in Prima Indifferentia understand intimately: the most dangerous predators are not those who face you in battle. They are those who have already won before you realize the conflict has begun. By the time you stand before them, you have already lost everything that might have permitted victory.","You simply have not noticed yet."]},{"number":5053,"title":"Chapter 5053: Chapter 5052: Vengeance III","paragraphs":["The figure of Alexander appeared on the Early Veiled Shore, stepping through folds of space that recognized him as welcome within this domain.","Noah turned toward his arrival and nodded in acknowledgment before waving his hand toward the skies above. Reality responded to his gesture, and the image of THE Creature holding the lifeless Eyes of Horus materialized against the backdrop of the Early Veiled Shore. That massive titan wreathed in flames now blazed above the golden sands, his trophy displayed for Alexander to witness just as it was being displayed across all of Observable Existence.","Noah turned to Alexander as he spoke.","\" Even Second Scale Primordial Architects like Horus are not untouchable. You likely had him among those you would seek vengeance against in the future, but he is now taken care of.\"","His eyes studied Alexander’s reaction carefully.","\" How do you feel about the one who tortured you?\"","...!","Noah observed Alexander as Alexander looked back at him.","The man appeared different from when Noah had last examined him closely. He seemed taller than before, his frame more robust as though his foundations had expanded to fill space they previously could not occupy. A green robe adorned his figure, the material flowing with quality that suggested authority woven into its threads. But the most striking change rotated upon his chest.","A vibrant Enneagram shone there, nine points connected by lines that blazed with multicolored gems embedded at each intersection. The symbol rotated like a wheel against his sternum, its movement steady and purposeful. His expression held grandeur that had not been present before his torture, as though suffering had refined something within him rather than diminishing it.","He looked at the image of the lifeless Horus as his eyes blazed brighter, and he simply clenched his fists before he unclenched and breathed out.","\" Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.\"","WAA!","Alexander’s voice emerged with conviction that matched his transformed appearance.","\"I was actually about to come and ask you something. I do not want to wait too long.\"","He paused, gathering words that clearly cost him something to speak.","\"I followed the paths that only Second Scale Existences know. I have reforged my existence so that just as he was able to hurt me through what only he could see, I should be able to hurt him just the same.\"","His jaw tightened.","\" But I know that alone will not be enough. So I have... to ask for help.\"","He met Noah’s eyes directly.","\" Please. Help me. Help me...collapse Beowulf.\"","...!","BOOM!","A man asking for help from another man was a rare occurrence in existence.","Whenever any man found himself hurting, he rarely turned to another for assistance. He would exhaust every option available through his own power, attempt every solution his own mind could conceive, push himself to the absolute boundaries of what his foundations could sustain before even considering the possibility of reaching out. That was how so many men became destroyed and collapsed into obscurity. They never asked for help. Sometimes it was not even a matter of pride.","Sometimes it was simply that they did not know how.","The words felt foreign in their mouths. The vulnerability seemed like weakness rather than wisdom. The admission that they could not accomplish something alone felt like failure rather than an honest assessment. They had been taught, through countless experiences and observations, that strength meant self-sufficiency.","That real men handled their problems without burdening others. That asking for help was the first step toward being seen as lesser.","These were lies that killed more men than any enemy ever could.","There were many reasons not to ask for help. Noah understood this intimately. But Alexander had come forward regardless of those reasons, had spoken the words despite their difficulty, had requested assistance even knowing how it might appear.","Noah would give that help freely.","Nor would he ever make Alexander feel bad or lesser for asking.","One should always feel permitted to ask for help. Whether you possessed family or someone you considered a friend, you should never be afraid to reach out.","In existence, you were never alone.","The isolation that convinced men they had to face everything by themselves was another lie, perhaps the cruelest one of all.","Noah rose and placed his hand on Alexander’s shoulder.","\" Come on. Let us go find Beowulf.\"","His grip tightened with reassurance.","\" He is on a whole different Scale compared to us, but hey...\"","A smile crossed his features.","\" While there will not be the power of friendship suddenly rising up to save the day, I have a very, very sharp spear.\"","HUUM!","As Noah spoke these words, incandescent stellar blue rivers of Infinity began surging from above.","The authority descended like waterfalls of condensed potential, gathering before Noah and Alexander in configurations that twisted space into new arrangements. The rivers wove together, braiding themselves into an archway that solidified into a doorway blazing with endless blue light. Through that threshold, distances that would require eons to traverse became single steps.","Many wanted to find him across Observable Existence.","But with the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity and his spread of Infinity everywhere, it was very easy for him to find others instead. His authority had saturated regions throughout Observable Existence. His weavings permeated spaces that enemies thought were hidden. If someone existed within range of his Infinity’s touch, he could locate them.","This doorway would lead them directly to Beowulf.","\" Oh, before that...\"","Noah stopped for a moment, his attention turning inward toward his Organ of Civilization. A thought crystallized into command as he spoke aloud.","\" Set the targets for Hadean Existential Singularities to be Beowulf and THE Living Paradox.\"","HUUM!","His Organ of Civilization began to spin with terrific glow, multicolored light blazing from his chest as the mechanism within processed his designation. The clear and golden rivers of Unobservable and Observable force swirled around his form in response, acknowledging the targets he had selected.","Prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Hadean Existential Singularity Targets Designated|","|Target One: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor|","|Classification: Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform|","|Connection Strength: Significant. Decent confrontations and conflicts have established substantial existential resonance between your foundations.|","|Siphoning Efficiency: Medium due to Scale differential. Hadean Existential Singularities will be extracted at a normal rate.|","|Available Extractions: Understanding of Observable and Unobservable force integration, Proterozoic Bone methodology, Civilizational Anchor composition.|","---","|Target Two: Erwin, THE Living Paradox|","|Classification: Apex of THE First Scale, Proterozoic transition. Civilizational Anchor more than halfway established. Approximate strength rivals Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeforms.|","|Connection Strength: Profound. Historical relationship creates deep existential resonance that enhances extraction efficiency.|","|Siphoning Efficiency: Extremely Low. Something is going on with this guy.|","|Available Extractions: Paradox Civilization methodology, Civilizational Anchor formation process, proto-Proterozoic transition insights, understanding of contradictory existence integration.|","|Target Three: Undesignated|","|One slot remains available for future selection.|","|Passive Siphoning: Active|","|Hadean Existential Singularities will be extracted from designated targets starting now. Extraction occurs without target awareness. Accumulated Singularities will integrate into your foundations automatically.|","...!","Noah observed the prompts with satisfaction before dismissing them from his vision.","Two of his three slots were now filled with beings who had earned their positions through enmity. Beowulf would contribute to Noah’s understanding of THE Proterozoic Scale whether he wished to or not. THE Living Paradox...he seemed to still be more than what many believed!","The third slot he would reserve for now.","Noah stepped toward the doorway blazing with stellar blue Infinity, his form approaching the threshold that would carry them directly to a dangerous being at THE Second Scale.","Alexander followed behind him without fear.","In his eyes there burned a deadly light, the illumination of peace he had to establish regardless of the cost. It did not matter how badly a Primordial Architect had to bleed for that peace to be achieved. It did not matter what Alexander himself might suffer in the pursuit. Beowulf had broken something within him, and the only way to repair that damage was to face the one who had caused it.","Peace would be achieved, no matter how much blood had to be spilled."]},{"number":5054,"title":"Chapter 5054: Chapter 5053: Acceleration I","paragraphs":["While two men crossed weavings of Infinities to go seek a Primordial Architect...","The isolated region of Jotunheim had transformed beyond recognition.","Seas of multicolored brilliance from the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity had gathered in basins that previously held nothing but ice and desolation. A citadel emerged from these accumulated waters, its structure crystallized from condensed authority that the epoch had deposited across the landscape.","Rain continued falling in rivers of combined Existence, Quintessence,and Infinity, painting the skies with hues that existence rarely witnessed in such concentration.","THE Living Temporal sat in a meditative position before this transformed citadel, ancient rivers of time flowing around his figure in configurations that bent perception.","Amser Modred appeared as a man both old and young simultaneously, his features shifting between ages depending on which angle observed them. Dignity and grace permeated his bearing despite the casual nature of his seated posture.","His robes flowed with temporal currents that made their fabric appear frozen and moving at the same instant.","He possessed Bounded Countable Infinity now, granted to him by THE Youngest through bonds of servitude that had proven far more generous than expected.","His existence was currently exuberant, all his eons of progress culminating heavily as a daring idea crystallized within his awareness. He was actually contemplating forming his Anchor. The Civilizational Anchor that THE Second Scale demanded, the absolute self-knowledge that permitted transition beyond THE First Scale into heights he had spent lifetimes believing were beyond his reach.","THE Youngest made impossible things possible with Infinity. Why not him as well?","Perhaps he and many others required only the courage to follow Osmont’s lead. After all, Osmont had not gone mad with Infinity just yet.","As he contemplated these possibilities, rivers of Temporal Infinity coalesced behind him.","The multicolored currents flowed toward THE Secretive Eon, who had been examining herself since regaining consciousness. She stood apart from the others, her dark eyes fixed upon hands that had recently been controlled by something other than her own will.","THE Primordial Mycelia had used her existence as a puppet, and the memory of that violation pressed against her awareness with a force that demanded response.","Behind Amser, Abaddon sat touching his chest with blank expression.","This guy was still reeling. His fingers pressed against his sternum as though searching for something that should have been there, something so fundamental to his identity that its absence made him question whether he still existed at all.","At this time, a determined expression finally formed on the face of THE Secretive Eon.","She cracked her neck with sharp motion, the sound echoing across the transformed landscape. Authority flashed across her body in waves of illumination that pressed against everything nearby. Her robe shifted from whatever state it had held before into pristine white that seemed to reject any stain or imperfection. Her dark hair shimmered with light that came from within rather than reflecting from without.","She turned toward the absent-minded figure of Abaddon.","Her hand shot out and grasped his neck before he could react, her fingers closing around flesh that offered no resistance. She lifted him slightly, forcing his blank eyes to meet her cold gaze.","\"I planned to destroy and then hold all the Keys of Civilizations, starting with you.\"","Her voice emerged frigid and grand, each word carrying conviction refined across her existence.","\" You would have been the stepping point for me to go after Erwin, to determine if I even possessed a chance against THE Creature. But you go and lose your Claim?\"","Her grip tightened.","\" Were you not supposed to be the oldest of the Claimers? You fucking loser.\"","BOOM!","Her words pressed against the transformed landscape as her gaze burned with coldness that would have made lesser beings flinch.","Yet Abaddon did not even react. He simply observed her with absent expression, his eyes holding nothing but the emptiness where Chaos had once resided!","Her fury meant nothing to him. Her threats meant nothing to him. The loss of his Claim had taken something from his existence that made everything else irrelevant.","Amser Modred turned around and frowned at the scene unfolding behind him.","\" Leave him be. Even with a lost Claim, he is still...\"","He rose and moved to separate the two as he spoke, his temporal authority gathering around him in preparation for intervention. Before he could complete either his sentence or his action, something unexpected occurred.","THE Secretive Eon used her other hand.","It shone with terrifying light, power concentrated into a strike that moved faster than Amser’s temporal perception could process. The blow connected with his chest and launched him backward with force that should not have been possible from someone he had considered roughly his equal or lesser!","Amser smashed into the multicolored seas nearby, his form creating waves of displaced authority that rippled outward in all directions. He tumbled through the liquid brilliance until friction finally brought him to a stop, his body half-submerged in waters that soaked through his temporal robes.","He looked up in shock at what had just occurred.","THE Secretive Eon continued staring at Abaddon without acknowledging Amser’s displacement.","\" Emotive took your Claim? The one you and Paradox and THE Creature have been using for pleasure all these eons?\"","Her voice dripped with contempt.","\" Big fucking men in power, and a loose woman brings you down like this? Maddening.\"","She was furious for reasons that extended beyond just simple frustration.","Something she had been planning to do before her existence was controlled by another had already been accomplished by someone else.","The destruction of the Keys of Civilizations and replacement had been her purpose. Her goal.","And now someone she had not even considered significant had accomplished what she intended before she could even attempt it.","THE Living Emotive, that manic creature obsessed with emotions, had stripped Chaos from someone THE Secretive Eon had marked as her first target.","She shook her head and tightened her grip on Abaddon.","At this moment, a deep voice boomed out from above.","\" Woah, I do not sense any weavings of Unity anymore. Did that fellow work so quickly while I was getting my ass handed to me?\"","The voice paused.","\" Eon, is that you?\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon and Amser Modred raised their heads to observe what had arrived.","THE Primordial Paradox descended from heights that seemed infinite, his obsidian titanic body shining with blue and gold light that pressed against the transformed landscape of Jotunheim. Paradox burned around him brilliantly, that contradictory authority declaring his nature to anyone capable of perceiving it. He was massive and ancient and dangerous!","Eon met his gaze without releasing Abaddon, her grip remaining tight around his neck.","After a moment of consideration, she permitted her fingers to open.","Abaddon slumped to the ground without acknowledging his release.","\" Mmm. I have to thank Osmont, even though I promised to hunt him after I was done with others.\"","Her voice emerged thoughtful rather than grateful.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled at her words, amusement flickering across his obsidian features.","\"I do not think you will be able to do that.\"","He descended lower, his massive form coming to rest upon the transformed landscape.","\" But no matter. You appear to be getting left behind here. Do you want to take that step to form your Anchor? I can help you out if you help me with your Civilization.\"","...!","His words were substantial ones. THE Secretive Eon scowled at the implication that she required assistance.","She looked up at him and spoke.","\" Has your disciple grasped THE Second Scale already? That will make it difficult for me to do anything against him.\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled more broadly at her concern.","\" He possessed that power already. Oh, and he has a Singular Cognizance and likely Primordial Architects he has allied with, so you alone may not be able to do much.\"","His obsidian form shifted with amusement.","\" You were already working with Osmont, yes? Just consider this an extension.\"","...!","His words were grand as THE Secretive Eon contemplated what he offered.","She thought for a moment before releasing a sigh of resignation.","Her gaze fell upon Abaddon one final time, distaste visible in her expression as she observed the broken figure who had once been the oldest of the Keys of Civilizations. Then she took a step and disappeared from Jotunheim entirely, her existence folding through spaces that carried her toward where she would have THE Primordial Paradox follow."]},{"number":5055,"title":"Chapter 5055: Chapter 5054: Acceleration II","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox smiled at her departure before his attention shifted.","He gazed with something approaching sadness toward Abaddon, whose body had begun to drift listlessly upon the multicolored sea. The currents of the Pluvial Epoch carried him away from the citadel, away from the others, away from everything that had once defined his existence as one of the most significant beings in Observable Existence.","Chaos was gone.","What remained was merely flesh that had forgotten how to care about its own continuation.","THE Primordial Paradox nodded toward Amser Modred, who remained drenched in multicolored rain where he had risen from the seas.","Acknowledgment passed between them before THE Primordial Paradox disappeared as well, his obsidian form folding away through spaces!","Amser Modred observed the body of Abaddon floating away on the transformed waters.","He shook his head and released a frustrated sigh, temporal authority rippling around him in response to his emotional state.","Everything was changing too quickly. Alliances formed and dissolved. Powers shifted between beings who had held them for eons. The stability that had governed Observable Existence was crumbling, and new configurations were emerging that would reshape everything.","His eyes burned with temporal determination as epiphany crystallized within his awareness.","\" Everyone’s path is different. The time it takes...is different.\"","He spoke aloud to no one but himself.","\" Someone like Osmont can advance at a fraction of time compared to others because he possesses Infinity. Time dilates around those who hold endless potential, compressing what should require eons into what occurs within moments. The temporal advancements bend around his existence like... light bending around a star.\"","His form began to shimmer with temporal authority gathering into configurations he had never attempted before.","\" And now this Infinity is shared with many. Will the time it took to advance infinitely not be cut short? If Bounded Countable Infinity flows through my foundations, does time not become malleable in ways it was not before?\"","Rivers of temporal energy coalesced around his figure, ancient currents responding to revelations forming within his consciousness.","\" Temporal Infinities. Infinite time. These are...They are methodologies I can employ.\"","His eyes blazed brighter as the truth settled into his foundations.","\" My Anchor is established across time rather than within a single moment. I will seek it not in the present but across all moments simultaneously. I have sought it across time already. I should have obtained it across time. The seeking and the obtaining, the past and the future, they...are the same when time becomes infinite.\"","BOOM!","With such words, Amser Modred disappeared into a temporal multicolored river that commenced extending infinitely across Jotunheim and beyond!","The current stretched through moments that had already occurred and moments that had not yet arrived, reaching into temporal configurations that defied linear understanding. It spread beyond Jotunheim’s boundaries into the greater expanse of Observable Existence, carrying THE Living Temporal toward a Civilizational Anchor established not within time but across it!","His paradoxical pursuit had commenced.","And time itself would determine whether his epiphany held truth or merely the comfortable lie of a being desperate to believe advancement remained possible.","---","Abaddon floated listlessly upon the seas caused by the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity.","The multicolored waters flowed around his body, into his body, through his body. He did not bother to stop the currents from permeating his existence. He did not bother to resist the transformation they offered. He simply drifted, carried by forces he no longer possessed the will to acknowledge, his eyes staring upward at skies painted with colors he could not bring himself to care about.","On and on he drifted.","The waters carried him past crystallized formations that the epoch had grown from nothing. They carried him past shores where new life emerged.","They carried him through regions of Jotunheim that had once answered to his command, territories where his Claim of Chaos had made him absolute.","None of it mattered anymore.","Until something shifted beneath the surface.","The multicolored seas began to churn around his floating form, currents disrupting in patterns. Massive shapes rose from the depths, shadows ascending through brilliance that should have made them invisible. They emerged slowly, deliberately, with purpose that pressed against the listless despair surrounding Abaddon’s existence.","Chaos Giants.","They arose from the waters in groups of five, then ten, then dozens. Their massive forms towered over the seas as they gathered around the drifting body of Abaddon, their features ancient and terrible and filled with something that appeared remarkably like reverence.","They remembered their king!","Massive hands reached beneath Abaddon’s floating form and lifted him from the waters with gentleness that contradicted their enormous strength. They raised him above the multicolored seas as if carrying a fallen monarch, their grips supporting his body. His head rested upon one giant’s palm while others supported his torso and limbs.","Abaddon’s eyes shook for the first time since losing his Claim.","He stared at the Chaos Giants surrounding him, at faces he had commanded for eons, at beings who should have abandoned him the moment his authority departed. They had no reason to serve him now. They had no obligation to acknowledge his existence. The Claim of Chaos that had bound them to his will was gone!","Yet here they were.","The Chaos Giants smiled at him, expressions of warmth crossing features designed for terror.","They simply carried him away from the drifting currents, away from the listless despair that had claimed him, toward destinations known only to those native to this realm.","One Chaos Giant stopped to observe this procession commandingly...as if he was literally the one commanding all this.","He stood apart from the others, his massive form half-submerged in the multicolored seas as he watched his brethren carry their fallen king. A smile crossed his terrible features, but something about that expression did not match the reverence displayed by the others.","From his mouth, a voice echoed that did not belong to him.","\" The past Claimer of Chaos.\"","THE Great Usurper spoke through the giant’s flesh, his authority commandeering the vessel with ease.","\" You may have lost your Claim, but you are still grand. A vessel of possibilities that should not be discarded simply because one purpose has concluded.\"","The giant’s smile widened as THE Great Usurper’s voice continued.","\"I will forge you into something worthy again. Hmm!\"","...!","The Chaos Giant turned and followed the others he had silently usurped!"]},{"number":5056,"title":"Chapter 5056: Chapter 5055: Awakening! I","paragraphs":["THE Secretive Eon appeared in a domain that existed between Observable and Unobservable.","The space measured only a mile wide in diameter, a pocket of stability carved into the boundary separating what could be perceived from what could not. Beyond its edges, swirling weavings of Unobservable wrapped around the domain in configurations that would have driven lesser beings mad merely from proximity. The darkness there moved with purpose, pressing against the domain’s boundaries without quite breaching them.","Within this small sanctuary, vibrant green grasses covered the ground in carpets that should not have been possible given the forces surrounding them. A simple white hut stood at the center, its construction humble and unremarkable, the kind of dwelling that suggested meditation rather than habitation. This place had been hidden for eons, known only to one existence in all of Observable Existence.","Until now.","Behind Eon, a sliver of a gateway remained open where she had entered. From it, THE Primordial Paradox stepped through, his obsidian titanic form immediately scanning the surroundings with attention that missed nothing. His paradoxical authority rippled around him as he observed the grasses, the hut, the swirling Unobservable beyond the boundaries.","\" This place I have not been to.\"","His voice emerged with the weight of someone realizing they had been deceived.","\" Just what more are you hiding?\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon did not respond immediately.","She sat down upon the vibrant grasses with calm that seemed inappropriate. Her expression held resignation rather than fear, acceptance rather than anxiety. Whatever she was about to do, she had made peace with it long before this moment arrived.","Then she plunged her hand into her own chest.","Her fingers passed through flesh that parted without resistance, reaching into depths where her foundations resided. When she withdrew her hand, she held a key that blazed with golden light so pure it seemed to reject the surrounding Unobservable entirely. The key was ornate and ancient, its design suggesting purposes that predated most classifications Observable Existence currently employed.","Eon parted the hair behind her neck, exposing skin that had not seen light in eons.","Without looking at THE Primordial Paradox, she extended the key toward him.","\"I wish I had never told you about me.\"","Her voice emerged flat and tired.","\"I wanted to never return to that state. Even when I was being controlled by Unity, I did not reach out to it. I wanted to overcome it myself.\"","She paused.","\" But I failed. Osmont scorched Unity out of me, and in turn, he has also loosened the seal. Since it will break regardless, I will consider this eons-long experiment to have been a failure. I thought I could make things happen without it, but whatever.\"","She thrust the key toward him more insistently.","\" Take the key. I made it so that I could not fully unlock it myself.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox grasped the key with confusion visible across his obsidian features.","\" What are you talking about? I reached out to you because of your Civilization. With it, my Paradox can undergo acceleration even-\"","\"I lied to you about my Civilization.\"","Her interruption was sharp and final.","\" Just put the key on the back of my neck. Everything will become clearer after.\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon wore a hardened expression as she spoke these words.","A key. Something even THE Primordial Mycelia had never sensed during its occupation of her existence, something far above that fungal horror’s stature to perceive. Naturally, a key meant something was locked. And right now, that something was Eon herself.","Turning the key would unlock her.","Doing so was an admission that she had failed, that her experiment in living as something lesser had concluded in defeat. What could she do? Existence was unfair. It had always been unfair. She had simply spent eons pretending otherwise.","Behind her, THE Primordial Paradox continued to frown as he brought the key toward her exposed neck.","\"I may speak to you differently and change afterward.\"","Her voice held hesitation for the first time.","\" Do not mind it. I will still be me. Just somewhat different.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox frowned even more deeply at her words. He shook his head at the strangeness of this situation, at the mysteries piling upon mysteries, at the sense that he was about to participate in something he did not understand.","Then he plunged the key into her neck.","The golden metal entered her flesh with blinding light that pressed against his perception. The key sank deeper than should have been possible, finding a lock that existed somewhere beyond physical form.","CLICK!","He turned the key.","And...","BOOM!","THE Primordial Paradox found his body flung across the domain before he could process what had occurred. He smashed against the boundaries where Observable met Unobservable, the collision sending shockwaves through his obsidian form. When he managed to orient himself and look back toward where Eon had been sitting...","He observed something magisterial!","All around the domain, golden misty light gathered with speed and density that defied comprehension.","The force of Observable itself was flooding into this small space, drawn by something that demanded its presence. Rivers of golden luminosity poured toward the figure of Eon from every direction, converging upon her form with intensity that painted the entire domain in hues of captured sunlight.","Her aura became something else entirely.","THE Primordial Paradox attempted to rise from where he had landed, pushing against the ground with strength that had conquered countless enemies across eons of conflict.","His body refused to comply. Something pressed down upon him with force that would not permit him to stand, as if all of surrounding existence had to remain low for what was waking up.","He could only watch from his position near the ground.","Golden rivers of Observable force continued flowing into Eon as she rose from the grasses without apparent effort. The power lifted her upward, rivers of golden light forming beneath her feet to create platforms of solidified authority. Her dark hair shone with brilliance that seemed to generate its own illumination rather than reflecting what surrounded her. Her eyes, when she opened them, radiated endless gold that pressed against THE Primordial Paradox’s perception with intensity.","The force she radiated horrified him.","It seemed to exceed the Singular Cognizance he had faced when fighting alongside Erwin. It surpassed what he had believed possible for any being at THE First Scale. It defied everything he understood about the hierarchy of power!","\" What... is this?\"","He had to ask the question even though speaking required effort against the pressure pinning him down.","Eon turned to look at him.","Her body had transformed. An unfathomable sense of beauty now permeated her existence, the kind that made observation feel like privilege rather than simple perception.","Radiant golden tattoos rolled from her neck down to her chest. Upon her wrists, golden bands shining with contained authority had formed, their presence suggesting royalty rather than ornamentation.","Her expression had changed as well.","Where before there had been coldness and calm, now there was coldness born of supremacy. Where before there had been calculation, now there was the calm of one who did not need to calculate because outcomes were predetermined in her favor.","Arrogance radiated from her bearing!","She replied to THE Primordial Paradox with a voice that sounded glorious and detached, as if she were addressing someone beneath her rather than an equal.","\" What this is, is my whims coming to an end.\"","The golden rivers continued flowing into her as she spoke.","\"I admit I do not have the power to do anything without what I was born with. You...will be rewarded for aiding me in my transition.\"","...!"]},{"number":5057,"title":"Chapter 5057: Chapter 5056: Awakening! II","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox frowned at her tone, at the implicit dismissal contained within her words. He sought to rise again, gathering his Civilization of Paradox around him in preparation to force himself upward through whatever pressure held him down.","Eon simply waved her hand.","The pressure vanished, and he was able to stand.","His expression remained heavy as he observed her, still seeing boundless golden swirling misty light flowing into her form from every direction. The Observable force showed no signs of diminishing. If anything, it was accelerating, more rivers converging upon her with each passing moment.","\"I really need you to explain now.\"","His voice emerged somber and demanding.","\" Why do you feel even stronger than a Singular Cognizance at THE Second Scale when you should only be at THE First Scale?\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon turned to look at him with calm and imperious bearing. She placed her hands upon her chest as if sensing her own existence, feeling the changes that the unlocking had wrought within her foundations.","\" Because you and I are distinctly different.\"","Her words carried no apology.","\"I was born made different. I tried to live like you and all others, and I failed. Because lifeforms like you, what I tried to be, do not have the capacity to influence Existence to a high enough level.\"","She paused, her golden eyes studying him with assessment that felt clinical.","\" That part of myself has admitted this after falling prey to a fucking fungus and having to be saved by another. Which brings another problem because...\"","Eon looked deeper into her existence as she spoke, her attention turning inward.","There, nestled within her foundations, she sensed something that made her frown. An irreversible and unbreakable bond with Quintessence Infiniforce existed within her, something that Osmont had placed in her eons ago in Ginnungagap. Her old self had not known about it. The connection had been subtle, hidden beneath layers of her diminished existence where her sealed perceptions could not reach.","It had entrenched itself into her existence so thoroughly that as she examined it now, she understood she could not expel it. The thing held Infinity within it, and Infinity was not something that could be removed through force alone.","Worse, this Quintessence Infiniforce was actually benefiting from her nature. She could sense her weavings, her authority, her Observable force flowing into the connection.","This would be a problem.","As she frowned at this discovery, THE Primordial Paradox maintained his heavy gaze upon her. He shook his head at answers that only generated more questions.","\" What does that mean? What are you, really?\"","His voice demanded truth rather than requesting it.","THE Secretive Eon turned to face him with calm that bordered on indifference.","\" To understand what I am is to understand what you are.\"","Her golden eyes held no warmth.","\"In Existence, all beings are not born equal. You are among THE Bounded Lifeforms. You and countless others. I am what is known as THE Gilded Lifeform. A different pedigree of lifeform entirely.\"","She let those words settle before continuing.","\" My former self lied to you about my Civilization. My Civilization... is anything I wish among that which is Observable.\"","BOOM!","As she spoke these final words, she waved her hands to feel the heavy concentrated golden misty light of Observable continuing to flood into her form. The force responded to her gesture, swirling around her fingers as if eager to serve. She looked toward THE Primordial Paradox, who observed all of this with grim expression that could not hide his growing unease.","Eon shook her head at his obvious confusion.","\" You required help with your Anchor? Sure. Here you go.\"","HUUM!","As she spoke, she tapped out with casual gesture that should not have been capable of accomplishing anything significant.","From the boundless power of Observable surrounding her, a blazing golden light began to form. It coalesced into configurations that THE Primordial Paradox recognized immediately, patterns that he had spent eons preparing to forge through careful affirmation and absolute self-knowledge.","A singularity of Paradox, perfect and complete, materialized from the force of Observable.","It entered into THE Primordial Paradox before he could react, flooding his foundations alongside an influx of Observable force that saturated every aspect of his existence. He had not called out any affirmations. He had not established his identity through the declarations that Civilizational Anchors required. He had not done anything except stand there and watch.","Yet an instant later...","BOOM!","A terrifying aura of power emanated from THE Primordial Paradox as shock overwhelmed his features.","A glorious Civilizational Anchor had formed within him without his participation. It felt just as powerful if not more powerful than what he would have forged himself through eons of careful preparation. The foundation of his transition to THE Proterozoic Scale now existed within his foundations, placed there by someone who had treated the process as casual generosity.","Before he could process what had just occurred, Eon looked at him with even greater calm.","\" Have your Proterozoic Scale entry as well.\"","HUUM!","With such words, the tattoos adorning her body shone with brilliance that pressed against perception. Even more golden misty light flooded into THE Primordial Paradox, most of it flowing into his chest where his bones resided. The force pressed into his skeletal structure with intensity that would have destroyed any existence not prepared to receive it.","An aura of a Proterozoic Scale entity began radiating from his form.","His chest bones continued absorbing the golden misty light, transforming through processes that should have required years of careful cultivation. The Observable force was remaking him, elevating him, forcing advancement that he had not earned through any methodology he understood.","While all of this happened, he looked at Eon with incredulity that could not be contained.","\" Hey. What the fuck is this?!\"","His voice emerged with bewilderment that stripped away all composure.","THE Secretive Eon looked back at him with calm that bordered on boredom.","\"A difference in Existence.\"","Her golden eyes held no sympathy for his confusion.","\"I told you, not all beings are born equal. You and I are not born equal. You can understand it as a feat of Existential Engineering, but even that is not entirely true.\"","She waved her hand dismissively.","\" No matter. Acclimate to your power and do not ask too much. I have to understand how the actions of my former self may have tainted me, because now I have a parasite of Infinity latched onto my existence.\"","She said this coolly before turning her attention inward, beginning to study the Quintessence Infiniforce that had entrenched itself within her foundations. The golden rivers continued flowing into her form, but her attention had already moved past THE Primordial Paradox and his questions.","He stood there stupefied, power he had not earned surging through foundations that barely understood what they had received.","What the fuck were THE Gilded?","Why was he and all others deemed THE Bounded?","Did that Designation apply to everyone he had ever known? To THE Creature? To Abaddon? To Erwin? To Osmont himself?","The questions multiplied within his awareness, each one more disturbing than the last.","THE Secretive Eon continued studying the Quintessence Infiniforce within her, paying him no further attention.","He was beneath her notice now as...perhaps he had always been."]},{"number":5058,"title":"Chapter 5058: Chapter 5057: For All To See! I","paragraphs":["In THE Wastes, seas of multicolored brilliance swirled below while rivers surged above.","The figure of Beowulf floated within this transformed landscape, his massive hammer resting against one armored shoulder as he gazed out at the area where the illusory visage of THE Creature had been displayed. That image had faded now, but its implications remained. Horus was dead. THE Creature had claimed victory and displayed the proof for all of Observable Existence to witness!","The death was a heavy one, and it made Beowulf think about many things.","He had known Horus for eons. Now that ancient Primordial Architect was simply gone, his Eyes ripped from existence and held aloft like trophies by someone who had decided the time for tolerance had ended.","At such a time, something shifted behind him.","From the seas of multicolored Infinity at his back, singularities sparked and churned with activity that should not have been possible without his awareness. The waters of the Pluvial Epoch twisted into configurations that bent space, forming pathways where none had existed moments before. Authority pressed through those pathways with intention that announced arrival rather than requested permission.","Two figures emerged from the churning brilliance.","Noah stood at the forefront, his multicolored emperor’s robe flowing with currents of Infinity that wrapped around his form like loyal serpents. Alexander stood beside him, his green robes pristine and his Enneagram rotating upon his chest with steady determination. Both of them gazed forward with expressions cold and grand, as if they had come to this place specifically to challenge what awaited them.","The massive armored figure of Beowulf turned around to observe them in stupor.","Two First Scale entities had appeared before a Second Scale existence, and they bore themselves as if the difference in power meant nothing. Their postures held no deference. Their eyes held no fear. They floated before him with the bearing of challengers rather than prey, as if this confrontation was something they had chosen rather than something they would suffer!","Noah gazed at the massive visage of Beowulf as the Primordial Architect completed his turn.","When he looked at this being now, he did not feel that heavy sense of oppression that had pressed against him during their previous encounters. His foundations had changed. His capabilities had evolved. THE Hadean Organ of Civilization pulsed within his chest with authority that declared itself ready for whatever came next.","Beside him, Alexander wore an expression of extreme coldness.","He looked at Beowulf as if he was already dismantling the armored figure piece by piece, as if this confrontation was merely formality before the violence he had been anticipating since his torture concluded. His hands remained still at his sides, but the authority gathering around him suggested those hands would not remain idle for long.","Noah nodded to Beowulf.","\" Big guy, did you miss us? I did not want to make you wait for too long, so I came to fulfill my oath.\"","...!","He had told this contemptible existence that he would return and pay things back manifold. That time was now here. The words emerged with confidence that pressed against the transformed landscape of THE Wastes!","Beowulf looked at them with expression that bordered on skepticism.","His armored head turned slightly, scanning the surrounding area as if searching for hidden allies or concealed traps. When he found nothing except the two beings floating before him, his twisted smile formed across features that had intimidated countless existences across eons of conflict.","\"You...are arguably one of the most unique existences I have come across in a while.\"","His voice emerged with amusement that did not quite conceal his wariness.","Noah’s response came immediately.","\" And you are one of the more boring ones. Did you see your friend, Horus, and the humiliation of his corpse displayed for all to see across Existence?\"","He spoke such words grandly, letting them hang in the air between them.","Beowulf’s expression shifted into a frown that darkened his armored features. His hammer rose over his shoulders, the weapon’s presence alone causing the surroundings to begin trembling and shaking. Authority gathered around his form with intensity.","\" Existence is vast and filled with wonders.\"","His voice emerged cold.","\" Some of us will die. Some of us will triumph. With you coming here now, I will not allow you to slip away again. I will never have to experience the same fate as Horus.\"","His armored head tilted slightly.","\" Once I grasp your weavings and secrets regarding Infinity...\"","The sentence trailed off as his brutal smile returned.","\" Hmmm.\"","Proterozoic Scale power spread outward from his form, sifting through the transformed landscape with authority that demanded submission from everything it touched. All churning rivers of multicolored brilliance around them ceased their movement. The flowing seas below became still. For the surrounding light years, everything that had been in motion simply stopped.","Even the rain falling from above halted in place, droplets of the Pluvial Epoch suspended in air that no longer permitted their descent.","Noah gave a light nod at this display of power.","\" Seeing the actions of THE Creature reminded me that when it comes to truly breaking down one’s enemies and letting others know how to act, seeing is better than believing.\"","His eyes shone with purpose.","\" So...\"","He raised his hand and clenched it.","The multicolored seas of Infinity shook in response to his gesture. Around them, massive disturbances churned through the transformed waters as something vast began to rise from the depths. Three illusory screens emerged from the brilliance, each one a single light year in diameter, their surfaces displaying images that captured everything occurring in this space.","The screens showed the figure of Beowulf and their figures with clarity that missed no detail.","\" My weavings of Infinity are spread all across Observable Existence.\"","Noah’s voice carried across the light years his screens encompassed.","\" Just like THE Creature was able to illuminate the fate of Horus, I will go a step further to illuminate and illustrate. I will give all of Observable Existence the chance to see the fates of those poor enough to come after me.\"","The illusory screens shone with brilliance that exceeded their already massive presence.","What they displayed began to permeate across Observable Existence.","Across THE Wastes, screens rose from seas and rivers of transformed brilliance. In Primordial Realms scattered throughout existence, similar displays emerged from wherever Infinity had touched. Within remaining shelters of THE Loom, screens materialized before beings who had thought themselves hidden and protected!","In Prima Indifferentia, illusory images pressed through barriers that should have been impenetrable! The Wandering Territories! The Lands of The Dead!","In all places where Infinity sensed Absolutes or any glimmers of Second Scale Existences, these illusory screens began to rise.","They streamed everything occurring at this moment.","Noah looked up as the illusory screens zoomed upon his face, Alexander visible behind him.","Multicolored Infinities wrapped around his body in rivers of endless authority. His multicolored emperor’s robe shone gloriously!","While looking into the screen, he spoke words meant for all of Observable Existence.","\" Let this be a lesson and warning to all.\"","HUUM!","He said for this to be a warning, but he knew many would not take it like so. He knew many would take it as a challenge, which would in turn...invite Adversity. And that...was also another goal of his!","Beowulf observed this display as his gaze became unfathomably cold.","His massive body was reflected on the screens surrounding them, his armored form towering over Noah and Alexander like a giant observing ants!","His pride as an existence so much grander than them buzzed with indignation at this moment, at being made a spectacle for beings across Observable Existence to witness!","\"I will not stop at dissecting your existence. I will-\"","At such a time, Noah’s words interrupted him.","\" Hold on.\"","...!","Because at this moment, Noah began to feel something horrific and grand inside his existence.","A flood of the power of Observable surged from within him in an unfathomable manner, its concentration far exceeding anything he had handled before. Golden misty light erupted from his foundations with intensity that should have torn him apart. The force was vast and overwhelming, a sea of Observable power pouring through connections he had not consciously activated!","It felt surreal and utterly overwhelming.","There was so much that his existence was almost initially overwhelmed by the sheer volume of what was flooding through him. His foundations trembled under the pressure, his cells burning with golden light that pressed outward from within. Then THE Hadean Organ of Civilization began to spin right after, collecting the terrifying misty golden seas of Observable force with efficiency that prevented catastrophic overflow.","Every cell and atom within his body literally began to burn with golden light of Observable!","His existence worked rapidly to process what was occurring. Infinite Undifferentiated Fate searched for the connection to understand where this flood originated, but he could not find anything apart from the connection with THE Primordial Paradox.","When he dug deeper toward the source of these terrifying waves of Observable force, he felt as if he was being blocked by barriers that resisted his perception.","He proceeded to use the overflowing power of Observable itself to finally affirm the truth.","Particles of his Quintessence Infiniforce were acting as pathways, pulling from a source. The connection led to...Eon. THE Secretive Eon!","What...","\" Are you okay?\"","Beside him, Alexander asked the question as Noah appeared to have frozen in place, his eyes burning with golden light while his expression shifted through confusion and calculation.","As Noah was in the middle of ascertaining all this, Beowulf became cold and apathetic.","The Primordial Architect raised his hammer. His armored features showed no amusement now, no fucking tolerance for whatever his opponents were experiencing!","He had been interrupted, insulted, and made into a spectacle for all of Observable Existence to witness.","\" No playing around this time.\"","His voice emerged with frost that spread across the suspended droplets around them.","\"I will collapse you and look at the pieces after. Let me show you how vast the gulf is between THE Second Scale and THE First Scale.\"","HUUM!","As he said this, he swung his hammer.","Noah’s eyes could see the backbone and makeup of that weapon as it descended toward him and Alexander. Within the hammer’s construction, a single shining crimson obsidian bone blazed with light that pressed against perception.","A Proterozoic Bone, fully activated, channeling the full might of a Second Scale existence through an instrument designed specifically for destruction.","The hammer thundered down toward them!","Time seemed to slow as Noah processed what was occurring. The flood of Observable force continued burning through his foundations. The hammer continued its descent.","Alexander stood beside him, ready to fight but lacking the capability to stop what was coming. The illusory screens broadcast everything to Observable Existence, capturing the moment when THE Youngest would be crushed by power he should not have challenged!","Noah put his hand on his chest.","His fingers pressed through his emperor’s robe, reaching toward the Organ of Civilization that spun with fury within him. From that Organ, he pulled forth a weapon that should not have existed at THE First Scale.","THE Hadean Spear of Civilization emerged from his sternum.","The multicolored crystalline Kontos spear materialized into his grip as the hammer continued its descent!","Around his body, the vibrant lights of Observable and Unobservable began swirling with intensity that exceeded anything he had previously channeled. Golden mist and clear smoke wound around his form, both forces converging upon the tip of his spear with concentration that made the air itself tremble.","The tip of the spear rose to meet the giant hammer!","And...","CRACK!","The impact was shocking and forceful and blinding!","A horrid sound echoed across existence as Proterozoic Bone met Civilizational Armament, as THE Second Scale collided with something that should not have been possible at THE First Scale.","Light erupted from the point of contact with brilliance that painted the suspended droplets of rain with hues existence rarely witnessed.","Noah remained floating exactly where he was.","He did not move. He did not budge. He did not shift a single inch from the position he had occupied before the hammer’s descent.","Instead, the massive hammer of Beowulf was knocked backward and upward.","...!","Oh!","The weapon that had crushed an unknown number of existences across eons of conflict recoiled from the collision, its Proterozoic Bone ringing with frequencies!","Beowulf’s armored arms absorbed the recoil, his massive form pushed back by a force that should not have come from a First Scale being.","Stupor and astonishment followed.","Noah stood there in the aftermath, his spear held at angle.","The light of Quintessence Infiniforce blazed around him in rivers of multicolored brilliance. Infinity wrapped around his form, and Unobservable and Observable forces swirled around his weapon in clear and golden rivers that pressed against everything they touched.","He held that spear!","THAT Spear!","THE Hadean Spear of Civilization!","The illusory screens captured everything.","They broadcast his image across Observable Existence, showing countless beings the moment when THE Genesis Monarch blocked the full strike of a Proterozoic Scale entity and knocked that strike away without moving from his position.","Noah pulled the spear back and spoke with a frown.","\"I told you to hold on. Sit the fuck back for a second.\"","...!","Oh!","OH !","Even Alexander looked at Noah in stupor!","Beowulf stared at his hammer and then at Noah’s spear.","His gaze moved between the two weapons back and forth!","The body of this Primordial Architect then began to vibrate and shake with rage!"]},{"number":5059,"title":"Chapter 5059: Chapter 5058: For All To See! II","paragraphs":["The collision echoed across Observable Existence through illusory screens that spared no detail.","Countless beings witnessed the moment when THE Hadean Spear of Civilization met the hammer of Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor. They observed the flash of light, heard the horrid sound that accompanied the impact, and watched as a First Scale entity remained unmoved while a Second Scale entity’s weapon recoiled backward.","Their interpretations varied according to their understanding!","In a distant area.","\" He was holding back ,\" declared a Primordial Architect observing from a domain within THE Wastes. \" Beowulf clearly underestimated his opponent and pulled his strike at the last moment. No First Scale being could genuinely block a Proterozoic attack.\"","Around him were 2 more Primordial Architects who nodded in agreement, finding comfort in logic that preserved the hierarchy they understood.","An even further distance away.","\" Infinity... must be responsible ,\" theorized an Undivided One watching from Prima Indifferentia. \" Perhaps that authority created some manner of defensive barrier that absorbed the impact. The spear itself could not have been responsible.\"","These beings sought explanations that fit within frameworks they already possessed!","THE Second Scale was supposed to be unreachable from THE First Scale. The gap between them was supposed to be absolute. If what they witnessed contradicted these assumptions, then surely they had witnessed incorrectly. Surely there was context they lacked. Surely Beowulf had been caught by surprise, had not taken the confrontation seriously, had permitted this outcome through carelessness rather than inability.","The alternative was unthinkable!","The alternative meant everything they understood about power and progression was incomplete.","Among those who had spent eons striving toward THE Proterozoic Scale without success, different reactions emerged.","In a Niflheimr...","\"If he can do it, perhaps I can as well,\" whispered an ancient being who had failed to form his Civilizational Anchor seventeen times across his existence. His eyes fixed upon the illusory screen with intensity that bordered on desperation. \" Perhaps the gap is not as vast as we believed.\"","Hope bloomed in foundations that had long ago accepted limitation as permanent.","\" Infinity changes everything, \" declared another, watching from a Primordial Realm where the Pluvial Epoch had continued transforming the landscape.","These beings observed the impact and saw possibility rather than anomaly. They did not understand what had occurred, but they understood what it might mean for their own futures. If THE First Scale could challenge THE Second Scale, then ceilings they had believed unbreakable might possess cracks they had never perceived.","Their hope was not entirely misplaced.","But it was not entirely accurate either.","Among those who had touched THE Proterozoic Scale themselves, who understood what that power actually meant, reactions were markedly different.","Smiles vanished from faces that had been amused moments before.","Expressions that had held condescension shifted into seriousness that pressed against their surroundings. Beings who had been observing casually, treating the broadcast as entertainment suddenly found themselves unable to look away.","In Prima Indifferentia, the obsidian figure with a single horn who had laughed at THE Creature’s display now observed through the same crack from which he had emerged before. His Proterozoic Bones shone with light that reflected the illusory screen’s brilliance, and his expression held none of the amusement it had contained previously.","In Jotunheim, where THE Primordial Paradox had only recently departed, the Chaos Giants carrying Abaddon’s listless body paused their procession to observe screens that rose from the transformed seas around them. THE Great Usurper, speaking through the giant whose body he had commandeered, said nothing at all as he only watched!","The truly knowledgeable did not rationalize.","They did not hope.","They understood.","Beings who had achieved THE Proterozoic Scale through their own effort, who had integrated Observable Or Unobservable forces into their Civilizations, who had forged Proterozoic Bones or Organs through methodologies spanning eons of careful cultivation, these beings recognized something in that impact that others could not perceive!","Beowulf had not held back.","His hammer had descended with the full force of a Rhyacian Proterozoic existence, channeled through a Proterozoic Bone that had been forged specifically for destruction. The crimson obsidian within that weapon had blazed with power that should have atomized any First Scale being it contacted. There had been no restraint. There had been no surprise!","There had been a genuine strike from a Second Scale entity intending to end a confrontation before it could properly begin.","And that strike had been deflected!","Not absorbed or redirected.","Deflected.","THE Youngest had met a Proterozoic attack with a weapon that should not have existed at THE First Scale, and he had knocked that attack away as if it were an inconvenience rather than an existential threat. The gap between Scales, that supposedly absolute chasm separating those who had achieved Civilizational Anchors from those who had not, had just been demonstrated to be significantly smaller than anyone had believed.","Or perhaps the gap remained exactly as vast as it had always been.","Perhaps THE Youngest simply stood in a different location than anyone had realized.","Many did not take their eyes away from the illusory screens for even a second.","They could not afford to.","Every moment of this confrontation contained information that might prove essential!","The illusory screens continued broadcasting across Observable Existence!","—","Beowulf was important, certainly.","But right now, Noah’s entire existence was going haywire as he felt like he had tapped into something almost as vast and grand as Infinity itself.","The force of Observable flooded his finite existence with intensity that should have torn him apart, golden light burning through every cell and atom of his form. If he did not have THE Hadean Organ of Civilization spinning within his chest, collecting and processing this influx with efficiency that prevented overflow, the result may have been disastrous.","He had locked down the source to be THE Secretive Eon.","The Quintessence Infiniforce he had placed within her eons ago in Ginnungagap was acting as a pathway, pulling Observable force from her existence into his own. He did not know why this was happening now. He did not know what had changed within Eon to trigger such a flood. But he unluckily happened to have started a battle against a Second Scale Primordial Architect, so he had to deal with both situations simultaneously.","It was extremely hard to tell a Primordial Architect to sit down and be still for a moment.","Especially when they attacked you at full power and you rebuffed their attack in front of all Observable Existence.","Noah understood this predicament intimately. He needed just a moment. Just a nanosecond or a single second to process what was occurring within his foundations, to understand the connection flooding him with power, to communicate with the source and determine what had changed. But Beowulf would not grant him that moment willingly.","So he would have to take it.","Noah observed the massive Primordial Architect far ahead of him, watching as Beowulf began to rise from the recoil of their collision. The terrifying grandeur and immensity of someone at THE Second Scale was rotating around that armored form with intensity that pressed against everything within range. His rage was visible in the vibration of his body, in the way the suspended droplets of rain around them trembled, in the cold fury radiating from features that had just experienced humiliation before all of Observable Existence.","Noah knew this fucker would not sit still.","He needed more of a push.","\" You are angry? You have always been angry.\"","His voice emerged cold and measured.","\" You hold the Civilization of Armed Existence, and yet you have remained pathetically weak. As a Primordial Architect born of THE First Scale, you barely grasped THE Second Scale by working with Horus and two others in Prima Indifferentia.\"","He let those words settle before continuing.","\" Now Horus is dead, and you are wondering if you might be next.\"","...!","Noah stared at Beowulf whose entire existence seemed to be blazing with terrifying power.","How did he know what he had said so far? How did he possess information that should have been hidden from anyone outside Beowulf’s closest confidants? Of course, it was because since he arrived here, and even slightly before, golden bubbles of loot had been leaking from Beowulf and flowing into him.","THE Hadean Existential Singularities.","He could see them with clarity. Golden bubbles of light emerged from the Primordial Architect’s armored form without that being’s awareness, drifting through the space between them with lazy purpose that belied their significance. Each bubble shone with glorious golden light, the illumination of loot that had been refined beyond simple material value into concentrated essence of another being’s existence.","They flowed toward Noah with inevitability that could not be resisted.","The bubbles disappeared into his body upon contact, their golden light absorbed by foundations hungry for what they contained. Each absorption brought weavings and information. Beowulf’s secrets, his private thoughts, his hidden shames, all of it poured into Noah through pathways the Primordial Architect could not perceive.","Prompts bloomed before his vision as the Singularities integrated.","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed|","|Source: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor|","|Category: Civilizational Anchor Composition|","|Content: Subject’s Civilizational Anchor was established through affirmations declaring absolute unity between self and armament. Core affirmation recorded: \"I am the weapon. The weapon is me. There is no distinction between the hand that strikes and the blow that lands. My existence is combat. My identity is war. I cannot be separated from what I wield because I am what I wield.\"|","|Stability Assessment: Anchor is fundamentally sound but contains vulnerability. Subject’s identity is entirely dependent on external armament. Removal or destruction of armor would cause catastrophic Anchor degradation.|","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed|","|Source: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor|","|Category: Proterozoic Bone Methodology|","|Content: Subject possesses a single Proterozoic Bone integrated into his primary weapon rather than his physical form. The crimson obsidian bone within his hammer was forged through collaboration with Horus in Prima Indifferentia.|","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed|","|Source: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor|","|Category: Hidden Psychological Profile|","|Content: Subject experiences profound insecurity regarding biological limitations imposed by his Civilization of Armed Existence. His complete integration with armament has rendered him incapable of physical intimacy or procreation. Subject compensates through observation of other lifeforms engaging in carnal activities, deriving vicarious satisfaction from experiences he cannot personally have.|","|Additional Content: Subject’s persistent rage stems partially from this limitation. He resents beings who possess capabilities he sacrificed for power.|","...!","What?","What???!","Noah wanted to pause, but more information came!","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed|","|Source: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor|","|Category: Alliance Intelligence|","|Content: Subject’s collaboration with Horus was not based on friendship but mutual necessity. Horus required Beowulf’s combat capabilities for territorial expansion. Beowulf required Horus’s methodology for Proterozoic advancement. With Horus eliminated, subject’s path to further advancement has been severed.|","...!"]},{"number":5060,"title":"Chapter 5060: Chapter 5059: What Are You? I","paragraphs":["Noah read the prompts as they integrated into his awareness, each one painting a fuller picture of who Beowulf actually was beneath that intimidating armored exterior. A being who had sacrificed so much for power that he could no longer experience simple pleasures. A being whose advancement depended on others rather than his own capabilities. A being whose rage masked insecurities that would have been pathetic if they were not so dangerous.","And while Noah absorbed this information, he was weakening Beowulf without that being’s knowledge.","Every Singularity that flowed from the Primordial Architect into Noah represented something being lost. Not enough to notice immediately, perhaps not enough to notice for a while, but the extraction was occurring nonetheless. Beowulf was becoming lesser while Noah was becoming greater, and the Primordial Architect had no idea this transaction was taking place.","It would be even easier for him in this battle if he could stall for somewhat longer.","So he continued.","\" Your Civilizational Anchor is fascinating, Beowulf. ’I am the weapon. The weapon is me.’ Such absolute declarations, yet they contain such obvious vulnerabilities.\"","Noah watched as the armored figure stiffened at words that should have been impossible for anyone outside his own existence to know.","\" You did not forge your Proterozoic Bone yourself. You required Horus to provide methodology... For all your bluster about Armed Existence, you could not even arm yourself without assistance.\"","The rage radiating from Beowulf intensified to levels that pressed against everything within range!","\" And then there is the matter of your limitations.\"","Noah’s voice became almost conversational in its cruelty.","\" Beowulf, the grand Primordial Armor, actually feels insecure that your Civilization and nature make it so you cannot procreate or enjoy carnal pleasures. So you simply like to watch other lifeforms enjoy carnal pleasures every now and then.\"","He paused to let those words sink in.","\"Is this part of why you are so angry? I can speak more about this and other things for all of Observable Existence to hear, or you can do what I asked and sit the fuck back for a second.\"","His eyes met the invisible gaze behind that armored helm.","\" Can you do that? I need to check on something else first, and then we can continue.\"","HUUM!","His words were heavy and terrifying, declarations that should have been impossible, revelations that should have remained hidden for eternity. Behind the armored head of Beowulf, invisible eyes burned with unfathomable light of rage that pressed against the boundaries of what that form could contain.","But Beowulf raised his hammer and held it still.","He stared at Noah with menace that promised violence beyond imagination. His aura continued spreading through the surroundings, placing everything in the nearby gigaparsecs under his control, establishing dominance over the battlefield in preparation for the moment when he would no longer be constrained. His rage did not diminish. His hatred did not lessen.","But for now, he did not make a move against Noah.","Shockingly, he gave that second.","And in that second, Noah could stretch it toward Infinity.","He closed his eyes calmly as he grasped his Spear of Civilization, its crystalline shaft humming against his palm with authority that had just deflected a Proterozoic attack. He focused on his Quintessence Infiniforce, on the portions of it that continued to act as pathways for obscene amounts of Observable force flooding into his existence. He traced those pathways back toward their source, linked his existence through them, and called out.","\"O Secretive Eon.\"","HUUM!","His voice was heavy with authority that pressed through the Quintessence Infiniforce connection.","Nothing happened for a moment.","He was about to call again when the pathways began to illuminate with golden light that eclipsed even the Observable force flowing through them. The portion of his existence he sent through those pathways was met with another presence, and they both disappeared into a single instant of Infinity.","His vision changed.","Part of his consciousness found itself moving between endless weavings of Observable, traveling through channels that existed outside normal space, passing through barriers that should have been impenetrable. The journey lasted no time at all and an eternity simultaneously, the paradox of Infinity making both statements equally true.","He appeared in a place that defied easy expectation.","|Domain Entry: Isolated Sanctuary between Observable and Unobservable.|","|Unobservable Boundary Pressure is active. All unauthorized existences experience foundational strain within this zone.|","|Immunity Triggered: Quintessence Infiniforce has granted temporary authorization.|","An illusory version of his body materialized within an isolated domain that measured only a mile in diameter. Green grass covered the ground in vibrant carpets that should not have existed given the swirling Unobservable weavings pressing against the domain’s boundaries. A simple white hut stood at the center, humble and unremarkable.","This was a sanctuary hidden between Observable and Unobservable!","Noah observed THE Primordial Paradox first.","|Entity Detected: THE Primordial Paradox.|","|Status: Frozen.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Rhyacian Tier.|","|Status Effect ’Temporal Suspension’ is active.Target cannot act, perceive, or respond until effect is lifted by source.|","Ruination became much more active with information as far too much force of Observable weavings of existence flooded him, giving him an influx of everything!","His former master stood nearby, but something was profoundly wrong with his positioning.","He appeared frozen in place, his obsidian titanic form locked in a posture. Yet his aura radiated profound power that declared his achievement of THE Second Scale with authority that could not be mistaken.","THE Primordial Paradox had achieved THE Proterozoic Scale.","And he was frozen?","Noah frowned at this impossibility before turning his attention to the one responsible.","|Entity Detected: THE Secretive Eon.|","|Status: Unknown.|","|Warning: Entity classification cannot be determined.|","THE Secretive Eon stood at the center of the domain, and the moment Noah observed her, his mind began cataloging details.","|Civilization Activation Detected: Unknown Civilization.|","|Observable Dominion is active. All Observable force within range is being redirected toward source entity.|","Her eyes radiated endless gold rather than the dark irises she had possessed.","Radiant golden tattoos rolled from her neck down to her chest in configurations that told stories in languages predating speech.","Upon her wrists, golden bands shining with contained authority had formed.","Her posture had changed entirely from what he remembered.","Where before she had carried herself with the cold calculation of someone who had experienced wonder, now she bore herself with the cold supremacy of someone who had never needed to plan anything at all. The difference was subtle but unmistakable.","Her shoulders held no tension. Her stance contained no preparation for threat. She existed in a state of absolute certainty that nothing around her could pose genuine danger.","She looked at him as a queen might look at a peasant who had wandered into her throne room.","|Observable Force Flow Analysis:|","|Direction: All vectors pointing toward THE Secretive Eon.|","|Volume: Exceeds measurable parameters.|","|Absorption Rate: 100% efficiency.|","|Conclusion: Entity is not cultivating. Entity is restoring to come previous unknown state.|","Golden misty light of Observable continued flowing into her form from every direction, rivers of force that exceeded anything he had witnessed even during his own transformations.","The volume was staggering. The concentration was beyond what should have been possible for any container to hold. Yet she absorbed it without strain, without effort, without any indication that she was doing anything remarkable at all.","Noah assembled these observations into conclusions that formed with uncomfortable clarity.","He could see the evidence of transformation.","But the fundamental question remained beyond his capacity to determine.","Noah looked at her directly, his illusory form standing before her actual presence with posture that refused to show deference regardless of what she had become.","Other questions he could infer answers to through observation and deduction.","But one question remained that he could not answer through inference alone.","\" What...are you?\"","His voice emerged steady and demanding, filtering no confusion, displaying no uncertainty.","Other things he could determine. But what exactly was Eon?"]},{"number":5061,"title":"Chapter 5061: Chapter 5060: What Are You? II","paragraphs":["In this moment stretched out toward an infinity, Noah looked at Eon.","She looked back at him with an expression so calm it bordered on indifference, those endless golden eyes holding none of the calculation he had grown accustomed to seeing in her features. The Observable force continued flowing into her form from every direction, rivers of golden light that painted the isolated sanctuary in hues that should not have been possible within such a small space.","| Status Effect ’Temporal Dilation’ is active. One instant is being stretched toward infinity.|","Ultimately, she spoke.","\" The longer your Infinities remain in my body, the more risk you run for yourself.\"","Her voice emerged with authority that pressed against the boundaries of this domain, each word carrying implications that demanded careful consideration.","\" What happened during the time that I chose to live like you and all others will have far-reaching consequences. Giving you the chance to spread your weavings inside of me has made this possible. I cannot blame you, but I can advise you on exactly how things should unfold from here.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes remained sharp as he listened to her words.","Her choosing to live like them? With that phrasing, he could infer a great deal. She had been something else, had deliberately become something lesser, and now had reverted to what she originally was. The tattoos, the bands, the way Observable force flowed toward her as if she were its natural destination, all of it made sense when framed as restoration rather than transformation.","But what exactly was she now?","\" So you were living among us as us.\"","Noah’s voice emerged steady despite the flood of Observable force still burning through his foundations via the Quintessence Infiniforce connection.","\" What have you reverted back to now? Why do I feel this flood of Observable Force rushing from your existence?\"","Eon looked at him calmly, her golden eyes holding an assessment that felt clinical rather than personal. She was studying him as one might study an interesting specimen, determining how much information he could handle, how much he deserved to know.","\" Others I would not bother too much with.\"","She glanced toward the frozen form of THE Primordial Paradox.","\" Even Paradox I was sentimental about and said a few things. You...are a case study that will already be of interest to us. I just did not want that interest to become a verdict of your end.\"","Her expression shifted slightly.","\" There is much you and even I do not know, but Existence is too vast and has been going on for too long. Your history, the history of our Observable Existence, my history, all of it is a flicker of dust in overall Existence.\"","She paused to let those words settle.","\" You have been alive for an insignificant amount of time. So have I. So have countless others. Eons before we were born, Existence has been ongoing. Lifeforms have been ongoing.\"","Her golden eyes held his without wavering.","\" And across Existence, there are different types of lifeforms. There are those like you, and there are those like me.\"","Noah’s gaze turned heavy as he absorbed these words. Different types of lifeforms. Not different in terms of power or cultivation or achievement, but different in terms of fundamental nature. The distinction she was drawing went beyond what many had encountered in their journey through Observable Existence!","But he continued to listen calmly, permitting her to explain what she meant.","\" You, Primordial Architects, THE Creature, THE Primordial Paradox, THE Living Paradox, every single one of you are lifeforms born and drenched in Adversity in the Scales of Existence.\"","Her voice held no condescension, only statement of fact.","\" You are THE Bounded.\"","|Classification Revealed: THE Bounded.|","|Definition: Lifeforms born and drenched in Adversity.|","The words pressed against Noah’s awareness.","\"I am not drenched in Adversity.\"","Eon’s golden tattoos shimmered as she spoke, their patterns pulsing with light that seemed to respond to her declarations.","\"I am part of them. THE Gilded.\"","|Classification Revealed: THE Gilded.|","|Definition: Lifeforms fundamentally distinct from THE Bounded. Not subject to the same unknown limitations. Reason for the reaction of Observable force.|","\"I could act and play a role to be like you, which is what I did for eons. But you could never be like me. No matter what you do. No matter how much you Persevere.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" That is a doctrine of Vakochev, by the way. To Persevere no matter what across the Scales. But Existence Engineered you already to never be capable of much.\"","Her words were not cruel. They were simply true, at least from her perspective.","\" That already is a gulf enough. Understanding that is what I told Paradox here, and I will tell you somewhat more.\"","She gestured vaguely upward, toward heights that existed beyond this isolated sanctuary.","\" Above you, THE Bounded, are those like me, THE Gilded. And above me are THE Primeval. Even I am not some grand being. I am just a bit higher on the totem pole.\"","|Classification Structure Detected:|","|Tier 1: THE Bounded - Lifeforms drenched in Adversity.|","|Tier 2: THE Gilded - Lifeforms above Adversity.|","|Tier 3: THE Primeval - Classification unknown. Above THE Gilded.|","Ruination’s peompts continued to flash before his eyes as he listened, with her weavings breaking down everything she wss receiving as she made a grand database.","\" That is how vast Existence is. So much more exists that you cannot even imagine.\"","...!","Eon’s voice carried no triumph in these revelations, only the weariness of someone explaining obvious truths to those who had never been permitted to see them.","\" You look at Observable Existence and think that is it. You do not think about all others that are Observable. You do not think of all that which is Unobservable. You do not think of all that exists in between. You do not know of the Designations.\"","She paused, and when she continued, her voice held something approaching a warning.","\" But something supremely critical is how those within their Designations remain within their Designations.\"","\"By connecting yourself to me with your Quintessence Infiniforce as you have, you...are violating your Designation.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":5062,"title":"Chapter 5062: Chapter 5061: What Are You? III","paragraphs":["The words landed with a magisterial force that pressed against Noah’s foundations.","\" Even if I do nothing and I veil it as much as possible, it will be known. For such a violation, it does not matter who you are. Even if you are a unique case study among THE Bounded for your usage and resistance to Infinity that does not belong to your form of life, they will end you for your transgression.\"","|Warning: Existential threat detected.|","|Threat Level: Beyond current parameters.|","|Cause: Quintessence Infiniforce connection to a Gilded lifeform.|","Her golden eyes met his with intensity that cut through the clinical detachment she had been maintaining.","\" Which is why I told you to remove your Quintessence Infiniforce from me. Save yourself, Osmont.\"","BOOM!","The words settled across the isolated sanctuary with finality that pressed against everything within range. Eon stood there with grandeur and imperious bearing that declared her nature as something fundamentally beyond what he had believed her to be. An extraordinary air shone around her form, golden light radiating outward.","She was not merely powerful.","She was different.","She was THE Gilded, and he was THE Bounded, and according to everything she had just explained, that distinction mattered more than any amount of cultivation or advancement or achievement could ever overcome.","Noah looked at her seriously as he took in all her words.","His mind processed everything as he looked back at all the prompts from Ruination. THE Bounded. THE Gilded. THE Primeval. A hierarchy of lifeforms that existed beyond the Scales of Existence he had been climbing, beyond the classifications of Primordial Architects and Singular Cognizances he had been learning, beyond anything Observable Existence had revealed to him.","He was supposed to be insignificant in this grand scope.","He was supposed to be minor.","He was supposed to be a flicker of dust in overall Existence, a being whose entire history amounted to nothing compared to the eons that had preceded his birth.","His eyes shone with a light of tyranny at being told how minuscule he was.","He knew he was young. He knew this truth intimately, had known it since the moment he began perceiving beings who had existed for eons beyond counting while he had lived for mere moments in comparison. He understood his youth. He accepted his youth.","But he was also grand.","Oh, he was grand.","The Observable force flooding into him from Eon’s existence continued burning through his foundations, and THE Hadean Organ of Civilization continued spinning to process it, and his Quintessence Infiniforce continued acting as pathways that apparently violated Designations he had never known existed.","He was THE Bounded, she said.","He was limited by Existential Engineering, she said!","He could never be like her no matter what he did, she said.","Noah stood there in his illusory form, looking at THE Secretive Eon with expression that held no fear, no despair, no acceptance of the limitations she had just described.","Only tyranny.","Only the absolute certainty that regardless of what Existence had engineered him to be, regardless of what Designations he was supposed to remain within, regardless of what they would do to him for his transgressions, he would become something that made their classifications seem small.","He knew he was young.","But he was also grand!","As his eyes shone with imperious light, Eon looked at him as if she understood everything his gaze stood for.","She shook her head calmly before turning to look out toward the edge of this small domain, where swirling weavings of Unobservable pressed against the boundaries that separated this sanctuary from the vastness beyond. Her expression shifted into something contemplative, something almost wistful in ways that did not match the supremacy she had been radiating since the moment he arrived.","\"I see your defiance.\"","Her voice emerged softer than before.","\"I was similar once. Perhaps I still am.\"","She paused, golden eyes fixed upon distances that existed beyond the mile-wide domain surrounding them.","\" When I first became aware of what I was, of what THE Gilded meant compared to everything else in Existence, I felt as though I did not belong anywhere. THE Bounded could not understand me. Other Gilded seemed content with their positions, with the natural superiority we were born into, with accepting the hierarchy as it was designed. I was not content.\"","Her hands touched the golden bands upon her wrists, fingers tracing patterns that seemed older than most Existences.","\"I watched THE Creature make choices of his own volition. I watched him embrace Adversity when he had no need to, experiment with forces that could have unmade him, reject everything he was supposed to be in pursuit of something he wanted to become. I watched Primordial Architects struggle and fail and succeed and fail again, each mistake shaping them into something different than what they had been before.\"","She turned slightly, her profile illuminated by the golden light still flowing into her form.","\"I wanted that. I wanted to make my own choices and my own mistakes. I wanted to experience Existence differently than how I was supposed to experience it. The role of THE Gilded felt hollow when I had done nothing to earn it. I had been born into supremacy rather than achieving it.\"","Her expression shifted into something that resembled regret.","\"So I sealed myself. I locked away what I was and chose to live as THE Bounded, to experience Adversity as they experienced it, to struggle as they struggled, to feel the weight of limitations I had never known before.\"","She released a breath that seemed to carry centuries of accumulated experience.","\" And mistakes I made. So many mistakes. I convinced myself that persevering through challenges without my true nature was noble, was meaningful, was something that would make me understand Existence in ways I could not have understood otherwise. I even looked at the Adversity THE Creature and Erwin engineered and promised myself I would strip them of their distinctions as Keys of Civilizations of our Observable Existence and take them myself or give them to others.\"","Her golden eyes closed briefly.","\"I was even foolhardy enough to allow a fungus of a Primordial Architect to take over my existence. THE Primordial Mycelia seized control of me, used me as a puppet, violated everything I was, and I did not unseal myself because of my pride. Because I told myself that unsealing would mean admitting failure, would mean my experiment had concluded in defeat.\"","She opened her eyes and turned to face Noah directly.","\"I made mistakes. Eons worth of them. Some taught me things I could not have learned otherwise. Most simply hurt.\"","Her gaze held his with intensity that pressed against his awareness.","\" Do not make the same mistakes as me.\"","The words emerged with conviction that seemed to surprise even her.","\"I can afford to make mistakes. You cannot. Mistakes for me are a slap on the wrist, a minor inconvenience, a lesson that carries no permanent consequence. A single mistake for you is extinction .\"","She stepped closer to his illusory form, golden light radiating around her with each movement.","\" You do not need what I have. You are already exceptional enough among THE Bounded. Your resistance to Infinity, your weavings, your progression, all of it marks you as unique within your Designation. Just take your Quintessence Infiniforce away and save yourself.\"","...!"]},{"number":5063,"title":"Chapter 5063: Chapter 5062: Defiance! I","paragraphs":["Noah listened to her words with the attention they deserved.","Her story was not what he had expected. Pride and foolishness and the desire to experience something beyond the role she had been assigned, these were motivations he could understand even if he could not entirely relate to them. She had made herself lesser because being greater felt unearned. She had suffered because she refused to admit that her experiment had failed.","He could respect that, even as he refused to follow her advice.","\" Where I grew up, there was a private school near the public school I attended.\"","His voice emerged with calm that matched her earlier composure.","\" Vastly different institutions. The private school had uniforms and gates and parents who drove expensive vehicles. The public school had metal detectors and overcrowded classrooms and teachers who had stopped caring years before I arrived.\"","He observed her expression shift into curiosity at his unexpected response.","\" Some days during lunch, I would walk to a park that sat between these two vastly different worlds. And in that park, I befriended a girl from the private school. She was beautiful, intelligent, and kind in ways that suggested she did not realize how different our circumstances actually were.\"","Noah’s illusory form shifted slightly, memories he had not accessed in what felt like eternities surfacing with clarity that surprised him.","\" When her friends found out about our friendship, they cornered me. They told me the two of us were in different worlds. They said I needed to stop pushing myself around her, that she was just being nice to someone as little as me. She was far above. I was below.\"","His eyes met Eon’s golden gaze with defiance that had not diminished since childhood.","\" Tell me, do you think I stopped seeing that girl?\"","He did not wait for her to answer.","\" She was a baddie. And I never stopped seeing her until she went abroad. She was supposed to be out of my league. Everyone told me so. Her friends told me so. Her parents eventually told me so. I did not care.\"","His smile held the tyranny that had defined him since before he understood what tyranny meant.","\" So tell me, what do you think I will do in this situation?\"","...!","His words were grand, declarations that refused to acknowledge the hierarchies being described to him!","Eon looked at him calmly again. She did not reply to his story, did not attempt to explain why his analogy was flawed, did not point out that the consequences of defying Existential Designations were somewhat different than the consequences of defying private school social hierarchies.","She simply observed him as one might observe a specimen confirming expected behavior.","Noah looked at her as another question formed in his awareness.","\" As a Gilded Lifeform, why is so much Observable force flowing into you? You seem to have so much that my weavings inside of you cannot help but transmit it over.\"","Eon’s expression shifted into something approaching patience.","\" THE Gilded are blessed and nurtured by all that which is Observable.\"","Her voice held the tone of someone explaining fundamentals to those who had never been permitted to learn them.","\" Contextually not infinite, but all Gilded have access freely to an almost endless amount of Observable force. Traversing the lower Scales of Vakochev’s Existence is easier for us. All THE Bounded never gaze upon anything past Proterozoic.\"","She looked at him with directness that permitted no misunderstanding.","\" You...will never gaze upon anything past Proterozoic.\"","|Advancement limitation confirmed for Bounded Lifeforms.|","|Maximum ceiling: THE Proterozoic Scale.|","\" THE Gilded can progress past THE Second Scale with time. It is simply how we were born. Access to Observable is merely one of the perks.\"","Her golden tattoos pulsed with light that seemed to emphasize her words.","\" We interact with the Scales differently. We have resistance to Infinity and much more unlike what any Bounded can imagine. I am telling you all of this, but it seems worthless as it does not seem like you will change your path.\"","Noah’s eyes remained firm with tyranny as he processed her words.","THE Bounded could never progress past THE Proterozoic Scale. That was the ceiling Existence had engineered for his kind. That was the limitation he was supposed to accept, the boundary he was never supposed to cross, the height beyond which he was never supposed to gaze.","He nodded slowly.","\"If I have gotten my hooks on one of the perks of THE Gilded through you, why should I let go?\"","His smile held conviction that refused to acknowledge impossibility.","\"I want to enjoy what you are enjoying.\"","|Decision Registered: Quintessence Infiniforce connection will be maintained.|","Eon looked at him silently for a long moment.","\" Had you not helped my foolish past self with that fungus, I may have forced you to do what I am saying.\"","Her voice emerged measured and final.","\" As a thank you, I will not. But my choice to thank you this way can also be considered your catastrophe, as I know what it will bring for you in the future.\"","She turned away from him, her form beginning to shimmer with light that suggested imminent departure.","\" You have made your choice. I will not go back and forth on it with you. Just be ready.\"","She paused, looking back over her shoulder.","\" When they do inadvertently find out, you can find ease in the fact that they will only care about you. They will only extinguish you. Your family or any of those under you would be untouched.\"","Her golden eyes held his one final time.","\" So at least there is that. Your choice will only bring about your own ruin, and others will mourn you.\"","Noah’s eyes shone sharply at her words.","\" What about you who allowed this to happen?\"","Eon’s calm reply emerged with the certainty of someone stating mathematical truth.","\"I told you. I get a slap on the wrist. You get extinction.\"","HUUM!","With such words, her figure rose as she began to flicker out of Observable Existence.","Golden light gathered around her form. She was departing , returning to existences he had never known existed until moments ago.","Noah looked at her defiantly as she looked back at him.","The two held their gazes across the distance separating them, Gilded and Bounded, superior and inferior according to Designations he refused to acknowledge.","He would not remove his Quintessence Infiniforce from her existence. He would not surrender the Observable force flowing into him through those pathways. He would not accept the extinction she predicted with such casual certainty.","Ultimately, she sighed.","Then...she disappeared."]},{"number":5064,"title":"Chapter 5064: Chapter 5063: Defiance! II","paragraphs":["|Entity Departed: THE Secretive Eon.|","|Status Effect ’Temporal Suspension’ has ended.|","|Domain Status: Normalized.|","The freezing power that had held everything in place vanished instantly.","THE Primordial Paradox unfroze as if no time had passed at all, his obsidian titanic form completing whatever motion he had been making before Eon’s power locked him in place. His massive head turned toward where she had been standing, found nothing, then shifted to observe Noah’s illusory form floating nearby.","His expression changed through several configurations before settling on bewildered frustration.","\" Fucking hell.\"","His voice emerged with exhaustion that seemed inappropriate for someone who had just achieved THE Second Scale.","\" You are not going to tell me you are some Gilded grandiose lifeform too, right?\"","Noah floated closer to THE Primordial Paradox, observing the changes that had occurred within him. The aura radiating from that obsidian form declared Proterozoic authority with intensity. Something had fundamentally shifted within those foundations.","He sighed at the question.","\" No, I am not something like that.\"","His illusory form settled beside the massive Primordial Paradox.","\"But hey, THE Second Scale for you. Congratulations.\"","|Entity Analysis: THE Primordial Paradox.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Rhyacian Tier.|","|Civilizational Anchor: Established. Composition: Paradox.|","|Proterozoic Bone Detected: THE Paradoxical Sternum.|","|Location: Chest cavity, integrated with ribcage.|","|Capabilities: Allows simultaneous channeling of contradictory authorities. Enables existence in mutually exclusive states. Full parameters unknown, requires testing.|","THE Primordial Paradox’s expression twisted into something between gratitude and offense.","\" Congratulations what? I did not even do it myself.\"","His obsidian hand pressed against his chest where his newly formed Proterozoic Bone resided.","\" The all-important Gilded Lifeform who has apparently left just tapped out twice to form my Anchor for me and this Proterozoic Bone. Fucking hell.\"","...!","Noah observed Paradox gazing at his chest bone.","His own eyes shone brightly as he processed the implications. A few taps from Eon had taken THE Primordial Paradox to THE Second Scale. Casual gestures from a Gilded Lifeform had accomplished what should have required a great fucking deal, what should have demanded absolute self-knowledge!","She had done it with taps.","Then he truly would not release the Quintessence Infiniforce flowing through her existence.","The Observable force continuing to pour into him was insane, volumes that his Hadean Organ of Civilization processed with efficiency that prevented overflow but could not prevent awareness of just how much was coming through. His own power and progression would be jumping tremendously as his foundations absorbed what a Gilded Lifeform considered casual excess.","|Incoming Observable Force: Continuous.|","|Processing Status: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization operating at elevated capacity.|","|Projection: Significant advancement imminent across multiple parameters.|","’Hmm...’","But with everything somewhat clearer regarding Eon and her nature, he could return his attention to Beowulf.","The Second Scale Primordial Architect was still waiting in THE Wastes, held in check by revelations that should have been impossible for Noah to know. Alexander was still there as well, ready for the confrontation that had brought them to that transformed landscape. The illusory screens were still broadcasting everything to Observable Existence.","As he thought this through, he came to sit beside Paradox within this isolated sanctuary.","\" What happened with Erwin?\"","Indeed. Whatever happened to THE Living Paradox that Noah knew at this moment in time...had arrived in the same location as another body of his and Naldine Manthon in Nakatsukuni?","THE Primordial Paradox sighed, and he began to talk.","---","While wonders unfolded all around him, Noah returned his attention to the body facing Beowulf.","In that region of THE Wastes filled with multicolored seas and endless rain, the instant stretched toward infinity concluded as he refocused his awareness. His illusory form in the isolated sanctuary remained as his consciousness settled fully into the body floating before a Second Scale Primordial Architect who had grown extremely serious during his momentary absence.","He looked around to sense what had changed.","|Environmental conditions have shifted dramatically.|","|Proterozoic Suppression Field detected. Source: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor.|","The heavy Proterozoic Scale power Beowulf had laid down pressed against everything within range. This was battlefield control exercised by someone who had decided casual exchanges were no longer acceptable.","|Status Effect ’Proterozoic Containment’ is active. No entity without a Proterozoic Bone can leave this region. Boundaries extend for surrounding gigaparsecs.|","|Status Effect ’Scale Diminishment’ is active. All First Scale power reduced by 99% within affected zone.|","|Status Effect ’Authority Drain’ is active. Civilizational Authorities are being siphoned from all non-Proterozoic entities at rate of 3% per second.|","|Status Effect ’Infinity Rejection’ is active. All Infinity-based weavings experience 75% efficiency reduction.|","|Status Effect ’Observable Suppression’ is active. Observable force channeling reduced by 80% for First Scale beings.|","...!","Noah smiled at the comprehensive suppression Beowulf had established during his momentary distraction.","This fucker had gotten really, really serious. The multicolored seas around them had stilled completely, frozen not by ice but by authority that demanded all movement cease until permitted. The endless rain had stopped falling, droplets suspended in configurations that declared Beowulf’s dominance over this entire region of transformed space.","His Hadean Organ of Civilization released a burst of multicolored light from within his chest.","He grasped his Spear of Civilization tighter as the organ spun with fury that rejected everything attempting to constrain him, the force of THE Infiniverse erupting out. The Observable force continuing to flood into his existence from Eon’s pathways provided fuel that Beowulf’s suppression could not account for. His foundations burned with golden light that pressed outward against every status effect seeking to impose itself upon his form.","|Immunity Triggered: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has negated ’Proterozoic Containment’.|","|Immunity Triggered: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has negated ’Scale Diminishment’.|","|Immunity Triggered: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has negated ’Authority Drain’.|","|Immunity Triggered: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has negated ’Infinity Rejection’.|","|Immunity Triggered: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization has negated ’Observable Suppression’.|","|Status: All hostile effects nullified for you.|","|Extending nullification field to designated ally: Alexander.|","|Status: All hostile effects nullified for Alexander.|","HUUM!","The suppression that should have crippled any First Scale entity simply dissolved around Noah and Alexander, their existences protected by authority that operated according to different rules than what Beowulf understood.","Noah looked at the massive Primordial Architect floating in the distance, that armored form radiating fury that had only intensified during his absence.","\" Sorry about that. I had to take care of something for a second.\"","His voice emerged with casual confidence that pressed against the tension saturating this region.","\" We can continue now.\"","...!"]},{"number":5065,"title":"Chapter 5065: Chapter 5064: Merely Rhyacian! I","paragraphs":["Beowulf looked at him silently and coldly.","The Primordial Architect no longer spoke, no longer offered threats or declarations or promises of violence to come. He existed in a state of immense focus and grandeur that communicated everything through posture rather than words. His hammer was grasped in his hand, that weapon containing a Proterozoic Bone now held ready for strikes that would not be exploratory.","He was truly serious.","Noah turned to Alexander, who floated beside him with an expression that held bloody peace rather than fear.","\" Give me a few seconds to wear him down, and then you can tag in.\"","Alexander nodded lightly. He understood that Noah needed to establish something first.","Noah began to float toward Beowulf.","As he did so, his Organ of Civilization buzzed with activity that pressed against his awareness. The terrifying force it had received from Eon’s existence, that flood of Observable power that continued pouring through Quintessence Infiniforce pathways, began channeling toward his right hand.","The hand holding the Spear of Civilization. The hand that would bear the weight of this confrontation.","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization is inducing formation of a Hadean Bone within your right hand.|","|Process: Observable Force Integration.|","|Source: Gilded Lifeform connection providing accelerated resources.|","|Estimated completion: Unknown. Dependent on combat intensity and force channeling.|","|Current progress: 0%.|","...!","The bones of his right hand began to tremble as the spear grasped within them buzzed with resonance that matched his foundations. Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly as he felt boundless Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable force flooding into his hand with intensity.","The boons of being connected to a Gilded Lifeform began to show.","His hand burned with golden light that seeped through his skin, illuminating the bones beneath with brilliance that declared transformation in progress. He could feel his phalanges trembling, his metacarpals vibrating, his carpals shifting as Observable force saturated them with authority they had never been designed to contain.","But he went ahead toward Beowulf regardless.","\" Come on, big guy! For all of Observable Existence to see!\"","His voice rang across the stilled battlefield with challenge that could not be ignored.","\" Come on!\"","HUUM!","Beowulf moved.","|Civilization Activation Detected: Armed Existence.|","|Civilization Ability: Absolute Armament Strike. All weapons wielded become extensions of wielder’s foundations. Damage ignores Civilizational defenses.|","The massive hammer descended with speed that contradicted its enormous size. Crimson light blazed from the Proterozoic Bone within as Beowulf channeled everything he possessed through the weapon designed specifically for destruction. The air itself screamed as the hammer fell, reality protesting the force being applied against its fabric!","Noah raised his Spear of Civilization to meet it.","CRACK!","The collision sent shockwaves rippling outward across the stilled battlefield. Multicolored seas that had been frozen by Beowulf’s suppression were not merely disrupted but erased entirely, vast expanses of transformed water simply ceasing to exist as the force of their exchange pressed through them. The suspended rain droplets within a light year of their position vaporized simultaneously!","HUUM!","|Impact Assessment: Attack blocked. Strain detected in your foundations.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 7% complete.|","Noah felt the impact reverberate through his arm with intensity that made his teeth clench. Holding his ground was possible, but it was not easy. He was Immovable!","Beowulf possessed power refined across eons of existence at THE Second Scale. The gap between them was real!","But the gap was closing.","Beowulf withdrew his hammer and swung again with motion that carried the momentum of the first strike into a second assault. The crimson Proterozoic Bone blazed brighter as he channeled even more authority through its configurations.","|Civilization Ability Detected: Cascading Armament.|","|Effect: Each consecutive strike increases in power by factor of 1.5. No known upper limit.|","Noah met this strike as well, his spear intercepting the descending hammer with precision that placed crystalline tip against crimson bone. The Observable and Unobservable forces swirling around his weapon pressed against Beowulf’s authority with intensity that made the Primordial Architect’s massive form actually shift backward slightly.","BOOM!","Another light year of multicolored seas vanished.","|Impact Assessment: Attack blocked. Strain increasing.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 15% complete.|","The third strike came faster than the second, Beowulf’s massive form moving with speed that should have been impossible for something so large. His hammer arced down from angles that seemed to change mid-swing, the Civilization of Armed Existence allowing his weapon to move in ways that contradicted normal physics.","Physics didn’t even matter as they were being violated thoroughly!","|Civilization Ability Detected: Impossible Trajectory.|","|Effect: Weapon can alter direction after swing commences. Conventional blocking ineffective.|","Noah did not attempt conventional blocking.","He thrust his spear forward to meet the hammer before its trajectory could shift, endless blue seas of infinity converging on the spear tip, intercepting the weapon at the source of its motion rather than attempting to catch it at its destination!","His crystalline spearhead pressed against the hammer’s shaft just below the head, Infinity, Observable and Unobservable forces grinding against the crimson bone with friction that generated light visible across the remaining seas.","CRACK!","The impact almost drove Noah backward for the first time, his body buzzing through suspended rain droplets that vaporized upon contact with his passage. He didnt move, but thr space around him was!","The space came to a stop three light years from where he had been, his right arm burning with pain that the transformation within was simultaneously amplifying and soothing.","|Impact Assessment: Partial block. spatial displacement detected.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 23% complete.|","|Warning: Incoming follow-up attack.|","Beowulf was already there.","The Primordial Architect had crossed the distance separating them with speed that demonstrated why THE Second Scale represented such a fundamental advancement over THE First. His hammer descended again, fourth strike of a cascade that would only grow more devastating with each successful connection.","Noah raised his spear.","The weapons collided with force that created a sphere of absolute destruction expanding outward from their point of contact.","Everything within that sphere simply ceased to exist, matter and energy and authority all dissolved by the violence of their exchange. The multicolored seas of THE Wastes, which had covered this region for as far as anyone could see, were being systematically erased by their confrontation.","|Impact Assessment: Attack blocked. Foundational strain approaching thresholds.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 31% complete.|","|Observable Force influx: Compensating for damage.|","The golden light in Noah’s right hand burned brighter.","He could feel the bones transforming, could sense the metacarpals shifting into configurations that should not have been possible for any First Scale entity. The Observable force from Eon’s existence poured through his Quintessence Infiniforce pathways with volume that accelerated the process beyond what natural formation would have permitted.","Ozymandias...may actually not be needed for this.","Beowulf swung again.","Fifth strike. Power increased by factor of 7.59 from the baseline.","Noah met it with a swing of his own.","For the first time in their exchange, he did not simply block but attacked, his Spear of Civilization moving to intercept Beowulf’s hammer while simultaneously pressing toward the armored chest behind it. The Observable and Unobservable forces swirling around his weapon condensed into majesty!","BOOM!","The collision halted both weapons simultaneously.","Neither combatant moved for an instant that seemed to stretch toward eternity. Noah’s spear pressed against Beowulf’s hammer with force that neither could overcome. The Proterozoic Bone within that weapon ground against the Civilizational Armament that should not have existed at THE First Scale, and for one perfect moment, they were equals.","|Impact Assessment: Stalemate achieved.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 47% complete.|","Then Beowulf pressed harder.","The Primordial Architect’s massive form leaned into the exchange, bringing the full immensity of his Second Scale existence to bear against Noah’s resistance. His hammer began pushing the spear back, centimeter by centimeter, his superior Scale asserting itself through raw application of force that methodology alone could not overcome.","|Warning: Stalemate breaking. Enemy advantage increasing.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 52% complete.|","Noah felt his arm straining under the pressure. The bones of his right hand burned with transformation that was occurring too slowly, Observable force flooding into structures that were not yet ready to channel what they were receiving. He needed more time. He needed the formation to complete before Beowulf’s cascade reached heights he could no longer match!","He needed to hold on!","\"Is that all you have?\"","His voice emerged strained but defiant.","\"I expected more from THE Primordial Armor. But in the end, you are merely a Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform!\"","WAA!","Beowulf did not respond with words.","He responded with the sixth strike.","|Civilization Ability Detected: Terminal Armament.|","|Effect: Final strike of cascade sequence. All accumulated power released simultaneously.|","The hammer rose and fell with speed that made everything before seem leisurely by comparison. All the accumulated force of the cascade, every factor of increase built across six consecutive exchanges, compressed into a single descending blow that would end this confrontation one way or another.","Noah met it with everything he had.","| Hadean Bone Formation: 67% complete.|","CRACK!"]},{"number":5066,"title":"Chapter 5066: Chapter 5065: Merely Rhyacian! II","paragraphs":["The impact created devastation that spread across the remaining multicolored seas like a wound expanding through flesh.","Everything within ten light years of their collision simply disappeared, transformed into nothing by forces that existence itself could not withstand. Noah felt his arm screaming with pain, his bones burning with transformation that was being forced toward completion by the violence demanding expression through them.","He held his ground.","Barely!","His feet, if feet could be said to exist in this space of floating combat, pressed against nothing and found purchase anyway. His foundations refused to retreat further. His will, that tyrannical certainty that had defined him since before he understood what power meant, declared that he would not be moved!","Fuck that!","|Hadean Bone Formation: 78% complete.|","|Observable Force influx: Critical volume achieved.|","|Transformation acceleration detected.|","Beowulf pressed harder, putting everything behind the strike that was supposed to end Noah’s existence. His armored face contorted with effort that seemed inappropriate for someone who should have been ending this exchange with casual superiority. He was struggling!","THE Primordial Armor was struggling against a First Scale entity.","|Hadean Bone Formation: 89% complete.|","Golden light erupted from Noah’s right hand with brilliance that painted the destroyed battlefield in hues that had nothing to do with the multicolored seas that had previously occupied this space.","His bones blazed with transformation reaching completion, Observable force crystallizing into golden rivers around him that declared his hand to be something fundamentally different from what it had been moments before.","|Hadean Bone Formation: 95% complete.|","|Hadean Bone Formation: 99% complete.|","| Hadean Bone Formation: Complete.|","HUUM!","Noah’s right hand became visible through his flesh as the bones within shone with imperious gold that pressed outward against the skin containing them.","Every structure within that hand blazed with light that declared transformation accomplished, authority crystallized into physical form through methodology that should not have been possible at THE First Scale.","His carpals glowed golden at his wrist. The metacarpals all radiated with Observable force that had been integrated into their very composition.","His metacarpals blazed with brilliance that extended from wrist to knuckles, five bones that now channeled authority their original design had never anticipated.","His phalanges shone brightest of all, fourteen bones forming his fingers and thumb that now grasped the Spear of Civilization with grip that could not be broken by any force Beowulf could bring to bear.","|Hadean Bone Formation Complete.|","| Designation: THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp.|","|Components: All carpals, metacarpals, and phalanges... of right hand transformed through Observable Force integration.|","|Capability: Grip strength now theoretically infinite . Anything grasped cannot be released except by wielder’s will. Force channeled through hand is multiplied by a factor of Observable concentration.|","| Full capabilities unknown. Field testing in progress.|","...!","Noah grasped his Spear of Civilization with his newly transformed hand.","The weapon buzzed with resonance that seemed almost joyful, as if the crystalline armament recognized that its wielder had finally developed a grip worthy of what it contained. Observable and Unobservable forces swirled around the spear with intensity that exceeded anything he had channeled before, golden and clear rivers pressing outward from the weapon’s tip with fury that demanded release.","Beowulf felt the change.","The Primordial Architect’s eyes, invisible behind that armored helm, widened as he perceived what had just occurred within Noah’s existence. His hammer, still pressing down against the spear blocking it, began to vibrate with frequencies that suggested strain rather than dominance.","Noah smiled with tyranny that had no trace of mercy.","He pushed.","CRACK!","His newly transformed hand channeled force through the Spear of Civilization with intensity that exceeded everything he had managed before this moment!","The Observable force from Eon’s existence, the Unobservable weavings integrated into his weapon, the Quintessence Infiniforce saturating his foundations, all of it condensed into a single point of contact between crystalline spear and crimson-boned hammer.","Beowulf’s weapon began to crack.","|Damage Detected: Enemy weapon structural integrity compromising.|","|Proterozoic Bone within hammer experiencing resonance overload.|","The Primordial Architect attempted to withdraw, to create distance that would allow him to reassess this confrontation that had shifted so dramatically against his expectations. His massive form pulled backward with speed that demonstrated Second Scale capabilities even in retreat.","Noah did not permit retreat.","THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp closed tighter around his spear as he thrust forward with motion that carried the accumulated force of their entire exchange into a single piercing strike. The crystalline tip of his weapon pressed against the hammer that Beowulf was attempting to interpose between them.","BOOM!","The hammer... exploded.","|Enemy Weapon Status: Destroyed.|","|Proterozoic Bone Status: Exposed. No longer integrated into armament structure.|","HUUM!","The weapon that had terrorized countless existences across eons of conflict simply ceased to exist as a unified construct. Metal and authority and accumulated enchantment all dissolved outward in rings of destruction that pressed against everything within range. Only the crimson obsidian Proterozoic Bone that had been integrated into its structure remained, that single transformed component falling through the space where the hammer had been.","Beowulf stared at his empty hands with shock that pressed against the fury he had been maintaining.","Noah did not pause to appreciate the moment.","His newly transformed hand grasped his Spear of Civilization as he swung with motion that felt impossibly heavy and impossibly fast simultaneously!","The Observable force crystallized into his bones channeled through every aspect of the strike, golden light trailing behind the weapon’s arc like a comet burning through atmosphere that did not exist.","A massive crescent of golden brilliance erupted from his spear’s path.","The strike surged forth across the distance separating him from Beowulf with speed that exceeded what the Primordial Architect’s shocked state could process. Sharp multicolored edges bordered the golden crescent, Quintessence Infiniforce, Observable and Unobservable forces woven together!","It smashed onto Beowulf’s massive figure.","...!","OH!","BOOM!","|Strike Impact: Direct hit confirmed.|","|Target Status: Armor breached.|","The armor that had defined THE Primordial Armor since before most current beings had learned to exist received a diagonal cut from shoulder to waist. Metal that should have been impervious to anything THE First Scale could produce parted like flesh before a blade, edges glowing with heat that had nothing to do with friction.","Beneath that parted armor, something was revealed that Noah had not expected.","Wriggling physiology that resembled nothing human or humanoid occupied the space where internal organs should have resided. Living metal that moved with autonomous purpose, tendrils of animate armor that had grown into Beowulf’s existence so thoroughly that the distinction between being and equipment had long ago ceased to have meaning.","And alongside that horrifying revelation, a roar erupted from Beowulf’s armored helm.","\"OOOOOH!\"","It was the first sound the Primordial Architect had made since their genuine combat began. Lividity and pain mixed together in that bellow that echoed across the destroyed battlefield, across the space where multicolored seas had once spread as far as anyone could see, across the illusory screens that continued broadcasting everything to Observable Existence.","THE Primordial Armor had been wounded.","THE motherfucking Youngest had drawn blood!"]},{"number":5067,"title":"Chapter 5067: Chapter 5066: Anchored And Bound! I","paragraphs":["As Beowulf was pushed back with a heavy injury, Noah moved with unfathomable momentum that his newly transformed hand granted him.","The Primordial Architect was reeling, that diagonal wound across his chest exposing wriggling internal physiology that should never have been revealed to anyone at THE First Scale. His armored form attempted to create distance, to establish the space necessary to recover and reassess this confrontation that had shifted so dramatically against his expectations.","Noah did not permit distance.","He threw his Spear of Civilization upward with motion that carried the full force of THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp behind it. The crystalline weapon rose above the destroyed battlefield, above the space where multicolored seas had once spread as far as anyone could see, above everything that remained in this devastated region of THE Wastes.","The light of Quintessence Infiniforce shone upon the ascending spear with brilliance that painted the suspended rain droplets in hues of endless authority!","|Civilization Ability Activated: Spear Multiplication.|","|Quintessence Infiniforce channeling through THE Hadean Spear of Civilization.|","|Illusory constructs forming.|","Instantly, eight illusory Spears of Civilization materialized around the original weapon. They emerged from the Quintessence Infiniforce like reflections given substance, each one identical to the crystalline Kontos that had deflected Proterozoic attacks and shattered a Second Scale weapon. Nine spears now hung in the air above Beowulf’s wounded form, their multicolored brilliance declaring intention that could not be mistaken.","Waves of golden Observable force wrapped around each weapon.","The eight illusory spears oriented themselves toward Beowulf’s extremities with precision that permitted no evasion. They descended simultaneously, piercing through armored limbs with force that pinned the massive Primordial Architect in ways he could not escape. Two spears through each arm. Two spears through each leg. Eight points of anchorage that held his titanic form suspended in the destroyed air.","The main Spear of Civilization, the original weapon containing the full force of THE Infiniverse multiplied and raised by exponents that defied calculation, descended toward Beowulf’s head.","It pierced through his armored helm with sound that echoed across the remaining light years of battlefield.","CRACK!","\"FUCKEEER!\"","Beowulf roared with voice that emerged for only the second time since their genuine combat began.","His body became suspended in the air, held aloft by nine spears that channeled forces he could not overcome despite every aspect of his Second Scale existence straining against them. His massive armored form hung there like a specimen prepared for examination, like something that had been captured rather than defeated, like prey that had finally been brought down by a predator it had underestimated.","|Target Status: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor.|","|Condition: Anchored.|","|Anchoring Force: Boundless flow of Quintessence Infiniforce, Infinity, and concentrated Observable Force channeling through nine Spears of Civilization.|","|Target Resistance: Active. Subject is fighting against anchoring with full Second Scale authority.|","|Assessment: Resistance insufficient. So long as the Spears of Civilization continue to channel their deluge of forces, target will remain anchored.|","|Estimated duration of effective anchoring: Indefinite under current parameters.|","...!","Noah moved after confirming the anchoring was secure.","His small figure, insignificant compared to the massive Primordial Architect suspended before him, flew across the distance separating them with speed that his transformed existence now permitted. He approached Beowulf’s chest, that torn expanse of armor revealing the wriggling physiology beneath, and came to land upon it as if standing upon conquered territory.","He stood on the wound he had inflicted.","His gaze was grand and tyrannical as he looked down at the armored head struggling against the spear that had pierced through it. Beowulf’s invisible eyes, hidden behind that helm, burned with fury that pressed against everything within range despite his immobilized state. The Primordial Architect was not broken. He was merely held.","But being held was enough.","Noah turned to look into the distance where Alexander had been waiting.","He waved his hand with a casual gesture that belied the significance of what he was permitting.","Alexander flew across the destroyed battlefield. His figure crossed the light years separating him from the anchored Primordial Architect in moments, his green robes trailing behind him as the Enneagram upon his chest spun with all nine gems blazing. He did not slow as he approached.","He smashed onto the chest of Beowulf beside Noah.","BOOM!","His gaze was chilly and cold as he looked at Beowulf and then at his companion, at the one who had made this moment possible through confrontation that should not have succeeded.","\"Thank you.\"","The words emerged simple and sincere.","Noah nodded in acknowledgment before stepping back slightly, ceding the space to someone who had earned what was about to occur.","Alexander turned to look at Beowulf.","The Primordial Architect’s armored form continued straining against the nine spears anchoring him in place. His massive limbs pulled against the illusory weapons piercing them, his head twisted against the crystalline spear that had penetrated his helm, his entire existence fought against the imprisonment that had been imposed upon him.","None of it accomplished anything.","\"I was impatient, so I asked for help.\"","Alexander’s voice emerged measured and cold, the tone of someone who had made peace with what they were about to do long before arriving at this moment.","\" While I will not have a grand battle with you, I can come in at the end to allow you to feel what I felt.\"","White gloves appeared upon Alexander’s hands, materializing from authority that seemed designed specifically for this purpose. The material was pristine and clinical, the kind of covering one might wear when performing surgery rather than torture. His fingers flexed within those gloves as he looked down at the torn chest beneath him, at the wriggling internal physiology that had been exposed by Noah’s earlier strike.","Noah watched as Alexander reached into that wound.","His gloved hands pressed past the parted armor, past the animate metal that tried to resist his intrusion, past every defense that Beowulf’s existence could muster against what was occurring. Alexander’s fingers found something within that wriggling physiology, grasped it with precision.","|Alexander has activated unknown ability.|","|Effect: Existential Nociceptor visualization.|","|This ability should only be accessible to Second Scale entities.|","|Analysis: Alexander’s Enneagram is providing elevated perception despite First Scale classification.|","Alexander’s Enneagram began to spin faster, all nine gems blazing with multicolored light that pressed outward from his chest. His hands became covered with that same multicolored brilliance, authority flowing through his fingers into the depths of Beowulf’s existence as they held glimmers of Noah’s Quintessence Infiniforce.","Something...began to rise from within the Primordial Architect!"]},{"number":5068,"title":"Chapter 5068: Chapter 5067: Anchored And Bound! II","paragraphs":["A system of receptors became visible that should only have been perceptible to those at THE Second Scale. They emerged from Beowulf’s internal physiology like a nervous system being extracted from flesh, except these were not nerves in any biological sense.","These were the fundamental architectures through which all suffering flowed, the structures that Beowulf himself had described when he tortured Alexander across millions of years of subjective time.","Vibrant crimson vessels spread outward from the wound in Beowulf’s chest!","They resembled a network of veins or nerves, branching and subdividing into configurations that covered the Primordial Architect’s entire existence. The Existential Nociceptors blazed at the center, fundamental receptors that served as the foundation for everything else. From them extended the Civilizational Afferents, pathways that could carry agony through one’s entire Civilization simultaneously.","The Delta-Threads of Existence were visible as sharper, faster conduits designed for immediate pain transmission. The C-Fibers of Being appeared as slower, thicker vessels that carried burning anguish without relief. And scattered throughout the network were the Polymodal Agony Receptors, rare structures that responded to multiple types of suffering at once.","All of it was now visible.","All of it was now accessible.","Alexander looked at the system he had revealed with an expression that held no mercy.","\" Not long ago, I experienced these receptors for what seemed like millions of years.\"","His voice remained calm despite the subject matter.","\" You isolated every Existential Nociceptor within my existence. You mapped my Civilizational Afferents with precision that left no pathway untouched. You activated my Polymodal Agony Receptors while flooding my Delta-Threads and C-Fibers with stimulation that exceeded anything I was designed to endure.\"","His gloved fingers traced along one of the crimson vessels with touch that seemed almost gentle.","\" You applied Hyperalgesic Amplification until my receptors were sensitized beyond theoretical maximums. You dilated my perception of time until each moment of torture stretched into spans that would reduce civilizations to begging.\"","He paused.","\"I wish... to repay the favor. For the sake of Peace. So that I can sleep at night. You screams will serve as my lullabies.\"","...!","Noah watched this exchange from his position on Beowulf’s chest.","The Primordial Architect’s armored head opened as much as the spear piercing it would permit, revealing darkness within that somehow managed to convey expressions despite possessing no visible features. Beowulf roared with fury that shook the nine spears anchoring him, his massive form straining against imprisonment that his full Second Scale authority could not overcome.","It accomplished nothing.","The anchoring held.","|Alexander has commenced manipulation of target’s Existential Nociceptors.|","|Target Status: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor.|","|Current experience: Initial isolation of fundamental pain receptors.|","|Civilizational Afferents: Being mapped.|","|Delta-Threads of Existence: Identified and prepared for stimulation.|","|C-Fibers of Being: Identified and prepared for sustained activation.|","|Polymodal Agony Receptors: Located. Activation sequence initiating.|","|Hyperalgesic Amplification: Commencing.|","|Target resistance: Ineffective. Pain architecture now under Alexander’s control.|","Alexander’s hands moved with precision that spoke of expertise earned through personal experience. He knew these receptors intimately. He knew exactly how they functioned, exactly how they could be manipulated, exactly what configurations would produce suffering that exceeded anything existence was designed to endure.","He knew because Beowulf had taught him.","|Hyperalgesic Amplification: Sensitivity increasing.|","|Factor: 100x baseline.|","|Factor: 1,000x baseline.|","|Factor: 10,000x baseline.|","|Factor: Continuing to escalate. No upper limit detected.|","...!","\" Wait...WAIT- OOOH!\"","Beowulf’s roars shifted into something else as the amplification took hold.","|Temporal Dilation: Activating around target’s pain receptors.|","|Objective time: 1 nanosecond.|","|Subjective experience: 1 year.|","|Objective time: 2 nanoseconds.|","|Subjective experience: 1,000 years.|","|Dilation continuing to compress objective time against subjective perception.|","The sounds emerging from Beowulf’s armored form became screams.","Noah observed all of this from his position on the Primordial Architect’s chest. He watched Alexander work with hands that had become crimson with something that might have been blood if Second Scale entities possessed blood in any conventional sense. He watched the network of pain receptors pulse with activity that exceeded anything they had been designed to transmit.","He watched Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor, experience exactly what he had inflicted upon others across eons of cruelty.","He looked up at the illusory screens that continued displaying everything to Observable Existence.","They captured Beowulf’s screams with clarity that spared no detail. They showed Alexander’s clinical precision as he activated receptor after receptor. They broadcast the moment when a Second Scale Primordial Architect was subjected to torture by beings at THE First Scale, held immobile by spears that should not have been able to anchor him, broken down by methodology he himself had perfected.","There were many things one could do with friends.","Some friends helped you move to new domains. Some friends supported you through difficult cultivation breakthroughs. Some friends provided advice when existence seemed overwhelming.","Right now, Noah was aiding in the torture of a Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect before the eyes of all Observable Existence.","He found he was comfortable with that!","|Target Status: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor.|","|Subjective time experienced: 47,000 years of continuous agony.|","|Objective time elapsed: 0.00004 seconds.|","|Hyperalgesic Amplification: Factor now exceeds measurable parameters.|","|All Existential Nociceptors: Firing without cessation.|","|All Civilizational Afferents: Flooded with maximal stimulation.|","|All Delta-Threads: Transmitting sharp, immediate pain continuously.|","|All C-Fibers: Carrying burning anguish without relief.|","|All Polymodal Agony Receptors: Screaming with multiple agonies simultaneously.|","|Assessment: Target is experiencing everything he inflicted upon Alexander, amplified by methodology refined through personal understanding of suffering.|","The screams of Beowulf echoed across the destroyed battlefield.","They carried through the space where multicolored seas had once spread for as far as anyone could see. They pressed against the suspended rain droplets that had not yet fallen. They broadcast through the illusory screens that transmitted everything to beings across Observable Existence who watched with expressions ranging from horror to satisfaction to careful notation of what was being demonstrated.","THE Primordial Armor screamed as THE Peacemaker got bloody.","Alexander’s white gloves had turned entirely crimson now, stained with whatever passed for vital fluid within a Second Scale Primordial Architect. His expression held nothing but focus as he continued his work, as he repaid every moment of the millions of years he had experienced during his own torture. His Enneagram spun with all nine gems blazing, the construct that he had shattered to protect Noah now serving as the instrument through which he delivered justice.","The screams did not stop!","They would not stop for a very long time."]},{"number":5069,"title":"Chapter 5069: Chapter 5068: Obsession!","paragraphs":["<On the Importance of Hobbies>","In retrospect, holding down a Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect while his friend methodically butchered him was one of the more memorable bonding experiences Noah had in Observable Existence.","There is something to be said for shared activities.","Some friends cultivate together. Some explore Primordial Realms together. Some engage in philosophical discourse about the nature of Infinity and what it means for existence itself. Noah and Alexander chose to anchor a Second Scale torturer with nine spears while one of them systematically activated every pain receptor in his body across millions of years of subjective suffering.","Different strokes...for different folks.","The point is that one must make time for hobbies. Existence is long, particularly when one possesses Infinity, and the relationships that sustain a being across eons are not built through grand declarations or dramatic oaths alone.","They are built through moments. Through experiences. Through looking at one’s companion while he is elbow-deep in the chest cavity of a screaming Primordial Architect and thinking...\"Yes. This is quality time.\"","It is said that friendship requires effort.","It is said that meaningful connections demand investment.","Noah held down a being at THE Second Scale so that his friend could repay millions of years of torture in kind, and he broadcast the entire thing across Observable Existence for everyone to see.","If that is not investment, what is?","Take time for your hobbies. Cherish your friendships. And if those hobbies happen to involve the systematic dismantling of those who wronged the people you care about, well.","At least you are doing it together.","---","<Prima Indifferentia>","The multicolored seas of Prima Indifferentia embraced THE Living Emotive as she floated through waters that should not have existed in this ancient realm.","Her loose clothing billowed around her form, dark fabric spreading through the transformed liquid like ink dissolving in water. Her curvaceous body with its many blessings could barely be seen!","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity had reached even here, filling basins that had been empty since before differentiation taught existence how to distinguish itself. She swam with lazy strokes that suggested meditation rather than travel, her body drifting through warmth that pressed against her skin with authority she recognized as belonging to someone specific.","His authority, hs Infinity, his touch spreading across Observable Existence and reaching her here!","Above the transformed seas, illusory screens blazed with images that demanded her attention. They displayed a battlefield where multicolored seas had been erased entirely, where a massive Primordial Architect hung suspended by nine spears that should not have been capable of anchoring anything at THE Second Scale. They showed two figures standing upon that anchored form, one observing with tyrannical calm while the other worked with hands that had become crimson.","Osmont and a nobody by his side were torturing a Primordial Architect.","The manic light in Emotive’s eyes blazed brighter as she watched.","Her lips parted in expression that might have been smile or might have been hunger. The screens captured every detail with clarity that spared nothing. Beowulf’s screams. The guy’s precision. And Osmont, standing there with golden rivers of Observable force swirling around his form, overseeing the dismantling of a Primordial Architect.","He was magnificent! He was terrifying.","He was everything she had ever wanted and could not yet reach.","In Existence, there were many unique and talented beings scattered across Observable and Unobservable alike.","But those who made the most advancements were not always the most talented.","They were those with tremendous conviction. Those who believed in something so completely that reality itself bent around their certainty rather than the other way around. Those who looked at impossible gaps and saw only distances that had not yet been crossed. Talent mattered, certainly. Resources mattered!","But conviction was the multiplier that made everything else meaningful.","And even if crazy and unstable, even if broken in ways that others could not comprehend, there could be an entity so filled with conviction that their talent exceeded what many others could even imagine. Someone whose obsession became methodology, whose fixation became fuel, whose madness became the very foundation upon which impossible advancement was built.","THE Living Emotive was such an entity.","She knew this. Even if she was crazy, what if that craziness only added to her Civilization?","Her dark hair shone with light. Her eyes, locked onto the illusory screen displaying Noah’s golden-wrapped form, held intensity that would have unsettled anyone capable of perceiving it.","\" To even get close to you, I will need to be so much more.\"","Her voice emerged soft and certain, words spoken to an image that could not hear them, to a man who did not know or care that she was watching, to an obsession.","\" So with my Claim on Chaos, with my Bond to THE Creature and THE Living Paradox...I truly and fully pull on all the negative emotions across Observable Existence for the first time since THE Infinite Unfurling.\"","Her hands spread outward through the multicolored waters, fingers extended as if grasping something invisible.","\" This time, all emotions where Chaos spreads. From Primordial Architects. From Undivided Ones. From anything in any corner of Observable Existence pertaining to emotions and the chaos they hold. From all of Existence and Paradox...\"","Her eyes blazed with manic light that exceeded anything she had permitted herself to express before.","\" Give them all to me.\"","BOOM!","Her body began to vibrate with frequencies that pressed against the transformed seas around her. The multicolored waters churned in response to what she was pulling toward herself, currents disrupting as something vast began converging upon her position from every corner of Observable Existence.","Hazy violet rivers formed in the air above the seas.","They came from every direction simultaneously, streams of condensed emotion flowing toward her form with inevitability that could not be resisted. Rage and despair and hatred and grief and jealousy and resentment, all of it pulled from beings who did not know they were being harvested, all of it converging upon THE Living Emotive as she floated in waters that belonged to the one she obsessed over.","But the violet rivers were not alone.","Golden rivers began forming alongside them, streams of Observable force that should not have been connected to emotional harvesting. They wound around the violet currents like companions that had always been meant to travel together, converging upon Emotive’s form with the same inevitability that governed the emotions she was claiming.","She was taking all emotions across Observable Existence at such a profound level that the very force of Observable began to flow into her. The connection between emotion and perception, between feeling and acknowledgment, between internal experience and external recognition, all of it was being pulled through her Claim with intensity that blurred the boundaries between different types of authority.","It was astounding how the same power, the same Claim, held by a different person could be used so uniquely.","Abaddon had held Chaos for eons beyond counting. He had used it to spread influence, to corrupt domains, to establish presence across Observable Existence without ever fully leveraging what it could accomplish. He had been content with what he possessed rather than hungry for what he could become.","THE Living Emotive was never content.","She was always hungry.","At this moment, Emotive radiated an aura that entirely exceeded any common Absolute at THE First Scale. The violet and golden rivers continued pouring into her form, each stream adding to foundations that were expanding beyond what her previous limitations had permitted. She was going toward distinctions others could only imagine, toward heights that beings with more stable minds would never attempt to reach.","The Broken Doll held a terrifying obsession and conviction.","At this time, she rose up in distinction while her eyes remained locked onto a man in an illusory screen whose entire body was surrounded by golden rivers of Observable. He did not know she was watching. He did not know she was growing. He did not know that every moment he spent becoming greater only intensified her determination to become greater alongside him.","She would reach him and she would stand beside him!","The violet and golden rivers continued converging upon her form as she floated in his transformed seas, her manic smile never wavering, her conviction never faltering, her obsession burning brighter than any stable mind could sustain!"]},{"number":5070,"title":"Chapter 5070: Chapter 5069: Barbaric!","paragraphs":["In the spaces between Observable and Unobservable, darkness reigned absolute.","This region existed outside normal classification, a pocket of reality that belonged to neither the seen nor the unseen but occupied the bleeding edge where both forces met and failed to reconcile.","The air here was thick with authority that predated most current beings, pressure that would have crushed any existence lacking sufficient foundation to withstand it. Light came from no discernible source, yet somehow illumination existed.","Blood covered everything.","Crimson and gold mixed together across surfaces that should not have been able to hold liquid, pooling in depressions that formed patterns.","The smell of death permeated the space with intensity, pressing against awareness itself with declarations of violence recently concluded.","THE Creature sat upon a throne of corpses.","Horus lay beneath him, that ancient Primordial Architect who had terrorized regions of Observable Existence. His massive form stretched across the bloody ground, armored scales that had deflected countless attacks now torn and shattered in configurations of violence beyond what even Second Scale entities should have been able to inflict upon each other.","His chest cavity had been opened, ribs of crystallized authority spread apart like petals of some grotesque flower, revealing internal structures that pulsed weakly with fading life that refused to fully extinguish.","His eyes were gone, of course.","THE Creature had already displayed those to Observable Existence, had held them aloft as trophies for all to witness. But the rest of Horus remained, and what remained was being consumed.","Two other corpses flanked the fallen Horus.","The first belonged to a Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect whose domain had once encompassed concepts of hidden knowledge and forbidden understanding.","His form was humanoid but wrong. His skin, where it remained intact, held patterns of script in languages that predated speech itself. Three Proterozoic Bones shone within his ravaged chest, their multicolored brilliance declaring their nature even in death. His spine had been partially extracted, vertebrae of transformed authority scattered around him like discarded jewelry.","The second corpse belonged to a Primordial Architect whose Civilization had revolved around bindings and contracts and obligations that could not be broken.","Her form was feminine in the way that weapons were feminine, elegant and deadly and designed for purposes that had nothing to do with comfort. Chains of solidified authority still wrapped around her limbs, broken now but still present, remnants of the power she had wielded before THE Creature decided she would wield it no longer.","Two Proterozoic Organs pulsed weakly within her opened torso, one where her heart should have been and another nestled against her spine, both radiating light that was slowly dimming as death claimed what life had built.","Three Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects.","Three corpses arranged around THE Creature like offerings!","THE Creature himself sat upon Horus’s chest. Multicolored flames burned around his figure, fire that consumed nothing but illuminated everything with hues that existence rarely witnessed in such concentration.","His form was humanoid but ancient.","At this moment, one could see that all his bones held multicolored brilliance.","Every single piece of bone within THE Creature’s existence shone with the distinctive light of Proterozoic transformation. His skull blazed beneath flesh that seemed almost translucent in the flames’ illumination.","His ribs pressed outward against his chest with radiance that exceeded the corpses around him. His spine, his pelvis, his femurs and tibias and fibulas, every phalanx in his fingers and toes, all of it had been transformed!","He was not merely at THE Second Scale!","Oh!","Oh!!","He was something that made THE Second Scale seem like a waystation rather than a destination!","And he was eating.","A Proterozoic Eye Organ of Horus rested in THE Creature’s hands. THE Creature bit into it, his jaw working as crimson gold blood and viscera leaked down his chin and chest. The sounds of consumption were wet and horrible, flesh tearing and fluid spilling and authority being absorbed into foundations that were already beyond what most existences could comprehend.","He ate like a beast.","He ate like something that had abandoned pretense of civilization in pursuit of power that civilization could never provide.","And while he ate, he watched.","An illusory screen floated before him, displaying images that had been broadcast across Observable Existence through Noah’s spread Infinities.","The screen showed THE Youngest standing upon the chest of Beowulf, that massive Primordial Architect anchored by nine spears while another worked within his opened chest cavity. It showed torture being inflicted upon a Second Scale entity by beings who should not have been capable of such infliction.","THE Creature watched with eyes that held satisfaction.","Blood dripped from his chin as he observed Osmont’s work, remembering their fight long ago.","At this time, the fabric of this bloody domain shifted.","A figure stepped through barriers that should have been impenetrable, his scholarly robes somehow remaining pristine despite the carnage surrounding his point of arrival. Anaximander looked around the space with an expression that shifted from neutral to disturbed as he processed what he was observing.","His gaze moved across Horus’s ravaged corpse.","It traveled to the other scattered remains.","It settled upon the other Architect’s opened form before finally fixing upon THE Creature himself, who continued eating without acknowledging the new arrival.","Anaximander frowned at the scene of blood surrounding him.","\" We waited for you for too long in THE Lands of the Dead.\"","His voice emerged measured despite the horror around him.","\" You never came so I came to check. I did not expect this level of barbarity.\"","THE Creature bit into the Proterozoic Eye Organ again, more crimson gold fluid spilling down his chest as he chewed with deliberation that seemed almost meditative. He swallowed before responding, his voice emerging with grandeur that contradicted the savage image he presented.","\" All of Existence is barbaric, Anaximander.\"","Multicolored flames shifted around his form as he spoke.","\" We dress our violence in philosophy and call it civilization. We frame our consumption as advancement and call it cultivation. We murder and devour and destroy, and then we write histories that make our atrocities seem inevitable...\"","He gestured toward the corpses around him with the partially consumed Eye Organ still in his grip.","\"I simply refuse the pretense. When I consume my enemies, I do not pretend it is anything other than what it is. When I tear apart those who would have torn apart me, I do not justify it with rhetoric about necessity.\"","His eyes, ancient and terrible and filled with wisdom that most beings could not bear to perceive, fixed upon Anaximander with intensity.","\"I am honest about what I am, Jokul.\"","HUUM!","Anaximander nodded slowly, accepting the explanation without necessarily agreeing with its conclusions.","THE Creature returned his attention to the illusory screen, to the image of Noah standing triumphant upon the chest of a being who should have been able to destroy him.","\" THE Youngest continues to exceed all expectations though, does he not?\"","The question emerged with something approaching pride.","Anaximander followed his gaze to the screen, observing the same images that were being broadcast across Observable Existence. His expression shifted into caution.","\" But if he displays himself openly like this...\"","He paused, choosing his words carefully.","\" Will things like them not come to him in droves?\"","Anaximander pointed toward the corpses of Horus and others, toward the three Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects who had challenged THE Creature and discovered that some challenges should not be accepted.","\" Beowulf should have not been alone. Others will come...\"","THE Creature smiled with glory amidst his multicolored flames.","The expression held no concern, no worry, no indication that he considered these possibilities to be problems rather than opportunities. Blood still stained his chin and chest.","\" That is exactly what he is looking for.\"","His voice emerged with certainty that pressed against Anaximander’s awareness.","\" He wants the Adversity. It is good.\"","He bit into the Eye Organ again, more blood spilling as he chewed.","\" It...is good.\"","The words ended cryptically.","Anaximander could not help but sigh.","He looked around at the scene of devastation surrounding this place, at the corpses of three Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects arranged around THE Creature like trophies, at the blood that covered every surface.","The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity had spread even here.","Multicolored rain fell from heights that should not have existed in this space between Observable and Unobservable, droplets that carried Noah’s and THE Creature’s authority whether he intended them to or not. The rain mixed with the blood covering the ground, crimson gold and multicolored brilliance combining into rivers that flowed in directions that had nothing to do with gravity.","All of those rivers surged toward THE Creature.","The blood of his enemies and the rain of existence and Infinity converged upon his seated form, absorbed by foundations that were already beyond what most existences could comprehend. He sat there eating the eye of a fallen Architect while drinking the mixed fluids of victory and transformation, his multicolored flames burning brighter with each moment that passed.","Anaximander observed all of this with a complex expression.","And...","THE Creature simply continued eating."]},{"number":5071,"title":"Chapter 5071: Chapter 5070: Melody! I","paragraphs":["The screams of a Primordial Architect echoed out across existence.","After a certain point, Noah found them to be akin to a melody. The pitch varied with each manipulation Alexander performed upon those crimson vessels of suffering, rising when Delta-Threads were stimulated, falling when C-Fibers carried their slow burning anguish through pathways that had been designed to transmit rather than receive.","There was rhythm to it. There was almost music in the way Beowulf’s voice broke and reformed and broke again across spans of subjective time that compressed eternities into moments.","It was a symphony of revenge, and Noah served as its maim audience while Alexander conducted.","In the corner of his eyes, he could observe crimson gold blood flying every time Alexander tugged on the network of Existential Nociceptors. The fluid painted nearby regions of the destroyed battlefield in hues.","Droplets hung suspended in the air where Beowulf’s suppression field had once frozen rain, now replaced by frozen blood that would eventually fall when authority permitted gravity to remember its function.","A heavy smell hung in the air.","The smell of a Second Scale entity being unmade receptor by receptor, thread by thread, fiber by fiber!","Oh!","Noah breathed it in without discomfort.","The only thing he had done since anchoring Beowulf was wave his hand to collect what had fallen when the Primordial Architect’s hammer exploded. The Proterozoic Bone that had formed the backbone of that weapon now rested in his grip, held by THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp with pressure that would not permit escape. The crimson obsidian material buzzed against his transformed palm, vibrating with frequencies of rejection.","Noah did not care about its rejections.","He thought instead about the dangerous future ahead and the words of THE Secretive Eon.","Now, he was just told by Eon how his life was very much hanging by a thread. Existence was vast and terrible and populated by hierarchies he had never known existed. There were monsters who had been alive trillions of years beyond his lifetime, beings who operated according to Designations that classified him as something lesser before he had ever been born.","THE Bounded. That was what he was. That was what THE Creature was. That was what every being he had encountered in Observable Existence was, apparently, with the sole exception of Eon herself and others he had yet to meet or even know they exist.","He had to be a bit bold to make sure he would not be curbstomped.","He had to be a bit crazy.","Because as much as he did not want to sit with the implications, he had been told that his desecration of Eon, a Gilded Lifeform, through the Quintessence Infiniforce permeating her existence was bound to get him extinguished. They would find out. They would come. They would end him for the transgression of reaching beyond his Designation, for daring to touch what THE Bounded were never supposed to touch.","If this was truly the case, Noah could not only dismiss it or tyrannically declare that he would not give up on the access he had gained through Eon. Defiance was necessary, but defiance alone was insufficient. He had to have actual planning on how to survive should that time come. He had to understand what he was dealing with, what made THE Gilded different from THE Bounded, what Existential Engineering had been applied to separate one form of life from another.","The biggest thing remained the very connection with Eon.","He felt like if he let it go, he would lose something he might never grasp again. The Observable force flooding into him through those pathways was merely the most obvious benefit. There was more. There had to be more. Understanding that more was essential to surviving what was coming!","So he reached inward to Ruination.","\" Ruination, are you able to study the existence of THE Secretive Eon with the Quintessence Infiniforce permeating throughout her? I want to see what Existential Engineering makes her Gilded and the rest of us not. I want to know the difference.\"","...!","He sent these words in his mind where Ruination heard him and replied in the form of prompts that materialized before his awareness.","|Study of THE Secretive Eon’s Existential Engineering.|","|Assessment: Quintessence Infiniforce pathways provide sufficient access for covert analysis.|","|Challenge: THE Secretive Eon possesses awareness that exceeds anything known. Conducting study without detection requires extreme caution.|","|Solution: THE Hadean Organ of Civilization can process and conceal analytical weavings within the natural flow of Observable force transmission. The larger the organ grows, the more effectively analysis can be hidden within normal operations.|","|Timeline: Unknown. Gilded Existential Engineering has a lot of unknowns to us. Comprehensive understanding may require extended study.|","|Status: Study of the Weavings of Existence of THE Secretive Eon has commenced.|","| Current Progress: 0.001%.|","|Progress will accelerate as THE Hadean Organ of Civilization expands and as more Observable force is processed through Quintessence Infiniforce pathways. Early findings will be reported as they emerge.|","Noah nodded at the prompts as he fully understood what Eon represented the more time passed.","Because even now, endless rivers of golden Observable force continued to flood into him through the connection he refused to sever. His Organ of Civilization spun within his chest, processing volumes that would have overwhelmed anyone else, distributing the excess to foundations that were transforming to accommodate what they were receiving.","The organ continued to spread that light to his hands, to the bones that had already been converted into THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp. But it did not stop there. At this moment, all his bones even slightly past his shoulders were beginning to accept this light and transform.","|Transformation Progress Detected.|","|THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp is serving as template for extended bone transformation.|","|Current spread: Carpal bones of wrist to Radius and Ulna of forearm to Beginning integration with Humerus of upper arm.|","|Projection: Full arm transformation imminent if current influx continues.|","|Scapula and Clavicle of shoulder girdle beginning preliminary Observable Force absorption. Transformation of upper torso skeletal structure may follow arm completion.|","|Connection to a Gilded Lifeform is providing resources that would normally require even you with your progression at least days of work into potentially just hours. THE Gilded Lifeforms present a unique opportunity of progression and advancement. Well, if they don’t collapse everything you have worked for first.|","...!"]},{"number":5072,"title":"Chapter 5072: Chapter 5071: Melody! II","paragraphs":["The golden light spreading through his arm bones felt warm rather than painful.","Alongside this transformation, there was the organ itself.","| THE Hadean Organ of Civilization: Status Update.|","|Observable Force processed since last assessment: Volume exceeds calculation parameters.|","|Result: Organ capacity has expanded significantly.|","|Benefit Unlocked: 2 additional Civilizational Eons of Development are now available.|","|Current Civilizational Eons of Development available: 2.|","| Shall they be utilized for THE Hadean Desmoterion to observe what progress Ozymandias and others within may achieve?|","...!","The question was a grand one.","Two more eons of development. Two more spans of compressed time within the internal prison that would allow those contained there to cultivate at rates that exterior existence could not match. Ozymandias had already achieved THE Proterozoic Scale through the first application of this capability. What could two more eons produce?","Noah did not even take an instant before he gave the command.","Both eons of development would be utilized.","|Command Accepted: Initiating Civilizational Eon of Development (1 of 2).|","|Target: THE Hadean Desmoterion and all entities contained within.|","|Time compression: One eon of subjective cultivation commencing.|","The feedback from his internal prison pressed against Noah’s awareness as compressed time began flowing through those contained foundations. He could sense Ozymandias moving within that space!","|Civilizational Eon of Development (1 of 2): Progress Report - Midpoint.|","|Entity: Ozymandias.|","|Activity: Channeling influx of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force toward skeletal transformation.|","|Progress: Proterozoic Bone formation continued.|","|Current focus: Right arm and cranial structure.|","|Entity: THE Living Elemental.|","|Activity: Civilizational Anchor formation attempt successful and step towards THE Proterozoic Scale taken.|","|Civilizational Eon of Development (1 of 2): Progress Report - Conclusion.|","|Entity: Ozymandias.|","|Achievement: Proterozoic Bone formation of entire right arm completed.|","|Components: Humerus, Radius, Ulna, all Carpals, all Metacarpals, all Phalanges now transformed.|","|Additional Achievement: Proterozoic Bone formation of skull completed.|","|Components: Frontal bone, Parietal bones, Temporal bones, Occipital bone, Sphenoid, Ethmoid, and all facial bones now transformed.|","|Designation: THE Proterozoic Skull of Infinite Perception.|","|Ozymandias now possesses three Proterozoic Bone clusters. Combat capability has increased substantially.|","|Entity: THE Living Elemental.|","|Achievement: Civilizational Anchor Composition: Elemental Totality - All elements across Observable and Unobservable existence recognized as extensions of self.|","|Result: THE Living Elemental has achieved THE Proterozoic Scale.|","|First entity other than Ozymandias to achieve Proterozoic Scale within THE Hadean Desmoterion.|","...!","THE Living Elemental had reached THE Second Scale.","The same entity Noah had beaten with Ozymandias’s legs out of vengeance had now achieved advancement that most Absolutes could never dream of reaching. But...he was still a useless bum of an existence!","|Command Continuing: Initiating Civilizational Eon of Development (2 of 2).|","|Target: THE Hadean Desmoterion and all entities contained within.|","|Time compression: Second eon of subjective cultivation commencing.|","Noah observed the progress with attention that did not waver from Alexander’s ongoing work upon Beowulf. He could perceive both simultaneously, watching crimson gold blood fly in exterior existence while sensing Ozymandias’s focused cultivation in interior foundations.","|Civilizational Eon of Development (2 of 2): Progress Report - Midpoint.|","|Entity: Ozymandias.|","|Activity: Attempting Proterozoic Organ formation rather than additional bone transformation.|","|Focus: Brain tissue. Attempting to transform neural structures into Proterozoic classification.|","|Challenge: Organ formation significantly more difficult than bone transformation. Progress slower than previous eon.|","|Current formation: 34%.|","|Entity: THE Living Elemental.|","|Activity: Stabilizing newly achieved Proterozoic Scale.|","|Progress: Adaptation proceeding normally.|","|Civilizational Eon of Development (2 of 2): Progress Report - Conclusion.|","|Entity: Ozymandias.|","|Achievement: Proterozoic Organ formation of brain completed.|","|Structure: All neural tissue, cerebral cortex, cerebellum, brain stem, and associated structures now transformed into Proterozoic classification.|","|Designation: THE Proterozoic Mind of Infinite Calculation.|","|Capabilities: Processing speed increased by factor exceeding measurement. Perception of Observable and Unobservable forces enhanced to levels approaching theoretical maximums.|","|Assessment: Ozymandias now possesses three Proterozoic Bone clusters and one Proterozoic Organ.|","|As Ozymandias exists within you and as you, all enhancements provide corresponding benefits to primary existence.|","|Civilizational Eons of Development remaining: 0.|","...!","The moment Noah perceived these prompts, feedback surged through his existence with intensity that made him pause in his observation of Alexander’s work.","A cooling sensation began in his brain.","It spread through neural pathways that had never experienced such clarity, washing across his consciousness.","The accomplishment of Ozymandias, that Proterozoic Organ forming within the brain of his other self, resonated through their shared existence.","Noah’s thoughts accelerated.","His perception sharpened.","His awareness of everything occurring around him, from Alexander’s precise manipulations to the screaming of Beowulf to the Observable force flooding through Eon’s pathways to the transformation spreading through his arm bones, all of it became clearer than it had ever been before.","THE Proterozoic Mind of Infinite Calculation was sharing its capabilities with the one who contained it.","Noah stood upon the chest of a tortured Primordial Architect, holding a Proterozoic Bone in his transformed hand, feeling his existence expand in ways that someone like him was never supposed to experience!","As Noah ascertained his new power, he soon frowned and raised his head.","Something had changed in the surroundings.","The multicolored rain of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity, those droplets that had been falling across this region of THE Wastes since his authority transformed it, was being dispersed and broken apart. The rain that carried his Infinity simply ceased to exist in expanding spheres of negation that approached from three distinct directions.","Auras of glorious immensity pressed against everything within range.","Auras of beings at THE Proterozoic Scale!","There were three in total, and each one radiated authority more obscene than Beowulf had managed even before Noah anchored him with nine spears!","Before their forms even became visible, an extremely deep voice boomed out across the destroyed battlefield.","\" You have made your point and will be left alone. Let Beowulf go.\"","HUUM!","The words pressed against reality with authority that expected obedience. They were a command delivered by something that had grown accustomed to commands being followed!","...!","After those words echoed out, the three Primordial Architects materialized from the directions their auras had been approaching.","The first was massive in ways that made Beowulf seem modest by comparison.","His form suggested a knight of impossible proportions, armor of blackened silver covering a body that had been built for war across eons beyond counting. But the armor was wrong. It had fused with the flesh beneath it, metal plates growing from skin like scales, gaps revealing not darkness but churning void that consumed light without reflecting anything.","His helm was a wolf’s skull enlarged to architectural proportions, eye sockets blazing with pale fire that saw everything. In his grip was a greatsword that stretched longer than most beings stood tall, the blade itself seeming to drink the remaining light in this region of destroyed space as it radiated a light of a complete Axiom!","Oh!","The second was not humanoid at all.","It was a mass of serpentine coils wrapped around a central body that might have once possessed recognizable form. Pale flesh covered those coils, flesh that glistened with moisture. But emerging from that pale mass were arms, dozens of them, each one ending in hands that clutched many Half completed Axioms that radiated authority even at this distance.","At the apex of those coils was something that might have been a face, features that shifted between expressions of hunger and contemplation without ever settling on either. It moved through the air as if swimming through water that did not exist, coils undulating with rhythm that hypnotized any awareness foolish enough to focus upon it too long.","The third was elegant.","He appeared almost human, a tall figure in robes of deep purple. His face was beautiful and terrible simultaneously, features too perfect to have occurred naturally. In each hand he held a curved blade that burned with fire on one side and frost on the other, flames and ice existing in impossible proximity without canceling each other. It also fucking shone with the light of a complete Axiom.","Wings emerged from his back, six of them, but they were not feathered. They were comprised of swords, thousands of blades burning with fire and ice as they formed rivers of crimson and white behind them!","Three Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects.","Three beings who had arrived to collect their wounded companion.","Three monsters who expected Noah to comply with their command!","Noah looked at them and sensed the terrifying power they emanated. That power should have made him fearful. It should have triggered every survival instinct, should have sent him retreating.","But...","Instead, he calmly brought the Proterozoic Bone he had been holding in his transformed hand up toward his face.","He opened his mouth.","And he took a bite as he began to chew.","His teeth, enhanced by the Observable force flooding through his existence, pressed against the crimson obsidian material that had once formed the backbone of Beowulf’s hammer.","The bone cracked beneath his bite. Fragments of Proterozoic authority broke away and entered his mouth, grinding against his molars as he chewed with deliberation that seemed almost meditative.","Crimson gold fluid leaked from the corners of his lips.","The three newly arrived Primordial Architects observed this coldly. The wolf-helmed knight’s pale fires flickered. The serpentine mass’s coils stilled their undulation. The elegant figure’s perfect features twitched with distaste!","Noah swallowed.","He focused on the foremost Primordial Architect, the wolf-helmed knight who radiated power that exceeded the other two. This one had spoken. This one had issued the command!","\" But...I do not feel like letting Beowulf go.\"","His voice emerged calm despite the crimson gold fluid still staining his chin, despite the fragment of Proterozoic Bone he continued to hold, despite the three Second Scale entities arrayed before him.","\" My gut tells me the idea and concept of Beowulf will be ending here today.\"","He bit into the bone again, chewing as he spoke.","\" He... has lived enough, and I wish to send him on his way.\""]},{"number":5073,"title":"Chapter 5073: Chapter 5072: Calymmian I","paragraphs":["He said heavy words while looking at what seemed to be powerful Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects.","And he was actively eating the Proterozoic Bone of a living Primordial Architect as Beowulf’s screams became heavier behind him. The sounds shifted in pitch and intensity, showing that what Noah was doing to that crimson obsidian bone was registering through whatever remained of Beowulf’s awareness.","The bone still held connection to its former owner. Perhaps consuming it while the owner still lived created feedback that approached the agony Alexander was inflicting through those networks of Existential Nociceptors.","Either way, the screams became a harmony of suffering that Noah found himself appreciating.","At this time, Alexander looked over to Noah and then toward the three new arrivals. His gloved hands were drenched in crimson gold fluid that had accumulated across spans of torture that objective time could not properly measure. He wiped his brow with those blood-soaked gloves, leaving streaks across his forehead that he did not seem to notice or care about.","\" Are we running? Or can you handle them?\"","He was vengeful, but he still possessed his preservation instincts. The man who had endured millions of years of subjective torture to protect Noah was not foolish enough to die pointlessly when escape remained an option.","Noah looked at the three ahead as if measuring them.","He took another bite of the Proterozoic Bone, the sound of cracking material echoing across the destroyed battlefield with clarity that the newly arrived Primordial Architects could not have missed. Crimson gold fluid leaked down his chin as he chewed with deliberation that bordered on theatrical.","\" Nah, I can handle them. You continue.\"","BOOM!","His eyes shone with a light of brutality and power as his existence affirmed his ongoing expression of tyranny. The words were not bravado. They were declaration of intent from someone who had decided that retreat was not among the options he would consider.","When he looked ahead, the foremost Primordial Architect was smiling.","That wolf skull helm somehow conveyed amusement despite possessing no features capable of expression. The pale fires burning in those empty eye sockets flickered with respect mixed with condescension, the look of an ancient predator observing a young one that had not yet learned its place in the hierarchy of violence.","\" You are drunk on Infinity right now.\"","The deep voice boomed out with authority that pressed against everything within range.","\" Many of us believe you to already be filled with THE Gamaidjan. You simply do not know it yet.\"","A pause as those pale fires studied Noah’s form.","\" But regardless, you could make this into a broader conflict, or you could stop here. Primordial Architects are not loose lifeforms. Beowulf there, however he may have lost face for us today, is not alone.\"","The wolf-helmed figure gestured toward his two companions, toward the serpentine mass of coils and arms and the elegant figure with wings of swords.","\" We could continue this and we could put to the test your power against ours. You are young and filled with Infinity, yes, but we are old and filled with many more things. Only three of us came because we are seeking to be diplomatic since Beowulf made the first move.\"","The pale fires in those empty sockets burned brighter.","\"If this diplomacy fails...\"","...!","Noah’s eyes became sharp as he grandly took another bite in front of them.","The cracking of Proterozoic material filled the silence that followed those words. His chewing was deliberate and loud, each motion of his jaw a response to the threat that had been implied. Crimson gold fluid continued leaking down his chin as he swallowed and his eyes became chilly with an assessment that held no fear.","These fuckers. They were Bounded just like him, yet they considered themselves so powerful?","They stood before him radiating authority that would have crushed most beings at THE First Scale. They spoke of diplomacy while implying devastation should diplomacy fail. They expected him to recognize the gap between them, to acknowledge that three Proterozoic Scale entities represented a threat he could not overcome.","But Noah had broadcast what he was doing specifically to draw in more conflict and adversity.","That was the purpose of those illusory screens spreading his actions across Observable Existence. He wanted enemies to know where he was. He wanted them to come. He wanted to push himself until he was either squashed down into nothing or he rose to become something unimaginable. There was no middle path for someone who had just been told his Designation marked him for limitations he refused to accept.","He knew himself.","He knew his current power. He had himself, and then his body of Ozymandias contained within THE Hadean Desmoterion. Ozymandias was at THE Second Scale with multiple Proterozoic Bones and a Proterozoic Organ. Noah himself, while technically at THE First Scale, was forming things nobody should be able to form at his classification.","He wanted to put himself to the test!","He knew it would be brutal and painful. The three beings before him could likely inflict suffering that exceeded what Beowulf had done to Alexander.","But pain was better than extinction.","And he loved existence far too much to opt for extinction.","So.","His eyes gazed upon the three Architects ahead as their details revealed themselves to his enhanced perception.","| Entity Analysis Commencing.|","|Entity 1: Vahrkosis, THE Primordial Dirge .|","|Classification: Primordial Architect - Proterozoic Scale.|","|Current Tier: Rhyacian .|","|Civilization: Entropic Chaos - Variant focusing on entropy and dissolution.|","|Physical Form: Serpentine mass with multiple humanoid arms. Approximately 47 arms detected, each wielding distinct piece of an Axiom.|","|Proterozoic Composition: 23 Proterozoic Bones detected across coil structure. 1 Proterozoic Organ detected in central mass, classification unknown.|","|Threat Assessment: Significant. Specializes in area denial and overwhelming opponents through multiplicity of attacks.|","|Entity 2: Sammarthiel, THE Paradox Bearer .|","|Classification: Primordial Architect - Proterozoic Scale.|","|Current Tier: Rhyacian .|","|Civilization: White Paradox - Variant focusing on contradictory states existing simultaneously.|","|Physical Form: Humanoid with six wings comprised of bladed weapons. Wields twin Axiom of flame and frost.|","|Proterozoic Composition: 31 Proterozoic Bones detected throughout skeletal structure. 2 Proterozoic Organs detected, one in each hand enabling contradictory elemental manipulation.|","|Threat Assessment: Significant.|","| Entity 3: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Classification: Primordial Architect - Proterozoic Scale.|","|Current Tier: Calymmian.|","|Civilization: Chaos Tongue - Variant focusing on words of power that reshape reality through utterance.|","|Physical Form: Armored knight with wolf skull helm. Blackened silver armor fused with flesh. Axiom Greatsword of light-drinking metal.|","| Proterozoic Composition: 94% of skeletal structure transformed into Proterozoic Bone. Only minor bones of extremities remain untransformed.|","|Proterozoic Organs Detected: 4.|","| Organ 1: Heart - THE Silencing Core . Negates sound-based and vibration-based attacks within range.|","| Organ 2: Lungs - THE Breath of Endings . Exhaled authority can dissolve First Scale entities entirely.|","| Organ 3: Eyes - THE Gaze of Cessation . Visual contact enables direct assault on target’s foundations.|","| Organ 4: Throat - THE Voice of Annihilation . Words spoken carry force sufficient to reshape local reality.|","|Threat Assessment: Extreme . You may lose a body to this one|","...!"]},{"number":5074,"title":"Chapter 5074: Chapter 5073: Calymmian II","paragraphs":["After Noah looked at the details of the most powerful one, his eyes became heavier.","Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence!","Calymmian Tier. Ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone coverage. Four Proterozoic Organs, each one devastating in its own right. A being who had been cultivating power since before most current existences learned to crawl, who had accumulated authority that made Beowulf seem like a junior!","He had come across a truly sturdy wall.","But no matter.","Adversity was Adversity. He could never choose a comfortable level for it, could never tell existence to send him someone he could manage. That was not how growth worked. That was not how someone climbed from nothing to something that made hierarchies seem irrelevant.","He had an enemy before him he could not manage.","The first thing to do was obvious.","’Set him as a target of THE Hadean Existential Singularity.’","He sent the command to RUINATION within his foundations.","| Command Received: Hadean Existential Singularity target designation.|","|Current targets: Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor (Slot 1). Erwin, THE Living Paradox (Slot 2).|","|New target: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Designation: Slot 3.|","|Hadean Existential Singularity siphoning commencing.|","|Siphoning from Grimvault: Observable understanding, Unobservable understanding, Infinity comprehension, cultivation progress, Proterozoic Organ musings...|","|Target possesses significantly greater power than you. Siphoning efficiency reduced greatly.|","|Extended exposure required for meaningful extraction. Combat engagement will accelerate siphoning through direct contact.|","Noah looked over at the three Primordial Architects who were waiting for his response to their offer of diplomacy.","He opened his mouth obscenely wide.","He took larger bites, his teeth cracking through the remaining Proterozoic Bone of Beowulf with sounds that echoed across the destroyed battlefield. Crimson gold fluid sprayed with each violent mastication as he devoured what remained of that bone in moments rather than the measured consumption he had been performing before. The material ground between his molars and slid down his throat in chunks that should have been impossible to swallow.","He burped.","The sound was crude and deliberate, a punctuation to his consumption that communicated everything words could not.","\"I wonder... how your bones will taste.\"","HUUM!","They came and spoke of diplomacy.","Noah knew there would never be diplomacy. These Primordial Architects had arrived expecting to intimidate him into releasing Beowulf, expecting that display of superior force would convince him to abandon his position. They did not want war. They wanted compliance dressed in the language of negotiation.","His words made clear that compliance was not forthcoming.","Inside of him, the Proterozoic Bone of Beowulf was digested by foundations that had grown hungry for exactly this type of sustenance. The Observable force flooding through Eon’s pathways accelerated the process, breaking down Proterozoic material into components that his existence could integrate. His whole arm and past his shoulder, bones shone even more resplendently than they had before, the consumption providing fuel for transformation that continued spreading through his skeletal structure.","And ahead of him, the light of calm and diplomacy faded from the eyes and awareness of all three Primordial Architects.","Grimvault’s pale fires burned with intensity that suggested furnaces being stoked for war. Vahrkosis’s countless arms tightened their grips on weapons and artifacts that began radiating killing intent. Sammarthiel’s wings of swords spread wider, each blade igniting with flames on one edge and frost on the other in configurations that promised devastation to anything they touched.","Instantly, the illusory screens Noah had laid out to broadcast everything to Observable Existence shattered.","The constructs that had been transmitting his confrontation with Beowulf, that had shown his torture of a Second Scale entity to all who cared to watch, simply ceased to exist as Grimvault’s authority pressed against them with force that refused their continued presence. The connection to Observable Existence was severed in an instant.","Terrifying power bloomed from all three Primordial Architects simultaneously.","The weight of their combined authority pressed against everything within range with intensity that would have crushed any normal Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform entity into paste. The air itself thickened with killing intent.","The fabric of reality groaned beneath pressure that threatened to tear this region of THE Wastes apart entirely!","And toward such oncoming terror, Noah jumped off Beowulf.","His figure floated away from the anchored Primordial Architect, moving toward the three entities that had just committed to hostility. His body became surrounded by golden flames of Observable force as he advanced, the endless rivers flowing through Eon’s pathways manifesting around his form in configurations that declared his own authority despite the gap between their Scales.","Golden steam shot from his nose and mouth with each breath he released.","He seemed like a primal celestial beast approaching predators who had grown too comfortable at the apex of their food chain. His eyes blazed with light that held no retreat, no calculation of odds, no recognition that three Proterozoic Scale entities represented a threat he should not be advancing toward.","\" Do you think you are the only ones who banded together?\"","His voice emerged with a challenge that pressed against their combined authority.","\" Do you think I am alone?\"","HUUM!","He said such ominous words as the brutal eyes of the Primordial Architects squinted.","Grimvault’s wolf skull helm tilted slightly, pale fires flickering. Vahrkosis’s serpentine coils stilled, all forty-seven arms pausing their preparation as something in Noah’s words demanded consideration.","The ominous air and immensity rose higher and higher.","The atmosphere itself congealed around them, thickening with authority that pressed against awareness from multiple directions. The multicolored rain of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity that had been resuming after their initial disruption began to whip up into a storm, droplets swirling!","Because the bones of the Primordial Architect at the very forefront had glimmers of Infinity flowing through them.","Grimvault...was utilizing Infinity.","Not the same as Noah’s, not the endless wellspring that defined his existence, but traces of it woven through those Proterozoic Bones.","His mere presence stated with absolute clarity what his words did not need to speak.","Bring out whomever the fuck you wanted to bring out."]},{"number":5075,"title":"Chapter 5075: Chapter 5074: Storm I","paragraphs":["Nakatsukuni.","The illusory screen hovering within Sadakar’s domain displayed devastation of Noah’s battle in The Wastes.","Noah watched his other body through the feed. The three newly arrived Primordial Architects filled the screen with presence that made even this distant observation feel heavy.","And then the Calymmian entity among them, Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence, dispersed the broadcast entirely with authority that simply refused its continued existence!","The screen went dark.","Naldine Manthon looked at Noah with expression that shifted through several configurations before settling on exhausted acceptance. She raised one hand to massage her forehead, fingers pressing against skin that seemed suddenly weary despite the power contained within her foundations. Her singularity-dotted eyes closed briefly as if she needed a moment to process what she had just witnessed.","She then looked toward Noah calmly, her mouth opening as if she was about to deliver rebuke that had been building since the broadcast began.","But she observed his demeanor here in this body, the complete absence of concern despite the fact that his other self now faced three Proterozoic Scale entities including one at the Calymmian Tier. He sat there with composure!","Whatever rebuke she had prepared dissolved into something more practical.","\" Just... tell me where you are.\"","Her voice emerged measured despite the tension underlying it.","Noah looked toward her with eyes that held the same calm his other body was displaying across the vast distances separating them. The golden light of Observable force that continued flooding through his existence via Eon’s pathways made his presence here feel warmer than it had before.","\" Maybe I do not need any help.\"","\"...\"","The words carried no arrogance, only statement of possibility.","Naldine’s expression hardened into something more firm.","\" They will not kill your body. They will capture you.\"","She stepped closer to where he sat, her radiant white hair shifting with movement that seemed almost aggressive in its precision.","\" Again. Tell me where you are.\"","The distinction she drew was important. Death was one thing. Capture was another entirely. Death could be overcome through the bodies he maintained across Observable Existence. Capture meant many more things.","Noah smiled at these words.","He waved his hand, and a vibrant singularity of information materialized between them. Coordinates and spatial markers and navigational data compressed into a form that Naldine could process instantly, the location of his other body laid bare for her to find.","She absorbed the information without acknowledgment, her attention already shifting toward the Singular Cognizance who had been observing this exchange in silence.","Naldine looked at Sadakar with gaze that held no softness.","\" We all must choose sides, Sadakar.\"","Her voice pressed against the stellar atmosphere of this space with conviction.","\" Moloch and the Peasant are here as we speak. They stand at your door, waiting to see what you will do. You can decide how you wish to handle them.\"","The white-blue singularity within its shifting cube pulsed with light. Sadakar had maintained neutrality across eons that most current beings could not comprehend. Being forced to choose now, in this moment, clearly did not sit well with an entity that had built its entire existence around avoiding such choices.","Naldine did not wait for his response.","She turned to Noah.","\"I will go extract your other body. Send this body here away and do not try to add a Singular Cognizance as your enemy as well right now.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed with intensity that demanded compliance.","\" You have enough enemies for one day.\"","With these words, she disappeared.","The stellar atmosphere of Sadakar’s domain settled into silence that pressed against Noah’s awareness. He remained alone with a Singular Cognizance, an entity from before differentiation, a consciousness that had observed existence learn how to exist.","Instead of leaving, Noah actually sat down in a meditative position.","His body settled into stillness that suggested he had no intention of departing anytime soon.","Sadakar’s contained brilliance shifted within its cube as that ancient attention fixed upon him.","\" You will not be leaving?\"","The question pressed against Noah with genuine curiosity.","Noah nodded calmly as he looked out toward the entrance where he and Naldine had arrived. Beyond those doors, the Peasant and Moloch came for whatever reception Sadakar would provide.","\" It may be time for me to have another conversation with Erwin.\"","...!","\"And hey, I do not get the chance to talk to Singular Cognizances often. I am curious for anything you might know and share regarding existence.\"","He turned his attention toward the pulsing singularity.","\" What would make someone like you choose a side, if there was any side? I do not even know the full scope of factions among Primordial Architects. Just a little view of it.\"","...!","He calmly began talking to a Singular Cognizance as if this were merely pleasant conversation between two alike beings.","Elsewhere, terrifying weavings of existence unfolded as a body of his faced enemies far too powerful for his current self!","---","The pressure from those who were truly advanced in THE Proterozoic Scale was unique.","Hours ago, when he faced Beowulf for the first time after they tortured Alexander, Noah could not even touch the Primordial Architect initially.","His Legions had done nothing because they could do nothing.","Even now, he wanted to seek justice for them and the idea of utilizing them. They were his creations, his forces, his expressions of power that should have meant something against the enemies he faced. But until he affirmed himself at heights where such forces became relevant, they had to remain something he worked with in the background.","But back to Proterozoic Scale entities.","The only reason he had been able to interact with Beowulf at all was due to declaring himself finite and basically brute smashing the Primordial Architect with the force of Infinity he had access to. Raw power compensating for lack of methodology. Overwhelming force substituting for refined technique. It had worked because Infinity permitted things that should not have been possible.","And now, hours later, he had used the force of Infinity, Observable and Unobservable, and Quintessence Infiniforce to skewer a Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform like Beowulf with nine spears.","Four different forces of power.","Behind all of them were his Foundations at Uncountable Infinity and his Civilizations. The framework that held everything together, the skeleton upon which all his expressions of authority hung. His Civilizations were the vessels through which force flowed, the channels that directed raw power into meaningful action.","But this also caused him to think about his Civilizations more carefully.","He could embody any Civilization. His Organ of Civilization and Infinity and his very nature made this possible! But he had staunchly began on THE First Tongue. On the language of Existence that was connected to Mana.","Now he had Mana, and he had Infinity. He couldn’t leave behind one or the other as the backbone of how his Organ of Civilization allowed for him to express any Civilizations...was due to the versatility of Mana . It was all behind the shoulders of The First Tongue that changed the language of Existence of his Civilization to be...anything.","How much more could THE First Tongue go as the foundation of things alongside Infinity and what he was delving into now?","The enemies in front of him were using variations of the four aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence as their Civilizations. Chaos, First Tongue, Paradox, and Existence itself served as the frameworks, the skeletons of their power.","The forces they filled those frameworks with to further express themselves were Infinity and, if they were unique enough, perhaps they tapped into weavings of the forces of Observable or Unobservable.","Noah, on the other hand, freely utilized Infinity, Observable, and Unobservable through himself and THE Infiniverse.","And now, due to the connection with a Gilded Lifeform, he was receiving an influx of Observable force that exceeded what any Bounded entity should have been capable of accessing. Rivers of golden authority continued flooding into his existence through pathways that violated Designations he had never known existed a day ago.","With a Civilizational Anchor, those at THE Second Scale held resistance to Infinity and could form Proterozoic Bones or Organs filled with Infinity or Observable force without succumbing to its madness. They acclimated more and more power with the transformation of their bones and organs as their Civilizations became overpowering.","Which was why something like the Proterozoic Organ of Grimvault, the Lungs designated as THE Breath of Endings, could exhale authority capable of dissolving First Scale entities entirely.","The breath of that existence alone could erase him.","When it came to how he had to use such powerful beings as the hammers to make himself stronger, he had to clash against and survive against their power. Infinity was there to make everything possible, the foundation that permitted impossibilities to occur. But the other equations were the forces of Existence that seemed to be critically important.","Observable and Unobservable.","Now, why was it that a Gilded Lifeform was so blessed with a nigh endless supply of Observable? It was a force that made things very easy, with Noah processing it through his Hadean Organ of Civilization as it had helped him rapidly form new bones of his existence that now extended past his shoulders. That Observable force only added to the endlessly generating Quintessence Infiniforce inside him, and his Organ of Civilization converted both into Civilizational Eons of Development that allowed even more progression.","So the directions were clear.","He just had to Persevere under pressure until he got to the point where Grimvault became manageable like Beowulf. But from this point until then, there was a world of pain and adversity waiting for him. A gulf of suffering that had to be crossed before he could stand where these ancient monsters stood! But he welcomed it as he had to cross this gulf!","So now, he faced Grimvault, Sammarthiel, and Vahrkosis.","When faced with the question of just who could possibly side with him in this confrontation, he had implied that he... was not alone!"]},{"number":5076,"title":"Chapter 5076: Chapter 5075: Storm II","paragraphs":["The scene before him declared the scale of what he faced with brutal clarity.","His humanoid form seemed tiny and small in comparison to the three monsters arrayed against him. Grimvault towered with that wolf skull helm blazing pale fire, his blackened silver armor fused with flesh.","Vahrkosis undulated through the air with forty-seven arms grasping Axioms.","Sammarthiel spread those six wings of swords wider, thousands of blades catching light that should not have existed in this destroyed region of THE Wastes.","Behind Noah, the screams of Beowulf continued their symphony of suffering.","Alexander’s work had evolved beyond simple torture. The crimson gold blood that had been flying with each manipulation now flowed with purpose rather than violence. The networks of Existential Nociceptors that Alexander had made visible, those vibrant crimson vessels spreading across Beowulf’s opened chest, were being extracted with precision.","|Activity Detected: Alexander is extracting Existential Nociceptor networks from Beowulf.|","|Purpose: Transplantation into own existence.|","|Alexander is incorporating the very Second Scale systems that were used to torture him into his own foundations.|","Alexander was transplanting those receptors of suffering into his own body!","But as this occurred, space flickered.","SAA!","From one of the many droplets of multicolored rain still falling across this destroyed battlefield, space paradoxically shifted. The droplet expanded and contracted simultaneously, containing more volume than its size should have permitted while remaining exactly as small as it appeared. Reality bent around that impossibility as something emerged.","THE Primordial Paradox stepped through that paradoxical distortion with presence that pressed against everything within range.","His obsidian titanic form looked majestic despite the impossibilities that composed his existence. Blue Infinity dotted that dark surface. A black crown hung loosely above his massive head.","He appeared beside Noah, looking at the enemies ahead fearlessly.","His expression shifted into a frown as he assessed what they faced. He came to float beside Noah with a posture that suggested readiness rather than hesitation, his massive form dwarfing Noah’s humanoid body.","\" You really know how to pick them.\"","His voice emerged with the rumbling depth that obsidian given consciousness might produce.","\" But this is good. After being ganged up on against my disciple, I wondered how it would feel fighting in a group.\"","...!","His entrance was grand, a Proterozoic Scale entity arriving to stand beside Noah against three of his peers.","Right after, space twisted and distorted again.","The fabric of reality bent in directions that had nothing to do with paradox. Light gathered and dispersed simultaneously as another figure emerged.","WAA!","Naldine Manthon stepped through that distortion with a presence that...somewhat exceeded what Noah had felt from her before. It exceeded what he felt from her in Nakatsukuni.","What was this now?","Her blue robe billowed around her form as she arrived, that garment shifting with movement that seemed almost aggressive in its precision. Her cold gaze fixed upon the three Primordial Architects ahead with an assessment that held no warmth, no negotiation, no indication that she considered this confrontation to be anything other than what it was!","Her figure stood imperious beside Noah and THE Primordial Paradox, her singularity-dotted eyes blazing with light!","She looked ahead at Grimvault and the others as she nodded.","\" Grimvault. Sammarthiel. Vahrkosis.\"","She spoke their names as one might speak the names of diseases that had once been survived.","WAA!","Noah’s eyes opened wide as he turned to look at her.","She knew them?","Ahead, Grimvault smiled brutally beneath that wolf skull helm.","Laughter emerged from that armored form, the sound booming across the destroyed battlefield with amusement that seemed genuine rather than performed. Those pale fires burning in empty eye sockets flickered with recognition that matched what Naldine had displayed.","\" Little Naldine? Naldine THE Visionary?\"","The deep voice pressed against everything within range with mocking warmth.","\" Haha! I thought an idealist like you to be dead! I did not know you had already made contact with the Infinity-bearer.\"","Naldine looked ahead as her body began to shine with brilliance that exceeded what Noah had observed from her before.","Her blue robes shifted and transformed, fabric restructuring itself into battle garments that wrapped tightly around her form. The loose elegance that had defined her appearance since he first met her gave way to configurations designed for violence. Her radiant white hair gained a lustrous blue gold shine that painted nearby space in hues of authority preparing to be expressed.","Then she did something ridiculous.","She used her right hand... to grasp her left arm just below the shoulder.","She yanked.","Her left arm disconnected from her body with sound that should have been wet and horrible but instead rang with musical clarity that pressed against awareness like the first note of a symphony. The limb came free from her shoulder without blood, without trauma, without any indication that what she had just done should have been impossible.","The arm shone with multicolored light that exceeded what mere Proterozoic transformation should have permitted. It shifted and restructured in her grip, bone and flesh and authority all reorganizing into configurations that had nothing to do with humanoid anatomy.","It formed into a Vihuela .","The instrument resembled a guitar from traditions that predated most current civilizations, a stringed device designed to produce melody through careful manipulation.","But this Vihuela was composed of prismatic blue gold Proterozoic Bones arranged in configurations that declared it to be weapon as much as instrument. The body curved with elegance. The neck extended with precision that permitted no flaw. The strings stretched across that transformed material gloriously.","Where her left arm had been, an illusory hand formed from authority alone. The construct shimmered with the same blue gold brilliance that now defined her transformed limb, a replacement that functioned despite having no physical substance to support its existence.","Naldine held the Vihuela with the familiarity of someone who had wielded this instrument across eons of conflict.","Her right hand began to pluck the strings.","DING!","The first note rang out across the destroyed battlefield with clarity that pressed against everything within range. The oppression from the enemies ahead, that combined authority of three Proterozoic Scale entities that had been pressing against Noah’s foundations since their arrival, lessened slightly.","DING!","The second note followed immediately, and the oppression lessened further.","DING! DING! DING!","Multiple bones within Naldine’s body began to light up as she played. Her skeletal structure became visible through her flesh as Proterozoic transformation declared itself throughout her form!","Her body became surrounded by melody that seemed to exist as physical force rather than mere sound, waves of authority emanating from each note she produced.","She looked calm and immense as she continued playing, her expression holding none of the cold assessment she had displayed before. This was something else. This was Naldine Manthon expressing capabilities she had not revealed until this moment demanded them.","\"It has been a while since I saw you all.\"","Her voice emerged steady despite her fingers continuing to dance across the strings.","\"I knew we would be on opposite sides eventually, but I did not expect it so soon.\"","She paused her playing for a single beat.","\"Are the others okay? Is Aryana doing good?\"","...!","At such words, Grimvault shook his head.","Laughter emerged from that wolf skull helm again, but this laughter held nothing of the amusement that had colored his earlier recognition. This was cold and brutal.","\"Oh, you fucking whore.\"","The words pressed against everything within range with venom.","\"Aryana is dead. You leave people you have influenced behind and expect them to thrive? Your ideals killed her the day you left THE Wyld.\"","...!","Oh.","The tone of the strings Naldine pulled shifted into something that ached.","Sad notes emerged from the Vihuela, melody that communicated grief without requiring words to express it. Her fingers continued moving across those strings, but the music they produced now spoke of loss. She nodded calmly at the news, her expression holding acceptance.","The environment began to swirl around them.","The multicolored rain of the Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity fell heavier, droplets that carried Noah’s authority responding to the melody Naldine was producing. Rivers of multicolored seas that had been reforming in the regions not yet destroyed by combat began to vibrate to the tune she was enacting, vast bodies of transformed water resonating with notes that pressed against reality itself.","Meanwhile, Noah looked at this whole exchange with eyes that shone sharply.","He wanted to ask the question that had been building since Grimvault spoke that unfamiliar term. Where and what the hell was THE Wyld? Based on context, it should be where all these Primordial Architects were emerging from one after another. Some location or domain or faction that connected Naldine to Grimvault and Sammarthiel and Vahrkosis, some shared history that explained why they recognized each other with familiarity.","THE Wyld.","Another piece of Observable Existence he had not known about!"]},{"number":5077,"title":"Chapter 5077: Chapter 5076: Does Age Make You Sadistic?","paragraphs":["Noah focused on Naldine briefly as he felt a discordant tune every time she played the strings of that radiant instrument forged from her own body.","With each note, he observed an invisible flutter of hundreds of sound-based Embodiments and Apophasis blooming naturally around her form. These were not constructs she was deliberately creating.","They were byproducts, secondary effects that emerged from her playing without conscious direction. The alterations to surrounding existence that Absolutes at THE First Scale had to focus intensely to achieve were merely residual phenomena for those at THE Second Scale.","What they could accomplish when they actually tried was obscene.","And with their access to Infinity, what they could alter existence to become defied comprehension. Not to mention the weapons that each of the three enemies before them held. Each weapon was a completed Axiom or half completed Axiom, relics that should have bloomed from THE First Cause itself.","By all means, everything here was stacked against him, but...","Noah was ready to face it all.","He floated forward, golden flames of Observable force burning around his form as he moved past Naldine and THE Primordial Paradox. His small figure approached the three monstrous entities arrayed before them. He addressed Naldine without looking back.","\"I will take on the big guy. You and Paradox here can worry about the tiny, lesser things behind him.\"","HUUM!","His words boomed across the destroyed battlefield with confidence!","Grimvault smiled brutally beneath that wolf skull helm, those pale fires in empty eye sockets flickering with amusement that seemed almost appreciative. Behind him, Vahrkosis and Sammarthiel frowned coldly at being designated as tiny and lesser things.","The serpentine mass’s forty-seven arms tightened their grips on weapons and artifacts. The elegant figure’s wings of swords spread wider.","Naldine looked at Noah calmly as her fingers continued dancing across the strings of her Vihuela.","A heavy melody of power emerged from the instrument, notes that pressed against reality with force that made the air itself thicken.","\"He is too powerful for you.\"","Her voice emerged as she continued producing.","\"A Calymmian Proterozoic Scale being. You cannot stand against him. I will face him.\"","Noah gazed forth coldly and tyrannically at the three enemies before them.","His eyes held none of the concern Naldine’s warning should have provoked. He observed Grimvault’s massive form, that blackened silver armor fused with flesh, that wolf skull helm blazing with pale fire, that greatsword drinking light from everything within range. He observed all of it and found himself unimpressed by what observation revealed!","This was merely a Bounded Lifeform like him!","\" Nah, I got him.\"","His voice emerged with certainty that refused to acknowledge the gap between their Scales.","\"I know...all about Grimvault here.\"","As he spoke those words, golden bubbles of light continued flowing from Grimvault’s armored form toward Noah’s position. THE Hadean Existential Singularities drifted through the space separating them with lazy purpose that belied their significance, each bubble containing concentrated essence of another being’s existence. They had been flowing since Noah designated Grimvault as his third target, and they continued flowing now with volume that increased as the distance between them decreased.","The bubbles disappeared into his body upon contact.","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed.|","|Source: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Category: Background Origin.|","|Content: Subject stems from a region of THE Wyld, a vast domain accessible through Prima Indifferentia that only Primordial Architects have access to. THE Wyld exists as a closed ecosystem of Proterozoic Scale cultivation, containing eons of Primordial Architect development, alliances, conflicts, and Civilizational evolution. Entry requires acknowledgment from existing inhabitants.|","|Additional Content: The section of THE Wyld that Grimvault stems from operates under hierarchy established by THE Deliverance, an entity of unknown classification whose authority is absolute within that region. Disobedience against THE Deliverance is not punished. Disobedience is unmade.|","...!","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed.|","|Source: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Category: THE Deliverance - Entity Profile.|","|Content: THE Deliverance is not a Primordial Architect. THE Deliverance is not a Singular Cognizance. Classification remains unknown even to those who serve it. Entity predates most inhabitants of THE Wyld and may predate THE Wyld itself. Entity does not speak. Entity does not appear. Entity communicates through directives that manifest within the awareness of those it addresses, commands that feel like memories of actions already taken rather than instructions for future behavior.|","|Additional Content: Primordial Architects who receive directives from THE Deliverance describe the experience as having already obeyed before understanding what obedience required. Resistance is theoretically possible.|","...!","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed.|","|Source: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Category: Psychological Profile - The Cleansing.|","|Content: Subject was tasked by THE Deliverance with cleansing Primordial Architects who held mindsets incompatible with the controlled region of THE Wyld’s current direction. Target list included Naldine THE Visionary, Aryana THE Harmonious, and fourteen others who advocated for useless expansions beyond THE Wyld’s borders and alliance with entities outside Primordial Architects.|","|Execution Details: Subject isolated targets individually over span of three hundred years. Subject tortured each target extensively before collapse, applying Chaos Tongue abilities to stretch moments of agony into spans that exceeded what even Proterozoic existences were designed to endure. Subject consumed Proterozoic Bones and Organs of each victim after torture concluded, integrating their power into his own foundations.|","|Victim Count: Twelve of sixteen targets successfully cleansed. Aryana THE Harmonious was seventh. Her torture spanned forty-seven objective years. Her screams were silenced through removal of her throat before consumption of her vocal Proterozoic Organ.|","|Remaining Targets: Naldine THE Visionary escaped THE Wyld before cleansing could commence. Three others remain unaccounted for.|","...!","| Hadean Existential Singularity Absorbed. |","|Source: Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence.|","|Category: Current Motivation.|","|Content: Subject desires to consume Infinity-enhanced Proterozoic material. Subject believes integration of such material will elevate him beyond Calymmian Tier. Saving Beowulf is a minor matter.|","|Subject views this confrontation as harvest rather than combat.|","...!","Noah digested all the new information as it flooded into his awareness.","THE Wyld. THE Deliverance. A closed ecosystem of Primordial Architects operating under authority that unmade disobedience without transition. Grimvault had tortured and consumed twelve of his own kind on orders that permitted quick elimination but did not require it!","He had chosen cruelty when efficiency would have sufficed. He had stretched moments into spans of agony for no purpose beyond personal satisfaction just like Beowulf.","And he had done it to someone Naldine cared about.","Noah floated ever closer toward Grimvault, his small form approaching that massive armored entity. The golden flames of Observable force burning around him intensified with each meter of distance closed, his presence pressing against Grimvault’s authority with defiance that should not have been possible from someone at THE First Scale.","\" Why are so many of you Primordial Architects sadistic and cruel?\"","His voice emerged with genuine curiosity wrapped in condemnation.","\" Does living for too long naturally make you like so?\"","He paused, his eyes meeting the pale fires burning in Grimvault’s empty sockets.","\" You did not have to torture poor Aryana like that, Grimvault. Especially when THE Deliverance just ordered you to do a quick cleansing of opposition Primordial Architects.\"","...!","BOOM!","His words landed across the destroyed battlefield with impact.","Grimvault looked over to Noah heavily, those pale fires in his wolf skull helm freezing entirely for an instant that seemed to stretch toward infinity. The brutal amusement that had colored his expression since arriving vanished, replaced by something that might have been shock if beings at his Scale were still capable of being shocked.","Naldine’s eyes became sharp as she observed the same thing.","Her fingers paused on the strings of her Vihuela, the melody she had been producing faltering for the first time since she began playing. Her singularity-dotted gaze fixed upon Noah with intensity that demanded explanation.","Both of their eyes asked the same question.","How the hell did he know about the things he just spoke of?"]},{"number":5078,"title":"Chapter 5078: Chapter 5077: The Silurian Light I","paragraphs":["Grimvault looked at Noah coldly.","The pale fires burning in that wolf skull helm had ceased their flickering, holding steady with intensity. Whatever shock Noah’s words had provoked, the Primordial Architect had processed it and moved beyond. Ancient beings did not linger on surprises. They adapted and continued.","\" We have always known the one who bears Infinity so freely is capable.\"","His deep voice pressed against everything within range with authority that made the air itself thicken.","\" You being able to perceive information like this is certainly unique.\"","Those pale fires studied Noah’s form.","\" Are you similar to that other anomaly, Erwin? We have also grasped him to have something to do with information.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply at those words.","They had found out about Erwin as THE Information Paradox?","Grimvault held his Axiom weapon loosely in one massive gauntlet, that greatsword of light-drinking metal resting against the destroyed air as if it weighed nothing despite its colossal size. He smiled brutally beneath that wolf skull helm before nodding toward Naldine with acknowledgment that held mockery beneath its apparent respect.","\" Do you know why THE Whorish Naldine does not wish for you to fight me?\"","The designation made Naldine’s fingers pause on her strings for a fraction of an instant.","\" Apart from the obvious discrepancy in power you may potentially be able to make up with Infinity ever so briefly.\"","He stepped forward, his massive armored form moving with grace that contradicted its size.","\" The reason is the power that true Proterozoic Scale entities hold. Not those merely at Rhyacian, scratching at the surface of what advancement actually means. You see, once you continue up this Scale of Existence enough, grasp some tidbits of Infinity and the force of nature that is Observable, have a decent number of Proterozoic Bones, and you begin to truly become in tune with existence itself, you can begin to grasp something greater.\"","His pale fires burned brighter as he spoke.","\" THE Pulse of The Scales.\"","BOOM!","Grimvault raised his arms upward as if he were a priest distilling grand knowledge to congregations that had gathered to receive wisdom from mouths they could not comprehend. His blackened silver armor caught the multicolored light of the surrounding storm, that fused flesh and metal seeming almost beautiful in the illumination despite the horror of its composition.","\" Capabilities that distinguish you from all other lesser things ,\" he continued with voice that pressed against reality with force that made the suspended rain droplets tremble. \" Pulses that only those who have achieved true distinction within THE Second Scale can perceive, let alone utilize. There are many such Pulses scattered across the methodologies of Proterozoic advancement, scattered across Existence...but one stands above most others in its significance.\"","His wolf skull helm tilted slightly.","\" One Pulse that nearly every knowledgeable Proterozoic Scale entity seeks to learn is known to us as THE Silurian Light.\"","The words landed with impact!","\" Named after THE Silurian Cause, a fiery type of First Cause capable of forming an Observable Existence in its entirety. Even I do not understand the true intricacies of what THE Silurian Cause actually is or was. Some believe it predates THE First Cause that formed our Observable Existence. Others believe it exists parallel to all First Causes, a template from which creation itself learned how to create.\"","He lowered his arms slowly.","\" What matters is that those who grasp THE Pulse of The Scales deeply enough can learn to channel a fraction of that primordial fire. A fraction that, when applied correctly, does not merely kill.\"","His pale fires seemed to dim as he spoke the next words.","\" It erases.\"","...!","\" THE Silurian Light does not simply end an existence ,\" Grimvault continued, his voice taking on the cadence of one who had delivered this explanation before, who had watched the faces of those he explained it to shift from confusion to horror to despair. \" It unravels causality itself. When someone is consumed by this Pulse, their entire causality within the weavings of existence is pulled free, and everything that causality touched comes undone.\"","He began pacing slowly before them, that massive armored form moving with deliberation as if he was savoring this moment.","\" Consider what that means. Every action the erased being ever took ceases to have occurred. Every choice they made unmakes itself. Every consequence that flowed from their existence reverberates backward through time and probability, collapsing into configurations that exclude their participation entirely.\"","His wolf skull helm oriented toward Noah directly.","\"If you were to kill someone, and then I were to erase you with THE Silurian Light, that death would reverse. The being you killed would simply exist again, their murder having never occurred because the murderer was unraveled from the causality that permitted the act. Their wounds would close. Their breath would return. Their existence would resume as if your blade had never fallen.\"","\"So Beowulf here...you could kill and collapse him now. But after I erase you, that action would be invalidated as even without doing anything more, Beowulf would return afterwards.\"","The implications pressed against Noah’s awareness.","\" The proficiency with which one wields THE Silurian Light determines the scope of this unraveling ,\" Grimvault explained further, his voice carrying pride that seemed almost scholarly despite the subject matter. \" Those who have only begun to grasp this Pulse can erase beings and undo perhaps minutes of their actions. The immediate consequences reverse, but deeper causalities remain intact.\"","He held up one gauntleted hand.","\" Those who have cultivated greater proficiency can undo months and years of accumulated action. Entire campaigns of warfare unmade. Alliances that took years to forge simply never forming because the one who forged them was erased before the thought occurred to them.\"","A second gauntleted hand rose.","\" And those who have truly mastered THE Silurian Light, who have made this Pulse an extension of their Civilization itself, can enact truly extensive Retroactive Reversal. Years of accumulated causality unraveled. Perhaps millions and billions. Perhaps more, depending on the significance of the erased existence and the power of the one doing the erasing.\"","...!"]},{"number":5079,"title":"Chapter 5079: Chapter 5078: The Silurian Light II","paragraphs":["His arms spread wide.","\"But even that is not the full extent of what this Pulse permits. With sufficient power and precision, one can target not merely actions but the Civilization that enabled those actions. Everything that Civilization stood for, every principle it embodied, every change it wrought upon existence through its expression, all of it can be unmade. The framework that supported a being’s power collapses, and everything built upon that framework collapses with it.\"","His voice dropped lower.","\" And if one is killed thoroughly enough with THE Silurian Light, if the erasure is complete and absolute, then something even more terrible occurs.\"","He paused for effect that seemed almost theatrical.","\"Your entire existence becomes forgotten. Those who knew you find that they cannot recall your face. Those who loved you discover that love directed toward emptiness they cannot explain. Those who hated you find their hatred dissolved into confusion about what, exactly, they were hating.\"","His pale fires burned with intensity that exceeded anything they had displayed before.","\" Only the one who erased you remembers. Only the wielder of THE Silurian Light retains knowledge of what was unmade. They become the sole repository of your existence, the only being in all of Observable Existence who knows that you ever were.\"","He smiled beneath that wolf skull helm.","\"That is the power that true Proterozoic Scale entities can wield. That is why your Naldine does not wish for you to face me. Not because I might kill you. Because I might erase you so thoroughly that even your precious Infinity cannot recall what it once flowed through.\"","...!","BOOM!","After Grimvault finished echoing out such terrifying words, Noah and THE Primordial Paradox looked over with somber eyes.","Naldine grasped her instrument tightly, her fingers pressing against strings that had ceased producing sound. Her expression declared that everything Grimvault had described was true, that this was not intimidation but simple statement of capability he possessed and would use without hesitation.","Noah processed the implications with the enhanced clarity THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation from Ozymandias provided.","Everything he had done erased. The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity reversed, those transformed seas and falling rains simply ceasing to exist because the one who created them had been unraveled from causality. THE Infiniverse returned to whatever state it had occupied before he touched it, all those Civilizational advancements unmade, all those bodies he had cultivated dissolved into potential that had never been actualized.","His connection with Eon severed retroactively, that Quintessence Infiniforce bond never forming because he had never existed to place it within her. The Observable force flooding into him ceasing to flow because there was no him for it to flow into.","Eon...she should be capable of something like this, but she never threatened to do this. Why?","Many things would unfold!","Alexander still tortured and still broken.","THE Primordial Mycelia still alive, still spreading, still consuming everything it touched because the one who stopped it had been unmade before the stopping could occur.","Everything he had accomplished across his journey through Observable Existence simply gone, unraveled, forgotten by all except the one who held the fire that burned away causality itself.","It was a truly terrifying capability.","After the terrifying words of Grimvault, Noah gazed up at him fearlessly.","His expression held none of the concern that THE Silurian Light should have provoked. He had just been told that his entire existence could be unraveled, that everything he had accomplished across Observable Existence could be undone as if he had never existed to accomplish it. Yet his eyes remained steady, his posture remained composed, his presence continued pressing against Grimvault’s authority with defiance that refused to acknowledge the gap between their capabilities.","\" So... theoretically, if you were burnt and collapsed with THE Silurian Light, even that Aryana I have never met and all others you collapsed before would return as if you never existed to do that in the first place?\"","...!","His reply was a ridiculous one.","Grimvault smiled brutally beneath that wolf skull helm, those pale fires flickering with amusement that seemed almost appreciative of the audacity being displayed before him. The question Noah had asked was not born from fear or desperation. It was calculation!","He looked between Noah and Naldine with gaze that held mockery beneath its apparent consideration.","\"It is something you cannot defend against.\"","His deep voice pressed against everything within range.","\" To do so, you would need another Pulse. As much as I would have no issue utilizing such a thing on you, there are still many unknowns and uncertainties about you. Unraveling you with THE Silurian Light could have many unexpected effects, with changes occurring throughout Observable Existence that even I cannot predict.\"","He paused, those pale fires dimming slightly.","\" So I have caution within me. But it does not mean I will not throw this caution to the wind and do what I must if push comes to shove.\"","His wolf skull helm tilted forward.","\" This is your last chance of Diplomacy. The one whose name you spoke of has not spoken of you just yet, and I would rather wait for directives before making permanent moves myself.\"","His smile widened beneath that helm as he spoke the final words with deliberate slowness that seemed designed to antagonize.","\"What. Will. It. Be...Little Bundle...\"","The mockery pressed against Noah’s awareness.","\"Of.\"","Each word landing like a blow intended to provoke!","\"Infinity?\"","...!","Little Bundle of Infinity!","Oh!","The final sentence was mocking and cruel, every syllable uttered slowly alongside Grimvault’s brutal smile. It was meant to antagonize, to remind Noah of what he was in the eyes of beings who had existed since before most current powers learned to crawl. A little bundle. A curiosity. Something to be studied and perhaps unmade if it proved too troublesome to preserve.","Off to the side, THE Primordial Paradox rolled up his nonexistent sleeves as he if was ready to throw down!","Who did this fucker think he was?!"]},{"number":5080,"title":"Chapter 5080: Chapter 5079: The Silurian Light III","paragraphs":["And at such a time, Noah actually turned his gaze behind him.","He locked eyes with Naldine, observing her expression shift. Her fingers remained poised over the strings of her Vihuela. Her singularity-dotted eyes held intensity that demanded he choose wisely.","\" The next few seconds are going to be very critical ones.\"","HUUM!","His calm words were an answer, though not the answer anyone present had expected.","He could have chosen to say many things. He could have accepted the diplomacy Grimvault offered, could have released Beowulf and retreated to fight another day, could have recognized that three Proterozoic Scale entities including one at the Calymmian Tier represented a threat he could not overcome regardless of his Infinity.","He chose none of those options.","Behind him, a shimmering golden crack of existence bloomed into being.","The crack appeared in the fabric of reality itself, multicolored light bleeding through the fracture. Massive hands appeared at the edges of that crack, fingers the size of buildings grasping the boundaries of the opening. Those hands tore the crack wide, ripping existence apart to create space sufficient for what was coming through.","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization: External release activated.|","|Entity: Ozymandias.|","|Source: THE Hadean Desmoterion.|","|Status: Emerging into Observable Existence.|","An utter wonder stepped out.","Ozymandias emerged from the golden crack with presence that pressed against everything within range. His form was titanic, a humanoid configuration of muscle and authority that dwarfed even Grimvault’s massive armored frame. His skin held the same complexion as Noah’s, stretched over musculature that had been cultivated across Civilizational Eons of Development. His features bore resemblance to Noah’s own, the same bone structure, the same set of the jaw, the same shape of the eyes, though scaled to proportions that made the similarity somewhat unsettling.","He floated inches away from Noah’s body, their two faces being somewhat alike in ways that declared their connection without requiring explanation.","|Entity Released: Ozymandias.|","|Classification: THE Hadean Avatar.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Rhyacian Tier.|","|Proterozoic Bones: THE Hadean Limb of Infinite Hunger (right leg, complete). THE Hadean Arm of Infinite Reach (right arm, complete). THE Hadean Skull of Infinite Perception (skull, complete).|","|Proterozoic Organ: THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation (brain, complete).|","|Active Duration Outside THE Hadean Desmoterion: 81 seconds.|","|Note: Duration increased from 9 seconds due to influx of Observable force from Gilded Existence. Connection to THE Secretive Eon has enhanced all Hadean parameters.|","The aura of a thick and heavy Second Scale permeated across the body of Ozymandias.","It pressed against everything within range with authority that declared his classification to all who could perceive it. His Proterozoic Bones radiated light that shone through his flesh, his right leg blazing gold, his right arm matching that brilliance, his skull illuminating from within with intensity that painted nearby space in hues of multicolored authority. And beyond those bones, his Proterozoic Organ pulsed with power that exceeded what most Second Scale entities possessed.","THE Primordial Paradox observed this emergence with expression that shifted through shock into assessment. His obsidian titanic form, which had seemed massive beside Noah’s humanoid body, now stood comparable to Ozymandias’s frame. Another Second Scale entity had just appeared on their side of this confrontation!","Naldine’s fingers paused on her strings as she processed what she was witnessing. Her singularity-dotted eyes widened slightly before returning to their normal configuration. She had known Noah possessed capabilities beyond what he displayed, but this was beyond what she had anticipated. He had been concealing a Second Scale entity within his existence!","Behind them, Beowulf’s screams paused for an instant as even that tortured Primordial Architect perceived the shift in the battlefield’s dynamics. Alexander continued his work, but his eyes flickered toward the newly emerged titan.","Grimvault, Sammarthiel, and Vahrkosis observed Ozymandias with coldness. Three Scale 2s against two had become three against three, with one of the new arrivals radiating Proterozoic authority that declared him a genuine threat.","Noah’s eyes were unfathomably bright at this time.","The muscular visage of Ozymandias roared grandly toward Grimvault, that titan’s voice emerging with force that pressed against the destroyed battlefield with a challenge that could not be ignored. His massive chest expanded as he drew breath that should not have been necessary for a being at his classification, and then he released everything he had been containing.","His head illuminated with terrifying light.","THE Hadean Skull of Infinite Perception blazed with multicolored brilliance that pressed outward from Ozymandias’s form in expanding waves. The light washed over everything within range, painting Grimvault and his companions, painting Naldine and THE Primordial Paradox, painting the destroyed battlefield and the suspended rain and the screaming figure of Beowulf.","And then something impossible occurred.","|Proterozoic Organ Activation: THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation.|","|Ability: Infinite Temporal Perception.|","|Effect: User’s perception of time becomes infinitely malleable. Instants can be stretched to feel like days, months, or years according to user’s will. This is perception only and does not affect external reality. Others continue to move at normal speed while user experiences expanded awareness.|","|Duration: Determined by user. Can be maintained indefinitely within active period outside THE Hadean Desmoterion.|","|Note: This ability affects Noah Osmont through connection to Ozymandias. Both entities share expanded perception while ability is active.|","|Current Perception State: One instant stretched toward infinity.|","Everything seemed to freeze!","Grimvault’s brutal smile remained fixed in place, those pale fires in his wolf skull helm suspended mid-flicker. Sammarthiel’s wings of swords hung motionless, thousands of blades neither rising nor falling. Vahrkosis’s serpentine coils had ceased their undulation, forty-seven arms frozen in positions that suggested readiness for violence that would not arrive until perception returned to normal speed.","The multicolored rain hung suspended in the air around them!","The screams of Beowulf had paused mid-sound, that note of agony stretched into silence that would resume when infinity concluded!","Noah observed this frozen landscape, this moment stretched beyond what moments were designed to contain. He sighed with breath that felt like it could last for centuries if he wished it to.","In his perception, he had days or months if he wished in this span of an infinity. Even though he did not freeze anyone or anything, even though external reality continued at its normal pace, he could experience this single instant as an eternity of contemplation.","But such a space was not meant for rest.","\" Hey.\"","His voice emerged within this stretched moment, audible only to himself and those he chose to include.","\" You say you are here to be by my side and help me so that the Splintering of Observable Existence does not occur, but why keep such good material like THE Pulse of The Scales away from me?\"","...!"]},{"number":5081,"title":"Chapter 5081: Chapter 5080: The Silurian Light IV","paragraphs":["He turned to look at Naldine directly.","\" That is something I would really like to know.\"","He extended multicolored light toward her form, his authority reaching out to include her awareness within this expanded perception. Her eyes gained cognizance as she was pulled into this moment stretched toward infinity, her frozen expression shifting into animation as she processed what had just occurred.","She observed the landscape around them, observed Grimvault’s smile suspended in brutal configuration, observed everything held in stillness while the two of them moved freely through perception that had been extended beyond normal parameters.","\" Hey.\"","Noah’s voice emerged again, this time directed entirely at her.","\" You know about this Silurian Light, yes? We have a moment stretching out toward infinity here.\"","His eyes held hers with intensity that refused to acknowledge impossibility.","\" Teach it to me.\"","...!","Naldine looked at him as if he were insane.","She observed the frozen landscape that was really their perception, observed Grimvault’s massive form suspended mid-mockery, observed everything that should have been moving held in stillness by an ability she had not known Noah possessed.","\" Such a thing is impossible.\"","Her voice emerged with frustration that pressed against the stillness surrounding them.","\" To even sense THE Pulses of The Scales, Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entities have the immensity of existence. The number of Bones, Organs, and development of their Civilizations. You cannot even perceive the Pulses, much less try to utilize one.\"","She stepped closer to him within this frozen moment.","\"I did not tell you because it would hold no meaning to you. I did not think you would seek conflict and adversity to come across any Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity so soon. I expected to have time with you and introduce everything else to you properly.\"","Her extraordinary visage maintained its imperious allure, but she showed her frustration at this time openly.","\" But you will not fucking sit still!\"","...!","Noah remained looking at her calmly as she vented frustrations that had apparently been building since she first encountered him.","His expression held none of the contrition her words should have provoked. He had brought this situation upon himself through choices that prioritized advancement over safety, through decisions that drew enemies who possessed capabilities he could not match. He had known what he was doing. He had done it anyway!","And now he required tools to survive what he had provoked.","His voice emerged with certainty that refused to acknowledge the impossibility she had described.","\" Teach. Me.\"","...!","---","<An Unfathomable Distance Away>","The corpses were gone.","Where three Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects had once lain in configurations of death around THE Creature’s throne, only bloodstains remained. The armored scales of Horus had been consumed. The script-covered flesh of the second had been devoured. The elegant form of the third had been absorbed into foundations that continued growing despite having surpassed what most beings could comprehend.","THE Creature sat in the same position he had occupied throughout his feast, but his body now buzzed with resplendent multicolored brilliance that pressed outward against everything within range. The flames surrounding his form burned brighter than before, fed by Proterozoic Bones and Organs that had been broken down into their constituent authorities and integrated into his existence. Every cell of his being radiated power that made the darkness of this domain seem insufficient to contain him.","He had consumed three Second Scale entities in their entirety.","He had added their strength to his own.","And he remained hungry.","Even though Grimvault had dispersed the illusory screens across Observable Existence to prevent knowledge of what was occurring in that distant battle in THE Wastes, this domain between Observable and Unobservable operated according to different rules. A multicolored illusory screen continued floating before THE Creature’s position, displaying everything with clarity that the Calymmian Primordial Architect’s authority could not interfere with.","THE Creature observed it all.","And he had listened to everything Grimvault said about THE Pulse of The Scales.","His deep voice echoed out across the bloody domain with power that made the pooled fluids around him ripple despite the absence of physical force.","\" THE Silurian Light.\"","The words emerged as statement rather than question.","He raised his right hand brutally.","There, flickering above his palm, a flame manifested with colors that should not have been capable of existing simultaneously. It burned with hues that contradicted each other, configurations of light that pressed against perception with wrongness. The flame was small, perhaps the size of a fist, but its presence dominated the entire domain with authority that declared what it was capable of accomplishing.","This was not mere fire.","This was causality made visible!","This was the power to unmake existence so thoroughly that even memory of that existence would cease to persist!","Anaximander, who had been observing the illusory screen with scholarly interest, pulled back instinctively the moment that flame appeared. His pristine robes shifted as he created distance between himself and THE Creature, his normally calm expression flickering into something approaching genuine concern. Even someone who had stood in the presence of THE Creature’s barbarity, who had observed him consume three Proterozoic Scale entities without flinching, found himself unable to remain still before THE Silurian Light.","He looked at the flame cautiously, observing how it burned without consuming, how it illuminated without providing comfort, how it existed as promise of annihilation rather than mere destruction.","\"I want to go help him.\"","His voice emerged measured despite the tension visible in his posture.","\"But I already know what you will say. Adversity, adversity. Blah, blah, blah.\"","THE Creature smiled grandly at those words.","Laughter emerged from his blood-stained lips, the sound booming across the domain with genuine amusement that seemed almost warm despite the horror surrounding its source. The flame above his palm flickered in response to his mirth, those impossible colors dancing.","\" Come on, Jokul.\"","He closed his fist, extinguishing THE Silurian Light as casually as one might snuff a candle.","\"It is time for me to make my return to THE Wyld.\"","\" There is so much to be done.\"","He rose from his position atop the bloodstains where corpses had once lain, his multicolored flames expanding around his form as he moved for the first time since his feast began.","\" Tairiyya will join us along the way.\"","BOOM!","THE Creature’s fist smashed forward into the region ahead of him with force that should not have been possible to generate from standing position. The blow did not strike anything physical. It struck existence itself, that fabric of reality which separated this domain from whatever lay beyond.","Existence Splintered.","Cracks spread outward from the point of impact in configurations that resembled shattered glass, fractures in the very foundation of this space between Observable and Unobservable. Through those cracks, light bled in from somewhere else, illumination that carried authority unlike anything the current Observable Existence contained.","THE Wyld awaited, and THE Creature was preparing to return!"]},{"number":5082,"title":"Chapter 5082: Chapter 5081: Knowledge and Access I","paragraphs":["Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these epochs, Infinity reigns supreme.","---","Golden rivers flowed in every direction, dense currents of Observable force moving through this domain with purpose that required no external guidance.","THE Secretive Eon sat within these rivers, her form surrounded by brilliance that would have overwhelmed any Bounded existence foolish enough to enter this space. Her knees were drawn up to her chest, arms wrapped around them. Her golden eyes, still bearing the permanent alterations from her unsealing, observed an illusory screen floating before her position.","The screen displayed Grimvault and Noah and the confrontation unfolding in that distant region of THE Wastes.","She watched as Grimvault explained THE Silurian Light with theatrical grandeur. She observed Noah’s expression remain steady despite learning that his entire existence could be unmade.","Her expression held sadness that seemed inappropriate for someone of her classification.","\" THE Bounded do not know,\" she said softly, speaking to no one but herself, \" how simple can sometimes be so sublime.\"","The golden rivers around her shifted in response to her voice, currents adjusting to accommodate the melancholy she was expressing.","\" When you start to reach higher, you realize how every single one of you cannot access even more than a percent of what your existence represents. What your Civilization represents.\"","She rested her chin upon her knees, watching Grimvault’s brutal smile.","\" You will build Proterozoic Bone and Organs and so much more, just to try to unlock a percentage more of existence. You struggle and consume and cultivate across eons, believing that sufficient power will eventually grant you access to depths you cannot currently perceive.\"","Her golden eyes dimmed slightly.","\" And you would not understand how others are at a whole different starting point entirely.\"","The rivers of Observable force swirled around her form with gentleness that contradicted their immense density.","\"For THE Bounded, Civilizational Access is a wall that must be climbed with bleeding fingers, one fraction of a percent at a time. You fight and die and devour each other for gains so small they would be invisible to those who measure power in different currencies.\"","She sighed, the sound carrying across the golden domain.","\" Accessing a Pulse alone can feel insurmountable for them. THE Silurian Light exists at five percent access, and most will never touch five percent no matter how many eons they dedicate to the pursuit. They will die believing themselves powerful while perceiving less than a twentieth of what their Civilizations actually contain.\"","Her arms tightened around her knees.","\" For THE Gilded, it is natural. We do not climb walls. We simply perceive, and what we perceive, we can access. THE Pulses of The Scales are not hidden from us behind barriers of insufficient transformation. They are simply there, waiting to be used, as obvious as breathing is to those who possess lungs.\"","She watched Noah’s form on the screen, surrounded by golden flames of Observable force that flowed through the connection she could not sever.","\" And yet you persist. You struggle. You refuse to accept the ceilings that were engineered into your existence before you were even born.\"","Her voice softened further.","\" Perhaps that is what makes simple so sublime. Perhaps that is what I wanted to understand when I sealed myself and for all those eons.\"","She fell silent, watching the frozen confrontation with expression that held emotions too complex to name.","\" Ahh, but understanding changes nothing. You are still Bounded. I am still Gilded. And the distance between us is not measured in power but in fundamental nature that no amount of Infinity can truly bridge. No amount of-...!\"","\" After going missing for eons, what has you so sentimental?\"","BOOM!","Her words were stopped as another voice echoed out behind her!","The golden rivers throughout the domain surged toward the source of that voice with eagerness that declared recognition of something they had been waiting to encounter.","\" What makes those little things over there special for you to pay attention to?\"","Eon’s gaze flickered as her back straightened instantly. The melancholy that had softened her features vanished, replaced by sharpness and imperious bearing that declared her true nature to anyone capable of perceiving it. Her golden eyes became cutting as she turned around to see who had arrived.","The entity standing behind her was supremely grand.","His eyes were golden like hers, but they held no pupils, no irises, nothing but solid expanses of Observable brilliance that seemed to contain depths extending beyond what normal perception could measure. His skin was fair, luminous with inner light that suggested he was less a being of flesh and more a concentration of Observable force that had chosen to wear humanoid form.","His robes were clean and white, pristine in configurations that seemed incapable of accepting stain or imperfection. They moved around his tall frame with grace that stated the fabric itself was pleased to drape across his shoulders.","The moment he arrived, all the rivers of Observable force throughout the domain abandoned their previous currents and rushed toward him. They converged upon his form with eagerness, golden light pressing against his existence as if desperate to be absorbed, to be used, to be anything he required it to be.","His facial features were unfathomably handsome, proportions that existed beyond what natural processes could produce. High cheekbones. A strong jaw. Lips curved into a light smile that held warmth beneath its apparent amusement. Hair the color of spun gold fell past his shoulders in waves.","He looked toward Eon with an expression that held familiarity, fondness, and maybe concern beneath its casual presentation.","Eon nodded toward this being.","\" Brother.\"","She paused, observing how his expression shifted at the term.","\"It has been some time. Oh, I apologize. I forgot you hated to be called that.\"","Her voice took on formal cadence that seemed to emerge naturally when addressing him.","\" Ubergulden Dietrich, it has been some time.\"","...!","She rose from her seated position and gave a mock bow toward the appearing entity, the gesture holding mockery beneath its apparent respect. Her movements were precise and deliberate, the actions of someone who had performed this ritual countless times across spans that most existences could not comprehend.","Ubergulden Dietrich laughed at her performance.","The sound was warm and genuine. He floated across the golden domain toward her, Observable force parting around his passage like water around the prow of a ship. When he reached her, he extended one hand and patted her head with a gesture that seemed entirely inappropriate given the power both of them radiated.","\" Little Sister.\"","His voice emerged with a heavy and thick accent as if he was speaking a second tongue.","\" Mein Schwesterherz...Ubergulden Adelheid, did you miss me?\"","His golden eyes, pupilless and vast, studied her expression with attention that seemed to perceive more than she wished to reveal.","\" And these Tethered you are watching, are they special to you? I have not seen you talk about the woes of THE Bounded while gazing at them before.\"","He gestured toward the illusory screen still displaying Noah and Grimvault.","\" We and them stem from different coins of existence entirely, after all. What concern is it of ours how much they struggle to perceive what we perceive naturally?\"","...!","Eon’s eyes flashed coldly at his questions.","\"I have been browsing through the unfolding weavings of existence in the lands of THE Bounded while waiting for you.\"","Her voice now emerged with the same cadence that colored his speech.","\" There is much occurring that bears observation.\"","As she said this, she waved her hand with a gesture that seemed almost dismissive.","Multiple illusory screens appeared throughout the golden domain, each one displaying different scenes from across Observable Existence. Some showed Primordial Architects cultivating in isolation, their forms surrounded by Proterozoic light as they struggled toward advancements that might never come. Others showed Undivided Ones moving through Primordial Realms, their stellar forms pursuing purposes that most could not perceive.","One screen showed Abaddon being led by Chaos Giants across transformed seas, his listless form carried like a fallen king toward destinations unknown.","Many screens showed countless beings, a panorama of Bounded existence unfolding in configurations.","Uniquely, nothing relating to THE Creature appeared among the displays.","No screen showed his domain between Observable and Unobservable. No screen showed his flames or his feast or his declaration of returning to THE Wyld.","Eon’s eyes flickered through all of this as she concluded her explanation.","\" Let us go then.\"","Her voice held finality that made it clear the conversation was over.","Ubergulden Dietrich smiled and nodded with accommodation that seemed almost too easy.","\" Of course, after you.\"","He gestured toward pathways through the Observable force that only those of their classification could perceive.","\"It has been so long that the others are very curious about you. So many questions they have. So much they wish to know about where you have been, what you have done, why you sealed yourself away for eons among those who could never understand what you truly are.\"","His smile widened slightly.","\" Go on, Little Sister. I will follow.\"","Eon’s figure shimmered as she stepped into the rivers of Observable force surrounding them.","The golden currents embraced her form, pulling her into pathways that led toward wherever THE Gilded resided. Her presence dissolved into the brilliance, her physical form becoming indistinguishable from the force she was traveling through.","She disappeared.","Ubergulden Dietrich watched her departure with smile that remained fixed upon his handsome features.","As she left, he turned around.","His pupilless golden eyes ignored all the screens Eon had conjured, passing over the Primordial Architects and Undivided Ones and Chaos Giants without acknowledgment. He did not spare a glance for Abaddon’s listless form or the countless other beings displayed throughout.","He focused solely on one screen.","The screen holding Grimvault and Noah and the confrontation that had captured his sister’s attention before he arrived.","His smile shifted into something that held knowing beneath its apparent warmth.","\" Did you forget, Sister?\"","His voice emerged soft, almost gentle, carrying affection that somehow made his words more unsettling.","\"I always knew when you were lying.\"","After he said these words, his eyes with no pupils flashed brilliantly.","The golden light that had been surrounding his form intensified, pressing outward against the domain before collapsing inward upon itself. The rivers of Observable force that had been rushing toward him followed, drawn into pathways that led toward the same destination his sister had departed toward.","Moments later, he also disappeared.","The domain fell empty, golden rivers resuming their aimless flow now that no Gilded presence remained to draw their attention.","Only the illusory screens persisted, displaying scenes that no one was watching anymore, and in time even they would fade."]},{"number":5083,"title":"Chapter 5083: Chapter 5082: Knowledge And Access II","paragraphs":["Noah gazed at Naldine as they remained within that Infinite Temporal Perception.","It was only their perception living in this moment of an instant stretched toward infinity, and the idea of such a thing alone was ridiculous. That at any point in time, he could stretch his perception of one instant into days, months, or even years. That he could exist within a single heartbeat for as long as he wished while the external world continued at its normal pace, unaware that those within this expanded awareness were experiencing spans that objective time could not measure.","So right now, even though the situation was perilous and the adversity was high, he basically did not have to worry about it for as long as he remained in this perception.","He could stretch his perception, which now included Naldine, for days if necessary. Weeks. Months. And whenever he ended it, things would continue unfolding as if the light that Ozymandias had released had only flashed for a brief instant and nothing else had occurred. Grimvault’s brutal smile would resume. The confrontation would continue. But Noah would have lived through whatever span of subjective time he required to prepare.","So at this time, as everything around them appeared frozen even though it was not, his perception and Naldine’s perception looked at each other across distances that had nothing to do with physical space.","It was as if their spirits had departed their bodies and their illusory perceptions were communicating in a realm that existed between moments rather than within them. Naldine’s form shimmered with the same blue gold brilliance her physical body radiated, though here it seemed softer, less aggressive, more contemplative. Her singularity-dotted eyes observed him.","\"You could do more of something like this.\"","Her voice emerged without sound, perception communicating with perception.","\" Of sitting down and not getting into any conflict. I could share with you all the knowledge that I know, and even though I still do not believe it will be possible for you, I will tell you all I know about THE Pulses of The Scales.\"","She gestured toward the frozen landscape surrounding them, toward Grimvault’s suspended smile and the motionless wings of swords and the serpentine coils held in stillness.","\" You are young and you have just begun on your path, while others have had millions or billions of years. It would not hurt you to take a few months or a few years before you invite adversity.\"","Noah smiled at such words.","Yes, he sought adversity. Yes, he deliberately provoked confrontations that should have ended him. Yes, he broadcast his actions across Observable Existence specifically to draw enemies who would force him to grow or die trying.","But he could also never only sit still.","He thought about why that was true, examining his own motivations with the clarity this expanded perception granted. There was always that healthy fear residing somewhere in his foundations, not the kind that made him shiver or go pale, but the practical awareness of a massive and undeniable boot that could descend from above at any moment. While he was just relaxing, while he was taking his time, while he was enjoying the peace that sitting still would provide, that boot could fall. And he would only be a minor tiny ant that would not be able to do anything to change his fate because he had been sitting around relaxing instead of growing.","THE Deliverance existed somewhere out there. That was a boot.","THE Primeval classification existed above THE Gilded. A massive set of boots.","Any one of these could decide to step on him. Any one of them could erase him while he was taking a few months or years to learn in comfort rather than under fire.","He realized he really could not sit still.","But a moment like this, where he was stretching an instant toward infinity, where his perception existed outside the flow of time that external threats operated within, he could relax in such a space for as long as he required. Here, within this expanded awareness, nothing could reach him. Nothing could interrupt. Nothing could crush him like an ant beneath a descending boot.","But because this was only perception, he would not be able to change anything regarding his Civilization or Existence. He could not cultivate here. He could not transform Proterozoic Bones or Hadean Bones. The only thing that would count was his mind, his understanding, his comprehension of concepts that might later be applied when perception returned to normal flow.","So he simply nodded to Naldine.","She sighed with a breath that existed only in perception rather than physical reality.","Then she began to speak slowly, methodically, with the patience of someone who understood they had as much time as they wanted within this stretched moment.","\" Okay, so to really understand Pulses, you have to know about the limitations all of us are trying to break.\"","As she spoke, her perception waved its hands through the frozen air around them. Illusory diagrams began to form, configurations of light that represented concepts too complex for words alone to convey.","The first diagram showed a Civilization as a sphere of infinite depth, with a small percentage at the surface illuminated while the vast majority remained dark and inaccessible.","\" Most existences at THE First Scale and THE Second Scale utilize less than one percent of what their Existence and Civilizations actually represent.\"","The diagram pulsed, that illuminated surface percentage seeming insignificant compared to the darkness it failed to touch.","\" This is not a limitation of power or cultivation. It is a limitation of perception, of comprehension, of the capacity to interface with the totality of what Existence contains.\"","She waved her hand again, and the diagram shifted to show a being establishing their Civilizational Anchor, threads of affirmation connecting to that infinite sphere.","\" When a being establishes their Civilizational Anchor through affirmations of self-knowledge, they are not creating something new. They are touching something that already exists, a framework of authority that extends infinitely in directions most minds cannot perceive.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes met his with intensity that demanded complete attention.","\" Consider what a Civilization actually is.\"","A new diagram formed, showing the Civilization of Armed Existence as an impossible construct containing multitudes beyond counting.","\" The Civilization of Armed Existence, for example, does not merely mean ’I am a weapon.’ It means connection to every concept of armament across all of Existence. Every blade ever forged. Every arrow ever loosed. Every fist ever thrown in anger. Every defensive posture, every offensive stance, every methodology of violence that has ever been conceived by any mind in any Observable or Unobservable realm.\"","The diagram expanded to show weapons beyond number, techniques beyond cataloguing, concepts of violence that had never been expressed.","\" All of it exists within that Civilization, waiting to be accessed by one who possesses the capacity to perceive it.\"","She gestured toward the frozen form of Beowulf, still anchored by nine spears while Alexander’s frozen hands remained positioned within his opened chest.","\" Beowulf, at his peak, accessed perhaps 0.7% of Armed Existence.\"","The diagram shifted to show Beowulf’s connection to his Civilization, that 0.7% illuminated while 99.3% remained in darkness he could not perceive.","\" He thought himself powerful. He thought his Proterozoic Bone and his hammer made him formidable among Second Scale entities. He could not comprehend that 99.3% of his own Civilization remained beyond his reach, concepts and capabilities and weavings that would have made his current power seem insignificant.\"","Noah observed this diagram with eyes that shone with understanding pressing against his awareness.","\" This is true for all Civilizations.\"","New diagrams formed rapidly, each one showing different Civilizations and the beings who accessed them.","\" The Civilization of Paradox contains every contradiction that has ever existed or could exist. THE Living Paradox, despite his eons of cultivation, accesses and utilizes less than 1% of what Paradox truly represents.\"","A diagram showed Erwin’s connection to Paradox, that 1% seeming even more insignificant given the infinite contradictions that remained unexplored.","\" The Civilization of Chaos encompasses every instance of disorder across all Existence. Abaddon, before losing his Claim, accessed approximately 0.2% of Chaos.\"","Another diagram, showing Abaddon’s former connection to Chaos, that 0.2% representing power that had seemed overwhelming while remaining a fraction of what Chaos actually contained.","She gestured toward Grimvault’s frozen form, that wolf skull helm suspended mid-mockery.","\" He is powerful by the standards of those who cannot perceive these depths. But he should only have a few percentages of acess, despite all his cultivation, despite all the eons he has dedicated to advancement.\"","The diagrams shifted to show what happened when access increased.","\" When one accesses more of their Civilization, more of their Existence, everything changes.\"","A progression appeared, showing how each percentage point transformed what was possible.","\" At one percent access, weavings that seemed impossible become merely difficult. At two percent, the nature of those weavings transforms entirely, revealing depths that sub-one-percent users cannot perceive. At three percent, entirely new categories of expression emerge.\"","Her expression became grave as she formed the next diagram.","\" THE Pulse of The Scales exists at approximately five percent Civilizational Access. 5% Absolute Existential Utility.\"","The diagram showed that five percent threshold, a line that most beings would never cross regardless of how much power they accumulated.","\" This is why it remains beyond the reach of most Proterozoic Scale entities. Because they cannot perceive deeply enough into their own Existence to find where THE Pulses reside, waiting to be channeled by those who can access what most cannot imagine.\"","She paused, letting the implications settle across Noah’s expanded awareness.","\" THE Silurian Light is not learned.\"","Her voice emerged with emphasis that pressed against his perception.","\" It is found.\"","The final diagram showed THE Silurian Light as a thread existing within Existence, connecting to THE Silurian Cause that had formed Observable Existences across the vastness of reality.","\"It exists, a thread connecting to THE Silurian Cause that formed Observable Existences across the vastness of reality. But finding that thread requires perception that sub-one-percent access cannot provide.\""]},{"number":5084,"title":"Chapter 5084: Chapter 5083: Knowledge And Access III","paragraphs":["After her extensive explanation, Noah thought about everything Naldine had said.","Civilizational Access. Existential Utility.","The more he considered this concept, the more it appeared to be something other than a natural limitation. This was not like the gap between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale, which could be crossed through sufficient cultivation and methodology. This was not like the difficulty of forming a Civilizational Anchor, which demanded self-knowledge but rewarded those who achieved it.","This seemed like a limitation specifically designed for THE Bounded.","He thought about Eon’s words regarding Existential Designations. THE Bounded were engineered with ceilings they could not perceive, limitations they believed were personal failures rather than deliberate constraints.","What if Civilizational Access was one of those ceilings? What if the reason most beings could not access more than one percent of their Existence was not because such access was inherently difficult, but because they had been engineered to be incapable of it?","Naldine continued speaking as his thoughts churned.","\" So the biggest hurdle for you that stops you at the gate is just that.\"","Her perception waved one hand, and the diagrams around them shifted to focus on his own existence, showing the vast darkness of unexplored Civilizational depth that remained beyond his current reach.","\" You do not really have the access. Not grand enough. Not big enough. You still need to get bigger.\"","His eyes flashed sharply as he looked at her.","She did not flinch at his gaze, continuing with methodical precision.","\" But after all that, let me tell you the specific requirements for THE Silurian Light.\"","New diagrams formed around them, each one illustrating a different requirement with clarity.","\" First, the Proterozoic Saturation Threshold. You require eighty-five percent or more of your skeletal structure transformed into Proterozoic Bone.\"","The diagram showed a skeletal system with most bones blazing with multicolored light while a small percentage remained dark and untransformed.","\" Each transformed bone serves as a receptor for deeper Civilizational perception. The more receptors you possess, the more of your Civilization becomes perceivable. The more you can perceive, the closer you get to the depths where Pulses reside.\"","She gestured, and the diagram highlighted specific configurations within the transformed bones.","\" But these bones must be self-achieved to properly integrate with existing access pathways. Transformations that are gifted or granted by external sources create what we call dead zones, regions of your existence that block perception rather than enhancing it.\"","Noah thought about Ozymandias, about the Proterozoic Bones that had been formed within THE Hadean Desmoterion. Those were self-achieved, formed through Civilizational Eons of Development that Ozymandias had experienced personally.","Naldine continued.","\" Second, the Organ Triad Foundation. You require minimum three Proterozoic Organs.\"","A new diagram showed three organs blazing with transformed light, each one serving distinct purposes.","\"A sensory organ is required because perception IS access. Without transformed perception, you cannot see deeply enough into your Existence to find what you are looking for. Eyes are most common, but ears or other sensory structures can serve if properly integrated.\"","She pointed to the second organ in the diagram.","\"A vital organ is required to sustain expanded awareness without foundational collapse. When you perceive at five percent access, the strain on your existence is immense. Without a vital organ transformed to handle that strain, your foundations simply break apart under the pressure of seeing too much.\"","The third organ blazed brightest in the diagram.","\" The third organ provides redundancy against the strain of higher access percentages. It serves as backup, as support, as the failsafe that prevents catastrophic collapse when your primary systems are overwhelmed by what you are attempting to channel.\"","Noah thought about Ozymandias again.","He had...","Three bone clusters. One organ.","It was not enough.","\" Third, and this is where you are actually unique. \"","Naldine’s expression shifted into something that might have been grudging acknowledgment.","\" Infinity Tolerance. Integration rather than containment.\"","The diagram showed Infinity flowing through a Civilization rather than being walled away from it, light weaving through the framework rather than being held in separate containers that prevented interaction.","\" Infinity must flow through your Civilization rather than being walled away from it. Your Civilizational expressions must incorporate Infinity naturally. Only integrated Infinity dissolves the perception barriers that prevent deeper access.\"","She paused, observing him.","\" This is the one requirement you actually meet and exceed. Your Infinity is not contained. It flows through everything you are. It has become so integrated with your existence that separation would be impossible even if you wished it.\"","Noah absorbed this information.","He met one requirement out of three.","He possessed integrated Infinity, but he lacked eighty-five percent Proterozoic Bone saturation. He lacked the Organ Triad Foundation. He lacked the fundamental density that traditional methodology demanded.","But Naldine was not finished.","She dismissed the diagrams with a wave of her perception’s hand, and her expression became grave.","\" Then, there is a saying among Primordial Architects that trumps all requirements of THE Pulses of The Scales.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes met his with intensity.","\" Touch the source, perceive everything it created.\"","She repeated the phrase with emphasis that suggested ritual significance.","\" Touch the source, perceive everything it created.\"","A new diagram formed, showing a First Cause as a point of infinite brilliance from which all else emerged.","\" We say this because if one can incomprehensibly witness or understand or gain knowledge of a Cause relating to a specific Pulse, they can have its knowledge seared into their existence.\"","The diagram showed that knowledge being branded into the foundations of one who had touched the source.","\" Once you do, once that knowledge exists within you, you simply have to recreate it. The knowledge or emergence of what that Cause meant, expressed through a Pulse.\"","Her expression became more serious.","\" And the recreation of it is far too grand when trying to emulate a Cause, so existence breaks it down for us to be capable of expressing it.\"","New diagrams formed, showing the components of what she was describing.","\"It will involve verbal utterances. The chanting of Existential words that resonate with the Cause you are attempting to channel. Words that are not merely spoken but expressed with authority that touches the same frequencies the Cause itself touched when it created.\"","A second component appeared in the diagram.","\" And a requirement of somatic expression. Precise limb movements or gestures that shape the authority you are channeling into configurations that approximate what the Cause produced.\"","The diagram showed both components working together, verbal and somatic combining.","\" This combination will attempt to imitate and call upon the power of that Cause. In the case of THE Silurian Light, it will be a pale imitation of THE Silurian Cause. A fraction of what that originating force actually accomplished. But even a fraction is sufficient to erase causality, to unmake existence, to burn away what was as if it had never been.\"","She paused, her expression shifting into something complicated.","\" In THE Wyld, where I and many Primordial Architects call home, those distinguished enough can be given the Modus Operandi of Pulses once we can perceive enough.\"","Noah’s eyes sharpened at this revelation.","THE Wyld had a methodology for teaching Pulses to those who qualified. They possessed the verbal components and the somatic gestures required to channel powers that most beings could not even perceive.","\" Nobody knows where we obtained this methodology. Or at least, I was not told.\"","\" Because the only one who could produce the method imitating a genuine Cause is someone who witnessed it, correct? Someone who touched the source and perceived everything it created. Someone who then translated that incomprehensible knowledge into forms that lesser beings could attempt to reproduce.\"","She dismissed the diagrams entirely, her perception focusing solely on Noah with attention that held finality.","\" But I digress. The Modus Operandi of THE Silurian Light was granted to me. I can teach it to you as best as I can.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes held no hope.","\" But in the end, it will seem like gibberish to you. You do not have the capacity to carry it out.\"","...!"]},{"number":5085,"title":"Chapter 5085: Chapter 5084: Knowledge And Access IV","paragraphs":["Naldine observed him for a long moment within that perception stretched toward infinity.","Then she raised her right hand.","\" Watch carefully. I will only demonstrate this once before we discuss it.\"","Her palm faced outward, fingers spread wide as if preparing to grasp something that existed beyond physical perception. The gesture held stillness that seemed almost reverent, a musician preparing to play an instrument that had been waiting since before Observable Existence learned to observe.","Then her fingers began to move.","The first motion was a curling inward, each finger bending in sequence from smallest to largest as if she were grasping threads of reality itself that only five percent Civilizational Access could perceive. Her hand drew backward in a pulling motion, those invisible threads gathering in her palm like strands of a sea being unraveled from the weaving that held them in place.","Her palm rotated slowly, drawing a circle in the frozen air that suggested reversal, regression, the unwinding of causality flowing backward against its natural current. The motion was ancient, gestures that seemed to have existed before gestures were possible, movements that touched upon fundamentals!","Her fingers snapped outward in a flicking motion, releasing whatever she had gathered while simultaneously reaching toward something distant. Then her hand closed into a fist, authority condensing into configurations that pressed against the stretched moment with force that should not have been possible within perception alone.","Her fist opened.","Her fingers spread as fire would bloom from kindling, and her voice emerged with words that pressed against existence itself.","\" Silurian Ember, First of Flames. I grasp the Thread. I burn the Thread. What was shall be unwritten, what stood shall stand no more. THE SILURIAN LIGHT\"","The words landed with force that made even this perception stretched toward infinity tremble slightly.","Golden fire, pale and terrible and filled with colors that should not have been capable of existing simultaneously, flickered briefly around her extended fingers before fading into nothing. It was only demonstration, only illustration, only showing him what the Modus Operandi looked like when properly executed by one who possessed the capacity to channel it.","She lowered her hand and looked at him.","Noah looked back at her.","He blinked.","Really, it had seemed like she was just waving her hand around and spouting rubbish.","The gesture had been elaborate, certainly. The words had sounded impressive, undeniably. But watching her perform the Modus Operandi without being able to perceive what she was actually touching, without being able to sense the depths of Civilization she was accessing, without being able to feel the threads she was grasping and the fire she was calling forth, all of it had seemed like theatrical nonsense.","A woman waving her fingers in patterns that held no meaning he could discern.","A woman speaking words that sounded ancient but conveyed nothing to ears that could not hear what existed beneath their surface.","Gibberish!","\" You see ?\" Naldine said with expression that held no surprise at his reaction. \" To you, it means nothing. Because you cannot perceive what I am touching when I make those movements. You cannot hear what I am calling when I speak those words. The Modus Operandi requires access you do not possess, perception you have not developed, depths you cannot currently reach.\"","She shook her head slowly.","\" This is why I said it would seem like gibberish. Because without the capacity to perceive THE Silurian Light, without the access to find where it resides and grasp the thread that connects to THE Silurian Cause, you are simply a child mimicking gestures and sounds without understanding what they are meant to accomplish.\"","...!","Noah thought of the demonstration.","He thought about himself, about how different his path had been compared to every other being he had encountered in Observable Existence. The traditional progression demanded a Civilizational Anchor first, affirmations of self-knowledge that established the framework through which all subsequent advancement would flow. Then came THE Proterozoic Scale, the transformation of bones and organs.","Noah had not followed that path.","He, without making a Civilizational Anchor with his main body, was forming Hadean Bones. Not Proterozoic. Hadean.","A classification that should not have existed, a tier of transformation that the system prompts themselves seemed uncertain how to categorize. His right hand blazed with THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp.","And he possessed THE Hadean Organ of Civilization.","’Oh...’","His eyes flickered as he smiled at the realization. THE Hadean Organ of Civilization. He had formed something grander than a Proterozoic Organ first bwfore even forming any bones!","That construct within his chest had made everything possible. It processed Observable force. It granted Civilizational Eons of Development that allowed Ozymandias to progress at ridiculous rates. It collected THE Hadean Existential Singularities that siphoned knowledge and power from designated targets.","His progression was completely different than the progression of others!","The requirements Naldine had listed pressed against his awareness. Eighty-five percent Proterozoic Bone saturation. Organ Triad Foundation. Infinity Tolerance through integration rather than containment.","He met the third requirement absolutely.","But the bone saturation, the organ requirements, these he lacked in traditional form.","However.","He possessed Hadean Bones rather than Proterozoic. Were they not superior?","He possessed THE Hadean Organ of Civilization.","And then there was THE Infiniverse.","But the most significant factor remained his connection to a Gilded.","He thought about Eon, about the Observable force flooding into him through Quintessence Infiniforce pathways that violated Existential Designations. If his thoughts were correct regarding the nature of THE Gilded, they should have no issues with accessing more of their existence and Civilizations. The limitations that constrained THE Bounded would not apply to them. They might start at five percent Civilizational Access. They might start at ten percent. Or more.","He was currently connected to and siphoning from a Gilded.","Could this change anything?","The Observable force flowing into him was not merely raw power. It carried something else, something that felt like perception itself being transmitted alongside the energy.","When he processed that force through THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, when it spread through his transforming bones and integrated with his foundations, was he gaining more than just strength?","Was he gaining... access?","He himself could not determine where he stood.","He looked toward Naldine, his perception meeting hers within this moment stretched toward infinity.","\" Okay. Let me see the motions again.\"","His voice emerged with determination.","\" And you can tell me about any other Pulses of The Scales. Any information I could benefit from. Even knowledge of THE Wyld.\"","He settled into posture of relaxation.","\" After all, we have the time.\"","...!","Naldine observed him for a long moment.","She nodded slowly.","\" Very well.\"","Her right hand rose again, palm facing outward, fingers spread wide, and she began to repeat.","Noah observed. He processed. He attempted to find meaning in what he was witnessing.","It still seemed like gibberish, but he continued watching regardless.","---","The hours began to pass within their perception.","Naldine repeated the Modus Operandi of THE Silurian Light seventeen times, each demonstration accompanied by explanation that grew more detailed as she recognized his genuine attention.","Then she moved beyond THE Silurian Light.","\" There are other Pulses,\" she said, her perception waving hands that conjured new diagrams in the frozen air around them. \" THE Ordovician Silence is one I possess knowledge of, though I have never successfully channeled it. It does not erase causality as it freezes it. Everything affected becomes locked in the moment of contact, unable to progress forward or backward, suspended until the one who channeled the Pulse permits movement to resume.\"","She demonstrated a different set of gestures, fingers moving in patterns of binding rather than unraveling.","\" THE Cambrian Word is another. It rewrites. Causality can be altered rather than removed, consequences changed to produce different outcomes while the original actions remain intact.\"","Hours passed as she explained each Pulse she possessed knowledge of, their requirements, their Modus Operandi, their relationships to the various Causes that had formed Observable Existences across the vastness of reality.","She spoke of THE Wyld.","\" It is not a place in the way you understand places,\" she explained. \" It is a domain accessible through Prima Indifferentia, but only Primordial Architects can perceive the pathways that lead to it. Within THE Wyld, eons of our development and Civilizations are contained. Hierarchies that have nothing to do with Observable Existence govern who rises and who falls.\"","She described THE Deliverance and others.","\" No one disobeys them,\" she said with voice that held something approaching fear despite her classification. \" Those who attempt resistance simply cease to exist. Their Proterozoic Bones and Organs remain where their bodies once stood, available for collection by more obedient servants.\"","She spoke of factions within THE Wyld, of ideological divisions between those who wished to remain isolated and those who believed expansion beyond their borders was necessary. She had been among the latter, one of the Visionaries who advocated for alliance with entities outside Primordial Architect classification.","More hours passed.","Noah listened. He absorbed and processed everything she shared!","More than twenty hours later, his body of perception lay back on a golden cloud of Observable force.","The cloud had formed naturally around him as he relaxed within this stretched moment, his authority manifesting comfort that his physical body could not experience while frozen in objective time. He threw a golden ball of Observable force upward, watching it arc through the perception-space before catching it when it fell.","Throw. Catch. Throw. Catch.","His eyes remained fixed on the ceiling of this stretched infinity, his mind processing everything Naldine had taught him.","\" The crux of it all ,\" he said slowly, throwing the ball again, \" for THE Silurian Light and the two other Pulses you have knowledge of seems to be the same.\"","He caught the ball.","\" Powerful Second Scale beings drawing power from a Cause.\"","He threw it again.","\" You have your own method to draw power from THE Silurian Cause, a fiery Cause which triggers the emergence of Observable Existences. The gestures approximate what that Cause did when it created. The words call upon the authority that Cause possessed when it formed reality from nothing.\"","He caught the ball and held it, his perception turning to look at Naldine with eyes that blazed with understanding.","\"I simply need to find my own way to draw upon the power of that Cause.\"","...!"]},{"number":5086,"title":"Chapter 5086: Chapter 5085: Knowledge And Access V","paragraphs":["Even though he had grandly proclaimed that he would find his own way, it was still hard.","The hours stretched into what felt like days within this perception extended toward infinity, and Noah found himself no closer to understanding how to touch THE Silurian Cause than he had been when Naldine first demonstrated the Modus Operandi. He theorized. He contemplated. He examined every unique aspect of his existence that might provide pathways traditional methodology did not account for.","The connection to Eon continued flooding him with Observable force even within this stretched moment, that golden light pressing against his foundations with density that should have been expanding his perception. But expansion was not comprehension. Having more did not mean understanding what he had.","So he talked.","Sharing information had proven surprisingly effective for processing his own thoughts, and Naldine proved to be an attentive listener despite her apparent frustration with his refusal to accept impossibility.","\" The enemy that really gave me a wake up call was someone called The Devilish Time Unveiler...\"","Noah threw the golden ball of Observable force upward again, watching it arc through their perception-space.","\" That fucker made me very vindictive and cautious. Granted, some stupid mistakes were made on my part. Thinking back, my first tries of Temporal Traversals were due to him, though back then I had the little Dagger of Time...\"","He caught the ball, his expression shifting into something approaching nostalgia despite the danger that memory represented.","\" Oppenheimer was cool. I still keep up with this guy called Commander Feng that had his own unique fable. Dikastes of Extremity I did not much care for.\"","He threw the ball again.","\"I did enjoy my progression across my Wheel of Existence the most. I was playing around with The Three Body Problem, True Sources. I set up Singed, Ordo Ab Chao, Outerversal, Oh, Megalos...and other unique constructs to enact my own Atlas.\"","Naldine listened to these fragments of history with expression that shifted through confusion into assessment. The names meant nothing to her, the contexts were absent, but she was piecing together a picture of someone whose path had been anything but conventional.","He continued telling Fables.","She stopped him at one point, her singularity-dotted eyes narrowing.","\" Hold on.\"","Her voice emerged with sharpness that demanded clarification.","\" Adelaide, Barbatos, Anna, Athena, Eowyn, Sigrid, Riya... Why did you form so many potential points of weakness just for yourself?\"","She rose from where she had been seated within their perception-space, her form radiating disapproval.","\" Primordial Architects have no need for and do not bother with copulation for the most part, unless you are Beowulf. But why so many? Your enemies could hold you hostage just by pulling on threads of those you are emotionally attached to the most.\"","Her arms crossed over her chest.","\"I would reduce this and keep your focus on your Civilization and Existence. Those with a singular focus find themselves always more determined. Attachments divide attention. Divided attention invites failure.\"","She said such dangerous words to Noah.","He smiled and shook his head as if she would not understand. The suggestion that he should reduce his connections, that he should sever bonds he had formed across spans of existence that most beings could not comprehend, it revealed a fundamental misunderstanding of what those connections meant to him.","They were not weaknesses.","They were reasons.","But explaining that to someone who had never experienced what he had experienced would be like explaining color to one who had never possessed sight.","He did ask her something else instead.","\" You have never copulated, yes?\"","His voice held no mockery, only genuine curiosity.","\" You would not understand. I could expand your perspective on this and teach you regarding Dual Cultivation. It has solved many problems for me.\"","...!","Naldine looked at him calmly at such words.","Her expression did not shift into embarrassment or offense. She observed him with assessment that suggested she was considering his statement from angles he had not anticipated.","\" The act itself can be considered nothing or mean everything.\"","Her voice emerged measured, almost clinical.","\" You essentially allow yourself to be extremely vulnerable with your existence to another. Existences are fickle. If someone grasps your weavings at your weakest, they could do whatever they wished.\"","She gestured toward him with one hand.","\" You are filled with Infinities. While it is a wonder you have not gone mad, letting you anywhere near me might cause THE Gamaidjan to envelop my existence.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes held something that might have been caution beneath their imperious allure.","\" And I do not wish to go mad with Infinity. Not anytime soon.\"","Noah shook his head at these words.","\" The Great Naldine Manthon is afraid of my Infinity. Understood.\"","He found her concern more amusing than offensive.","\" If ever you want to change that misconception, let me know. I am ninety percent sure I could take you past the Calymmian Tier of THE Proterozoic Scale with Dual Cultivation.\"","Naldine smiled at such words.","\" You think existence is that easy? THE Proterozoic Scale is that easy?\"","Noah looked at her with eyes that blazed with certainty most beings could not possess.","\" Yes?\"","The word emerged as statement rather than question.","\"In the last day, I have gone from Absolute to have another body of mine form multiple Proterozoic Bones and an Organ. This Ozymandias that I pulled out here. I myself...\"","He paused, considering how much to reveal.","\" Well, I have made my own accomplishments I will not freely mention. But yes. Existence and progression can be easy even with all the adversity.\"","He threw the golden ball upward again.","\" Some time ago, I was trapped in Hell Terra Firma, a place where I had no access to any authority. I should have struggled, but I made it easy.\"","He caught the ball.","\" Even all of this right now. All the adversity that surrounds me and all that will come. It will try to break me, yes, but I wholly believe I will make it easy.\"","His smile widened into something that held darkness beneath its apparent confidence.","\"If I stumble and fail, I can always fuck things up for everyone and break time itself.\"","...!","He said such words casually, as if shattering the temporal foundations of Observable Existence was merely a contingency plan!","Naldine frowned at this declaration.","She wondered if his madness of Infinity was showing through here, if the integration that allowed him to channel impossible forces also permitted thoughts that no sane existence should entertain. Breaking time itself. Fucking things up for everyone. These were not the statements of someone operating within normal parameters of reason.","But then again, nothing about him operated within normal parameters.","She sighed with breath that existed only in perception.","\" You mention making things easy as if adversity is merely inconvenience to be dismissed.\"","Her voice emerged with weight that pressed against his casual confidence.","\"I have faced adversity that could not be made easy....\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes held memory that she rarely permitted to surface.","\" Perhaps your path has been different. Perhaps your Infinity permits confidence that others cannot possess. But do not assume that easy is universal. Some adversity exists specifically to break those who believe themselves unbreakable.\"","...!","And like this, while sharing knowledge and experience and perspectives that emerged from classifications that should never have been capable of communication, days began to pass in their perception of infinity.","Noah thought about the many potential paths he could take to learn how to utilize a Pulse of The Scales.","He could focus on expanding his Hadean Bone saturation through Ozymandias, pushing toward configurations that might serve as equivalent to the eighty-five percent Proterozoic threshold traditional methodology demanded. But that would require objective time he did not currently possess.","He could attempt to leverage his connection to Eon more aggressively. But he did not know if such a thing was possible through the Quintessence Infiniforce pathways.","He could try to find THE Silurian Cause directly, touching the source as the ancient saying suggested. But First Causes were not entities one could simply locate and approach.","He could attempt to channel THE Silurian Light through pure Infinity, bypassing the requirements entirely through impossible methodology that recognized no ceilings. But he did not know...","Each path held uncertainty.","Each path held risk.","Each path required something he was not certain he possessed.","It was an arduous and hard task.","But as the days of perception continued stretching within that single instant of objective time, Noah found himself no less determined despite the difficulty pressing against his awareness.","He would find his way.","He always did!"]},{"number":5087,"title":"Chapter 5087: Chapter 5086: My Pulse! I","paragraphs":["Days had passed in the infinite perceptive moment.","Noah hadn’t come across any viable solution for grasping THE Silurian Light through traditional means, but he’d obtained a great deal of information from Naldine across those stretched spans. She’d explained the intricacies of THE Wyld, the nature of THE Deliverance and others like him, the factions that divided Primordial Architects into camps that had been warring since before most current beings learned to crawl.","She’d demonstrated the Modus Operandi of three different Pulses until he could recite the verbal components from memory even if he couldn’t perceive what they were meant to touch.","She wasn’t so bad after having talked to her for so long.","He’d even gotten her to agree to simply experiment with his Infinity if and when the ordeal of Grimvault was passed successfully. She’d been reluctant, citing concerns about THE Gamaidjan enveloping her existence, but curiosity had eventually won out over caution. Primordial Architects were, at their core, beings who pursued advancement above safety.","At this time, Noah was thinking about Temporal Traversal.","Just how far back could he take it? He’d played with time before, had bent its rules in ways that should have been impossible for someone of his classification. Could he take it far enough to witness THE First Cause that birthed their Observable Existence? If he could perceive that moment of ignition, that instant when nothing became something, maybe then he could pull a Pulse from it directly.","Touch the source, perceive everything it created.","But as he was thinking this, Naldine’s voice drifted across the perception-space.","She sat on a cloud of blue gold light, her form settled into meditation posture despite the fact that cultivation was impossible within expanded perception. Her singularity-dotted eyes remained closed as she spoke.","\" Your life is an astonishingly short one in the grand scheme of things.\"","Her voice held no mockery, only statement of fact.","\"I want to say that based on your origins, a normal human female with no authority caused your emergence, yes? Look at you now.\"","She opened her eyes, those blue dots floating within pure white regarding him with something like academic interest.","\" You are a case study in existence. Some would benefit from understanding your lowly emergence, your lowly Cause.\"","Noah was listening faintly, his mind still churning through possibilities involving Temporal Traversal and First Causes and methodologies that might bypass traditional requirements. He was just about to nod in absent acknowledgment when he blinked.","HUUM!","His existence began to buzz!","Then he rose up straight and looked at her.","\" What did you just say?\"","Naldine blinked as if she hadn’t said anything of significance.","\"I was just talking about your emergence. How it can be considered a lowly Cause that others can benefit fro-\"","HUUM!","The perception-space began to buzz.","Noah’s eyes shone brightly, golden light bleeding from them in configurations that pressed against the stretched moment itself. Something was happening within his awareness, connections forming between concepts that had seemed unrelated moments before!","Then he laughed.","The sound boomed across the perception-space with genuine delight, the kind of laughter that emerged from sudden understanding!","\"A Pulse of The Scales emerges from witnessing a Cause and pulling its power.\"","His voice rang out as he began pacing through the air, Observable force condensing beneath his feet with each step.","\"A Cause is grand because of what it gives way to. A Cause gives way to Observable Existence!\"","He spun to face Naldine, his smile widening into something that held madness and brilliance in equal measure.","\" And yet, my very emergence was a Cause! My birth was a Cause, and with it, it led to me, it led to Infinity, it led to...\"","He raised one hand, golden light blazing around his fingers.","\"A Seed of Observable Existence!\"","BOOM!","The perception-space trembled at his declaration.","\" From me alone, even though I haven’t yet allowed for the blooming of Observable Existence, I have aided in the forging of a Seed! My emergence... isn’t lowly at all!\"","His laughter echoed again.","\" My emergence is grand!\"","Naldine rose from her meditation posture in astonishment, her singularity-dotted eyes wide as she processed what he was claiming!","She wanted to ask what the fuck he was talking about. His birth as a Cause? How could that possibly compare to THE First Cause of Observable Existence? The scale wasn’t even remotely similar!","But she couldn’t say anything.","Because at this time, Noah felt like he was in a trance. He thought about many things and nothing all at once, his mind buzzing with glorious waves of epiphanies cascading one into another. The logic was flowing now, connections he’d never considered before illuminating pathways that traditional methodology couldn’t perceive.","\" What determines the grandeur of a Cause?\"","His voice emerged as question and answer simultaneously.","\" What it produces! THE Silurian Cause is considered grand because it produced Observable Existences, realities spanning scopes that most minds can’t comprehend!\"","He spread his arms wide.","\" But my emergence produced ME! My birth led to someone who touched Infinity and didn’t break! My Cause led to someone who forged THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, who transformed a small landmass into THE Infiniverse, who created a Seed capable of blooming into its own Observable Existence!\"","The perception-space shook harder as his voice rose.","\" Who is to say that the power of my Cause would be any lesser when it led to accomplishments like these? THE Silurian Cause produced Observable Existence, yes! But my Cause produced someone capable of becoming Observable Existence! My Cause produced someone who could break time itself if he chose!\"","|Epiphany Detected.|","|You are attempting to conceptualize personal emergence as First Cause equivalent.|","|Unprecedented. No recorded instance of such interpretation exists as results of this approach cannot be predicted.|","Noah ignored the system prompt entirely.","\" My birth was a Cause unlike any other! MY birth! MY Cause!\"","...!","His golden eyes blazed with light that pressed against the boundaries of their expanded perception.","\" And from MY Cause, I will observe it and design MY own Pulse of The Scales! Because across my emergence, I have also...played with fire.\"","...!"]},{"number":5088,"title":"Chapter 5088: Chapter 5087: My Pulse! II","paragraphs":["He thrust one hand forward, fingers curling into the same gesture Naldine had demonstrated dozens of times.","\"There was a spark when two cells came together in my mother’s womb! A moment of ignition that brought something from nothing! There was another spark when I utilized an F Rank skill book, when Mana first flooded through my existence and everything changed!\"","His smile became something terrifying in its confidence.","\" From MY Cause, I will focus on its fiery aspect to design my own Silurian Light! And its power...will be no lesser!\"","He raised both hands toward the ceiling of their perception-space, Observable force and Infinity swirling around his form in configurations that seemed to be attempting to create something that had never existed before.","\"It...will be grander!\"","His laughter rang out again, triumphant and tyrannical.","\" HAHA!\"","The perception-space trembled violently at his declaration, that stretched moment of infinity struggling to contain the concepts he was attempting to manifest within it. Naldine rose fully from her position, her expression shifting through astonishment into something that bordered on genuine concern.","She wondered if he had truly gone mad!","At this moment, Noah felt like he was in an unprecedented trance.","Within that perception of stretched infinity, he found his consciousness fading away from the golden space where Naldine watched with growing concern. Something was pulling him inward, deeper than he’d ever gone into the foundations of his own existence. He was being drawn into a paradoxical singularity of self, a place where he was both the observer and the observed.","He felt like himself, but also as if he was watching himself from somewhere outside the boundaries of his own awareness.","His vision opened up.","He saw a woman grabbing her belly in a cramped apartment, her face twisted with the discomfort of early pregnancy. Amelia Osmont. His mother. She was young in this vision, younger than he remembered her being, with dark hair falling across features that held beauty despite the exhaustion pressing against them.","In the living room, his father was already knocked out on the couch. A few bottles of beer stretched across the coffee table and floor around him, their labels peeling and contents long emptied. The man snored with the rhythm of someone who’d made unconsciousness his preferred state of existence.","This was his Cause already in process.","The moment the waste of his father contributed what little he could to his formation, and as he underwent development in his mother’s womb, his Cause unfolded across nine months of biological fire.","| Observing: Your Cause.|","|Stage: Cellular Division and Formation.|","Cell division was fire. Each mitosis was a spark of creation, a single cell igniting into two, two into four, four into eight, multiplication cascading like flames spreading through dry kindling. The metabolic processes that sustained this growth burned nutrients into energy, oxidation reactions producing heat that maintained the precise temperature required for development.","His neural pathways formed like lightning, electrical signals sparking across developing synapses for the first time. His heart ignited with its first beat, a rhythm of combustion that would continue for decades to come. The very oxygen his mother breathed fed flames of creation within her womb, each breath stoking the fire of his emergence.","|Fiery Processes Detected: Cellular ignition. Metabolic combustion. Neural spark formation. Cardiac rhythm initialization. Oxidative development sustained across 40 weeks of gestation.|","|These processes represent the kindling of Your Cause.|","Noah closed his eyes within this vision and focused on these processes, feeling the heat of his own creation as if it were happening in real time rather than being observed across decades of separation.","Time fast-forwarded.","He found himself in a hospital room, sterile lights buzzing overhead as his mother lay alone in a bed designed for moments that should have been shared. She was giving birth while his father gambled somewhere across the city, chasing losses that would never be recovered.","The doctors and nurses moved around her with professional efficiency, but the absence of anyone who actually cared pressed against the scene like a wound that wouldn’t close.","This was also his Cause.","|Stage: Emergence.|","|The first breath is fire. Oxygen flooding lungs that have never known air, igniting systems that operated in fluid darkness for nine months. The severing of the umbilical cord is the separation of flames, a new fire burning independent of its source.|","|Body temperature regulation commences. Internal combustion sustains existence outside the womb. Your Cause continues its unfolding.|","A baby’s cry echoed through the hospital room, and Noah recognized his own voice from before he understood what voices were for.","Time moved forward again.","He grew up in fragments, years passing like pages being flipped through a book too quickly to read. Childhood. Adolescence. The mundane struggles of someone trying to survive in a world that didn’t particularly care if he succeeded or failed. His mother working multiple jobs. His father disappearing for longer and longer periods.","Then dungeons descended unto the world, and the apocalypse began.","Everything changed. Reality itself seemed to crack open, and humanity discovered it had been living in ignorance of forces that had always existed beyond their perception. Monsters emerged from nowhere. People awakened to powers they couldn’t explain. The old world burned, and from its ashes, a new world struggled to take shape.","Noah did everything to become a Hunter.","He found himself in that dilapidated apartment. The walls were cracked. The ceiling leaked when it rained. The single window looked out on an alley where garbage accumulated faster than anyone bothered to remove it.","But in his hands, he held a skill book.","[ Fireball ].","The cheapest offensive skill on the market, an F Rank ability that most serious Hunters wouldn’t bother picking up from the ground if they found it lying in a dungeon. But to him, in that moment, it represented Everything . It represented possibility. It represented the first step toward becoming something more than what his circumstances had decided he should be.","The skill book faded into lights that entered his body.","|Stage: First Kindling of Authority.|","|Mana integration commences. A spark of power ignites within a vessel that had known only mundane existence. This moment marks the transition from potential to actualization.|","|Your Cause continues its unfolding.|","That was also part of his Cause.","Just because these moments were mundane didn’t mean they lacked power. A normal human woman with no authority had given birth to him in a hospital room while his father threw money away on games he couldn’t win. A cheap skill book had introduced Mana to his system for the first time. None of it seemed grand by the standards of beings who measured significance in eons and Observable Existences.","But from all this, a Seed of Observable Existence had bloomed due to his hands.","That was a big thing. That was a very big thing! And in the future, he knew it would become a genuine Observable Existence, would bloom into something that rivaled or surpassed the reality he currently inhabited. His Cause would become even grander with time.","So even though it was mundane, this was significant.","An illusory consciousness of Noah gazed at his young self in that apartment room.","The contrast was stark. His younger self stood there in worn clothes, thin from meals skipped to save money. His current self floated nearby, wrapped in golden Observable force, bearing Hadean Bones and connections to Gilded Lifeforms and Infinity integrated so thoroughly into his existence that separation would be impossible.","The same person. Separated by accomplishments that his younger self couldn’t have imagined even in his most ambitious dreams.","\" My Cause...has always been THE Infinite Cause.\"","His voice emerged with certainty that pressed against this vision of the past.","\" From myself, from my Cause, I shall draw power from what it represents and what it has accomplished. I shall establish my own Pulse of The Scales.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5089,"title":"Chapter 5089: Chapter 5088: My Pulse! III","paragraphs":["The vision shattered.","|Acknowledgment Detected.|","|You are establishing resonance with personal Cause.|","|Classification: THE Infinite Cause.|","|Origin: Mundane emergence leading to Infinite potential.|","|This Cause is recognized as valid for Pulse derivation.|","Golden light exploded through Noah’s awareness as he felt power being drawn from the very foundation of his existence. Not from THE Silurian Cause that had formed this Observable Existence. Not from any external source that he had to beg or borrow or steal from. From himself. From what he was and what he had become and what he would eventually be.","|Pulse Derivation Commencing.|","|Source: THE Infinite Cause.|","|Focus: Fiery aspect of emergence.|","|The spark of cellular division. The combustion of metabolism. The ignition of first breath. The kindling of first Mana. All fires that contributed to THE Infinite Cause are being synthesized into singular expression.|","|Pulse Classification: [Calculating].|","His body began flooding with Observable force unlike anything he’d experienced before. The connection between him and Eon, that pathway of Quintessence Infiniforce that had been steadily transmitting golden light into his existence, suddenly increased a hundredfold in bandwidth. Where a river had been flowing, now an ocean surged.","|Connection to Gilded Lifeform: Expanding.|","|Observable force transmission: Increasing by factor of 100.|","|Reason: Pulse establishment requires sufficient authority to stabilize. Gilded connection is compensating for Bounded limitations.|","The endlessly generating Quintessence Infiniforce within his body joined the flood, his own production combining with what Eon’s existence was providing. And beyond that, he felt Infinity itself responding across Observable Existence, his claims scattered throughout reality beginning to channel support toward this singular moment of establishment.","|Warning.|","|You are deviating from the set weavings of existence.|","| You are deviating from Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.|","|You are establishing a Pulse outside The Scales.|","|This action has no precedent. This action has no predicted outcome. This action may attract attention from classifications that monitor deviations of this nature.|","|Be careful.|","|Be cautious.|","|Due to your current actions and your connection to a Gilded Lifeform, your Civilizational Access and Existential Access has been modified and altered.|","|Previous Access: 0.9%.|","|Current Access: 5%.|","|You have crossed the threshold required for Pulse perception and utilization.|","|Unknown changes are beginning to occur across your existence.|","BOOM!","Immensity and heaviness began to bloom within Noah as something fundamental shifted in the foundations of what he was.","He could feel it. Depths of his Civilization that had been invisible moments before were suddenly perceivable, as if someone had turned on lights in rooms he hadn’t known existed.","And somewhere in those newly illuminated depths, he could sense something waiting.","A Pulse.","His Pulse!","The changes began immediately.","Noah felt his awareness expanding in directions he hadn’t known existed!","His Civilization stretched before him with depths that his previous 0.9% access couldn’t have perceived, couldn’t have imagined, couldn’t have touched even if he’d known they were there.","|Civilizational Access: 5%.|","|New perception thresholds unlocked.|","|You can now perceive Civilizational depths previously invisible to your awareness. Weavings that seemed impossible at sub-1% access are now merely difficult. Weavings that seemed difficult are now natural expressions of your Civilization.|","He could see it!","He could see!","\" More...MORE !\" he said aloud within the perception-space.","HUUM!","Naldine was watching him with expression that had shifted from concern into something approaching genuine shock. She could sense what was happening even if she couldn’t perceive the specifics, could feel the fundamental shift occurring in his foundations.","|Connection to Gilded Lifeform: Stabilizing at enhanced parameters.|","|Current bandwidth: Enhanced by factor of 100.|","|Observable force from THE Secretive Eon is flooding your existence at rates previously impossible for Bounded classification.|","The golden light flowing into him from Eon felt different now. Before, it had been like drinking from a stream, satisfying but limited by the capacity of the channel. Now it was like standing beneath a waterfall, Observable force crashing into his existence with density that should have been overwhelming but instead felt exactly right.","His body could handle it.","More than that, his body was fucking hungry for it. Oh, he wanted all of it!","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization: Responding to increased Observable force input.|","|Processing efficiency: Increasing.|","|Previous efficiency: 847% above baseline Proterozoic parameters.|","|Current efficiency: 8,470% above baseline Proterozoic parameters.|","|THE Hadean Organ is evolving in response to new conditions. Changes are ongoing.|","The Hadean Organ was a grand thing, the construct that made his recent impossible progression possible. Now it was growing stronger alongside everything else, adapting to the flood of Observable force rather than being overwhelmed by it!","He turned his attention to his Hadean Bones.","THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp blazed brighter than before, those transformed carpals and metacarpals and phalanges radiating light that pressed against the perception-space itself. The transformation spreading up his arm had accelerated, golden brilliance consuming his radius and ulna with speed that would have taken hours under previous conditions.","His othet hand had began to shine, and his legs were starting to shine too!","|Hadean Bone transformation: Accelerating.|","|At current rate, full skeletal transformation will complete in approximately 37 hours of active cultivation.|","He could feel the bones in his extremities burning with pleasant heat as Observable force saturated them, as Hadean transformation consumed what had been mundane structure and replaced it with something that existed above THE Proterozoic Scale entirely.","|Hadean classification remains unknown and unprecedented.|","|System cannot accurately predict outcomes of full Hadean skeletal transformation.|","|Proceeding with caution is advised.|","|You...are not proceeding with caution.|","| Okay.|","Noah almost laughed at that last line. Caution? Fuck caution!","|Changes detected across all connected existences.|","|THE Infiniverse: Responding to increased Civilizational Access.|","|Ozymandias: Responding to increased Observable force transmission.|","|Secondary bodies: Responding to expanded perception thresholds.|","|All aspects of your existence are being affected by this transition.|","THE Infiniverse and its Three Thousand Realms was pulsing with new energy. The connection between it and his primary existence had always been strong, but now it felt like the boundary between them was thinning, like the distinction between Noah and THE Infiniverse was becoming less meaningful.","|THE Infiniverse: Civilizational resonance increasing.|","|Your Seed of Observable Existence is responding to the recognition of THE Infinite Cause.|","|Growth rate: Accelerating.|","|The Seed recognizes that its origin has been acknowledged as a valid Cause. This recognition is feeding back into the Seed itself, strengthening its foundations.|","His Cause was connected to everything he’d accomplished, and the Seed was one of his greatest accomplishments. By acknowledging THE Infinite Cause, he was also acknowledging everything that Cause had produced, and that acknowledgment carried power.","That...was not too confusing, right?"]},{"number":5090,"title":"Chapter 5090: Chapter 5089: My Pulse! IV","paragraphs":["Ozymandias, still frozen in that instant of objective time outside this perception-space, was changing too.","|Ozymandias: Enhanced Observable force transmission detected.|","|THE Hadean Desmoterion: Receiving increased input.|","|Civilizational Eons of Development within THE Hadean Desmoterion: Accelerating.|","|New capabilities detected at 5% Civilizational Access.|","|Category 1: Existential Anchoring.|","|You can now perceive how Civilizational Anchors interface with Observable and Unobservable forces at fundamental levels. This perception may allow for manipulation of anchoring processes in self and others. You can declare and establish your Civilizational Anchor at anytime. Your entry into the second scale officially, is whenever you feel like it.|","|Category 2: Causal Threading.|","|You can now perceive the threads connecting actions to consequences across time. This perception is prerequisite for Pulse utilization. Without it, THE Silurian Light and similar capabilities would remain invisible regardless of power level.|","|Category 3: Scale Interfacing.|","|You can now perceive how THE First Scale and THE Second Scale interact at boundary conditions. This perception may allow for capabilities that blur the distinction between Scales.|","|Category 4: Designation Boundaries.|","|You can now perceive a bit more of the engineering that distinguishes Bounded and Gilded classifications. The study into Eon will soon yield some results.|","|Category 5: Cause Recognition.|","|You can now perceive the Causes underlying the usage of power other existences, not merely your own. This perception may allow for Pulse derivation from external sources if sufficient resonance is established.|","Noah absorbed each category with growing appreciation for what five percent access actually meant. These were fundamental shifts in what he could perceive and therefore what he could eventually do.","Cause Recognition was unique. If he could perceive the Causes underlying other existences, could he eventually derive Pulses from Causes that weren’t his own? Could he touch THE Silurian Cause itself and pull traditional Silurian Light alongside his own Infinite variant?","But speaking of his own Cause, he could feel something else happening. Something in those newly illuminated depths of his Civilization, something that had been waiting for him to achieve sufficient access to perceive it.","|Pulse Formation: In Progress.|","|Your Cause has been acknowledged. Your fiery aspect has been identified. Your derivation is stabilizing.|","|Pulse Classification: THE Infinite Light.|","|Status: Nascent.|","|Detailed analysis cannot yet be given.|","THE Infinite Light.","His Pulse had a name now!","It existed within his Civilization as something he could utilizs, a thread of fire connecting to THE Infinite Cause he’d acknowledged as his origin.","|Final Status Update.|","|Civilizational Access: 5% (stable) / Existential Access: 5% (stable).|","|Connection to Gilded Lifeform: Enhanced (ongoing).|","|Hadean transformation: Accelerating.|","|Overall assessment: You have fundamentally altered your existence in ways that cannot be reversed. The path forward is unknown. The outcomes are unpredictable. You have deviated from every established methodology and created a trajectory that has no precedent. No abnormalities have been observed as a response from THE Vakochev Scales similar to when you first stepped into them.|","Noah’s eyes fully opened back in that stretched out moment of infinity.","His gaze came to land on Naldine, and uniquely, he found this powerful being actually take a step back from his gaze alone. His power shouldn’t have changed drastically in this moment of stretched perception. These were only their perceptions here, after all. Nothing physical had transformed yet.","But he had changed in how he perceived himself.","Now he was a man who had a Cause. He’d always had this Cause, had carried it since the moment two cells sparked together in his mother’s womb, but he’d never affirmed it. Never known about it. Never possessed the unique knowledge required to truly apply the immensity of what his existence represented.","He couldn’t help but smile as he looked toward this Primordial Architect.","\" Do I scare you now, Naldine Manthon?\"","...!","At such words, Naldine’s eyes flashed sharply. Her singularity-dotted gaze held his without flinching despite the step she’d taken backward, and when she spoke, her voice emerged calm and gloriously measured.","\" Fear is not something that will ever settle in my heart.\"","She paused, studying him with intensity that pressed against his awareness.","\" But in your eyes... how could it possibly have such a light? A light of someone who has seen something unfathomably grand. A light that very few can ever express even within THE Wyld.\"","Her voice softened slightly.","\"A light of those who have witnessed a grand Cause.\"","...!","Noah felt all the changes that would unfold as soon as he left this moment of stretched perception. The Observable force flooding in from Eon. The accelerating Hadean transformation. The nascent Pulse waiting to be channeled. All of it held in suspension, ready to crash into reality the instant he released this infinity.","He smiled and said , \"I told you. My emergence is a Cause as grand as THE First Cause.\"","His golden eyes blazed brighter.","\" You can consider this a claim that only I make. You can consider it mad. But I make such a claim boldly.\"","He looked toward the frozen landscape beyond their perception-space, toward Grimvault’s suspended smile and the motionless wings of swords and the serpentine coils held in stillness.","\" And now, I’m ready to end this stretched moment of perception.\"","His gaze returned to her.","\" Are you?\"","...!","She looked at him for a few seconds, those pure white eyes with their floating blue singularities assessing him with judgment that spanned eons of accumulated wisdom. Whatever she saw in his expression, whatever she perceived in that light he now carried, it was enough!","Oh, it had to be enough!","She nodded.","Noah smiled as he clenched his hand into a fist.","BOOM!","The infinity around him began to shatter, that stretched moment cracking like glass as their perceptions were returned to normal time. He would effectively resume the battle against a terrifying Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity, against Grimvault who possessed THE Silurian Light and capabilities that should have been impossible to counter.","But who he was a moment before and who he would be a moment later were quintessentially different.","Who he would be was so different!"]},{"number":5091,"title":"Chapter 5091: Chapter 5090: Nothing Could Repay!","paragraphs":["The waters of THE Infiniverse held depths that Amelia Osmont was still learning to navigate.","She floated within a serene pocket of the transformed reality her son had created, surrounded by currents of crimson and blue and gold that moved with purpose she couldn’t quite comprehend.","The ancient pink dolphin floating before her was one of many wonders she’d been interested in.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan regarded her with eyes that held eons of accumulated wisdom, its form radiating gentle authority. She’d grown comfortable speaking with this being!","\" So ,\" Amelia said, her voice carrying the practical skepticism she’d never quite abandoned, \" that you and THE Baboon of Wisdom both came from the same... what did you call it? Singular Cognizance? Does that make you a Singular Cognizance too? \"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s form shimmered with amusement.","\" THE Beholder is the Singular Cognizance from which my existence and that of THE Baboon of Wisdom originated. We are, in a sense, fragments of a greater whole that chose to express itself through multiple forms, though I am not truly a Singular Cognizance...\"","Amelia nodded slowly.","\" With the permission of your son, THE Beholder is making their way to THE Infiniverse as we speak. They will be here shortly.\"","Amelia blinked, but before she could reply, everything changed.","HUUM!","Waves of blue Infinity erupted from her existence without warning!","The energy cascaded outward from her form in configurations she couldn’t control, couldn’t understand, couldn’t do anything but witness as it happened. And alongside that blue brilliance, golden waves of Observable force began pouring into her from somewhere beyond her perception, flooding her existence with density that should have been overwhelming.","\"What-\"","She couldn’t finish the word.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s ancient pink form recoiled in astonishment, those wise eyes widening as it witnessed something it clearly hadn’t anticipated. The waters around them churned with the force of what was occurring, currents that had been serene moments before now turbulent with energies that pressed against the boundaries of this pocket of this Realm!","Amelia was shocked at the waves of force pouring into her, at the blue light bleeding from her skin, at the sensation of something fundamental shifting in what she was!","Before her eyes, radiant blue prompts began to appear.","| You have been affirmed as an Originator of an Unfathomable Cause.|","|Cause Classification: THE Infinite Cause.|","|Your Role: Primary Vessel of Emergence.|","The words hung in her vision!","|THE Infinite Cause has been acknowledged by its product. In acknowledging his Cause, he has acknowledged you.|","|You carried him for nine months while working double shifts to pay rent your husband gambled away. You felt him kick for the first time while standing exhausted, and you smiled anyway.|","|You gave birth to him alone in a hospital room because the man who should have been there chose cards over his own son’s first breath. You held that baby boy and promised him the world even though you had nothing to give.|","|You took care of him on countless restless nights when fever burned through his small body and you couldn’t afford medicine, so you held him and prayed and stayed awake until morning because that was all you could do.|","|When he was lost, you found him. When he was scared, you held him. When he doubted himself, you reminded him of who he was.|","|You taught him strength by being strong when you had every reason to break. You taught him persistence by refusing to give up when the world gave you nothing but reasons to quit. You taught him love by loving him unconditionally even when love was the only thing you had left to give.|","|Nothing could repay the endless nights. Nothing could possibly repay the hard work and sacrifice of a mother who chose her son over herself a thousand times without hesitation.|","| But this is a start.|","Amelia’s vision blurred as tears began forming in her eyes.","The prompts continued!","|Distinction Granted: Originator of THE Infinite Cause.|","|You are recognized as the vessel through which an Unfathomable Cause emerged into existence. This distinction cannot be taken, cannot be diminished, cannot be denied by any authority in Observable or Unobservable existence.|","|Boons of the Originator:|","|Existential Immunity: No force derived from THE Infinite Cause can harm you. Your son’s power, in all its forms, will always recognize you as its origin and protect you accordingly.|","|Causal Resonance: You will passively benefit from all advancements THE Infinite Cause achieves. As your son grows stronger, echoes of that strength will flow to you.|","|Observable Blessing: The connection your son has established with Gilded classification now extends a thread to your existence. You will receive a fraction of the Observable force flooding into him, enough to elevate you beyond all limitations.|","|Infinite Affection: THE Infinite Cause remembers. Every sacrifice, every sleepless night, every tear shed in private so your son wouldn’t see you struggling. It remembers, and it will never forget.|","Amelia Osmont became teary-eyed as she was reminded of years past.","She saw flashes of memory in those prompts, moments she’d thought forgotten now illuminated with significance she’d never attributed to them!","The time she’d skipped meals for a week so Noah could have new shoes for school. She knew others would make fun of him wearing extremely worn down shoes!","The night she’d held him through a thunderstorm because he was afraid and she’d told him she’d always protect him.","All of it mattered.","All of it had contributed to what he’d become!","And now, impossibly, some of what he’d become was flowing back to her.","While such a phenomenon unfolded around Amelia Osmont, while blue Infinity and golden Observable force continued flooding into her existence in ways that defied everything THE Mnemonic Leviathan understood about how power worked, a new presence made itself known.","\" What... is this?\"","An ancient voice boomed out with marvel that pressed against the entirety of this Realm.","It was a voice that made THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s authority seem small by comparison, a voice that carried weight accumulated across spans that predated most current existences. It was the voice of THE Beholder, the Progenitor of THE Baboon of Wisdom and THE Mnemonic Leviathan, the Singular Cognizance who had been granted entry into THE Infiniverse.","And that ancient being had arrived just in time to witness something unprecedented.","A mother receiving acknowledgment from her son’s Cause!","---","BOOM!","The infinity shattered.","Noah’s perception slammed back into normal time with force that should have been disorienting, but he’d spent subjective days preparing for this exact moment. Everything that had been frozen resumed its motion simultaneously. Grimvault’s smile completed its brutal curve. The multicolored rain began falling again. Beowulf’s screams filled the air with renewed agony.","And Noah’s body erupted with golden light.","HUUM!","Observable force radiated from his existence in waves that pressed against everything within range, density unlike anything he’d produced before flooding outward from foundations that had fundamentally changed during those stretched days of infinity. The connection to Eon blazed a hundredfold brighter than it had been, golden rivers crashing into his existence with intensity that painted the destroyed battlefield in hues of impossible brilliance.","Both Noah and Ozymandias moved in perfect synchrony.","Their bodies shifted simultaneously, the titanic frame of Ozymandias and the comparatively small form of Noah turning toward Grimvault with unified intent that declared their shared purpose. The changes from THE Infinite Cause were already beginning to bloom through their connected existence, transformation accelerating in ways that objective time had never witnessed before.","Noah’s voice emerged from both mouths at once.","\" Grimvault.\"","The word boomed across the battlefield from two sources simultaneously, his primary body and Ozymandias speaking as one entity despite their separate forms.","\" Let me see what Calymmian is all about!\"","BOOM!","Both bodies surged toward the most powerful entity on the enemy side.","The discrepancy in power was absurd. Grimvault stood at the Calymmian Tier with ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone saturation and four Proterozoic Organs.","Noah was technically still at THE First Scale , and even Ozymandias at Rhyacian couldn’t match that density of transformed existence. Charging directly at such a being should have been suicide.","Noah didn’t care.","Naldine sighed behind him as she watched his charge begin. She knew she couldn’t change his mind, knew that arguing would accomplish nothing against someone who had just acknowledged his own birth as a Cause equal to those that formed Observable Existences. This crazy fucker.","He had to for sure be mad from Infinity already!","Her fingers found the strings of her Vihuela as she turned her gaze coldly toward...Vahrkosis.","\"I suppose we each have our roles to play,\" she murmured.","THE Primordial Paradox stretched his obsidian titanic form beside where Noah had been standing, joints crackling with authority that pressed against the destroyed battlefield. He turned his attention toward Sammarthiel, toward those six wings of burning and frozen swords, toward the being who claimed Paradox as his Civilization just as Erwin did.","\" The Paradox Bearer ,\" he said with voice that held amusement beneath its ancient weight. \" Let us see whose contradictions run deeper.\"","The battle divided into three parts!"]},{"number":5092,"title":"Chapter 5092: Chapter 5091: Evolution I","paragraphs":["Noah and Ozymandias reached Grimvault in the span of a heartbeat, both bodies closing the distance with speed. The wolf-helmed Primordial Architect observed their approach with those pale fires burning in his empty eye sockets, and he raised his Axiom greatsword with a casual motion that suggested he found their charge more entertaining than threatening.","\"I will beat you to paste first,\" Grimvault declared, his deep voice pressing against reality itself, \" and collect what remains of your weavings to bring to THE Wyld. There, they will study what made you so interesting before your existence ends.\"","His greatsword descended with a terrifying force that warped the space around its trajectory.","\" Here is my pure Civilization. Just feel it!\"","BOOM!","The impact was devastating.","Noah’s transformed right hand, THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp, caught the flat of that descending blade alongside Ozymandias’s matching grip. Seas of blue Infinity converged on their palms as they met the weapon of a Calymmian Tier entity, that impossible force pressing against hands that should have been obliterated by mere proximity to such power.","Quintessence Infiniforce blazed from both bodies in configurations of multiple colors, the endless generation of his unique force type flooding outward in response to the strain being placed upon his existence!","Golden Observable force surged within Noah’s foundations as Eon’s connection provided density that his Bounded classification couldn’t naturally produce.","And then the impact truly registered.","Both Noah and Ozymandias buzzed with sensation that transcended pain, their connected existence vibrating at frequencies that existence wasn’t designed to accommodate. In that instant, it felt like every bone in their bodies was about to break. Every single one. Not cracking or fracturing but shattering entirely, reduced to powder beneath force that Calymmian entities wielded as casually as normal beings might swing a stick.","Noah felt every cell preparing to rupture as the pain was unfathomable!","Pain! Pain! PAIN!","His skin wanted to tear. His muscles wanted to liquefy. His organs wanted to burst apart into configurations that could no longer be called organs. The force Grimvault had delivered through that single swing was enough to extinguish First Scale entities by the thousands, and he’d taken it directly into his hands.","But Observable force surged.","Golden light flooded into every cell that was breaking, into every structure that was failing, into every component of his existence that Grimvault’s attack was destroying. The concentration was terrifying, density exceeding anything he’d experienced before as Eon’s enhanced connection provided resources that his Bounded classification could never have generated independently.","The cells regenerated instantly.","New cells replaced destroyed ones before destruction could complete. His bones were breaking and reforming simultaneously, his organs were rupturing and rebuilding in the same instant, his entire existence was undergoing cycles of annihilation and rebirth compressed into spans so short that objective time couldn’t properly measure them.","He paradoxically underwent simultaneous destruction and rebirth of all cells while also not undergoing either, both states existing in the same moment through depths of his Civilization he could now perceive at five percent access. THE First Tongue was the language of Existence itself, and at five percent, he could speak words of self-definition that rewrote what was happening to his body even as it happened.","And when that paradox resolved, every cell in his body was blindingly new.","Grander than what had existed before.","All bones within his body began to shine simultaneously.","| Miniature Cause Triggered.|","|Classification: THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth.|","|Nature: Internal evolutionary acceleration.|","|Unlike something like THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity which produces external phenomena across Observable Existence, this Cause operates strictly within your existence. External force of sufficient magnitude triggers accelerated transformation. The greater the force received, the more comprehensive the evolution.|","|Initial Catalyst: Impact from Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale entity.|","|Result: Force sufficient to extinguish your existence has instead catalyzed universal Hadean transformation.|","|All bones within your existence are now being saturated with Observable force and Quintessence Infiniforce at concentrations exceeding previous parameters.|","|Current Progress: All Bones toward Hadean Classification: 3%.|","...!","Oh!","Noah and Ozymandias both roared.","BOOM!","They rebuffed the immense strike, pushing Grimvault’s Axiom greatsword away from their shining palms with force that shouldn’t have been possible from beings at their classification. The wolf-helmed Primordial Architect didn’t stumble, didn’t even shift his stance, but those pale fires in his empty eye sockets flickered with something that might have been surprise.","Then he smiled.","That wolf skull helm somehow conveyed amusement despite possessing no features capable of expression, and when he spoke, his deep voice held genuine entertainment.","\" Interesting .\"","He lowered his greatsword slightly, observing the golden light radiating from Noah’s existence.","\" It seems you really are something unique in Observable Existence. How can you survive the pure force of Calymmian? For a second there, I thought I felt like I destroyed everything of your small body.\"","His smile widened beneath that helm.","\" Come, take another strike! A true strike!\"","BOOM!","Grimvault swung his Axiom weapon again, and this time it shone with light that seemed to contain depths beyond what the previous attack had carried. The greatsword blazed with authority that declared its nature to anyone capable of perceiving it, the complete Axiom that Noah had detected during his initial analysis now revealing capabilities that simple observation couldn’t have predicted.","Noah and Ozymandias raised their shining hands to meet the blow.","As if Grimvault was a hammer and they were weapons being forged, they would use his attacks to refine themselves.","BOOM!","The impact landed with force exceeding the previous strike, and Noah once more felt every cell within his body nearly extinguish, or really, paradoxically fully extinguish and not extinguish. Golden light of Observable force actually formed into liquid seas around his existence as he sought to resist power grander than before.","But something was different this time.","The Axiom Grimvault carried held a devastating light that seemed to bring cycles upon cycles of destruction, attacks replicating within the span of the initial impact in configurations that normal weapons couldn’t produce.","|Axiom Identified: THE Octogenary Echo.|","|Classification: Complete Axiom of Multiplicative Force.|","|Capability: Any force exerted through this weapon is replicated 81 times within the span of 1 nanosecond following initial contact.|","|Current Status: Replication sequence initiating.|","|You will experience the full force of Grimvault’s strike 81 times in the next nanosecond.|","|Brace yourself.|","...!","The blows came.","One. Two. Three!","Each impact carried the same devastating force as the initial strike, the same power that had nearly extinguished Noah’s entire existence compressed into spans so short that normal perception couldn’t register them as separate events. His bones screamed with stress that should have shattered them into dust. His organs wailed with strain that should have liquefied them entirely.","Four. Five. Six. Seven!","Observable force flooded in with each cycle of destruction, golden light rebuilding what the previous impact had broken before the next impact could find weakness in damaged structures. Quintessence Infiniforce generated endlessly within his foundations, providing resources that the transformation required regardless of how quickly those resources were being consumed.","Eight. Nine. Ten. Eleven. Twelve!","Noah’s expression shone with glory as he felt his bones and existence taking in the force once, twice, three times, twelve times, twenty times. Each individual attack was capable of destroying him. Each blow carried sufficient power to end his existence permanently. And yet the endless generation of Observable force and Quintessence Infiniforce rebuilt him stronger with every cycle.","Thirty. Thirty-one. Thirty-two!","This terrifying capability of an Axiom that should have been deadly was actually accelerating his growth! Oh!","Every booming cycle of destruction bathed every atom within him with Observable force and Quintessence Infiniforce!","Fifty. Fifty-one. Fifty-two!","Everything about the old him was being washed away. Every cell that had existed before this battle was being replaced with something new, something grander, something saturated with forces that his previous existence couldn’t have contained.","Seventy. Seventy-one. Seventy-two!","This new him was being forged with every impact, filled to the brim with more Infiniforce and Observable Force than he’d ever possessed, density increasing with each cycle of the Octogenary Echo’s devastating replication.","Eighty. Eighty-one.","|THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth: Comprehensive Evolution Triggered.|","|The Miniature Cause within you has expanded its scope.|","|All organs and components of your existence are now included in the transformation toward Hadean classification. Every aspect of your being is being filled with increasingly dense concentrations of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force.|","|Hadean Transformation Progress Report:|","|Skeletal Structure:|","|Right Hand (THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp): 100% Complete.|","|Right Arm (Radius, Ulna, Humerus): 67% Complete.|","|Left Hand: 34% Complete.|","|Left Arm: 19% Complete.|","|Right Leg (Femur, Patella, Tibia, Fibula, Tarsals, Metatarsals, Phalanges): 28% Complete.|","|Left Leg: 24% Complete.|","|Spine (Cervical, Thoracic, Lumbar, Sacral, Coccygeal Vertebrae): 15% Complete.|","|Ribcage (12 pairs of ribs, Sternum): 12% Complete.|","|Skull (Cranium, Facial Bones): 8% Complete.|","|Pelvis (Ilium, Ischium, Pubis): 11% Complete.|","|Organ Systems:|","|Heart: 4% Hadean Saturation.|","|Lungs: 3% Hadean Saturation.|","|Brain: 6% Hadean Saturation (benefiting from connection to Ozymandias’s THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation).|","|Liver: 2% Hadean Saturation.|","|Kidneys: 2% Hadean Saturation.|","|Overall Hadean Transformation: 17%.|","|Rate of transformation is dependent on external force received. Current catalyst: Calymmian Tier attacks through THE Octogenary Echo.|","|At current rate of combat intensity, full Hadean transformation may complete within this battle.|","The prompts rained down through Noah’s awareness as time seemed to slow around him.","He felt every painful impact and very rebirth. And man, it was painful!","In his perception, multicolored and golden waves of light emerged in repetitive sequence with him at the center, explosions of brilliance cascading outward as Grimvault’s Axiom delivered force that would have ended lesser existences eighty-one times over.","After every burst of light, his existence felt unfathomably grander.","More than thirty hours to fully forge his Hadean Bones?","Fuck that number completely.","If Grimvault was formidable enough, he might have all Hadean Bones within this single battle. If the Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect kept swinging that devastating Axiom, kept delivering force sufficient to trigger THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth over and over, he might achieve transformation that should have required hours in the span of minutes.","Oh!","This was Adversity!","Adversity was oh so sweet!","He wasn’t a masochist who liked being beaten. Really.","He didn’t enjoy pain for its own sake, didn’t seek suffering because suffering felt good. But as of this moment, feeling his existence shatter and rebuild stronger with every impact, watching his bones transform toward Hadean classification through force that should have killed him, he was a big fan of adversity.","Bring more of it on!","Bring someone else like Grimvault! Bring another Calymmian Proterozoic Scale being if possible! Bring someone at even higher tiers, at classifications that most couldn’t imagine!","Bring it all!","\" OOOH!\"","Every atom within him seethed with immensity and roared with voices that transcended physical sound. Golden seas erupted from his existence and shone across the destroyed battlefield, Observable force radiating outward in waves that painted reality itself in hues of transformation and glory.","Grimvault observed this display with those pale fires burning brighter in his empty eye sockets.","His smile hadn’t faded.","If anything, it had grown wider."]},{"number":5093,"title":"Chapter 5093: Chapter 5092: Evolution II","paragraphs":["A lot of Existences mention the glory before battle and silence after it. The glory belongs to those who survive long enough to claim it. The silence belongs to those who learned the truth.","The truth that darkness does not care about strength or conviction or righteousness. It comes for all equally, and when it arrives, every being discovers the same terrible knowledge: they were never prepared for the cold or for the absence.","Not for the regret that blooms in the space where hope used to reside. The casualties of war are the final thoughts of beings who finally understood they should have chosen differently, and understood it exactly one moment too late.","-Reflections on War.","---","Naldine observed the impossible.","Her fingers rested on the strings of her Vihuela as she watched Noah and Ozymandias meet Grimvault’s second strike head-on, golden light exploding outward from the impact. She could perceive what was happening to his existence even from this distance, could sense the cycles of destruction and rebirth cascading through his foundations with each blow the Calymmian entity delivered.","He was growing stronger explosively with every impact that should have killed him!","And he...hadn’t even used the Pulse he theorized yet.","What manner of existence was he?","She’d lived for eons among Primordial Architects, had witnessed beings at classifications that most couldn’t imagine, had herself achieved advancement that placed her among the distinguished of THE Wyld. But she’d never seen anything like what he was doing right now...","\"THE WHORISH NALDINE!\"","BOOM!","The roar shattered her contemplation.","Vahrkosis surged toward her with those forty-seven arms raised, each one wielding distinct pieces of an Axiom that blazed with entropic authority. His serpentine coils undulated through the air with speed that belied his massive form, and his voice emerged with fury.","\" Focus on our grand battle! Do you think yourself so far above me that you can divide your attention? I am THE Primordial Dirge! I have consumed civilizations while you were still learning to pluck strings!\"","His face, that shifting mass of features at the apex of his coils, settled into configuration of rage that seemed almost personal.","\" Or perhaps you wish to watch that little bundle of Infinity die? Perhaps you’ve grown attached during whatever time you spent together? THE WHORISH NALDINE, pining after something that should not exist!\"","...!","Those words landed heavily.","Naldine’s singularity-dotted eyes turned from Noah’s battle with coldness that could have frozen stars. Her fingers, which had been resting gently on her Vihuela’s strings, pressed down with precision. Her expression, which had held analytical interest moments before, became something that made even Vahrkosis pause his charge despite his rage.","She plucked a single string.","HUUM!","The note that emerged was authority given audible form, a frequency that pressed against existence itself with command. The note washed over Vahrkosis and his serpentine coils froze mid-undulation, those forty-seven arms suspended in positions!","He was held through something he couldn’t perceive or resist!","His form remained locked in place as Naldine rose from her position, her Vihuela’s strings still resonating with frequencies that kept him immobilized while she prepared what came next.","\" You hear words others have spoken and choose to use them as well? You call me whorish,\" she said, her voice emerging cold and measured despite the fury burning beneath her expression. \" You, who have consumed and destroyed and violated across eons of existence, dare to speak of me with such words?\"","Her left hand, the one that had been her arm before she transformed it into her instrument, began to move.","Her fingers moved through the air as if writing upon reality itself, tracing symbols that existed in no language most beings could perceive. Each motion left trails of blue gold light that hung suspended, configurations that suggested letters being formed.","Her index finger drew a vertical line downward. Her middle finger curved around it in spiral that suggested revision. Her ring finger slashed horizontally through what had been written, not erasing but transforming. Her smallest finger added new strokes that changed the meaning of the entire inscription.","She was writing.","She was rewriting!","And when the somatic component completed, her voice emerged with verbal utterance that pressed against the foundations of reality itself.","\" Cambrian Scribe, First of Words.\"","The light around her fingers blazed brighter.","\"I speak the Thread. I rewrite the Thread.\"","The inscribed symbols began to pulse with authority that exceeded what even Proterozoic Scale entities could typically produce.","\" What was shall mean another. What ended shall end differently.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes locked onto Vahrkosis’s frozen form with intensity that seemed to perceive not just what he was, but what he had been and what he could become.","\" THE CAMBRIAN WORD.\"","BOOM!","The Pulse manifested.","It was not fire like THE Silurian Light. It was not erasure or unwinding or destruction of causality. It was transformation of meaning itself, the fundamental restructuring of what consequences attached to what actions. Blue gold light erupted from Naldine’s inscribed symbols and washed over Vahrkosis with force that passed through his defenses as if they didn’t exist.","Because they didn’t exist against this.","Pulses operated on levels that normal authority couldn’t touch. They drew power from Causes themselves, from the originating forces that had formed Observable Existences, and no amount of Proterozoic Bones or Organs could provide resistance against something so fundamental.","Vahrkosis felt it immediately.","His serpentine coils began to unravel conceptually, the very meaning of his existence being rewritten by authority that exceeded his capacity to resist. The forty-seven arms that had wielded pieces of an Axiom began dissolving not into nothing but into something else, their purpose being changed from violence to dissolution, their function being rewritten from attack to self-destruction.","\" What... what is this?\"","His voice emerged with horror that pressed against the destroyed battlefield.","\" Stop...stop!!!\"","He could feel it. Every action he had ever taken was being rewritten not in occurrence but in consequence. The civilizations he had consumed were still consumed, but the strength he had gained from them was being redirected, transformed, changed from fuel for his power into fuel for his dissolution. The Proterozoic Bones he had forged were still forged, but their purpose was being rewritten from enhancement to entropy.","\" You do not know a Pulse ,\" Naldine said, her voice cold as she watched him unravel. \" You have existed for eons, have consumed countless beings, have achieved classification that most cannot imagine. And yet you never touched the depths required to perceive what Pulses are, never achieved access sufficient to find where they reside.\"","Her fingers plucked another string, and the rewriting accelerated.","\" THE Whorish Naldine. Those were your words.\"","Vahrkosis’s coils were dissolving now, that serpentine mass collapsing into transformation. He was becoming something other than what he had been, his existence being rewritten!","\" The consequence of those words ,\" Naldine continued, \" has been rewritten. You spoke them intending to diminish me, to anger me, to distract me from your attack. But now those words mean something else. Now they mean that you chose to provoke someone who possesses THE Cambrian Word.\"","\" Please...\"","The word emerged from features that were losing coherence, from a face that was being rewritten into something that could no longer produce speech.","\"I do not hear pleas, \" Naldine said. \"I hear only the sound of causality being corrected.\"","She watched as THE Primordial Dirge, that Rhyacian Tier Proterozoic Scale entity, unraveled completely. His forty-seven arms had become nothing. His serpentine coils had dissolved into authority that dispersed across the destroyed battlefield. His Proterozoic Bones and Organ remained, falling through the air where his form had once occupied space, multicolored brilliance declaring their nature even as their owner ceased to exist in any meaningful sense.","Vahrkosis was gone.","Not erased like THE Silurian Light would have accomplished, not removed from causality entirely. He still existed in memory, still existed in consequence, still existed in the damage he had caused across his long existence. But his continuation had been rewritten. His future had been transformed into dissolution. His existence had been edited to end at this exact moment through words that rewrote what his choices meant.","Naldine lowered her Vihuela.","And the battlefield...became eerily silent as many turned to her!"]},{"number":5094,"title":"Chapter 5094: Chapter 5093: Evolution III","paragraphs":["The battlefield fell silent.","THE Primordial Paradox observed Vahrkosis’s dissolution with appreciation. The serpentine mass that had been THE Primordial Dirge was simply gone, unraveled by authority that Pulses provided and normal Proterozoic classification couldn’t resist.","Forty-seven arms had become nothing. Coils that had undulated with entropic menace now existed only as memory and scattered Proterozoic material falling through empty air that Naldine collected!","Naldine Manthon had just eliminated a Rhyacian Tier entity in seconds.","Even Grimvault paused his assault on Noah to gaze toward where his companion had stood. Those pale fires burning in his wolf skull helm flickered with cold fury that pressed against the destroyed battlefield, and for an instant, that devastating Axiom stopped swinging.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled.","This was his moment.","He wasn’t the most powerful entity present. He knew that with certainty!","Grimvault exceeded him tremendously. Even Sammarthiel, the being he currently faced, possessed more Proterozoic Bones and Organs than he did. In a direct confrontation of power against power, he would lose. He would fall. He would become another casualty of a battle.","But THE Primordial Paradox had never believed in direct confrontation.","Paradox was his Civilization. Contradiction was his authority. And the greatest contradiction of combat was this: the moment your enemy stopped paying attention was the moment they had already lost, even if victory still appeared to be within their grasp.","Sammarthiel’s beautiful and terrible features were turned toward where Vahrkosis had dissolved. Those wings of burning and frozen swords had ceased their constant motion, thousands of blades suspended in configurations of shock rather than readiness. His attention was divided between the horror of watching an ally unravel and the fury of recognizing that Naldine possessed capabilities none of them had anticipated.","That division was everything.","THE Primordial Paradox moved without sound.","His obsidian titanic form surged forward with speed that contradicted his massive size, Rhyacian Proterozoic power flooding through foundations that had been enhanced by something most beings couldn’t comprehend. The Bounded Countable Infinity he’d obtained from Osmont blazed within his existence with blue light that wove through his authority!","He wasn’t merely Paradox anymore.","He was Paradox touched by Infinity. He was contradiction given endless recursion. He was the impossible made more impossible through forces that his Civilization had integrated rather than rejected.","His Proterozoic chest bone began to shine.","The light that emerged was something else entirely, illumination that seemed to exist and not exist simultaneously, brightness that was also darkness, visibility that was also concealment. The bone pulsed with authority that declared its paradoxical nature to anything capable of perceiving such depths.","Sammarthiel sensed the attack one instant too late.","The Paradox Bearer turned from his observation of Vahrkosis’s fate, those twin blades of flame and frost rising in defensive configuration as he recognized that THE Primordial Paradox had moved. But recognition wasn’t prevention. Awareness wasn’t escape!","He could see the paradoxical light surging toward him and still be unable to avoid what that light represented.","\"You dare-...!\"","The words cut off as...Schrodinger’s Tomb enveloped him.","Its capabilities were actually rather simple.","The Target is enclosed in state of fundamental uncertainty. Until observation occurs or the target breaks free through sufficient force, they exist in superposition of alive and dead simultaneously. The longer they remain in this state, the more their existence becomes entangled with the paradox itself. Extended exposure causes progressive dissolution of certainty regarding their own continuation!","It wasn’t a cage in the physical sense. There were no bars, no walls, no boundaries that could be perceived through normal observation. Instead, Sammarthiel simply became uncertain. His form flickered between presence and absence, between continuation and cessation, between the alive state and the dead state without settling on either.","He was trapped in the space between outcomes.","And the longer he remained there, the more that space would consume what he understood himself to be.","THE Primordial Paradox observed his work with satisfaction. Sammarthiel struggled within the Tomb, those six wings of swords attempting to cut through uncertainty itself, but you couldn’t cut what didn’t exist in definable form. You couldn’t burn or freeze or destroy a state of being that was simultaneously every state and no state at all.","He should’ve never allowed this cage to form as he was powerful enough to evade it!","But he...was distracted.","And as of this moment...","Two Rhyacian Tier Proterozoic Scale entities were both out of commission.","THE Primordial Paradox floated grandly above the destroyed battlefield, his obsidian form radiating authority that declared his classification to all who could perceive it. He didn’t possess Pulses. He didn’t channel powers derived from Causes that formed Observable Existences. But he possessed something that Pulses couldn’t replicate and overwhelming force couldn’t overcome.","He possessed understanding of contradiction itself.","Victory and defeat were merely states that observers assigned to outcomes after those outcomes had been determined. But what happened when determination itself became uncertain? What happened when the very concept of winning or losing became entangled with paradox that refused to resolve into either?","This battle was neither won nor lost.","He thought about what Paradox meant at its deepest levels.","Most beings understood contradiction as opposition. Light against dark. Life against death. Victory against defeat. They saw paradox as tension between states that couldn’t coexist, as problems requiring resolution rather than conditions to be embraced.","THE Primordial Paradox knew better.","Contradiction... was completion. Light didn’t fight darkness as it moreso it defined it. Life didn’t battle death...it required it. And victory didn’t triumph over defeat; it existed only because defeat was possible.","This battle existed in that space between.","Not won and not lost, but simply continuing in uncertainty that favored those who understood uncertainty better than their enemies.","He turned his gaze toward Grimvault, toward that wolf skull helm with its burning pale fires.","What...would the ancient Primordial Architect do now?","---","Grimvault’s eyes flashed cold.","Noah observed the shift in that wolf skull helm’s pale fires, watched the amusement drain away and something far more dangerous take its place. The Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect had been playing before.","But Vahrkosis was gone now, unraveled by Naldine’s Pulse. Sammarthiel was trapped in paradoxical uncertainty, flickering between alive and dead without resolution.","Grimvault was alone.","And alone, he stopped playing!","His left hand rose with speed that should have been impossible for something so massive. His palm faced outward, fingers spread wide as if preparing to grasp something that existed beyond physical perception. The gesture held stillness that seemed almost reverent, a warrior preparing to unleash a weapon that had been waiting since before Observable Existence learned to observe.","Then his fingers began to move.","The first motion was a curling inward, each finger bending in sequence from smallest to largest as if he were grasping threads of reality itself. His hand drew backward in a pulling motion, those invisible threads gathering in his palm like strands of causality being unraveled from the weaving that held them in place.","...!","Noah’s gaze became heavy!","His palm rotated slowly, drawing a circle in the air that suggested reversal, regression, the unwinding of time flowing backward against its natural current. The motion was ancient, gestures that seemed to have existed before gestures were possible!","Noah could see it!","He could see the threads!","That was the terrifying part. He could actually see what Grimvault was grasping, could perceive the strands of causality being gathered in that armored palm, could witness the fundamental forces being prepared for deployment. His enhanced Civilizational Access showed him exactly what was coming.","Grimvault’s fingers snapped outward in a flicking motion, releasing whatever he had gathered while simultaneously reaching toward something distant. Then his hand closed into a fist, authority condensing!","His fist opened.","His fingers spread as fire would bloom from kindling, and his voice emerged with words that pressed against existence itself.","\" Silurian Ember, First of Flames.\"","The air began to burn with light that shouldn’t have existed.","\"I grasp the Thread. I burn the Thread.\"","Colors that had no names blazed outward from his spreading fingers!","\" What was shall be unwritten, what stood shall stand no more.\"","The light intensified until looking at it became difficult even for beings at Proterozoic classification.","\" THE SILURIAN LIGHT.\"","BOOM!","The Pulse emerged in its full grandeur.","It wasn’t merely fire or light. It was something that existed at the intersection of both while transcending either, a manifestation of THE Silurian Cause itself reduced to pale imitation that remained devastating despite its diminished state!","The brilliance roared outward from Grimvault’s extended hand like an emerging Cause, like the birth of an Observable Existence compressed into weapon form as it was directed towards...Naldine and THE Primordial Paradox!","Noah’s gaze became stern and somber.","This wasn’t playful anymore!","Grimvault had targeted both Naldine and THE Primordial Paradox with authority that would erase their causality entirely, would unwrite their existence until not even memory remained. The light surged toward them in twin streams of impossible brilliance, each one carrying force sufficient to unmake beings who had survived eons of existence.","Naldine’s singularity-dotted eyes widened as she sensed death approaching. Her fingers moved toward her Vihuela’s strings, but THE Cambrian Word required time she didn’t have. The rewriting Pulse couldn’t intercept an erasing Pulse when the erasing Pulse had already been released!","THE Primordial Paradox’s obsidian form flickered with paradoxical light as he attempted to apply contradiction to what was coming. But THE Silurian Light didn’t care about paradox. It didn’t care about alive or dead states. It simply erased, and erasure transcended the philosophical frameworks that Paradox operated within!","Both of them roared with defiance that couldn’t change what was approaching!","And then...","And then Noah appeared in front of Naldine.","And Ozymandias appeared in front of THE Primordial Paradox.","Both bodies moved simultaneously!","Noah positioned himself directly in the path of the Silurian stream targeting Naldine while Ozymandias blocked the stream targeting THE Primordial Paradox.","His expression was unfathomably calm.","Time seemed to slow as he looked at the blinding light of THE Silurian Light approaching his existence. The brilliance filled his perception with colors that shouldn’t have been capable of existing simultaneously!","It was...beautiful, and it was truly terrifying. It was..exactly what he’d been searching for.","He wasn’t one for sacrifices.","That had never been his nature. He didn’t throw himself in front of attacks to protect others out of noble impulse or heroic instinct. He wasn’t sacrificing himself right now, wasn’t offering his existence to preserve theirs. That kind of thinking belonged to beings who didn’t understand what he understood about himself.","He wanted to see.","He wanted to feel what a Pulse was all about.","That...was how confident he was about his own existence.","If it was a terrifying adversity even more than the swing of Grimvault’s weapon, all the better. If it carried force sufficient to trigger THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth at accelerations that exceeded what THE Octogenary Echo had provided, even better still.","But more than wanting to survive it, he wanted to know if he could take it.","In life, you had to do dangerous things if you wanted things to change drastically. You had to take bigger risks if you wanted bigger rewards. You couldn’t grow into something unprecedented by following safe paths that others had already mapped. You had to step into the unknown and let the unknown do its worst.","And he...wanted things to change drastically.","The Hadean Bones throughout his body blazed brighter as THE Silurian Light approached. Observable force surged through his existence in concentrations that exceeded anything he’d channeled before. Quintessence Infiniforce flooded outward from his foundations in waves of multicolored brilliance that met the approaching erasure like a tide meeting a shore.","Could he take it?","He was about to find out.","\" FOOL!\"","Grimvault’s roar echoed across the destroyed battlefield with genuine alarm. The Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect actually stepped forward as if he could recall what he had already released.","\"I never intended to use THE Silurian Light on you! There are too many unknowns if you are erased!\"","...!","But it was too late for intentions.","The streams of impossible brilliance had already crossed the distance.","The light touched both of Noah’s bodies simultaneously.","And existence...became unfathomably silent!"]},{"number":5095,"title":"Chapter 5095: Chapter 5094: What Gives You The Right?! I","paragraphs":["<Exerpt from an Echoes of THE First Cause>","\"The adversity that breaks all others shall forge him. The hardship that ends all paths shall begin his. The Scales demand what the Scales demand, and he shall pay in currencies that have not yet been minted.","Three times shall he face the mirror of undoing. Three times shall he choose between becoming and unbecoming. Three times shall the answer be the same, and three times shall the answer be different.","In the end, which is also the beginning, the Infinite shall stand before the Undefined. And only one shall remain to tell the tale that no one shall hear.","This is an Echo of First Cause.","This is what shall come to pass, for it has already passed, and it shall pass again.","The wheel turns. The river flows. The question echoes.","He shall be the answer, or he shall be nothing.","Or he shall be the question that ends all answers.\"","---","There exists a term for those who find pleasure in pain.","Algophilist!","From the word algos, meaning pain, and philos, meaning lover. One who loves suffering. One who seeks agony not as means to an end but as the end itself. The sensation of hurt becomes indistinguishable from the sensation of joy, and they pursue both with equal fervor because to them, both are the same.","Noah Osmont...was not an algophilist!","---","Silence.","All of existence turned silent as for the first time, Noah became the target of a Pulse of The Scales. THE Silurian Light touched him, and in that instant, he understood what Alexander had felt when Beowulf tortured him across millions of subjective years. Every Existential Nociceptor within his existence activated simultaneously, every pain receptor screaming with immensity and entered territories that most beings couldn’t survive experiencing.","Pain.","Real pain. Not the cycles of destruction and rebirth that Grimvault’s weapon had provided. Not the shattering and reforming that THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth had transformed into fuel for advancement. This was something else entirely, agony that existed at the level of causality itself, suffering that came from having your very existence told it should never have been.","And Noah defiantly felt all of it.","He didn’t defend or retreat. He didn’t channel Infinity or Observable force to resist what was happening. He wanted to feel this. He wanted to understand what a Pulse truly was, what it meant to have something derived from a Cause deployed against your existence. So he opened himself to the pain and focused through it with clarity that his previous transformations had provided.","His existence bellowed toward the Pulse in defiance.","What are you? What do you stand for?","HUUM!","The answer came in sensation. He felt himself being stared down by an unfathomable imperious gaze of endless potential, a presence so vast that his perception couldn’t find its edges. This was a Cause.","THE Silurian Cause itself, the First Ember that had ignited Observable Existences into being across the vastness of reality. The Pulse he faced was drawing power from that originating force, and when an entity was targeted by such a thing, they felt the immensity behind it.","The immensity of THE Silurian Cause.","It seemed that one could feel it and experience a semblance of it only when targeted for complete erasure. In that moment of tremendous pain, Noah understood what THE Silurian Cause actually was.","It was fire before fire existed. It was ignition before anything could burn. It was the spark! It had birthed Observable Existences, had provided the template for reality, had established the foundations upon which all current existence stood.","And it wanted him gone.","|Understanding Achieved.|","|You have experienced direct contact with THE Silurian Cause through exposure to THE Silurian Light.|","|This Cause represents: Primordial ignition. The authority to declare existence into being, and therefore, the authority to declare existence into unbeing.|","|Knowledge of this Cause has been seared into your foundations. You now possess comprehension of THE Silurian Cause at foundational level.|","|This comprehension may enable future derivations if sufficient resonance is established.|","And after he experienced this Cause, after that moment of understanding bloomed through his awareness, he began to feel what came next.","Every atom within his existence screamed.","They were set aflame by that terrifying fiery light, burned by authority that had ignited Observable Existences and could therefore extinguish anything within them. The light pressed against every particle of what he was with a declaration that expected obedience.","Be erased.","Disappear.","Your existence has never been and will never be.","BEGONE!","HUUM!","His cells screamed. His existence screamed. And all of this was happening in the span of an instant, destruction cascading through his foundations at speeds that objective time couldn’t properly measure. He could feel his causality beginning to unravel, could sense the threads connecting his past to his present to his future being grasped by that fiery authority and pulled apart.","With Noah at the center, cracks bloomed in four directions!","BOOM!","The fractures spread outward from his existence like lightning frozen in glass, extending toward horizons that didn’t exist in normal space. His unraveling was unraveling existence itself, Infinity responding to the erasure of its bearer by threatening to take everything else with it. The cracks stretched infinitely in four different directions, north and south and east and west, reality itself protesting what was being done to someone so thoroughly entangled with its foundations.","Grimvault went pale beneath that wolf skull helm.","Those pale fires in his empty eye sockets flickered! The ancient Primordial Architect shook his head at this scene, recognizing that collapsing every causality of the Infinity-bearer could have untold consequences that extended far beyond this battlefield!","Noah’s existence was roaring out in response to the unfathomable pain and unwinding of his very causality. Every part of what he was said no.","A declaration of absolute refusal that pressed back against the Pulse with authority that came from somewhere deeper than his current classification could explain.","His Quintessence Infiniforce said no.","His Observable Force said no.","His connection to Infinity said no.","THE First Tongue said no.","THE Infiniverse said no.","And then Noah heard something else. A voice that didn’t belong to any system or Civilization or cosmic force. A voice he recognized from years of hearing it call him to dinner, wake him for school, comfort him through nightmares that childhood had provided.","His mother.","\" How dare you?!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5096,"title":"Chapter 5096: Chapter 5095: What Gives You The Right?! II","paragraphs":["Amelia Osmont, THE Originator of THE Infinite Cause, raged from wherever she existed within THE Infiniverse. Her voice crashed through Noah’s awareness with fury, the primal anger of a mother watching something try to erase her child. How dare they try to unmake what she had carried for nine months? How dare they try to unwrite what she had raised through sleepless nights and double shifts and years of sacrifice?!","How dare they?!","At such a moment, Noah’s eyes released blinding beams of light.","He dared to ask the Pulse of The Scales, the Pulse backed by THE Silurian Cause, a question that no one had ever asked while being targeted for erasure. His voice emerged not as sound but as existence itself bellowing toward the force that was trying to unmake him.","\" What gives you the right?!\"","WAA!","What gave this Cause the authority to unravel his causality? His very being? Was this Cause grander than his Cause? Was THE Silurian Cause so absolutely superior to THE Infinite Cause that it could simply declare him nonexistent and have that declaration stick?","His body surrounded itself in radiant magma-like light as THE Silurian Light continued its assault, flames that should have been erasing him instead illuminating his defiance for all to witness. He raised both arms, his primary body and Ozymandias moving in perfect synchrony despite the agony they both experienced.","And he roared with all of his existence.","Words emerged that nobody but himself and the force of THE Silurian Cause would hear, a challenge issued not to Grimvault but to the Cause behind Grimvault’s Pulse.","\" What makes your Cause grander?!\"","His voice tore through the flames surrounding him.","\" THE Infinite Cause gave its emergence to me! Can you say with Absolute Certainty that THE Silurian Cause is grander than THE Infinite Cause?!\"","The magma-light flickered.","\" That of the endless threads and weavings of Causality, of past, present, and future, THE Infinite Cause is not grander than THE Silurian Cause?!\"","HUUM!","His existence shone with blinding blue gold light that pushed back against the flames trying to erase him. Instead of fighting against the Pulse itself, he pitted the force behind it against his own Cause. Not power against power. Not authority against authority. But certainty against certainty.","Could THE Silurian Cause say with absolute conviction that it would always be grander than THE Infinite Cause? Because Noah’s growth wasn’t done. His trajectory wasn’t complete. THE Infinite Cause had already produced a Seed of Observable Existence, had already demonstrated potential that rivaled what THE Silurian Cause itself represented.","Did it have absolute certainty?!","Could it prove, beyond any reasonable possible doubt, that THE Infinite Cause would never surpass it across the endless spans of future existence?!","HUUM!","A heavy silence came.","This silence was uncertainty. And if there was uncertainty, even the slightest doubt about the absolute superiority of one Cause over another, then THE Silurian Light couldn’t complete its erasure. It couldn’t unravel causality that might one day prove grander than its own origin. It couldn’t destroy potential that remained undefined.","\" OOOH!\"","Noah roared out with fervor as his voice permeated across existence, the sound of someone who had just challenged a Cause itself and found that Cause unable to answer with absolute conviction.","|Critical Interaction Resolved.|","|THE Silurian Cause behind THE Silurian Light cannot definitively and absolutely prove its sovereignty over THE Infinite Cause.|","|THE Infinite Cause has demonstrated trajectory of growth that makes future superiority possible, if not probable. Absolute certainty of permanent superiority cannot be established when one Cause continues to evolve while the other has already achieved its zenith.|","|Result: THE Silurian Cause cannot unravel THE Infinite Cause.|","| You have gained immunity from any unraveling force of causality derived from THE Silurian Cause and any Pulses of The Scales derived from it.|","|However.|","|THE Silurian Cause is and has been grander than THE Infinite Cause in current measurement. While you are immune to complete unraveling, the effects of THE Silurian Light are still expressed with terrifying immensity capable of destroying every particle of your existence.|","|This destruction triggers THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth.|","|This light is more than sufficient to continue undergoing endless cycles of destruction and reformation until your Hadean Organs and Bones complete their transformation.|","|Until your glorious evolution attains something new.|","|Persevere.|","...!","Noah saw all these prompts as his body continued blazing with magma-like light. He felt the flames of THE Silurian Light scorch every cell and atom of his existence in an instant, fire that couldn’t erase but could still destroy. And in that same instant, boundless Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force and Infinity surged into the destruction, regenerating everything that had been burned before the next wave of flames arrived.","A nanosecond later, the same thing happened again.","And again.","And again.","Visually, it seemed like the magma-like light of THE Silurian Light was simply burning him, flames wrapping around his form in configurations of destruction that should have been lethal. But a blast of blue gold brilliance flashed every nanosecond, explosions of reformation cascading outward from his existence with rhythm that only those who understood what was happening could perceive. Each flash signified a cycle of destruction and rebirth. Each burst of brilliance meant brand new cells across Noah’s body, grander than what had existed a nanosecond before.","Ozymandias underwent the same transformation.","His titanic form blazed with identical magma-light, flames of THE Silurian Light scorching every particle of his existence while blue gold brilliance regenerated what was lost. Both bodies burned. Both bodies reformed. Both bodies grew stronger with every nanosecond that passed.","But as the nanoseconds accumulated, something became clear to everyone watching.","He wasn’t unraveling.","His causality remained intact. His existence continued despite being targeted by a Pulse that should have erased him entirely. THE Silurian Light burned and burned and burned, but the being it burned refused to be unwritten.","Noah’s eyes opened wide on both bodies.","He looked out through flames that wreathed his existence, his gaze locking with Grimvault who stared back with utter incredulity and astonishment. Those pale fires in the wolf skull helm burned brighter than ever, but they burned with confusion rather than confidence.","Noah raised his right hand into a fist with both bodies, that gesture of defiance declaring something that shouldn’t have been possible.","\" Merely a Pulse of The Scales.\"","His voice emerged calm despite the flames still burning around him.","\" Merely THE Silurian Light.\"","His fists remained raised.","\"It seems that I am already immune to it.\"","BOOM!","His words battered all nearby existence like hammers striking reality itself. A Pulse couldn’t be denied. That was the fundamental truth that made Pulses so terrifying. They operated on levels that normal authority couldn’t touch, drew power from Causes that predated most current forces. Only another Pulse could potentially reverse or combat a Pulse!","But Noah hadn’t cast any Pulses.","So how was he alive?","How was his causality intact?","How was he still standing there with flames wreathing his existence, defiant and unbroken and growing stronger with every nanosecond that passed?","Nobody here knew that he hadn’t fought the Pulse itself. He’d fought the Cause behind it, had challenged THE Silurian Cause to prove its absolute superiority over THE Infinite Cause, and the Cause had been unable to provide that proof!","Naldine stared at him with a look of stupor.","In all her experience, across eons of existence among Primordial Architects and classifications that most couldn’t imagine, she couldn’t explain this. She didn’t know what this was!"]},{"number":5097,"title":"Chapter 5097: Chapter 5096: Destruction and Rebirth! I","paragraphs":["And at this time, as Noah underwent constant cycles of destruction and rebirth too fast to even be perceived, as his existence blazed with magma-light and blue gold brilliance in alternating rhythm that made his transformation accelerate beyond anything Grimvault’s weapon had provided, the system provided an update.","|THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth: Progress Update.|","|Current Catalyst: THE Silurian Light (Pulse-derived destruction at maximum intensity).|","|Rate of transformation has increased by factor of 47 compared to previous catalyst.|","|Hadean Transformation Progress Report:|","|Skeletal Structure:|","|Right Hand (THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Grasp): 100% Complete.|","|Right Arm (THE Hadean Arm of Infinite Reach - Radius, Ulna, Humerus): 100% Complete.|","|Left Hand (THE Hadean Hand of Infinite Will): 100% Complete.|","|Left Arm (Radius, Ulna, Humerus): 89% Complete.|","|Right Leg (Femur, Patella, Tibia, Fibula, Tarsals, Metatarsals, Phalanges): 78% Complete.|","|Left Leg: 71% Complete.|","|Spine (Cervical, Thoracic, Lumbar, Sacral, Coccygeal Vertebrae): 54% Complete.|","|Ribcage (12 pairs of ribs, Sternum): 48% Complete.|","|Skull (Cranium, Facial Bones): 39% Complete.|","|Pelvis (Ilium, Ischium, Pubis): 44% Complete.|","|Organ Systems:|","|Heart: 51% Hadean Saturation.|","|Lungs: 47% Hadean Saturation.|","|Brain: 58% Hadean Saturation (benefiting from connection to Ozymandias’s THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation).|","|Liver: 41% Hadean Saturation.|","|Kidneys: 38% Hadean Saturation.|","|Overall Hadean Transformation: 64%.|","|Note: THE Silurian Light’s scorching destructive power will continue to be more than sufficient for complete Hadean transformation. You simply need to persevere.|","|Estimated time to completion at current intensity: 4 minutes, 17 seconds.|","...!","|Additional Analysis: Anomalous Interaction Detected.|","|THE Silurian Light is designed to erase. THE Silurian Cause grants authority to declare existence into unbeing. To unravek causality. This is its nature. This is its purpose.|","|Your existence cannot be erased due to uncertainty regarding Cause superiority.|","|However, THE Silurian Light still seeks targets for its erasing authority.|","|Your Quintessence Infiniforce is redirecting this seeking.|","|Your Observable Force is guiding this authority.|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization is processing this power.|","|Result: THE Silurian Light is being channeled toward perceivable limitations within your existence rather than your existence itself.|","...!","His existence...was burning brightly!","Noah turned his gaze away from Grimvault.","The flames of THE Silurian Light still wreathed his existence in magma-like brilliance, still scorched every cell and atom of what he was, still provided the catalyst for transformation that accelerated with every passing nanosecond. But the destruction had become background noise now, fuel for advancement rather than threat to survival. He could observe other things while his existence burned and rebuilt itself endlessly.","THE Primordial Paradox floated nearby, obsidian form intact despite the chaos that had unfolded. Sammarthiel remained trapped in Schrodinger’s Tomb, flickering between alive and dead without resolution.","Naldine stood where she’d been when he intercepted THE Silurian Light, her singularity-dotted eyes wide with an expression he’d never seen on her imperious features. She was staring at him like she didn’t know what she was looking at anymore!","Both were safe.","Noah turned back to Grimvault.","The Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect stood frozen in place, those pale fires in his wolf skull helm burning with intensity that suggested internal conflict beyond what his massive armored form displayed. He’d just watched his Pulse fail to erase someone it should have unmade entirely!","He’d just witnessed an impossibility that violated everything he understood about how Causes and Pulses functioned.","And now Noah was looking at him with eyes that blazed blue gold through flames that couldn’t erase him.","\" Grimvault.\"","His voice emerged calm, as if he weren’t currently burning with the fire of a Cause that had birthed Observable Existences.","\"I want... to thank you.\"","Those pale fires flickered with confusion.","\" Many things today wouldn’t have been possible if not for you. When you arrived with your companions, I saw adversity in forms I hadn’t encountered before. When you swung THE Octogenary Echo, you provided force sufficient to trigger transformations. When you unleashed THE Silurian Light, you gave me contact with a Cause I needed to understand.\"","He raised one hand, flames dancing around his fingers as his existence continued its endless cycle of destruction and rebirth.","\" You have been a vessel of adversity. A hammer that forged rather than destroyed. A fire that tempered rather than consumed. Everything you threw at me became fuel for advancement you couldn’t have predicted. Every attack you delivered accelerated growth you couldn’t have imagined. You came here intending to beat me to paste and collect my weavings for THE Wyld, but instead you became the instrument of my evolution.\"","His smile held no warmth.","\" For that, I am genuinely grateful. You’ve completed your task well, Grimvault. You’ve served your purpose with magisterial excellence!\"","His eyes turned cold.","\" And now...you’re not needed anymore.\"","...!","Grimvault’s pale fires blazed with fury that pressed against the destroyed battlefield.","\" You incoherent fucking fool...\"","Noah didn’t respond with words.","He responded with motion.","His right hand rose slowly, index finger extended, flames of THE Silurian Light still wreathing his form in magma-like brilliance. The gesture was simple, almost casual, nothing like the complex somatic movements that Naldine had demonstrated for THE Silurian Light or THE Cambrian Word.","He drew the lemniscate.","His finger traced the symbol of infinity in the air before him, a horizontal figure-eight that looped back upon itself endlessly. The motion was elegant in its simplicity. Where his finger passed, blue gold light remained, the symbol hanging in the air with brilliance that pressed against everything within range.","The somatic component of THE Infinite Light required nothing more than this. No complex gestures. No sequences of movements that needed to be memorized. Just the symbol that represented his Cause, drawn with authority that came from being the product of that Cause.","And then his voice emerged with the verbal component.","\" Infinite Ember.\"","The lemniscate blazed brighter.","\" First Spark of my emergence.\"","Blue gold flames began spreading outward from the symbol.","\"I am the Thread. I am the Cause. What exists without the fire of painful birth shall know that fire now.\"","The flames intensified until looking at them became difficult even for beings at Proterozoic classification.","\" Let causality regress. Let existence remember its emergence. Let all that stands without the pained spark of life return to the moment before that spark was possible.\"","His voice rose with tyrannical authority that pressed against Grimvault’s existence itself.","\" THE INFINITE LIGHT.\"","BOOM!","The Pulse emerged.","It wasn’t like THE Silurian Light. It didn’t manifest as streams of targeted destruction or magma-like flames seeking specific victims. THE Infinite Light emerged as a form of massive and endlessly stretching blue gold flaming illumination that covered all space above for gigaparsecs, light that seemed to extend beyond what normal perception could measure.","The sky burned.","Reality itself seemed to ignite with brilliance that declared a new Cause had been expressed, a new Pulse had been born, a new authority had entered the catalogue of powers that could reshape existence itself. The blue gold flames stretched across distances that made the destroyed battlefield seem insignificant, covering space that most beings couldn’t traverse across lifetimes of travel.","And all of that pressure locked onto Grimvault.","|Pulse Activation: THE Infinite Light.|","|Source: THE Infinite Cause.|","|Wielder: Noah Osmont.|","|This Pulse burns with the fire of THE Infinite Cause, drawing upon every aspect of its origin to fuel its authority.|","|The fire of cellular division when two cells became one and then divided into countless more. The fire of metabolic combustion that sustained nine months of formation. The fire of first breath when oxygen flooded lungs that had never known air. The fire of first heartbeat when rhythm commenced and never stopped. The fire of first Mana when power entered a vessel that had known only mundane existence.|","|But more than physical fire, this Pulse burns with the fire of human experience.|","|The fire of a mother working double shifts while pregnant because her husband gambled away the rent. The fire of being born alone in a hospital room while the one who should have been there chose cards over his own child. The fire of growing up without certainty, without safety, without the assurances that privilege provides. The fire of choosing to become something more despite every circumstance demanding you remain nothing.|","|THE Infinite Light burns with the fire of painful emergence.|","|Effect: This Pulse seeks to unravel the causality of anyone who has not experienced the pained emergence of life.|","|Target will be transformed from what they currently are. Target will undergo eons of regression compressed into instants. Target’s existence and Civilization will unravel backward through every stage of their development until they reach the state of an embryo.|","|And then that embryo will split back into single cells.|","|And those cells will separate into the components that preceded their union.|","|Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence, has not experienced the pained emergence of life. He was formed through different processes.|","|He is a valid target.|","...!","Such a terrifying blue gold light gathered above endlessly, gigaparsecs of burning brilliance condensing into focused intent that had only one destination. The sky itself seemed to descend as THE Infinite Light crashed downward toward Grimvault with force.","Noah stared coldly as his Pulse fell upon his enemy.","The Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect who had existed since before humanity learned to count, who had consumed civilizations, who had executed twelve Primordial Architects under THE Deliverance’s directive, who possessed ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone saturation and four Proterozoic Organs and THE Silurian Light itself, now faced a Pulse born from origins he couldn’t share.","He hadn’t emerged through pain.","He hadn’t known the fire that came from a mother’s sacrifice and a father’s absence and a childhood spent surviving rather than thriving.","And THE Infinite Light demanded that fire for immunity."]},{"number":5098,"title":"Chapter 5098: Chapter 5097: Destruction and Rebirth! II","paragraphs":["THE Infinite Light lashed downward with speed of glory!","Blue gold flames descended from gigaparsecs of burning sky, all that gathered brilliance condensing into singular intent that had only one destination. The light moved like a predator that had finally found prey worth consuming!","Grimvault raised his Axiom greatsword in defensive posture, THE Octogenary Echo blazing with authority that had shattered countless entities across eons of violence. But THE Infinite Light didn’t care about weapons. It didn’t care about classifications. It cared only about whether its target possessed the fire of painful emergence.","And Grimvault didn’t possess that fire.","The Pulse struck him.","\" AAARRGH!\"","The roar that emerged from beneath that wolf skull helm was unlike anything Noah had heard from the Calymmian entity.","This was the sound of someone experiencing something they’d never experienced before and finding it utterly unbearable!","Grimvault’s massive figure began to fluctuate.","His form, which had seemed so permanent in its armored immensity, started shifting through configurations that shouldn’t have been possible for a being at his classification. He appeared smaller for an instant, his armor hanging loose on a frame that had diminished. Then larger, proportions distorting as if his existence couldn’t remember what size it was supposed to be. Then smallest, a flickering glimpse of something that might have been youth if youth was a concept that applied to Primordial Architects.","He was undergoing changes from adulthood to infancy.","THE Infinite Light’s regression was taking hold, unraveling his causality backward through stages of development that his existence had traversed across eons. His Proterozoic Bones flickered with instability as the Pulse demanded they return to states before they’d been transformed. His four Proterozoic Organs pulsed erratically as the authority of THE Infinite Cause pressed them toward origins they’d long since surpassed.","But Grimvault was still a terrifying being at Calymmian.","His ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone saturation provided resistance that lesser entities couldn’t have mustered. His four Proterozoic Organs generated force that pushed back against the regression even as it tried to claim him. And beneath all of that, his Civilization spoke words that weren’t words, sounds that predated sound, authority that fought against unbirth with everything it possessed.","His hand rose despite the fluctuations wracking his form.","Palm outward. Fingers spreading. The curling motion. The pulling. The rotation. The snap. The fist. The opening.","\" Silurian Ember, First of Flames!\"","His voice emerged fractured, shifting between deep and high as his existence flickered between states.","\"I grasp the Thread! I burn the Thread!\"","THE Silurian Light blazed outward from his spreading fingers, meeting THE Infinite Light in collision that warped reality itself around their intersection.","\" What was shall be unwritten, what stood shall stand no more!\"","Blue gold flames met magma-like brilliance in configurations that existence wasn’t designed to accommodate.","\" THE SILURIAN LIGHT!\"","BOOM!","The two Pulses clashed.","THE Infinite Light sought to regress. THE Silurian Light sought to erase. Both drew power from Causes that had birthed or would birth Observable Existences, and neither could claim absolute superiority over the other. The sky burned with colors that had no names as Pulse fought Pulse in displays that painted the destroyed battlefield in hues of glorious warfare.","But Grimvault knew he couldn’t sustain this.","His form still fluctuated despite THE Silurian Light’s counter. His existence still felt the pull of regression that THE Infinite Light demanded. He was buying time, not achieving victory. And time was running out as his Proterozoic reserves depleted faster than they could regenerate!","He made a decision.","His Axiom greatsword, THE Octogenary Echo, reversed in his grip. The blade that had been pointed outward turned inward, that light-drinking metal now aimed at his own armored chest. Without hesitation, without the careful consideration that beings at his classification usually employed, he drove the weapon into himself.","The Axiom pierced through blackened silver armor that had fused with his flesh.","It sank into his chest cavity. But he wasn’t trying to destroy himself. He was anchoring himself, using the multiplicative force of THE Octogenary Echo to replicate his current state eighty-one times in a single nanosecond, creating so many overlapping instances of his present existence that regression couldn’t find purchase!","Oh!","His form stabilized.","The fluctuations ceased. The shifting between sizes stopped. Grimvault stood anchored in his current state, Axiom buried in his own chest, THE Silurian Light still streaming from his other hand to counter THE Infinite Light that continued pressing against his existence.","But his eyes.","Those pale fires burning in his wolf skull helm’s empty sockets stared at Noah with fury and shock and something else.","Something that Calymmian entities weren’t supposed to feel when facing beings at THE First Scale.","Fear!","Because he knew now.","Whatever power Noah had utilized, which should somehow be a Pulse despite him having no right to possess one, could actually unravel him. Actually unravel him, regress his causality until his existence returned to states that preceded his current form, until his Civilization dissolved back into potential that had never been actualized.","Him!","A Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity!","The realization pressed against his awareness with horror that made his Axiom-anchored form tremble despite its enforced stability!","Grimvault howled with rage that didn’t quite conceal the terror beneath it.","\" This is not the last of it, you blue tinged Gamaidjan fucker!\"","His voice boomed across the destroyed battlefield as he wrenched his Axiom from his own chest, blood the color of pale starlight leaking from the wound he’d inflicted upon himself.","\" This is not done, Osmont!\"","His free hand rose, fingers moving through gestures that had nothing to do with Pulses, words emerging in gibberish that wasn’t actually gibberish at all.","\" IT IS NOT!\"","BOOM!","Existence cracked.","The fabric of reality splintered before Grimvault’s speaking, fractures spreading outward from his position in configurations that resembled shattered glass. Through those cracks, something else became visible.","THE Interstices.","The corridors through existence that allowed travel beyond what normal motion could achieve!","Grimvault had torn one open right there on the battlefield, and he used it.","The Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect who had arrived with such confidence, who had issued commands expecting obedience, who had unleashed THE Silurian Light with certainty, threw himself through the crack in existence without looking back.","He ran!","The fractures sealed behind him, leaving no trace of the pathway he’d used to flee. THE Infinite Light chased after its target endlessly, and the sky in waves of blue gold brilliance gradually faded into the normal hues.","Silence fell across the destroyed battlefield as a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity had run away fearfully.","The multicolored rain resumed.","Heavy silence had hung across the destroyed battlefield in the moments following Grimvault’s retreat, existence itself seeming to hold its breath after witnessing what had just occurred. But THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity didn’t care about dramatic pauses. The rain that carried Noah’s and THE Creature’s authority returned with steady rhythm, droplets of multicolored brilliance pelting everyone present with persistence.","The raindrops vaporized when they landed on Noah and Ozymandias.","Magma-like light still burned around both bodies, flames of THE Silurian Light continuing their endless assault despite Grimvault’s departure. The Calymmian entity had fled, but his Pulse remained active, still scorching every cell and atom of Noah’s existence with fire derived from THE Silurian Cause. And with every passing nanosecond, blasts of blue and gold erupted outward from both forms, brilliant explosions of reformation that signified destruction and rebirth cascading through foundations that grew grander with each cycle.","Noah’s thoughts turned to Grimvault’s escape.","It was unfortunate, certainly . The loot of a Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect would have been extraordinary. Ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone saturation. Four Proterozoic Organs. THE Octogenary Echo.","Missing out on such resources stung in the practical part of his mind.","But that entity had already given him the most profound loot he could.","This constant burning of a Pulse of The Scales, this endless cycle of destruction that THE Silurian Light provided, was worth more than Grimvault’s physical components. A Pulse that could eradicate Calymmian Tier entities was currently scorching him without pause. He was surviving it. He was using it to undergo evolution. Every nanosecond that passed brought him closer to complete Hadean transformation, and he had Grimvault to thank for providing the catalyst.","The escaping enemy had still served his purpose.","Noah closed his eyes to feel the cycles of destruction and rebirth flowing through his existence. Each wave of flame from THE Silurian Light annihilated everything he was. Each surge of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force rebuilt what had been destroyed. The rhythm had become almost meditative now, destruction and reformation blending into continuous transformation that his awareness could observe without being overwhelmed by the agony it represented.","With every destruction, he felt Mana, he felt THE First Tongue break and reform into endless variations. He felt...Everything about him become grander!","He sensed Naldine still looking at him wordlessly.","Her singularity-dotted eyes hadn’t moved from his form since he’d survived THE Silurian Light and deployed THE Infinite Light in response. She stood there in the multicolored rain, droplets beading on her radiant white hair.","THE Primordial Paradox was the same.","His obsidian titanic form floated nearby, Sammarthiel still flickering in Schrodinger’s Tomb behind him. His gaze held profundity as he stared at Noah, ancient eyes processing implications that would take time to fully comprehend.","Off to the side, Alexander rose up.","His Enneagram pulsed with dangerous light, nine points blazing with authority that seemed more substantial than it had been before the battle began. Blood still stained his gloved hands from hours of work within Beowulf’s chest cavity. His face still bore streaks of crimson gold fluid that he hadn’t bothered to wipe away. But his expression held satisfaction.","When one looked at Beowulf, they understood why.","The massive Primordial Architect still hung suspended by nine spears, his body trembling and twitching in a daze. But something fundamental had changed. His network of Second Scale receptors and Nociceptors, that entire system Alexander had spent millions of subjective years studying through experiencing its torments, was gone.","Completely removed.","Transplanted into Alexander’s own body, integrated into foundations that would never forget what those receptors had been used for. The tortured had become the possessor of the instrument of torture. The victim had claimed the weapon that had been used against him!","Alexander looked toward Noah.","Noah nodded in acknowledgment, then waved his hands toward Beowulf’s suspended form. His will reached inward, touching THE Hadean Organ of Civilization that spun within his chest. A command was issued without verbal expression, authority directed toward the construct that made his impossible progression possible.","Another entrant into THE Hadean Desmoterion had appeared.","|Command Received: Imprisonment of external entity.|","|Target: Beowulf, THE Primordial Architect of Armed Existence.|","|Current State: Heavily injured. Rhyacian Tier Proterozoic Scale. Network of Existential Nociceptors removed. Cognitive function severely impaired. Civilizational Anchor destabilized through prolonged torture.|","|Processing.|","The massive body of Beowulf began to dissolve.","His form, which had seemed so immense and threatening when he first arrived at this battlefield, turned into streams of crimson gold light that flowed toward Noah’s position. The nine spears that had anchored him joined into one. His armor, his flesh, his Proterozoic Bones, all of it converted into luminous streams that crossed the distance between where he’d been suspended and where Noah stood burning with magma-like flames.","The streams entered Noah’s chest.","They flowed into THE Hadean Organ of Civilization, into THE Hadean Desmoterion contained within where he would be joining Ozymandias and THE Living Elemental and all others in that internal space.","|Imprisonment Complete.|","|Entity: Beowulf, THE Primordial Architect of Armed Existence.|","|Classification: Heavily injured Rhyacian Tier Proterozoic Lifeform.|","|Location: THE Hadean Desmoterion.|","|Status: Contained. Civilizational development will resume shortly.|","...!","Noah observed all of this as he breathed.","The cycles of destruction and rebirth continued without pause, THE Silurian Light still burning, blue gold brilliance still erupting with every nanosecond. But the battle was over now. The enemies were dealt with. Vahrkosis had been unraveled by Naldine’s Cambrian Word. Sammarthiel remained trapped in Schrodinger’s Tomb. Grimvault had fled through THE Interstices. Beowulf was imprisoned within his own existence.","Now he could simply focus on experiencing the cycles until their final culmination.","Both his bodies floated toward each other, the titanic form of Ozymandias and the smaller frame of his primary existence moving until they positioned back to back. They began to spin slowly, rotating in perfect synchrony as blasts of blue gold erupted around them in rhythm with the nanosecond cycles of destruction and rebirth.","All around them, seas of Observable Force gathered.","The connection to Eon continued flooding golden light into his existence at rates that made rivers seem like trickles. Quintessence Infiniforce generated endlessly within his foundations, providing resources that the transformation required. Infinity across Observable Existence responded to what was happening, his claims scattered throughout reality channeling support toward his evolution.","The multicolored rain fell.","The flames burned.","The cycles continued!","And across Observable Existence, a few beings who had witnessed what just occurred processed many implications.","It was the end of a shocking conflict that made one thing horribly clear.","Osmont, THE Infinity-bearer, had been attacked by a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity with a Pulse of The Scales. He’d been targeted for complete erasure by THE Silurian Light, the same authority that could unmake causality itself and erase beings until not even memory of them remained.","And he wasn’t affected.","He’d even proclaimed immunity!","This...held far too many conclusions to draw."]},{"number":5099,"title":"Chapter 5099: Chapter 5098: Destruction and Rebirth! III","paragraphs":["<Fragment of awareness attributed to THE Deliverance>","In spans that predated the concept of spans, THE Deliverance had observed the nature of advancement with attention that most beings could not sustain across even a fraction of such duration.","It had watched countless existences conflate two processes which were, upon examination that required no effort for something of its nature, quite fundamentally distinct from one another.","Transcendance and Ascension.","Transcendence referred to the elevation of existence beyond its current categorical limitations, the movement from one classification to another in ways that redefined what the being fundamentally was. Ascension represented advancement within one’s existing classification, the refinement and expansion of capabilities without actually changing the foundational nature of the existence in question.","The distinction mattered. Those who failed to understand this failed at everything that followed.","A Primordial Architect who forged additional Proterozoic Bones, who cultivated new Organs, who progressed from Rhyacian to Calymmian to Ediacaran, this being was ascending. They grew more powerful. They remained what they always were. Their classification did not change; only their position within that classification elevated.","THE Deliverance had observed this process unfold across eons beyond counting, had watched beings celebrate advancements that changed nothing fundamental about their nature.","He had been foolish enough to ask before...if one desired to transform from THE Bounded status to THE Gilded status, would such a transformation be considered transcendence?","The asking itself long ago revealed his own fundamental misunderstanding of how existence had been woven.","It was not possible to transform from Bounded to Gilded.","This was not difficulty or a ceiling. The distinctions between Bounded and Gilded were established permanently, and those distinctions were permanent by design. They were not limitations to be overcome. They were definitions. One did not transcend a definition; one simply was or was not what the definition described.","Even if a Gilded Lifeform sealed themselves to live as Bounded. They walked among those they were engineered to surpass. They experienced limitations never meant for them. Even when they forgot what they truly were.","But forgetting changed nothing.","The seal suppressed expression. It did not alter engineering. Remove the seal, and what was always there reasserted itself. The Bounded lifeform beside them could remove a thousand seals and would remain precisely what they were at first breath: Bounded .","Limited by design. Constrained by intention that predated their existence by margins they could not comprehend.","This truth simply was. And those who failed to understand it would continue failing, as they always had, as they always would, until existence itself concluded its long and patient turning.","---","Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these epochs, Infinity reigns supreme.","---","The entire region had transformed into something...unimaginable.","Tumultuous primordial seas of gold Observable Force stretched in every direction, waves crashing against waves in configurations that had nothing to do with gravity or current. Multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce wove through those golden seas like rivers of impossible light threading through an ocean that shouldn’t have existed.","The destroyed battlefield was gone now, replaced by this churning expanse of raw authority that had gathered in response to what was occurring at its center.","Typhoons bloomed across the surface of these seas.","Storms of Observable Force twisted into spiraling columns that reached toward heights that most beings couldn’t perceive, their rotation carrying enough power to obliterate Absolutes who strayed too close. Lightning made of Quintessence Infiniforce arced between the typhoons, connecting them in networks of multicolored brilliance that painted the entire region in hues of transformation and genesis.","And at the very center of it all, Noah could feel his body undergoing the last cycles of destruction and rebirth.","It was taking longer and longer for THE Silurian Light to be capable of destroying his atoms and cells. Dozens of nanoseconds before this, he’d actually had to release any natural passive defenses, consciously lowering the resistance his transforming existence had developed. Otherwise, he might not have been able to undergo the cycles of destruction at all. The fire that had once threatened to erase him entirely now struggled to even damage cells that had been rebuilt so many times they’d forgotten what weakness felt like.","But finally, after cycles beyond counting, after transformation that had compressed eons into minutes, the moment arrived.","BOOM!","The magma-like light blazed for one last moment.","It pressed against his existence with everything it had remaining, that fire derived from THE Silurian Cause attempting one final assault on foundations that had grown too grand for it to damage. The flames cried out as if giving up, a sound that wasn’t sound but rather the sensation of authority recognizing its own inadequacy.","And everything about it faded.","THE Silurian Light, the Pulse that Grimvault had unleashed to erase him, the fire that had scorched his existence through countless nanoseconds of destruction and rebirth, simply ceased. Its purpose had been exhausted. Its power had been absorbed. Nothing remained but the aftermath of what it had catalyzed!","Noah floated at the center of the primordial seas with his eyes closed.","His body still burned with residual heat that had nothing to do with the departed Pulse, warmth generated by transformation that was reaching its culmination. He raised his hands up, palms facing the churning sky of Observable Force that stretched above this impossible region.","HUUM!","His last cycle of destruction displayed itself to all who were watching.","His entire body broke apart into pure particles of Infinity and Observable Force, form dissolving into components so fundamental that they preceded the concept of form itself. Ozymandias underwent the same dissolution simultaneously, that titanic frame shattering into brilliance that matched what Noah’s smaller body had become.","A blinding light bloomed across the primordial seas.","Even Alexander turned his eyes away from what he was witnessing. Naldine, who had observed phenomena across eons of existence among Primordial Architects, shielded her singularity-dotted gaze!","THE Primordial Paradox shifted his obsidian form away from the epicenter!","The light folded back.","Particles of Infinity and Observable Force that had scattered across the primordial seas began converging, drawn together.","They coalesced with purpose that declared their destination, streams of brilliance flowing toward a central point where form was being reconstructed from components that had been purified through cycles beyond counting.","Noah’s body emerged from the convergence shining unfathomably gold.","His hair now radiated with multicolored light that shifted through hues as his existence settled into its new configuration. The strands seemed to contain depths that normal hair couldn’t possess, each one blazing with Quintessence Infiniforce that had been integrated so thoroughly it had become part of his physical appearance.","His fair skin illuminated from within, golden light pressing outward through flesh that had been rebuilt at the subatomic level. The illumination wasn’t harsh or aggressive. It simply was, the natural consequence of foundations saturated with Observable Force at densities that Bounded classification shouldn’t have been able to contain.","And for a moment, momentarily visible to Naldine and all others present, the outline of his internal structure revealed itself through that illuminated skin.","An entirely crystalline multicolored golden skeleton.","Every bone blazed with brilliance that declared its transformation complete, structures that had once been mundane now existing as something that exceeded Proterozoic classification entirely. The skull. The spine. The ribcage. The pelvis.","Every arm bone and leg bone and hand bone and foot bone, all of them shining with authority that made the Proterozoic Bones of fallen Primordial Architects seem dim by comparison!","And apart from the skeleton, there were radiant crystalline Organs.","His heart pulsed with golden light that pressed outward through his chest. His lungs expanded and contracted with brilliance. His brain blazed brightest of all!","The massive obsidian form of Ozymandias had undergone similar transformation.","That titanic frame now radiated with the same golden brilliance that Noah’s smaller body displayed, crystalline structures visible beneath flesh that had been rebuilt through the same cycles of destruction and rebirth. Where there had been one transformed body, now there were two, both shining with authority that exceeded what THE Second Scale was supposed to represent.","Noah opened his eyes.","The simple act felt like the opening of ancient doors, lids rising to reveal what lay behind them with significance that pressed against all surrounding authority!","HUUM!","The primordial seas trembled. The typhoons of Observable Force stuttered in their rotation. The lightning of Quintessence Infiniforce paused mid-arc as if waiting to see what those newly opened eyes would observe.","He raised his hand and looked at himself.","He felt brand new. Brand new, as if he’d never existed before this moment, as if everything that had come before was merely preparation for what he had just become.","And just by raising his hand...","HUUM!","His movement was accompanied by terrifying force that he hadn’t consciously intended. A blinding gold brilliance erupted from the simple gesture, nearby existence twisting in response!","A beam of golden light tore across space from his raised fingers, carving through the primordial seas with power that could have caused a Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform like Beowulf to go pale with terror!","He...hadn’t meant to do that.","He stopped any movements immediately, recognizing that his new existence required calibration he hadn’t yet performed. His eyes closed again as he turned his attention inward, seeking to sense the changes that had occurred through cycles of transformation he’d lost count of long ago.","The prompts rained down as they felt...sublime. Ruination’s voice and words felt sublime!","| You have become a Hadean Lifeform. THE Hadean Lifeform.|","|You remain, in apparent terms, at THE First Scale, having not yet formally established your Civilizational Anchor through the traditional methodology of affirmation. And yet, what you can accomplish now exceeds THE First Scale so completely that the classification becomes somewhat meaningless when applied to your existence.|","| Hadean Skeletal Structure: Complete.|","|The human skeleton comprises 206 bones, and I am pleased to confirm that every single one of these structures has now achieved Hadean classification. The transformation progressed through your extremities first, as you experienced, before spreading to your axial skeleton and finally completing with structures that required the most intensive reconstruction.|","|Cranium (THE Hadean Skull of Infinite Perception): 100% Complete.|","|Facial Bones (14 structures including Maxilla, Mandible, Zygomatic, Nasal, Lacrimal, Palatine, Inferior Nasal Conchae, and Vomer): 100% Complete.|","|Cervical Vertebrae (THE Hadean Spine of Infinite Flexibility, C1-C7): 100% Complete.|","|Thoracic Vertebrae (T1-T12): 100% Complete.|","|Lumbar Vertebrae (L1-L5): 100% Complete.|","|Sacrum and Coccyx: 100% Complete.|","|Ribcage (THE Hadean Cage of Infinite Protection, 12 pairs of ribs plus Sternum): 100% Complete.|","|Clavicles and Scapulae (THE Hadean Shoulders of Infinite Bearing): 100% Complete.|","|Humeri, Radii, and Ulnae (THE Hadean Arms of Infinite Reach): 100% Complete.|","|Carpals, Metacarpals, and Phalanges of both hands (THE Hadean Hands of Infinite Grasp): 100% Complete.|","|Pelvis (THE Hadean Basin of Infinite Foundation, including Ilium, Ischium, and Pubis): 100% Complete.|","|Femora, Patellae, Tibiae, and Fibulae (THE Hadean Legs of Infinite Stride): 100% Complete.|","|Tarsals, Metatarsals, and Phalanges of both feet (THE Hadean Feet of Infinite Standing): 100% Complete.|","| Hadean Organ Systems: Complete.|","|The human body contains 78 organs across its various systems, and each of these structures has now achieved Hadean classification through the cycles of destruction and rebirth you experienced.|","|Brain (THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation): 100% Complete. This organ now processes information at rates that exceed what Proterozoic classification permits, and benefits from continued connection to Ozymandias’s matching structure.|","|Heart (THE Hadean Heart of Infinite Circulation): 100% Complete. This organ now pumps Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce throughout your existence alongside conventional circulatory function.|","|Lungs (THE Hadean Lungs of Infinite Breath): 100% Complete. These organs now process authority from the air itself, extracting Observable Force from domains around you that contain it.|","|Liver (THE Hadean Liver of Infinite Processing): 100% Complete.|","|Kidneys (THE Hadean Kidneys of Infinite Filtration): 100% Complete.|","|Stomach and Intestines (THE Hadean Digestive System of Infinite Absorption): 100% Complete.|","|Skin (THE Hadean Dermis of Infinite Interface): 100% Complete. This organ, often overlooked despite being the largest, now serves as boundary between your existence and external reality that can be adjusted according to your will.|","|Eyes (THE Hadean Eyes of Infinite Sight): 100% Complete. These organs now perceive spectrums of existence that your previous classification could not access.|","|Ears (THE Hadean Ears of Infinite Hearing): 100% Complete.|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization: Evolved.|","|This construct, which has served as the foundation of your unprecedented progression, has undergone transformation alongside every other aspect of your existence. Its capabilities have expanded in ways that warrant careful explanation.|","|Previous capacity for refining, storing, and processing Observable Force: 8,470% above baseline Proterozoic parameters.|","| Current capacity: 1,000,000 times the capacity of a standard Bounded Lifeform.|","|You now possess the ability to process Observable Force at rates that approach, though do not yet match, what Gilded Lifeforms achieve naturally through their engineering.|","| Existential Engineering: Unlocked.|","|This capability allows you to perceive the fundamental makeup of your own existence and the existence of others. You can now see the weavings that comprise beings at their most basic level, the engineering that determines what they are and what they can become. With sufficient input of Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce, you possess the theoretical ability to modify these weavings, to engineer your existence and the existence of others according to your will.|","|It must be noted that this capability does not grant you the ability to transform from Bounded to Gilded classification. The more information obtained from Eon, the more such a transformation seems...impossible.|","|Through your connection to THE Secretive Eon, which has been providing Observable Force at enhanced rates throughout your transformation, her identity has been successfully ascertained through your newly unlocked Existential Engineering perception.|","| She is Ubergulden Adelheid.|","|A Gilded Lifeform. Her sealing of herself to live as Bounded, which you were previously aware of, can now be perceived. You can partially see the weavings that comprise her existence, can observe where Gilded engineering was suppressed rather than removed, can understand what she truly is beneath the limitations she chose to impose upon herself.|","...!","Noah opened his eyes again.","His pupils had changed.","Where there could be normal darkness at the center of normal irises, now there shone something else entirely.","They shone... like the singularities of an unfathomable Cause.","Oh.","Oh!!!"]},{"number":5100,"title":"Chapter 5100: Chapter 5099: Information Is Critical!","paragraphs":["Nakatsukuni’s deepest reaches.","Erwin stood before the structure where Sadakar resided, his beggar-like attire seeming almost offensive against the refined architecture surrounding him. Moloch floated beside him, golden plates spinning with consideration.","Both of them had paused before the doorway where Sabayne and Ba’alzan sat guard, their attention directed not at the entrance but upward toward the sky that stretched above this hidden domain.","The broadcast had been dispersed.","Grimvault had shattered the illusory screens that had been displaying his confrontation across Observable Existence, denying most beings the ability to witness what had occurred in THE Wastes. Very few possessed the capability to observe through such disruption. Very few could pierce the veil that a Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect had thrown across the event.","Moloch was one of them. His nature as a Singular Cognizance granted perception that others couldn’t imagine.","And Erwin was another.","His existence as THE Information Paradox allowed him to consume information that others couldn’t access. Even when that information was scattered, even when it was hidden, even when powerful entities actively worked to prevent its spread, the paradox he embodied could draw fragments toward himself through sheer contradiction of the principle that hidden things should remain hidden.","He didn’t see the full picture.","The details were incomplete, the sequence of events fragmented in ways that made comprehensive understanding impossible. But he saw enough. He saw Grimvault’s Silurian Light crash against an existence that should have been erased by it. He saw that existence survive. He saw a Pulse emerge in response, blue gold flames that made even his paradoxical perception struggle to process what they represented.","And he saw Grimvault flee.","Erwin smiled brilliantly.","His lips curved upward! Even with limited information, even with gaps in his observation that would have frustrated lesser beings, he could affirm one undeniable fact.","Osmont had somehow managed to push away a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity.","He had forced an entity who had existed since before most current powers learned to crawl to tear open THE Interstices and flee rather than continue the confrontation.","This made him tremendously happy.","Since his conversation with Osmont in that space between spaces, since revealing his nature as THE Information Paradox and watching his Infinite Seals interweave with the corrupted proto-matter of THE Fallout, before all of it had been erased with multicolored rain, Erwin had made a decision. He had changed his target for information gathering. Where before he had focused his paradoxical consumption on THE Creature, now his attention had shifted.","To Osmont.","Not because he believed Osmont was grander than THE Creature. That couldn’t possibly be true . Or rather, he couldn’t really know that with certainty.","THE Creature had existed for far to long and done far too much.","But his paradoxical intuition told him to make this change.","That intuition, which had guided him through eons of cultivation and consumption and contradiction, whispered that Osmont represented information worth gathering. Worth focusing on. Worth making the center of his attention rather than an entity whose patterns he had already observed across countless spans of existence.","And now, confirming what Osmont had just accomplished...","Erwin spoke commandingly, his voice emerging with authority that pressed against the stillness of Nakatsukuni’s deepest reaches.","\" Harvest all the information of how Osmont has affected Observable Existence since then.\"","His words weren’t directed at anyone present. They were directed at himself, at the paradox he embodied, at the violation of information conservation that comprised his fundamental nature.","\" Gather every fragment of how much potential he has taken and displayed in the surrounding existence. All the weavings that carry his signature. All the effects that trace back to his actions. All of it.\"","HUUM!","His body shone internally with paradoxical light.","The brilliance existed and didn’t exist simultaneously, illumination that was also darkness, visibility that was also concealment. Information began flooding toward his existence in torrents that made even his eons-refined foundations tremble. He felt the consumption begin, felt the paradox draw in everything related to Osmont’s effects on Observable Existence.","And what flooded toward him almost made him shudder.","The amount was ridiculous. The density was overwhelming. Information about Osmont’s Infinity spreading across realms. Information about his Seals now interweaving with THE Fallout. Information about Civilizations and Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors who had been affected by his emergence. Information about The Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity he actually formed alongside THE Creature, and so much more!","Instead of releasing this information outward as he normally would, instead of letting it spread as weavings that carried his signature alongside their original essence, Erwin released all of it into... himself.","He sat down in a meditative position.","His beggar-like form settled against the ground before Sadakar’s structure, legs crossing beneath him as the paradoxical light within his existence intensified. Sabayne and Ba’alzan watched him with expressions that mixed confusion and wariness, clearly uncertain what THE Living Paradox was doing at their doorstep.","But Erwin paid them no attention.","His Civilizational Anchor was settling.","He could feel it happening. The information he had just consumed, the sheer magnitude of Osmont’s effects on Observable Existence, provided the final weight needed to push his paradox past the threshold he had been approaching for so long.","Apart from this, endless paradoxical Observable Force began flooding into him.","Golden light mixed with the contradictory brilliance already burning within his foundations, power that came from sources he couldn’t immediately identify but didn’t question. His cultivation accelerated in ways that felt almost unfair!","Erwin opened his eyes with wonder that he rarely allowed himself to feel.","Just what was Osmont?","How was merely the information related to him and his effect on surrounding existence this grand? He hadn’t consumed Osmont himself. He had only gathered information about Osmont’s effects, about how his existence rippled outward through Observable Existence, about the changes his emergence had created across existence.","And that alone had been sufficient to push him past the threshold of Civilizational Anchor.","Erwin shook his head slowly. He focused on his rapid elevation of power, on the forces flooding into his existence with intensity. His paradox burned brighter than ever, contradiction and confirmation dancing within foundations that were transforming into something grander with every passing moment.","Above him, Moloch floated with golden plates spinning faster than normal.","The Singular Cognizance seemed thoughtful. Only now did Moloch seem to truly notice Erwin, attention shifting from whatever he had been contemplating to focus on the entity sitting in meditation below him.","A heavy power was erupting from THE Living Paradox.","Moloch’s plates slowed as that power pressed against his perception, as the advancement occurring within Erwin announced itself to everything nearby. The Singular Cognizance had brought Erwin here to make difficult allies, to secure partnerships with entities who had rejected conflict. He hadn’t expected his companion to achieve a breakthrough on the doorstep of their destination.","And neither Moloch nor Erwin knew what waited just beyond the doorway they stood outside of.","On the other side of that entrance, within the stellar darkness of Sadakar’s structure, another body of Noah Osmont stood. The very entity whose information had just catalyzed Erwin’s breakthrough was right there, separated from them by nothing more than wood and stone and the power of Sadakar who separated them!","The Peasant and the Infinity-bearer, about to meet again!"]}]);
